</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "32691", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 6, 2012, 12:00:30 AM", "datetime": "2012-10-06T00:00:30-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:51:09+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (35068,'en-US','how-does-firefox-android-provide-secure-mobile-bro','How does Firefox for Android Provide Secure Mobile Browsing?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-does-firefox-android-provide-secure-mobile-bro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-does-firefox-android-provide-secure-mobile-bro/revision/35068',33927,'2013-01-07T13:17:20-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','adding phishing and malware protection for firefox 18 - text originaly written by garf at http://www.morbo.org/2012/10/phishing-protection-on-mobile.html',1,'2013-01-07T13:18:33-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2013-01-07T13:18:33-08:00','rtanglao','approved','Firefox for Android uses best practices for security testing and adheres to Mozilla secure-development guidelines just like desktop Firefox. Security testing called ''''fuzzing'''' is used, to make sure Firefox for Android is robust enough to handle all kinds of crazy data without crashing. We do specific testing for the ARM processor, conduct thorough design reviews, code reviews and perform hostile testing in the same form as is done for desktop Firefox.

__TOC__

=Permissions=
We also review the permissions to ensure we don''t have any that we don''t need and then document them, see [[How does Firefox for Android use the permissions it requests?]]. 

=Automatic Updates=
An important part of staying safe online is updating your browser regularly for security improvements. With Firefox, you get updates every six weeks that inherit all of the security updates we develop for desktop Firefox. So, you get the benefit of the 450 million users who depend on Firefox for security on their desktops when you use Firefox for Android. If there is a security threat out there, chances are we know about it and we''ll get a fix into Firefox for Android sooner than other mobile browsers will. Because you can get automatic updates through the market, without any dependence on your carrier, Mozilla can respond to any threat quickly.

=Content and Transport Security=
Firefox for Android also has the same strong content security policy and strict transport policy as your desktop Firefox, requiring pages be served over SSL so they can''t be intercepted and the connection is encrypted preventing scripting attacks. We also alert you to any known malicious sites before loading them in Firefox for Android.

=Data Encryption=
Mozilla offers Sync services, so you don''t need to type your password where someone might see it and you can use a strong password without having to type it on a mobile keyboard because it syncs with your desktop Firefox. And Mozilla encrypts your sync''d data so we don''t have access to bookmarks, history, passwords or form field data like your address and card info (possibly) name, anything else you type into a field. We lock it and no one but you has the key. Passwords are stored internally to Firefox; stored in a place where only Firefox can access them and cannot be accessed by other programs. Even if a malware infected your device, it couldn''t access your data. 

=Plugin Safety=
Firefox for Android {for not m14}doesn''t allow flash{/for}{for m14}uses ''tap to play'' for plugins by default{/for} so you can safely go to any website without the worry of being hacked by plugins. You would have to tap it to get hacked. This also enables you to browse with better performance and without annoying ads. You can also completely disable JavaScript in your settings for the safest possible mobile browsing, since pages can''t run any scripts. 

=Privacy Controls=
Firefox for Android provides a suite of Privacy & Security settings so you can regularly clear your history and private data to stay safe. You can also configure a master password and enable Do Not Track to secure your browser if your device is stolen and prevent advertisers from tracking your browsing patterns.

=Phishing and Malware Protection=
Firefox for Android''s phishing and malware protection works by regularly updating a local list of known bad sites, graciously [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Safe_Browsing provided by Google through their SafeBrowsing database]. Whenever Firefox detects that you navigate to such a site, or that a page you visit is trying to pull data from it, Firefox will present you with a warning page and allow you to abort the operation. 

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/Tgle8h]]','<p>Firefox for Android uses best practices for security testing and adheres to Mozilla secure-development guidelines just like desktop Firefox. Security testing called <em>fuzzing</em> is used, to make sure Firefox for Android is robust enough to handle all kinds of crazy data without crashing. We do specific testing for the ARM processor, conduct thorough design reviews, code reviews and perform hostile testing in the same form as is done for desktop Firefox.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_permissions"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Permissions</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_automatic-updates"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Automatic Updates</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_content-and-transport-security"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Content and Transport Security</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_data-encryption"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Data Encryption</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_plugin-safety"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Plugin Safety</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_privacy-controls"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">Privacy Controls</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_phishing-and-malware-protection"><span class="tocnumber">7</span> <span class="toctext">Phishing and Malware Protection</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_permissions">Permissions</h1>
<p>We also review the permissions to ensure we don''t have any that we don''t need and then document them, see <a href="/en-US/kb/how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests">How does Firefox for Android use the permissions it requests?</a>. 
</p>
<h1 id="w_automatic-updates">Automatic Updates</h1>
<p>An important part of staying safe online is updating your browser regularly for security improvements. With Firefox, you get updates every six weeks that inherit all of the security updates we develop for desktop Firefox. So, you get the benefit of the 450 million users who depend on Firefox for security on their desktops when you use Firefox for Android. If there is a security threat out there, chances are we know about it and we''ll get a fix into Firefox for Android sooner than other mobile browsers will. Because you can get automatic updates through the market, without any dependence on your carrier, Mozilla can respond to any threat quickly.
</p>
<h1 id="w_content-and-transport-security">Content and Transport Security</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android also has the same strong content security policy and strict transport policy as your desktop Firefox, requiring pages be served over SSL so they can''t be intercepted and the connection is encrypted preventing scripting attacks. We also alert you to any known malicious sites before loading them in Firefox for Android.
</p>
<h1 id="w_data-encryption">Data Encryption</h1>
<p>Mozilla offers Sync services, so you don''t need to type your password where someone might see it and you can use a strong password without having to type it on a mobile keyboard because it syncs with your desktop Firefox. And Mozilla encrypts your sync''d data so we don''t have access to bookmarks, history, passwords or form field data like your address and card info (possibly) name, anything else you type into a field. We lock it and no one but you has the key. Passwords are stored internally to Firefox; stored in a place where only Firefox can access them and cannot be accessed by other programs. Even if a malware infected your device, it couldn''t access your data. 
</p>
<h1 id="w_plugin-safety">Plugin Safety</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android <span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;">doesn''t allow flash</span><span class="for" data-for="m14">uses ''tap to play'' for plugins by default</span> so you can safely go to any website without the worry of being hacked by plugins. You would have to tap it to get hacked. This also enables you to browse with better performance and without annoying ads. You can also completely disable JavaScript in your settings for the safest possible mobile browsing, since pages can''t run any scripts. 
</p>
<h1 id="w_privacy-controls">Privacy Controls</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android provides a suite of Privacy &amp; Security settings so you can regularly clear your history and private data to stay safe. You can also configure a master password and enable Do Not Track to secure your browser if your device is stolen and prevent advertisers from tracking your browsing patterns.
</p>
<h1 id="w_phishing-and-malware-protection">Phishing and Malware Protection</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android''s phishing and malware protection works by regularly updating a local list of known bad sites, graciously <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Safe_Browsing">provided by Google through their SafeBrowsing database</a>. Whenever Firefox detects that you navigate to such a site, or that a page you visit is trying to pull data from it, Firefox will present you with a warning page and allow you to abort the operation. 
</p><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "35068", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jan 7, 2013, 1:17:20 PM", "datetime": "2013-01-07T13:17:20-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "adding phishing and malware protection for firefox 18 - text originaly written by garf at http://www.morbo.org/2012/10/phishing-protection-on-mobile.html", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jan 7, 2013, 1:18:33 PM", "datetime": "2013-01-07T13:18:33-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jan 7, 2013, 1:18:33 PM", "datetime": "2013-01-07T13:18:33-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:51:06+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (36122,'en-US','make-firefox-default-browser-android','Set Firefox as your default browser on Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-firefox-default-browser-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-firefox-default-browser-android/revision/36122',NULL,'2013-02-03T15:10:23-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','first version',1,'2013-02-04T03:25:59-08:00','mluna',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','__TOC__
This article explains how to make links on your Android device open in Firefox by default:
* First, clear the current browser that opens links.
* Then, open a link in an Android application like the mail application and set Firefox to be the default browser to open links.
=Clear the current browser that opens links=
# Open the Settings application and tap on {button Apps} (On some versions of Android this button is labelled "Applications").
# Tap on the {button All} tab.<br/>[[Image:Android ICS Manage Apps - Cropped]]
# Tap on the current browser that opens links. This is usually the default browser which is called "Browser" or "Internet".
# Tap on {button Clear defaults} to prevent this browser from opening links by default. If this "Clear defaults" is greyed out, then the default browser is another browser like Opera; go back to the previous step and repeat with the default browser.
[[Image:Android ICS Clear defaults - Cropped]]

=Set Firefox to be the default browser for opening links=
# Open a link in an Android application like the Mail application.
# Tap on {button Firefox} and then tap on {button Always}.
[[Image:Android ICS Complete Action using Firefox Always]]','<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_clear-the-current-browser-that-opens-links"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Clear the current browser that opens links</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_set-firefox-to-be-the-default-browser-for-opening-links"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Set Firefox to be the default browser for opening links</span></a></li></ul></div>
<p>This article explains how to make links on your Android device open in Firefox by default:
</p>
<ul><li> First, clear the current browser that opens links.
</li><li> Then, open a link in an Android application like the mail application and set Firefox to be the default browser to open links.
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_clear-the-current-browser-that-opens-links">Clear the current browser that opens links</h1>
<ol><li> Open the Settings application and tap on <span class="button">Apps</span> (On some versions of Android this button is labelled "Applications").
</li><li> Tap on the <span class="button">All</span> tab.<br><img alt="Android ICS Manage Apps - Cropped" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-03-22-21-18-1ea9c5.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li> Tap on the current browser that opens links. This is usually the default browser which is called "Browser" or "Internet".
</li><li> Tap on <span class="button">Clear defaults</span> to prevent this browser from opening links by default. If this "Clear defaults" is greyed out, then the default browser is another browser like Opera; go back to the previous step and repeat with the default browser.
</li></ol>
<p><img alt="Android ICS Clear defaults - Cropped" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-03-22-30-33-ca626d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_set-firefox-to-be-the-default-browser-for-opening-links">Set Firefox to be the default browser for opening links</h1>
<ol><li> Open a link in an Android application like the Mail application.
</li><li> Tap on <span class="button">Firefox</span> and then tap on <span class="button">Always</span>.
</li></ol>
<p><img alt="Android ICS Complete Action using Firefox Always" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-01-15-40-38-8668d9.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "36122", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 3, 2013, 3:10:23 PM", "datetime": "2013-02-03T15:10:23-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "first version", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Feb 4, 2013, 3:25:59 AM", "datetime": "2013-02-04T03:25:59-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "mluna", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:51:04+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (36251,'en-US','firefox-android-crashes-startup-how-fix','Firefox for Android Crashes On Startup - How To Fix','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-android-crashes-startup-how-fix','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-android-crashes-startup-how-fix/revision/36251',NULL,'2013-02-06T05:56:45-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','placeholder',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','If Firefox on Android crashes on startup with "OpenGL-accelerated layers are a hard requirement on this platform", here''s how to fix it:
# Uninstall Firefox for Android
# [[How do I install Firefox on an Android device?|Install Firefox for Android]]','<p>If Firefox on Android crashes on startup with "OpenGL-accelerated layers are a hard requirement on this platform", here''s how to fix it:
</p>
<ol><li> Uninstall Firefox for Android
</li><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/install-firefox-android-device-using-google-play">Install Firefox for Android</a>
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "36251", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 6, 2013, 5:56:45 AM", "datetime": "2013-02-06T05:56:45-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "placeholder", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:50:54+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (36252,'en-US','uninstall-firefox-your-android-device','Uninstall Firefox from your Android device','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/uninstall-firefox-your-android-device','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/uninstall-firefox-your-android-device/revision/36252',NULL,'2013-02-06T06:43:31-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','work in progress, do not approve, needs another screenshot to show finding Firefox on the Google App store',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','To uninstall Firefox, follow these steps:
# Open the Google Play Store application
# Search for Firefox and Tap on Firefox
# Tap on {button Uninstall}<br />[[Image:ICS - Android - Uninstalling from Google Play]]
Your uninstall of Firefox is finished.','<p>To uninstall Firefox, follow these steps:
</p>
<ol><li> Open the Google Play Store application
</li><li> Search for Firefox and Tap on Firefox
</li><li> Tap on <span class="button">Uninstall</span><br><img alt="ICS - Android - Uninstalling from Google Play" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-06-14-40-51-75b561.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
<p>Your uninstall of Firefox is finished.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "36252", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 6, 2013, 6:43:31 AM", "datetime": "2013-02-06T06:43:31-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "work in progress, do not approve, needs another screenshot to show finding Firefox on the Google App store", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:50:52+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (36253,'en-US','uninstall-firefox-your-android-device','Uninstall Firefox from your Android device','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/uninstall-firefox-your-android-device','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/uninstall-firefox-your-android-device/revision/36253',NULL,'2013-02-06T06:55:49-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','do not approve please further work in progress',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','To uninstall Firefox, follow these steps:
# Open the Google Play Store application
# Search for Firefox and Tap on {button Firefox}<Br />[[Image:ICS - Android - Searching for Firefox in Google Play]]
# Tap on {button Uninstall}<br />[[Image:ICS - Android - Uninstalling from Google Play]]
Your uninstall of Firefox is finished.','<p>To uninstall Firefox, follow these steps:
</p>
<ol><li> Open the Google Play Store application
</li><li> Search for Firefox and Tap on <span class="button">Firefox</span><br><img alt="ICS - Android - Searching for Firefox in Google Play" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-06-14-54-24-c3148f.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li> Tap on <span class="button">Uninstall</span><br><img alt="ICS - Android - Uninstalling from Google Play" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-06-14-40-51-75b561.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
<p>Your uninstall of Firefox is finished.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "36253", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 6, 2013, 6:55:49 AM", "datetime": "2013-02-06T06:55:49-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "do not approve please further work in progress", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:50:50+00:00');
