INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (36272,'en-US','get-started-firefox-android','Get started with Firefox for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/get-started-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/get-started-firefox-android/revision/36272',30495,'2013-02-06T13:58:32-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','Merge the content of "Getting started with Firefox for mobile" into this article now that marketing has decided to use ''Android'' instead of ''mobile''',1,'2013-02-06T14:02:12-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2013-02-06T14:02:12-08:00','rtanglao','approved','{for not m14}
New to Firefox for Android? Well you’ve come to the right place. This article covers all the basics and will get you up and running in just a few minutes. It also has links to other great articles that you might want to explore later.
{/for}
{for m14}
New to Firefox for Android? Well you’ve come to the right place. Here we show you how to start using Firefox for Android on your smartphone or {for =m14}7"{/for} tablet to safely and easily browse your favorite web sites, access Firefox bookmarks and history, and manage your Firefox settings.
{/for}

__TOC__

{for not m14}
[[Video:Getting started with Firefox for mobile]]

=Where are all of the controls?=
To save space on your device''s display, Firefox''s browser controls are stowed away on the sides of the screen. You can access them by swiping your finger left or right. 
*Swipe right to show your tabs and the {button New Tab} button. 
*Swipe left to reveal the bookmark {button Star} button, the {button Back} and {button Forward} buttons and the {button Gear} button which lets you access the Preference, Downloads and Add-ons screens.
*In addition, swiping either left, right or down will bring up the location bar which contains:
**''''''The site icon:'''''' Tap to see the site menu with page-specific options.
**''''''The location bar:'''''' Tap to open the Awesome Screen
**''''''The combination reload and stop button:'''''' Tap to stop loading or to reload a page.
[[Image:Mobile Controls v6]]
*Tap the hardware {button Menu} button on your device to view the Site Options, Preferences, Add-ons, Share Page, Find In Page and More controls.
*Tap {button More} to access Downloads, to Quit Firefox or to use the Save as PDF function.
[[Image: Hardware Menu Mobile]]

=How do I open a new tab?=
#Swipe to the right to select the {button New Tab} button located on the bottom, left side of the screen.
#You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 
[[Image:Mobile Tabs1]]
{note}For more tab tricks, see [[Use tabs to quickly switch websites on Firefox for mobile]].{/note}

=How do I quickly find the site I want?=
#Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the location bar at the top of any page or by creating a new tab.
#Then simply select a site from the list of your most visited sites. 
#* You can also search through your bookmarks, history, and desktop tabs. Just tap on one of the results to go to that page.<br>
[[Image:Awesome Screen - alt]]
{note}For more about the Awesome Screen, see [[Use the Awesome screen to search in Firefox for Android]]{/note}

=How do I bookmark a site?=
#Just go to the site you want to bookmark, swipe to the left and tap the {button Star} button. The star will turn yellow to let you know the bookmark has been saved.<br><br>[[Image:Mobile bookmark1]]
{note}For more about working with bookmarks, see [[Use bookmarks on Firefox for Android to keep track of your favorite websites]]{/note}

=How do I zoom into a website?=
To make Firefox zoom into a section of website, just double-tap the area you''d like to see. Double-tap again to zoom out.<br><br>[[Image:Zoom1]]
{note}For more about zoom settings, see [[Zoom in and out of websites on Firefox for mobile]]{/note}

=How do I copy and paste text?=
Just long-tap a word to select it on a web page or within an entry field, then tap it again to copy it to the clipboard.<br><br>[[Image:Select word]]
{note}For more about copy and paste, see [[How do I copy and paste text on mobile?]].{/note}

=How do I manage downloads?=
#Swipe to the left and tap the {button Gear} button located on the bottom, right side of the screen. 
#Select the downloads (downward arrow) tab to manage your downloads. 
[[Image:Mobile Downloads]]

=How do I sync Firefox between my desktop and mobile?=
You can use Firefox Sync to share your bookmarks, passwords, settings, history, and tabs between your desktop and mobile. First just set up Firefox Sync on your desktop and then add your mobile device with the easy setup code.
{note}For detailed instructions, see [[Use Sync to share your Firefox bookmarks, passwords and more with Firefox for mobile]]{/note}

=How do I find and install add-ons?=
You can browse through and search for add-ons right inside of Firefox.
#To start, swipe to the left and tap the {button Gear} button located on the bottom, right side of the screen. 
#Select the add-ons (puzzle piece) tab and scroll down to see an add-ons search bar and a list of popular add-ons . 
#To install an add-on, tap to select it and then tap {button Add to Firefox}.<br><br>[[Image:Mobile Add-ons1]]
{note}To learn more about add-ons, see [[Find and install Add-ons on Firefox for Mobile]]{/note}
{/for}
{for m14}
=Firefox for Android start page=
At the top of the Firefox app are the Title bar and the Tab. Tap the Title bar to open your Bookmarks, history, and top sites lists. 

[[Image:getting_started_native_gingerbread1]]<br><br>

''''''Firefox Sync'''''' - share your bookmarks, history, passwords and open tabs  [[Use Sync to share your Firefox bookmarks, passwords and more with Firefox for mobile|between your desktop and mobile]]. First just set up a Firefox Sync account on your desktop and then add your mobile device with the easy setup code.

''''''Main menu'''''' - Accessed from the hardware menu button at the bottom (or in the upper-right on Android 4). Use the main menu to access popular features like reload, forward, bookmark, share, and save as PDF. To install Firefox add-on features and configure Firefox privacy, security and content settings, go to More in the main menu.

=Browsing basics=
Firefox for Android is designed to help you search for information quickly and easily on-the-go.

==Searching==
#Open the [[Use the Awesome screen to search in Firefox for Android|Awesome search Screen]] by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by creating a new tab.
#Type your search and tap Enter or select from the list of your most visited sites. The sites that match any search terms come to the top of the list automatically! <br><br>
#:[[Image:awesome]]<br><br>
{note}For more about the Awesome Screen, see [[Use the Awesome screen to search in Firefox for Android]]{/note}

==Zooming==
To make Firefox  [[Zoom in and out of websites on Firefox for mobile|zoom into a section of website]], just double-tap the area you''d like to see. Double-tap again to zoom out. To increase the default font size, adjust your Firefox Settings in the main menu.

==Opening and Switching Tabs==
#Select items from your top sites, bookmarks and history to open multiple tabs.
#Tap the grey tab at the top of the screen to switch tabs.<br><br>

[[Video:tab_tutorial_small]] 

{note}For more tab tricks, see [[Use tabs to quickly switch websites on Firefox for mobile]].{/note}

==Bookmarking favorites==
#Just go to the site you want to bookmark, tap the hardware {button Menu} button. 
#Tap the Bookmark star. The star will turn yellow to let you know the bookmark has been saved.<br><br>
#:[[Image:bookmark_native]]
{note}For more about working with bookmarks, see [[Use bookmarks on Firefox for Android to keep track of your favorite websites]]{/note}

{for m15}
=Copy and paste text=
Just long-tap a word to select it on a web page or within an entry field, then tap it again to copy it to the clipboard.<br><br>[[Image:Select word]]
{note}For more about copy and paste, see [[How do I copy and paste text on mobile?]].{/note}
{/for}

=Controls=
The browser controls are all located under the main menu for a consistent experience. 

==Navigation, Sharing, Save as PDF and More Settings==
Tap the hardware {button Menu} button on your device to access the Back and Forward buttons along with the Bookmark, Share, Save as PDF and More buttons. Tap the {button More} button to view the Clear Site Settings, Add-ons, Settings, and Quit items. {note}Note: For Android 4 devices, the main menu is in the upper right.{/note}

[[Image:main_menu_native]][[Image:main_menu_native2]]<br><br>

Tap {button Settings} to modify your settings for Sync, Plugins, text size and Privacy and Security features like clearing history and clearing private data.<br><br>
[[Image:main_menu_native3]]

=How do I use privacy and security settings to stay safe online?=
Firefox for Android provides tools and features to help you stay safe online.

*''''''Keep your browser up-to-date''''''. You can enable automatic updates when you install Firefox for Android to make this part easy, see [[How do I install Firefox on a mobile device?]].

*''''''Look for the padlock icon'''''' [[Image:padlock]] in Firefox for Android before entering any personal information (passwords, credit cards, addresses, etc.) into a web site, see [[How does Firefox Mobile for Android provide secure mobile browsing]].

*''''''Use a Master Password'''''' to secure Firefox for Android in the event that you lose your device or if you share your device. Using a Master Password lets you have the convenience of a browser that remembers your passwords, but the safety of a master password to lock your username and passwords for all of your favorite sites, see [[Use Master Password to protect passwords in Firefox for Android]].

*''''''Clear your private data'''''' (cookies and passwords), history, and site settings easily with Firefox settings, see [[Clearing cookies, private data, history, and settings in Firefox for Android]]. For the most private and secure browsing, you can also choose to disable cookies and JavaScript. 

*''''''Tell sites not to track you'''''' for advertising purposes by using Do Not Track, see [[How do I turn on the Do-not-track feature on mobile?]].

*''''''Keep ads blocked'''''' by preserving Firefox''s default ''Click to Play'' plugin setting, see [[How do I watch Flash videos with Firefox for Android?]].

*''''''Set up syncing to your desktop'''''' so you don''t need to type your password when on the go and you can still use a strong password, see [[Use Sync to share your Firefox bookmarks, passwords and more with Firefox for mobile]].

