=How do I customize Firefox for Android features?=
You can customize Firefox with Android Mobile add-ons. If there is a feature of Firefox for Android that you want to add to the browser, there are many add-ons you can install that enable additional mobile browsing features. Here are some examples:
{for =m14}
*Install the Phony add-on to spoof your user agent if you want to change from the mobile view of web sites to the desktop view.
{/for}
*Install the Full Screen add-on if you want to use the entire mobile screen to view web sites
*Install the Adblock Plus add-on to regain control of the internet by filtering unwanted content.
#To start, tap the hardware {button Menu} button and select Add-ons. 
#The Add-ons Manager screen appears with an orange icon  in the upper right. 
#:[[Image:addon-manager]]
#Tap the orange icon [[Image:add-on-icon]] to view the Android Mobile Add-ons.
# Tap an add-on to select it and then tap {button Add to Firefox}.<br><br>
{note}To learn more about add-ons, see [[Find and install Add-ons on Firefox for Mobile]]{/note}
= Other Firefox for Android Documents =
