"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-find-and-install-add-ons"><span class="tocnumber">9</span> <span class="toctext">How do I find and install add-ons?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_firefox-for-android-start-page"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">Firefox for Android start page</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_browsing-basics"><span class="tocnumber">11</span> <span class="toctext">Browsing basics</span></a><ul><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_searching"><span class="tocnumber">11.1</span> <span class="toctext">Searching</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_zooming"><span class="tocnumber">11.2</span> <span class="toctext">Zooming</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_opening-and-switching-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">11.3</span> <span class="toctext">Opening and Switching Tabs</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_bookmarking-favorites"><span class="tocnumber">11.4</span> <span class="toctext">Bookmarking favorites</span></a></li></span></ul></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m15"><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_copy-and-paste-text"><span class="tocnumber">12</span> <span class="toctext">Copy and paste text</span></a></li></span></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_controls"><span class="tocnumber">13</span> <span class="toctext">Controls</span></a><ul><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_navigation-sharing-save-as-pdf-and-more-settings"><span class="tocnumber">13.1</span> <span class="toctext">Navigation, Sharing, Save as PDF and More Settings</span></a></li></span></ul></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-use-privacy-and-security-settings-to-stay-safe-online"><span class="tocnumber">14</span> <span class="toctext">How do I use privacy and security settings to stay safe online?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-customize-firefox-for-android-features"><span class="tocnumber">15</span> <span class="toctext">How do I customize Firefox for Android features?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_other-firefox-for-android-documents"><span class="tocnumber">16</span> <span class="toctext">Other Firefox for Android Documents</span></a></li></span></ul></div>
<div class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><p>The video "Getting started with Firefox for mobile" does not exist.
</p>
<h1 id="w_where-are-all-of-the-controls">Where are all of the controls?</h1>
<p>To save space on your device''s display, Firefox''s browser controls are stowed away on the sides of the screen. You can access them by swiping your finger left or right. 
</p>
<ul><li>Swipe right to show your tabs and the <span class="button">New Tab</span> button. 
</li><li>Swipe left to reveal the bookmark <span class="button">Star</span> button, the <span class="button">Back</span> and <span class="button">Forward</span> buttons and the <span class="button">Gear</span> button which lets you access the Preference, Downloads and Add-ons screens.
</li><li>In addition, swiping either left, right or down will bring up the location bar which contains:
<ul><li><strong>The site icon:</strong> Tap to see the site menu with page-specific options.
</li><li><strong>The location bar:</strong> Tap to open the Awesome Screen
</li><li><strong>The combination reload and stop button:</strong> Tap to stop loading or to reload a page.
</li></ul>
</li></ul>
<p><img alt="Mobile Controls v6" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-07-25-10-13-39-569d2a.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<ul><li>Tap the hardware <span class="button">Menu</span> button on your device to view the Site Options, Preferences, Add-ons, Share Page, Find In Page and More controls.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">More</span> to access Downloads, to Quit Firefox or to use the Save as PDF function.
</li></ul>
<p><img alt="Hardware Menu Mobile" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-08-26-16-19-24-223cd8.gif" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab">How do I open a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>Swipe to the right to select the <span class="button">New Tab</span> button located on the bottom, left side of the screen.
</li><li>You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 
</li></ol>
<p><img alt="Mobile Tabs1" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-11-04-25-94b63d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note">For more tab tricks, see <a href="/en-US/kb/manage-tabs-firefox-android">Manage tabs in Firefox for Android</a>.</div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-quickly-find-the-site-i-want">How do I quickly find the site I want?</h1>
<ol><li>Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the location bar at the top of any page or by creating a new tab.
</li><li>Then simply select a site from the list of your most visited sites. 
<ul><li> You can also search through your bookmarks, history, and desktop tabs. Just tap on one of the results to go to that page.<br>
</li></ul>
</li></ol>
<p><img alt="Awesome Screen - alt" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-17-00-09-b2ab30.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note">For more about the Awesome Screen, see <a href="/en-US/kb/customize-firefox-home-screen">Customize the Firefox home screen</a></div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-bookmark-a-site">How do I bookmark a site?</h1>
<ol><li>Just go to the site you want to bookmark, swipe to the left and tap the <span class="button">Star</span> button. The star will turn yellow to let you know the bookmark has been saved.<br><br>The image "Mobile bookmark1" does not exist.
</li></ol>
<div class="note">For more about working with bookmarks, see <a href="/en-US/kb/add-delete-and-view-bookmarked-webpages-firefox-android">Add, delete and view bookmarked webpages in Firefox for Android</a></div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-zoom-into-a-website">How do I zoom into a website?</h1>
<p>To make Firefox zoom into a section of website, just double-tap the area you''d like to see. Double-tap again to zoom out.<br><br><img alt="Zoom1" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-09-16-36-fd23d6.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note">For more about zoom settings, see <a href="/en-US/kb/zoom-and-out-websites-firefox-android">Zoom in and out of websites on Firefox for Android</a></div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-copy-and-paste-text">How do I copy and paste text?</h1>
<p>Just long-tap a word to select it on a web page or within an entry field, then tap it again to copy it to the clipboard.<br><br><img alt="Select word" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-08-26-15-19-34-b888a6.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note">For more about copy and paste, see <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-copy-and-paste-text-android">How do I copy and paste text on Android?</a>.</div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-manage-downloads">How do I manage downloads?</h1>
<ol><li>Swipe to the left and tap the <span class="button">Gear</span> button located on the bottom, right side of the screen. 
</li><li>Select the downloads (downward arrow) tab to manage your downloads. 
</li></ol>
<p><img alt="Mobile Downloads" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-16-44-32-fd4564.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-sync-firefox-between-my-desktop-and-mobile">How do I sync Firefox between my desktop and mobile?</h1>
<p>You can use Firefox Sync to share your bookmarks, passwords, settings, history, and tabs between your desktop and mobile. First just set up Firefox Sync on your desktop and then add your mobile device with the easy setup code.
</p>
<div class="note">For detailed instructions, see <a href="/en-US/kb/use-sync-share-bookmarks-and-more-with-firefox-mobile">Use Sync to share your Firefox bookmarks, passwords and more with Firefox for mobile</a></div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-find-and-install-add-ons">How do I find and install add-ons?</h1>
<p>You can browse through and search for add-ons right inside of Firefox.
</p>
<ol><li>To start, swipe to the left and tap the <span class="button">Gear</span> button located on the bottom, right side of the screen. 
</li><li>Select the add-ons (puzzle piece) tab and scroll down to see an add-ons search bar and a list of popular add-ons . 
</li><li>To install an add-on, tap to select it and then tap <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span>.<br><br><img alt="Mobile Add-ons1" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-14-20-33-a26098.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
<div class="note">To learn more about add-ons, see <a href="/en-US/kb/find-and-install-add-ons-firefox-android">Find and install extensions on Firefox for Android</a></div>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m14">
<h1 id="w_firefox-for-android-start-page">Firefox for Android start page</h1>
<p>At the top of the Firefox app are the Title bar and the Tab. Tap the Title bar to open your Bookmarks, history, and top sites lists. 
</p><p><img alt="getting_started_native_gingerbread1" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-02-14-15-19-55-c2c291.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</p><p><strong>Firefox Sync</strong> - share your bookmarks, history, passwords and open tabs  <a href="/en-US/kb/use-sync-share-bookmarks-and-more-with-firefox-mobile">between your desktop and mobile</a>. First just set up a Firefox Sync account on your desktop and then add your mobile device with the easy setup code.
</p><p><strong>Main menu</strong> - Accessed from the hardware menu button at the bottom (or in the upper-right on Android 4). Use the main menu to access popular features like reload, forward, bookmark, share, and save as PDF. To install Firefox add-on features and configure Firefox privacy, security and content settings, go to More in the main menu.
</p>
<h1 id="w_browsing-basics">Browsing basics</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android is designed to help you search for information quickly and easily on-the-go.
</p>
<h2 id="w_searching">Searching</h2>
<ol><li>Open the <a href="/en-US/kb/customize-firefox-home-screen">Awesome search Screen</a> by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by creating a new tab.
</li><li>Type your search and tap Enter or select from the list of your most visited sites. The sites that match any search terms come to the top of the list automatically! <br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="awesome" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-02-08-16-34-15-be1217.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</dd></dl>
</li></ol>
<div class="note">For more about the Awesome Screen, see <a href="/en-US/kb/customize-firefox-home-screen">Customize the Firefox home screen</a></div>
<h2 id="w_zooming">Zooming</h2>
<p>To make Firefox  <a href="/en-US/kb/zoom-and-out-websites-firefox-android">zoom into a section of website</a>, just double-tap the area you''d like to see. Double-tap again to zoom out. To increase the default font size, adjust your Firefox Settings in the main menu.
</p>
<h2 id="w_opening-and-switching-tabs">Opening and Switching Tabs</h2>
<ol><li>Select items from your top sites, bookmarks and history to open multiple tabs.
</li><li>Tap the grey tab at the top of the screen to switch tabs.<br><br>
</li></ol>
<p>The video "tab_tutorial_small" does not exist. 
</p>
<div class="note">For more tab tricks, see <a href="/en-US/kb/manage-tabs-firefox-android">Manage tabs in Firefox for Android</a>.</div>
<h2 id="w_bookmarking-favorites">Bookmarking favorites</h2>
<ol><li>Just go to the site you want to bookmark, tap the hardware <span class="button">Menu</span> button. 
</li><li>Tap the Bookmark star. The star will turn yellow to let you know the bookmark has been saved.<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="bookmark_native" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-05-08-11-31-18-7f3105.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li></ol>
<div class="note">For more about working with bookmarks, see <a href="/en-US/kb/add-delete-and-view-bookmarked-webpages-firefox-android">Add, delete and view bookmarked webpages in Firefox for Android</a></div>
<div class="for" data-for="m15">
<h1 id="w_copy-and-paste-text">Copy and paste text</h1>
<p>Just long-tap a word to select it on a web page or within an entry field, then tap it again to copy it to the clipboard.<br><br><img alt="Select word" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-08-26-15-19-34-b888a6.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note">For more about copy and paste, see <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-copy-and-paste-text-android">How do I copy and paste text on Android?</a>.</div>
</div>
<h1 id="w_controls">Controls</h1>
<p>The browser controls are all located under the main menu for a consistent experience. 
</p>
<h2 id="w_navigation-sharing-save-as-pdf-and-more-settings">Navigation, Sharing, Save as PDF and More Settings</h2>
Tap the hardware <span class="button">Menu</span> button on your device to access the Back and Forward buttons along with the Bookmark, Share, Save as PDF and More buttons. Tap the <span class="button">More</span> button to view the Clear Site Settings, Add-ons, Settings, and Quit items. <div class="note">Note: For Android 4 devices, the main menu is in the upper right.</div>
<p><img alt="main_menu_native" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-02-08-17-09-20-97ea5b.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><img alt="main_menu_native2" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-02-08-17-13-19-3cfd16.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</p><p>Tap <span class="button">Settings</span> to modify your settings for Sync, Plugins, text size and Privacy and Security features like clearing history and clearing private data.<br><br>
<img alt="main_menu_native3" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-02-08-17-14-49-a80919.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-use-privacy-and-security-settings-to-stay-safe-online">How do I use privacy and security settings to stay safe online?</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android provides tools and features to help you stay safe online.
</p>
<ul><li><strong>Keep your browser up-to-date</strong>. You can enable automatic updates when you install Firefox for Android to make this part easy, see <a href="/en-US/kb/install-firefox-android-device-using-google-play">Install Firefox on an Android device using Google Play</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Look for the padlock icon</strong> <img alt="padlock" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-03-08-14-11-49-255ef8.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> in Firefox for Android before entering any personal information (passwords, credit cards, addresses, etc.) into a web site, see <a class="new" href="/en-US/kb/new?title=How+does+Firefox+Mobile+for+Android+provide+secure+mobile+browsing" title="Page does not exist.">How does Firefox Mobile for Android provide secure mobile browsing</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Use a Master Password</strong> to secure Firefox for Android in the event that you lose your device or if you share your device. Using a Master Password lets you have the convenience of a browser that remembers your passwords, but the safety of a master password to lock your username and passwords for all of your favorite sites, see <a href="/en-US/kb/using-master-password-firefox-android">Using Master Password on Firefox for Android</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Clear your private data</strong> (cookies and passwords), history, and site settings easily with Firefox settings, see <a href="/en-US/kb/clearing-cookies-private-data-history-and-settings">Clearing cookies, private data, history, and settings in Firefox for Android</a>. For the most private and secure browsing, you can also choose to disable cookies and JavaScript. 
</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Tell sites not to track you</strong> for advertising purposes by using Do Not Track, see <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-use-do-not-track-firefox-android">How do I use Do-not-track on Firefox for Android?</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Keep ads blocked</strong> by preserving Firefox''s default ''Click to Play'' plugin setting, see <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-watch-flash-videos-firefox-android">How do I watch Flash videos with Firefox for Android?</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Set up syncing to your desktop</strong> so you don''t need to type your password when on the go and you can still use a strong password, see <a href="/en-US/kb/use-sync-share-bookmarks-and-more-with-firefox-mobile">Use Sync to share your Firefox bookmarks, passwords and more with Firefox for mobile</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p><h1 id="w_how-do-i-customize-firefox-for-android-features">How do I customize Firefox for Android features?</h1>
<p>You can customize Firefox with Android Mobile add-ons. If there is a feature of Firefox for Android that you want to add to the browser, there are many add-ons you can install that enable additional mobile browsing features. Here are some examples:
</p><div class="for" data-for="=m14" style="display: none;">
<ul><li>Install the Phony add-on to spoof your user agent if you want to change from the mobile view of web sites to the desktop view.
</li></ul>
</div>
<ul><li>Install the Full Screen add-on if you want to use the entire mobile screen to view web sites
</li><li>Install the Adblock Plus add-on to regain control of the internet by filtering unwanted content.
</li></ul>
<ol><li>To start, tap the hardware <span class="button">Menu</span> button and select Add-ons. 
</li><li>The Add-ons Manager screen appears with an orange icon  in the upper right. 
<dl><dd><img alt="addon-manager" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-03-08-15-47-08-be19ec.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Tap the orange icon <img alt="add-on-icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-03-08-15-23-34-203790.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> to view the Android Mobile Add-ons.
</li><li> Tap an add-on to select it and then tap <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span>.<br><br>
</li></ol>
<div class="note">To learn more about add-ons, see <a href="/en-US/kb/find-and-install-add-ons-firefox-android">Find and install extensions on Firefox for Android</a></div>
<h1 id="w_other-firefox-for-android-documents">Other Firefox for Android Documents</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-watch-flash-videos-firefox-android">Flash</a>
</li><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-mobile-android-tutorials">Firefox for Android video tutorials</a>
</li><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-firefox-android-tablet-browser">Get started with Firefox for Android on tablets</a>
</li></ul>
</div><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "36272", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 6, 2013, 1:58:32 PM", "datetime": "2013-02-06T13:58:32-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Merge the content of \"Getting started with Firefox for mobile\" into this article now that marketing has decided to use ''Android'' instead of ''mobile''", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Feb 6, 2013, 2:02:12 PM", "datetime": "2013-02-06T14:02:12-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Feb 6, 2013, 2:02:12 PM", "datetime": "2013-02-06T14:02:12-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:50:30+00:00');
