__TOC__
= How do I access the Firefox home page with the sites I have pinned? =
There are three ways to access the Firefox home page:
* The Firefox home page is shown when Firefox is first started.
* Firefox automatically bookmarks the home page when installed.  Tap on the title bar and then tap on the {button Bookmarks} tab and then tap on {button about:home}.
* Tap on the title bar and type ''''about:home''''.
=How do I organize my top sites on the Firefox home page?=
Firefox displays websites on the Firefox home page based on how frequently you visit each site and how recently you were there. You can easily pin, edit and delete the sites that show up on the Firefox home page to customize it just the way you want. 

You can pin up to six sites. If you have less than six sites pinned, then Firefox will dynamically fill in empty slots with top frequented sites. If you wish to keep a top frequented site, you can do this by pinning the site. If you wish to change the URL of a pinned site, you can edit the URL. 

==Pin a site==
# Go to the site you want to pin by typing its URL or tapping on it in Top Sites, Bookmarks, or your History.
# Tap on the title bar and type ''''about:home''''.
# Long tap on the site you want to pin <br /><br/>[[Image:long tap on mozilla.org home page - Android ICS]]<br /><br />.
#Tap {menu Pin Site}<br /><br />[[Image:after long tap tap pin site]].<br /><br />Firefox will display a visual indicator on the top right to confirm the site has been pinned.
<br/><br/>[[Image:visual indicator site pinned - Android ICS]]

==Remove a site by unpinning it==
# Tap on the title bar and type ''''about:home''''.
# Long tap on the site you want to remove and then tap {menu Unpin Site}.
<br/><br/>[[Image:umpin site - Android ICS]]

==Edit a pinned site''s URL==
# Tap on the title bar and type ''''about:home''''.
# Long tap on the site whose URL you want to change and then tap {menu Edit}.<br /><br />[[Image:edit pinned site - Android ICS]]
# Type in the site''s URL or choose it from the Top Sites, Bookmarks or History tabs.<br/><br/>[[Image:edit url of pinned site tap go - Android ICS]]
# Tap {button Go} to save the new URL to the Firefox home page.','<p>When you go to the Firefox home page, Firefox shows your top sites. Learn how to pin sites to this page, and edit sites on this page.
</p><div class="for" data-for="not m20" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox beta version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/beta">mozilla.org/beta</a>.</div>

