</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38343", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 1, 2013, 1:00:50 PM", "datetime": "2013-04-01T13:00:50-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "change metadata", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 1, 2013, 1:02:29 PM", "datetime": "2013-04-01T13:02:29-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Apr 1, 2013, 1:02:29 PM", "datetime": "2013-04-01T13:02:29-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:49:21+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (38345,'en-US','using-dark-theme-firefox-android','Using Dark Theme in Firefox for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/using-dark-theme-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/using-dark-theme-firefox-android/revision/38345',37383,'2013-04-01T13:13:35-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','change menu button parenthetical to use [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]]',1,'2013-04-01T13:14:41-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','A theme is a simple type of Firefox add-on which allows you to customize your browser skin. This article describes how to find, install, and manage Firefox for Android themes.

__TOC__

= What are themes? =

Firefox for Android themes allow changing of color schemes and background images of the Firefox toolbars.

= How to install themes =
You can access the Android themes from the settings menu inside Firefox for Android:
#Tap the menu {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {button Tools} and tap {button Add-ons}.
#Tap the orange {button Folder} icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to https://addons.mozilla.org/android/ to achieve the same result.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide]] 
#Tap on the {button Themes} tab to see available themes.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS FF19 amo Themes tab]]
#You will see ''''''Featured'''''' themes. You can search for themes or tap on the {button Popular} or {button Categories} tabs to find a theme you would like to try.
# To try out a theme, simply tap on the theme''s graphic; Firefox will display ''''''"You''re trying it on!"''''''. To learn more about a theme, tap {button Theme Info}.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS FF19 amo you are trying it on]] 
# Install the theme you want by tapping {button Keep it}. Firefox will confirm the theme is installed by displaying ''''''"Added to Firefox"''''''.

= Managing themes =
== How to switch themes ==
To switch themes, follow the instructions for ''''''How to install Themes'''''' above and install another theme.

== How to remove a theme ==
If you want to go back to the default Firefox for Android theme, uninstall the current theme add-on:
#Tap the menu {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {button Tools} and tap {button Add-ons}.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS FF19 tools addons sunshine in forest]]
#Tap on the add-on for the current theme and then tap on {button Uninstall}.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS FF19 uninstall theme addon sunshine in forest]]
#The theme will be removed.','<p>A theme is a simple type of Firefox add-on which allows you to customize your browser skin. This article describes how to find, install, and manage Firefox for Android themes.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_what-are-themes"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">What are themes?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-install-themes"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How to install themes</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_managing-themes"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Managing themes</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_how-to-switch-themes"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">How to switch themes</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_how-to-remove-a-theme"><span class="tocnumber">3.2</span> <span class="toctext">How to remove a theme</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_what-are-themes">What are themes?</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android themes allow changing of color schemes and background images of the Firefox toolbars.
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-to-install-themes">How to install themes</h1>
<p>You can access the Android themes from the settings menu inside Firefox for Android:
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the menu <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="button">Tools</span> and tap <span class="button">Add-ons</span>.
</li><li>Tap the orange <span class="button">Folder</span> icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/android/">https://addons.mozilla.org/android/</a> to achieve the same result.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-08-13-32-43-c1ffe4.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li><li>Tap on the <span class="button">Themes</span> tab to see available themes.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS FF19 amo Themes tab" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-05-23-10-18-4f2e92.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>You will see <strong>Featured</strong> themes. You can search for themes or tap on the <span class="button">Popular</span> or <span class="button">Categories</span> tabs to find a theme you would like to try.
</li><li> To try out a theme, simply tap on the theme''s graphic; Firefox will display <strong>"You''re trying it on!"</strong>. To learn more about a theme, tap <span class="button">Theme Info</span>.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS FF19 amo you are trying it on" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-05-23-15-08-408ab0.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li><li> Install the theme you want by tapping <span class="button">Keep it</span>. Firefox will confirm the theme is installed by displaying <strong>"Added to Firefox"</strong>.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_managing-themes">Managing themes</h1>
<h2 id="w_how-to-switch-themes">How to switch themes</h2>
<p>To switch themes, follow the instructions for <strong>How to install Themes</strong> above and install another theme.
</p>
<h2 id="w_how-to-remove-a-theme">How to remove a theme</h2>
<p>If you want to go back to the default Firefox for Android theme, uninstall the current theme add-on:
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the menu <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="button">Tools</span> and tap <span class="button">Add-ons</span>.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS FF19 tools addons sunshine in forest" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-05-23-26-54-72aafa.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>Tap on the add-on for the current theme and then tap on <span class="button">Uninstall</span>.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS FF19 uninstall theme addon sunshine in forest" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-05-23-30-59-9c8c70.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>The theme will be removed.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38345", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 1, 2013, 1:13:35 PM", "datetime": "2013-04-01T13:13:35-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "change menu button parenthetical to use [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]]", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 1, 2013, 1:14:41 PM", "datetime": "2013-04-01T13:14:41-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:49:18+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (38375,'en-US','pin-sites-firefox-android-start-screen','Pin Sites on the Firefox for Android start screen','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/pin-sites-firefox-android-start-screen','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/pin-sites-firefox-android-start-screen/revision/38375',38343,'2013-04-02T04:58:23-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','FF20 Android has been released so remove beta template',1,'2013-04-02T05:00:17-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','When you go to the Firefox home page, Firefox shows your top sites. Learn how to customize this page: how to pin sites to this page and how to edit sites on this page.
{for not m20}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=release|slug=mobile]]
{/for}

__TOC__
= How do I access the Firefox home page with the sites I have pinned? =

Firefox automatically bookmarks the home page when installed.  
* Tap on the title bar,  tap on the {button Bookmarks} tab, and finally tap on the {button Firefox Start} bookmark to access the Firefox home page.
<br /><br />[[Image:firefox home page default bookmark - Android ICS]]

=How do I organize my top sites on the Firefox home page?=
Firefox displays websites on the Firefox home page based on how frequently you visit each site and how recently you were there. You can easily pin, edit and delete the sites that show up on the Firefox home page to customize it just the way you want. 

You can pin up to six sites. If you have less than six sites pinned, then Firefox will dynamically fill in empty slots with sites that you visit frequently. If you wish to keep a frequently visited site, you can do this by pinning the site. If you wish to change the URL of a pinned site, you can edit the URL. 

==Pin a site==

*From the Firefox home page, long tap on the site you want to pin and then tap {menu Pin Site}<br /><br/>[[Image:long tap to pin a site - Android ICS]]<br /><br />.

Firefox will display a visual indicator on the top right to confirm the site has been pinned.<br /><br />
[[Image:pinned site visual indicator 2 - Android ICS]]

==Remove a site by unpinning it==
* From the Firefox home page, long tap on the site you want to remove and then tap {menu Unpin Site}.
<br/><br/>[[Image:umpin site - Android ICS]]

==Edit a pinned site''s URL==
# From the Firefox home page, long tap on the site you want to remove and then long tap on the site whose URL you want to change and then tap {menu Edit}.<br /><br />[[Image:edit pinned site - Android ICS]]
# Type in the site''s URL or choose it from the Top Sites, Bookmarks or History tabs.<br/><br/>[[Image:edit url of pinned site tap go - Android ICS]]
# Tap {button Go} to save the new URL to the Firefox home page.','<p>When you go to the Firefox home page, Firefox shows your top sites. Learn how to customize this page: how to pin sites to this page and how to edit sites on this page.
</p><div class="for" data-for="not m20" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox release version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile">mozilla.org/mobile</a>.</div>
<p></p></div>
