<h1 id="w_how-do-i-access-the-firefox-home-page-with-the-sites-i-have-pinned">How do I access the Firefox home page with the sites I have pinned?</h1>
<p>Firefox automatically bookmarks the home page when installed.  
</p>
<ul><li> Tap on the title bar,  tap on the <span class="button">Bookmarks</span> tab, and finally tap on the <span class="button">Firefox Start</span> bookmark to access the Firefox home page.
</li></ul>
<p><br><br><img alt="firefox home page default bookmark - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-28-16-08-14-90cdc6.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-organize-my-top-sites-on-the-firefox-home-page">How do I organize my top sites on the Firefox home page?</h1>
<p>Firefox displays websites on the Firefox home page based on how frequently you visit each site and how recently you were there. You can easily pin, edit and delete the sites that show up on the Firefox home page to customize it just the way you want. 
</p><p>You can pin up to six sites. If you have less than six sites pinned, then Firefox will dynamically fill in empty slots with sites that you visit frequently. If you wish to keep a frequently visited site, you can do this by pinning the site. If you wish to change the URL of a pinned site, you can edit the URL. 
</p>
<h2 id="w_pin-a-site">Pin a site</h2>
<ul><li>From the Firefox home page, long tap on the site you want to pin and then tap <span class="menu">Pin Site</span><br><br><img alt="long tap to pin a site - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-28-22-36-21-338306.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>.
</li></ul>
<p>Firefox will display a visual indicator on the top right to confirm the site has been pinned.<br><br>
<img alt="pinned site visual indicator 2 - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-28-22-41-30-82ec0f.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h2 id="w_remove-a-site-by-unpinning-it">Remove a site by unpinning it</h2>
<ul><li> From the Firefox home page, long tap on the site you want to remove and then tap <span class="menu">Unpin Site</span>.
</li></ul>
<p><br><br><img alt="umpin site - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-27-00-15-23-53eb3a.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h2 id="w_edit-a-pinned-sites-url">Edit a pinned site''s URL</h2>
<ol><li> From the Firefox home page, long tap on the site you want to remove and then long tap on the site whose URL you want to change and then tap <span class="menu">Edit</span>.<br><br><img alt="edit pinned site - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-27-00-03-01-de95b4.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li> Type in the site''s URL or choose it from the Top Sites, Bookmarks or History tabs.<br><br><img alt="edit url of pinned site tap go - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-27-00-10-53-9d2a01.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Go</span> to save the new URL to the Firefox home page.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38375", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 2, 2013, 4:58:23 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-02T04:58:23-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "FF20 Android has been released so remove beta template", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 2, 2013, 5:00:17 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-02T05:00:17-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:49:16+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (38382,'en-US','how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','How do I quit Firefox for Android?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android/revision/38382',NULL,'2013-04-02T09:55:41-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','work in progress - needs screenshots, do not approve please!',1,'2013-04-02T10:08:20-07:00','iNerd',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','For Android version 4 and above, ''''quit'''' was removed from the Firefox menu to meet Google''s application guidelines. If you wish, you can re-add it. Here''s how.
{for not m20}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=release|slug=mobile]]
{/for}

__TOC__

= How to add Quit back using a Firefox Android add-on =
You can access the Android themes from the settings menu inside Firefox for Android:
#Tap the menu {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {button Tools} and tap {button Add-ons}.
#Tap the orange {button Folder} icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to https://addons.mozilla.org/android/ to achieve the same result.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide]] 
# Search for ''''quitnow'''' and tap on it.
# Tap {button Add to Firefox} and then tap {button Install} to install it. Your Firefox Menu will now have a {button QuitNow} button.','<p>For Android version 4 and above, <em>quit</em> was removed from the Firefox menu to meet Google''s application guidelines. If you wish, you can re-add it. Here''s how.
</p><div class="for" data-for="not m20" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox release version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile">mozilla.org/mobile</a>.</div>
<p></p></div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-add-quit-back-using-a-firefox-android-add-on"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How to add Quit back using a Firefox Android add-on</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_how-to-add-quit-back-using-a-firefox-android-add-on">How to add Quit back using a Firefox Android add-on</h1>
<p>You can access the Android themes from the settings menu inside Firefox for Android:
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the menu <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="button">Tools</span> and tap <span class="button">Add-ons</span>.
</li><li>Tap the orange <span class="button">Folder</span> icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/android/">https://addons.mozilla.org/android/</a> to achieve the same result.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-08-13-32-43-c1ffe4.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li><li> Search for <em>quitnow</em> and tap on it.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span> and then tap <span class="button">Install</span> to install it. Your Firefox Menu will now have a <span class="button">QuitNow</span> button.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38382", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 2, 2013, 9:55:41 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-02T09:55:41-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "work in progress - needs screenshots, do not approve please!", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 2, 2013, 10:08:20 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-02T10:08:20-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "iNerd", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:49:13+00:00');
