</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38517", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 5, 2013, 3:04:06 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-05T03:04:06-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "changing as per feedback from italian contributors, thank-you!", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 5, 2013, 3:04:21 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-05T03:04:21-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "May 3, 2013, 7:53:09 AM", "datetime": "2013-05-03T07:53:09-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "Verdi", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:48:34+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (38522,'en-US','how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','How do I quit Firefox for Android?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android/revision/38522',38473,'2013-04-05T08:13:13-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','you can also quit by swiping from the app switch screen',1,'2013-04-05T08:13:31-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','For Android version 4 and above, ''''quit'''' was removed from the Firefox menu to meet Google''s application guidelines. 

You can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen (Ice Cream Sandwich: long press on the home button; Jelly Bean: tap on the app switch button [[Image:app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean]]).

If you wish, you can re-add ''''quit''''. Here''s how.
{for not m20}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=release|slug=mobile]]
{/for}

__TOC__

= How to add Quit back using a Firefox for Android add-on =
Here''s how to install an add-on to bring back Quit so you can close Firefox.
#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {button Tools} and tap {button Add-ons}.
#Tap the orange {button Folder} icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to https://addons.mozilla.org/android/ to achieve the same result.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide]] 
# Search for ''''quitnow''''<br/><br />[[Image:search for quit now - ICS Android]]<br /><br /> and tap on it.<br /><br />[[Image:tap on quitnow - Android ICS]]<br /><br />
# Tap {button Add to Firefox}<br /><br />[[Image:add to firefox - quitnow - Android ICS]]<br /><br /> and then tap {button Install} to install the QuitNow add-on. Your Firefox menu will now have a {button QuitNow} button that allows you to exit Firefox for Android.<br /><br />[[Image:quitnow in firefox menu - Android ICS]]','<p>For Android version 4 and above, <em>quit</em> was removed from the Firefox menu to meet Google''s application guidelines. 
</p><p>You can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen (Ice Cream Sandwich: long press on the home button; Jelly Bean: tap on the app switch button <img alt="app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-05-15-11-37-747d89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">).
</p><p>If you wish, you can re-add <em>quit</em>. Here''s how.
</p><div class="for" data-for="not m20" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox release version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile">mozilla.org/mobile</a>.</div>
<p></p></div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-add-quit-back-using-a-firefox-for-android-add-on"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How to add Quit back using a Firefox for Android add-on</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_how-to-add-quit-back-using-a-firefox-for-android-add-on">How to add Quit back using a Firefox for Android add-on</h1>
<p>Here''s how to install an add-on to bring back Quit so you can close Firefox.
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="button">Tools</span> and tap <span class="button">Add-ons</span>.
</li><li>Tap the orange <span class="button">Folder</span> icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/android/">https://addons.mozilla.org/android/</a> to achieve the same result.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-08-13-32-43-c1ffe4.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li><li> Search for <em>quitnow</em><br><br><img alt="search for quit now - ICS Android" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-02-17-04-01-27e40b.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br> and tap on it.<br><br><img alt="tap on quitnow - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-02-17-06-30-f321ce.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span><br><br><img alt="add to firefox - quitnow - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-02-17-10-21-a485b5.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br> and then tap <span class="button">Install</span> to install the QuitNow add-on. Your Firefox menu will now have a <span class="button">QuitNow</span> button that allows you to exit Firefox for Android.<br><br><img alt="quitnow in firefox menu - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-02-17-13-50-f77229.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38522", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 5, 2013, 8:13:13 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-05T08:13:13-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "you can also quit by swiping from the app switch screen", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 5, 2013, 8:13:31 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-05T08:13:31-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:48:31+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (38523,'en-US','forum-response-android-add-quit-back','Forum Response Android - Add Quit back','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/forum-response-android-add-quit-back','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/forum-response-android-add-quit-back/revision/38523',38479,'2013-04-05T08:18:24-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','clarify how to open the app switch screen',1,'2013-04-05T08:18:37-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2014-06-13T04:49:00-07:00','user917725','approved','Hi:

On Android 4 and higher, you can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen (Ice Cream Sandwich: long press on the home button; Jelly Bean: tap on the app switch button [[Image:app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean]]). 

If you need the menu item back, you can install an Add-on like the QuitNow Add-on to do that. Here''s [[How do I quit Firefox for Android?|how to install an add-on to add Quit back]]','<p>Hi:
</p><p>On Android 4 and higher, you can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen (Ice Cream Sandwich: long press on the home button; Jelly Bean: tap on the app switch button <img alt="app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-05-15-11-37-747d89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">). 
</p><p>If you need the menu item back, you can install an Add-on like the QuitNow Add-on to do that. Here''s <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android">how to install an add-on to add Quit back</a>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38523", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 5, 2013, 8:18:24 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-05T08:18:24-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "clarify how to open the app switch screen", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 5, 2013, 8:18:37 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-05T08:18:37-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jun 13, 2014, 4:49:00 AM", "datetime": "2014-06-13T04:49:00-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "user917725", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:48:29+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (38687,'en-US','how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','How do I quit Firefox for Android?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android/revision/38687',38677,'2013-04-09T05:23:04-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','change screenshot to show that it''s now ''Quit'' instead of ''QuitNow''',1,'2013-04-09T05:23:24-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','For Android version 4 and above, ''''quit'''' was removed from the Firefox menu to meet Google''s application guidelines. 

You can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen (Ice Cream Sandwich: long press on the home button; Jelly Bean: tap on the app switch button [[Image:app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean]]).

If you wish, you can re-add ''''quit''''. Here''s how.
{for not m20}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=release|slug=mobile]]
{/for}

__TOC__

= How to add Quit back using a Firefox for Android add-on =
Here''s how to install an add-on to bring back Quit so you can close Firefox.
#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {button Tools} and tap {button Add-ons}.
#Tap the orange {button Folder} icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to https://addons.mozilla.org/android/ to achieve the same result.<br><br>[[Image:Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide]] 
# Search for ''''quitnow''''<br/><br />[[Image:search for quit now - ICS Android]]<br /><br /> and tap on it.<br /><br />[[Image:tap on quitnow - Android ICS]]<br /><br />
# Tap {button Add to Firefox}<br /><br />[[Image:add to firefox - quitnow - Android ICS]]<br /><br /> and then tap {button Install} to install the QuitNow add-on. Your Firefox menu will now have a {button Quit} button that allows you to exit Firefox for Android.<br /><br />[[Image:quitnow is now quit in firefox menu - Android ICS]]','<p>For Android version 4 and above, <em>quit</em> was removed from the Firefox menu to meet Google''s application guidelines. 
</p><p>You can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen (Ice Cream Sandwich: long press on the home button; Jelly Bean: tap on the app switch button <img alt="app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-05-15-11-37-747d89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">).
</p><p>If you wish, you can re-add <em>quit</em>. Here''s how.
</p><div class="for" data-for="not m20" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox release version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile">mozilla.org/mobile</a>.</div>
<p></p></div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-add-quit-back-using-a-firefox-for-android-add-on"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How to add Quit back using a Firefox for Android add-on</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_how-to-add-quit-back-using-a-firefox-for-android-add-on">How to add Quit back using a Firefox for Android add-on</h1>
<p>Here''s how to install an add-on to bring back Quit so you can close Firefox.
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="button">Tools</span> and tap <span class="button">Add-ons</span>.
</li><li>Tap the orange <span class="button">Folder</span> icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/android/">https://addons.mozilla.org/android/</a> to achieve the same result.<br><br><img alt="Android ICS Orange Folder for Add-ons 320 px wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-03-08-13-32-43-c1ffe4.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li><li> Search for <em>quitnow</em><br><br><img alt="search for quit now - ICS Android" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-02-17-04-01-27e40b.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br> and tap on it.<br><br><img alt="tap on quitnow - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-02-17-06-30-f321ce.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span><br><br><img alt="add to firefox - quitnow - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-02-17-10-21-a485b5.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br> and then tap <span class="button">Install</span> to install the QuitNow add-on. Your Firefox menu will now have a <span class="button">Quit</span> button that allows you to exit Firefox for Android.<br><br><img alt="quitnow is now quit in firefox menu - Android ICS" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-09-12-21-21-e95905.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "38687", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 9, 2013, 5:23:04 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-09T05:23:04-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "change screenshot to show that it''s now ''Quit'' instead of ''QuitNow''", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 9, 2013, 5:23:24 AM", "datetime": "2013-04-09T05:23:24-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:48:27+00:00');
