__TOC__

{for not m14}
=Where are my tabs?=
To view your tabs in Firefox for Android, just swipe to the right and you''ll see a sidebar containing a thumbnail for each tab. You can select any tab by tapping on it. When you''re done, swipe to the left to bring the web page back in view.<br><br> [[Image:Mobile Tabs]]

=How do I open a new tab?=
#Swipe to the right to select the {button New Tab} button located on the bottom, left side of the screen.
#You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 
{note}See [[How do I use the Awesome Screen?]] for more Awesome Screen tricks.{/note}
[[Image:Mobile Tabs1]]

=How do I close and reopen tabs?=
Swipe to the right to see a list of your tabs. Tap the red close button on a tab to close it.

If you close a tab by mistake, you can reopen the last closed tab by tapping the green restore button at the bottom, left side of the screen. <br><br>
[[Image:Mobile Tabs2]]

=How do I open a link in a new tab?=
#To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
#Tap ''''''Open Link in New Tab''''''.
#You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.<br><br>[[Image:Mobile Tabs3]]
#To switch to your new tab, swipe to the right and tap on the new tab''s thumbnail.<br><br>[[Image:Mobile Tabs4]]
{/for}
{for m14}
=Firefox for Android tabbed browsing=
This tutorial shows you how to use tabs.

[[Video:tab_tutorial_small]]

=Where are my tabs?=
#To view your tabs in Firefox for Android, just tap the tab in the upper-right to see a drop-down of tabs with thumbnail images.
#Select any tab by tapping on it. <br><br> [[Image:tabs_native]]
#If you have [[How do I set up Firefox Sync? | Sync setup]], you can access tabs that are open on your desktop Firefox through the Synced Tabs link.

=How do I open a new tab?=
#Tap the + plus to open a new tab.
#You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 

=How do I close tabs?=
Tap the X next to the thumbnail to close a tab.

=How do I open a link in a new tab?=
#To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
#Tap ''''''Open Link in New Tab''''''. You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.
#To switch to your new tab, hit the back button. The number on the tab will increment and the web page appears.
{for m23}
=Switch to tab=
Tap the title bar and start entering text. If a match is found for one of your open tabs, then the results will display a tab icon and the text "Switch to tab". Tapping "Switch to tab" will switch you to the already open tab instead of creating a duplicate. 
:[[Image:Android switch to tab jelly bean 480 wide]]
{/for}

{/for}

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/LCXWUo]]','<p>Firefox for Android lets you easily create and manage multiple tabs. This article will show you how it''s done.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_where-are-my-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Where are my tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-close-and-reopen-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">How do I close and reopen tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a link in a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_firefox-for-android-tabbed-browsing"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Firefox for Android tabbed browsing</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_where-are-my-tabs_2"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">Where are my tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab_2"><span class="tocnumber">7</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-close-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">8</span> <span class="toctext">How do I close tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab_2"><span class="tocnumber">9</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a link in a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m23"><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_switch-to-tab"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">Switch to tab</span></a></li></span></span></ul></div>
<div class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;">
<h1 id="w_where-are-my-tabs">Where are my tabs?</h1>
<p>To view your tabs in Firefox for Android, just swipe to the right and you''ll see a sidebar containing a thumbnail for each tab. You can select any tab by tapping on it. When you''re done, swipe to the left to bring the web page back in view.<br><br> <img alt="Mobile Tabs" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-28-12-23-21-7b0afb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab">How do I open a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>Swipe to the right to select the <span class="button">New Tab</span> button located on the bottom, left side of the screen.
</li><li>You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 
</li></ol>
<div class="note">See <a href="/en-US/kb/customize-firefox-home-screen">Customize the Firefox home screen</a> for more Awesome Screen tricks.</div>
<p><img alt="Mobile Tabs1" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-11-04-25-94b63d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-close-and-reopen-tabs">How do I close and reopen tabs?</h1>
<p>Swipe to the right to see a list of your tabs. Tap the red close button on a tab to close it.
</p><p>If you close a tab by mistake, you can reopen the last closed tab by tapping the green restore button at the bottom, left side of the screen. <br><br>
<img alt="Mobile Tabs2" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-11-05-10-1d2d14.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab">How do I open a link in a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
</li><li>Tap <strong>Open Link in New Tab</strong>.
</li><li>You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.<br><br><img alt="Mobile Tabs3" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-28-12-22-36-7a0c87.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>To switch to your new tab, swipe to the right and tap on the new tab''s thumbnail.<br><br><img alt="Mobile Tabs4" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-11-05-55-544516.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m14">
<h1 id="w_firefox-for-android-tabbed-browsing">Firefox for Android tabbed browsing</h1>
<p>This tutorial shows you how to use tabs.
</p><p>The video "tab_tutorial_small" does not exist.
</p>
<h1 id="w_where-are-my-tabs_2">Where are my tabs?</h1>
<ol><li>To view your tabs in Firefox for Android, just tap the tab in the upper-right to see a drop-down of tabs with thumbnail images.
</li><li>Select any tab by tapping on it. <br><br> <img alt="tabs_native" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-23-16-04-57-906121.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>If you have <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-set-sync-my-computer"> Sync setup</a>, you can access tabs that are open on your desktop Firefox through the Synced Tabs link.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab_2">How do I open a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>Tap the + plus to open a new tab.
</li><li>You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-close-tabs">How do I close tabs?</h1>
<p>Tap the X next to the thumbnail to close a tab.
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab_2">How do I open a link in a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
</li><li>Tap <strong>Open Link in New Tab</strong>. You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.
</li><li>To switch to your new tab, hit the back button. The number on the tab will increment and the web page appears.
</li></ol>
<div class="for" data-for="m23">
<h1 id="w_switch-to-tab">Switch to tab</h1>
<p>Tap the title bar and start entering text. If a match is found for one of your open tabs, then the results will display a tab icon and the text "Switch to tab". Tapping "Switch to tab" will switch you to the already open tab instead of creating a duplicate. 
</p>
<dl><dd><img alt="Android switch to tab jelly bean 480 wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-04-18-18-35-10-eccbc8.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</div></div><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44031", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jul 30, 2013, 2:11:53 PM", "datetime": "2013-07-30T14:11:53-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "DO NOT APPROVE! WORK IN PROGRESS - needs feedback for switch to tab", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:33+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44032,'en-US','using-tabs-firefox-android','Using Tabs on Firefox for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/using-tabs-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/using-tabs-firefox-android/revision/44032',30573,'2013-07-30T15:47:33-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','revamp for new tab design and for tablets',1,'2013-07-30T15:48:55-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2013-07-30T15:48:55-07:00','rtanglao','approved','Firefox for Android lets you easily create and manage multiple tabs. This article will show you how it''s done.

__TOC__

{for not m14}
=Where are my tabs?=
To view your tabs in Firefox for Android, just swipe to the right and you''ll see a sidebar containing a thumbnail for each tab. You can select any tab by tapping on it. When you''re done, swipe to the left to bring the web page back in view.<br><br> [[Image:Mobile Tabs]]

=How do I open a new tab?=
#Swipe to the right to select the {button New Tab} button located on the bottom, left side of the screen.
#You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 
{note}See [[How do I use the Awesome Screen?]] for more Awesome Screen tricks.{/note}
[[Image:Mobile Tabs1]]

=How do I close and reopen tabs?=
Swipe to the right to see a list of your tabs. Tap the red close button on a tab to close it.

If you close a tab by mistake, you can reopen the last closed tab by tapping the green restore button at the bottom, left side of the screen. <br><br>
[[Image:Mobile Tabs2]]

=How do I open a link in a new tab?=
#To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
#Tap ''''''Open Link in New Tab''''''.
#You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.<br><br>[[Image:Mobile Tabs3]]
#To switch to your new tab, swipe to the right and tap on the new tab''s thumbnail.<br><br>[[Image:Mobile Tabs4]]
{/for}
{for m14}
=Firefox for Android tabbed browsing=
This tutorial shows you how to use tabs.

[[Video:tab_tutorial_small]]

=Where are my tabs?=
To view your tabs in Firefox for Android:
# On the upper right (upper left for tablets), tap on the numeric tab icon which displays the number of tabs currently open .<br /><br />
#:[[Image:Android Numeric Tab Icon phone 480 2]]
#You''ll see a list of thumbnails of tabs on top for phones (for tablets this list will be on top for portrait and on the left side for landscape). You can select any tab by tapping on it or go back just displaying the current tab by clicking on its content.<br/><br/>
#:[[Image:Android Tab List phone 480]]
#If you have [[How do I set up Firefox Sync? | Sync setup]], you can access tabs that are open on your desktop Firefox through the Synced Tabs link.

=How do I open a new tab?=
#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]] and then tap {button +} (the plus sign) to open a new tab.
#You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your Top Sites, Bookmarks and History. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and top sites. 

=How do I close tabs?=
[[#w_where-are-my-tabs_2|View your tabs]] and tap {button X} (to the right of the thumbnail in portrait and underneath in landscape for phones; underneath on tablets) in the tab thumbnail list to close a tab.

=How do I open a link in a new tab?=
#To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
#Tap {menu Open Link in New Tab}. You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.
#To switch to your new tab, [[#w_where-are-my-tabs_2|view your tabs]] and tap on its thumbnail.
{for m23}
=Switch to tab=
Tap the title bar and start entering text. If a match is found for one of your open tabs, then the results will display a tab icon and the text "Switch to tab". Tapping "Switch to tab" will switch you to the already open tab instead of creating a duplicate. 
:[[Image:Android switch to tab jelly bean 480 wide]]
{/for}

{/for}

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/LCXWUo]]','<p>Firefox for Android lets you easily create and manage multiple tabs. This article will show you how it''s done.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_where-are-my-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Where are my tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-close-and-reopen-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">How do I close and reopen tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a link in a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_firefox-for-android-tabbed-browsing"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Firefox for Android tabbed browsing</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_where-are-my-tabs_2"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">Where are my tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab_2"><span class="tocnumber">7</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-close-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">8</span> <span class="toctext">How do I close tabs?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab_2"><span class="tocnumber">9</span> <span class="toctext">How do I open a link in a new tab?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m23"><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_switch-to-tab"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">Switch to tab</span></a></li></span></span></ul></div>
<div class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;">
<h1 id="w_where-are-my-tabs">Where are my tabs?</h1>
<p>To view your tabs in Firefox for Android, just swipe to the right and you''ll see a sidebar containing a thumbnail for each tab. You can select any tab by tapping on it. When you''re done, swipe to the left to bring the web page back in view.<br><br> <img alt="Mobile Tabs" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-28-12-23-21-7b0afb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab">How do I open a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>Swipe to the right to select the <span class="button">New Tab</span> button located on the bottom, left side of the screen.
</li><li>You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your most visited sites. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and tabs. 
</li></ol>
<div class="note">See <a href="/en-US/kb/customize-firefox-home-screen">Customize the Firefox home screen</a> for more Awesome Screen tricks.</div>
<p><img alt="Mobile Tabs1" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-11-04-25-94b63d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-close-and-reopen-tabs">How do I close and reopen tabs?</h1>
<p>Swipe to the right to see a list of your tabs. Tap the red close button on a tab to close it.
</p><p>If you close a tab by mistake, you can reopen the last closed tab by tapping the green restore button at the bottom, left side of the screen. <br><br>
<img alt="Mobile Tabs2" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-11-05-10-1d2d14.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab">How do I open a link in a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
</li><li>Tap <strong>Open Link in New Tab</strong>.
</li><li>You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.<br><br><img alt="Mobile Tabs3" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-28-12-22-36-7a0c87.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>To switch to your new tab, swipe to the right and tap on the new tab''s thumbnail.<br><br><img alt="Mobile Tabs4" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-11-05-55-544516.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m14">
<h1 id="w_firefox-for-android-tabbed-browsing">Firefox for Android tabbed browsing</h1>
<p>This tutorial shows you how to use tabs.
</p><p>The video "tab_tutorial_small" does not exist.
</p>
<h1 id="w_where-are-my-tabs_2">Where are my tabs?</h1>
<p>To view your tabs in Firefox for Android:
</p>
<ol><li> On the upper right (upper left for tablets), tap on the numeric tab icon which displays the number of tabs currently open .<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="Android Numeric Tab Icon phone 480 2" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-04-18-18-31-15-c4ca42.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>You''ll see a list of thumbnails of tabs on top for phones (for tablets this list will be on top for portrait and on the left side for landscape). You can select any tab by tapping on it or go back just displaying the current tab by clicking on its content.<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="Android Tab List phone 480" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-04-18-18-33-29-c81e72.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>If you have <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-set-sync-my-computer"> Sync setup</a>, you can access tabs that are open on your desktop Firefox through the Synced Tabs link.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-new-tab_2">How do I open a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
 and then tap <span class="button">+</span> (the plus sign) to open a new tab.
</li><li>You''ll be taken to the Awesome Screen and a list of your Top Sites, Bookmarks and History. You can type the name or address of the website you''re looking for or just choose it from a list of your bookmarks, history and top sites. 
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-close-tabs">How do I close tabs?</h1>
<p><a href="#w_where-are-my-tabs_2">View your tabs</a> and tap <span class="button">X</span> (to the right of the thumbnail in portrait and underneath in landscape for phones; underneath on tablets) in the tab thumbnail list to close a tab.
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-open-a-link-in-a-new-tab_2">How do I open a link in a new tab?</h1>
<ol><li>To open a link in a new tab, do a long-tap on the link to open the contextual menu.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Open Link in New Tab</span>. You''ll see a notification that a new tab was opened.
</li><li>To switch to your new tab, <a href="#w_where-are-my-tabs_2">view your tabs</a> and tap on its thumbnail.
</li></ol>
<div class="for" data-for="m23">
<h1 id="w_switch-to-tab">Switch to tab</h1>
<p>Tap the title bar and start entering text. If a match is found for one of your open tabs, then the results will display a tab icon and the text "Switch to tab". Tapping "Switch to tab" will switch you to the already open tab instead of creating a duplicate. 
</p>
<dl><dd><img alt="Android switch to tab jelly bean 480 wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-04-18-18-35-10-eccbc8.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</div></div><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44032", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jul 30, 2013, 3:47:33 PM", "datetime": "2013-07-30T15:47:33-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "revamp for new tab design and for tablets", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jul 30, 2013, 3:48:55 PM", "datetime": "2013-07-30T15:48:55-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jul 30, 2013, 3:48:55 PM", "datetime": "2013-07-30T15:48:55-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:31+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44171,'en-US','how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','How do I quit Firefox for Android?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-quit-firefox-android/revision/44171',44103,'2013-08-01T14:00:53-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix very minor typos',1,'2013-08-01T14:01:11-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','{for not m20}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=release|slug=mobile]]
{/for}

For Android version 4 and above, the {menu Quit} menu item was removed from the Firefox to meet Google''s application guidelines. 

{note}''''''Note'''''': You can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen, by using the app switching button  [[Image:app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean]]. If you do not see the above button, long press on the home button to bring up app switch screeen.{/note}

== How to add {menu Quit} menu item back using a Firefox for Android add-on ==

Here''s how to install an add-on to bring back the {menu Quit} menu item so you can close Firefox.
#Tap the {menu Menu} [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {menu Tools} and tap {menu Add-ons}.
# Tap the [[Image:marketplaceIconAndroid]] icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to https://addons.mozilla.org/android/ to achieve the same result.<br><br>[[Image:androidAddonsScreenWithMarketplace]]<br><br> 
# Search for ''''quitnow''''.<br><br>[[Image:AndroidAddonsSearchEN]]<br><br>
# Tap search result.<br><br>[[Image:AndroidAddonsSearchResultsEN]]<br><br>
# Tap the {button Add to Firefox} button.<br><br>[[Image:addToFirefox]]<br><br>
# In the new displayed menu, tap {menu Install} to install the QuitNow add-on.

Your Firefox menu will now have a {menu Quit} menu item that allows you to exit Firefox for Android.
;[[Image:AndroidFirefoxQuitMenu]]','<div class="for" data-for="not m20" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox release version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile">mozilla.org/mobile</a>.</div>
<p></p></div><p>For Android version 4 and above, the <span class="menu">Quit</span> menu item was removed from the Firefox to meet Google''s application guidelines. 
</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Note</strong>: You can still close Firefox or any other app from the app switch screen, by using the app switching button  <img alt="app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-05-15-11-37-747d89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">. If you do not see the above button, long press on the home button to bring up app switch screeen.</div>
<h2 id="w_how-to-add-quit-menu-item-back-using-a-firefox-for-android-add-on">How to add <span class="menu">Quit</span> menu item back using a Firefox for Android add-on</h2>
<p>Here''s how to install an add-on to bring back the <span class="menu">Quit</span> menu item so you can close Firefox.
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="menu">Menu</span> (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="menu">Tools</span> and tap <span class="menu">Add-ons</span>.
</li><li> Tap the <img alt="marketplaceIconAndroid" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-07-31-03-34-04-e0588c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> icon in the upper-right of the Add-ons screen. Alternatively you could go directly to <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/android/">https://addons.mozilla.org/android/</a> to achieve the same result.<br><br><img alt="androidAddonsScreenWithMarketplace" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-07-31-03-36-24-5d9787.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br> 
</li><li> Search for <em>quitnow</em>.<br><br><img alt="AndroidAddonsSearchEN" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-07-31-03-39-25-6eb4f6.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</li><li> Tap search result.<br><br><img alt="AndroidAddonsSearchResultsEN" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-07-31-03-42-30-01406e.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</li><li> Tap the <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span> button.<br><br><img alt="addToFirefox" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-07-31-03-43-36-faf42c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</li><li> In the new displayed menu, tap <span class="menu">Install</span> to install the QuitNow add-on.
</li></ol>
<p>Your Firefox menu will now have a <span class="menu">Quit</span> menu item that allows you to exit Firefox for Android.
</p>
<dl><dt><img alt="AndroidFirefoxQuitMenu" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-07-31-03-46-21-e697a8.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44171", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 1, 2013, 2:00:53 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-01T14:00:53-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix very minor typos", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 1, 2013, 2:01:11 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-01T14:01:11-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:28+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44172,'en-US','search-and-find-tools-firefox-android','Search and Find tools in Firefox for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/search-and-find-tools-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/search-and-find-tools-firefox-android/revision/44172',34974,'2013-08-01T14:20:07-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','correction:it''s now "Set as Default" instead of "Make Default"',1,'2013-08-01T14:21:38-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2013-08-01T14:21:38-07:00','rtanglao','approved','Firefox for Android includes tools for making web and text searching easy with less typing.

{for m14}
__TOC__

=Search engines=
Firefox for Android includes built-in search for Google, Amazon, Twitter and Wikipedia.

#To start your search, tap the Title bar or + at the top of any screen.<br><br>[[Image:title_bar_and_tab]]
#Type your search keyword.
#:The list of built-in search engines appears.<br><br>[[Image:search_engines_native]]
#Tap the engine you want to use to complete your search.<br><br>[[Image:amazon_search_native]]
#The search is performed by the chosen engine and results are narrowed to that site. This example shows the result of choosing Amazon.com to complete a search for the word flowers. <br><br>[[Image:amazon_search_result]]
{/for}
{for =m14}
=Find in page=
Firefox 14 for Android does not support text selection or find-in-page, but it is fixed in the latest version!
{/for}

{for m15}
=Find in Page=
# To use Find in page, tap the main menu > More and select Find in page.
# Type the word you want to find.
#:The word gets highlighted on the screen.
# Use the up or down arrows to move to the next instance of the word.

=Search Suggestion=
Firefox lists Google search suggestions alongside relevant search history and bookmarks. To toggle the search sugggestion feature, tap the Menu > Settings and check the ''''''Show search suggestion''''''.
*Tap the Title bar or + at the top of screen and Firefox will show you suggestion on every search.
[[Image:search suggestion mobile new]] 
{/for}

{for not m14}
=Search engines=
Firefox for Android includes built-in search for Google, Amazon, Twitter and Wikipedia.

#To start your search, tap the Title bar at the top of any screen.
#Type your search keyword.
#:The list of built-in search engines appears.
#Tap the engine you want to use to complete your search.
#The search is performed by the chosen engine and results are narrowed to that site. 
{/for}

{for m23}
=How do I change the default search engine?=
Firefox for Android lets you change the default search engine from the add-ons manager. To change the default search engine:
#Tap the {menu Menu} [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {menu Tools} (on some phones you may have tap {menu More} first) and tap {menu Add-ons}.
#Tap on the search engine that you would like to set as default and tap on {button Set as Default} (Note: the {button Set as Default} button will be disabled for the current default search engine).<br><br>
#:[[Image:Android search engine set as default jelly bean 480]]
{/for}

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/TxgZTi]]','<p>Firefox for Android includes tools for making web and text searching easy with less typing.
</p><div class="for" data-for="m14">
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_search-engines"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Search engines</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="=m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_find-in-page"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Find in page</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_find-in-page_2"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Find in Page</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_search-suggestion"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Search Suggestion</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_search-engines_2"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Search engines</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m23"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-change-the-default-search-engine"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">How do I change the default search engine?</span></a></li></span></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_search-engines">Search engines</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android includes built-in search for Google, Amazon, Twitter and Wikipedia.
</p>
<ol><li>To start your search, tap the Title bar or + at the top of any screen.<br><br><img alt="title_bar_and_tab" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-12-49-51-7effcb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>Type your search keyword.
<dl><dd>The list of built-in search engines appears.<br><br><img alt="search_engines_native" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-05-11-13-07-58-8d3d3e.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Tap the engine you want to use to complete your search.<br><br><img alt="amazon_search_native" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-05-11-13-21-23-03f6cd.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>The search is performed by the chosen engine and results are narrowed to that site. This example shows the result of choosing <a href="http://Amazon.com">Amazon.com</a> to complete a search for the word flowers. <br><br><img alt="amazon_search_result" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-05-11-13-10-32-beeb90.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
</div><div class="for" data-for="=m14" style="display: none;">
<h1 id="w_find-in-page">Find in page</h1>
<p>Firefox 14 for Android does not support text selection or find-in-page, but it is fixed in the latest version!
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m15">
<h1 id="w_find-in-page_2">Find in Page</h1>
<ol><li> To use Find in page, tap the main menu &gt; More and select Find in page.
</li><li> Type the word you want to find.
<dl><dd>The word gets highlighted on the screen.
</dd></dl>
</li><li> Use the up or down arrows to move to the next instance of the word.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_search-suggestion">Search Suggestion</h1>
<p>Firefox lists Google search suggestions alongside relevant search history and bookmarks. To toggle the search sugggestion feature, tap the Menu &gt; Settings and check the <strong>Show search suggestion</strong>.
</p>
<ul><li>Tap the Title bar or + at the top of screen and Firefox will show you suggestion on every search.
</li></ul>
<p><img alt="search suggestion mobile new" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-11-08-13-16-23-d66f9c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;">
<h1 id="w_search-engines_2">Search engines</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android includes built-in search for Google, Amazon, Twitter and Wikipedia.
</p>
<ol><li>To start your search, tap the Title bar at the top of any screen.
</li><li>Type your search keyword.
<dl><dd>The list of built-in search engines appears.
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Tap the engine you want to use to complete your search.
</li><li>The search is performed by the chosen engine and results are narrowed to that site. 
</li></ol>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m23">
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-change-the-default-search-engine">How do I change the default search engine?</h1>
<p>Firefox for Android lets you change the default search engine from the add-ons manager. To change the default search engine:
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="menu">Menu</span> (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="menu">Tools</span> (on some phones you may have tap <span class="menu">More</span> first) and tap <span class="menu">Add-ons</span>.
</li><li>Tap on the search engine that you would like to set as default and tap on <span class="button">Set as Default</span> (Note: the <span class="button">Set as Default</span> button will be disabled for the current default search engine).<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="Android search engine set as default jelly bean 480" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-08-01-21-17-08-29f35f.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li></ol>
</div><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44172", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 1, 2013, 2:20:07 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-01T14:20:07-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "correction:it''s now \"Set as Default\" instead of \"Make Default\"", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 1, 2013, 2:21:38 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-01T14:21:38-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Aug 1, 2013, 2:21:38 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-01T14:21:38-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:26+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44177,'en-US','use-awesome-screen-search-web-bookmarks-and-more','Use the Awesome Screen to search the web, bookmarks and more','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/use-awesome-screen-search-web-bookmarks-and-more','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/use-awesome-screen-search-web-bookmarks-and-more/revision/44177',44030,'2013-08-01T14:42:20-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','add a link to how to change the default search engine',1,'2013-08-01T14:43:25-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','{for not m14}
The Awesome Screen gets you where you want to go quickly by giving you a list of your most often visited sites along with the ability to browse through your bookmarks, history and desktop Firefox tabs. Just tap on the site you want to visit. No typing involved! 
{note}This article talks about accessing bookmarks, history and tabs from your desktop computer. In order to do that you need to set up Firefox Sync. ''''''[[How do I sync Firefox between my desktop and mobile?]]'''''' will show you how.{/note}
{/for}
{for m14}
The Awesome Screen gets you where you want to go quickly by giving you a list of your most often visited sites along with the ability to browse through your bookmarks and history. Just tap on the site you want to visit. No typing involved! 
{/for}

__TOC__

{for not m14}
=How do I quickly find the site I want?=
First, open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the ''''''location bar'''''' at the top of any page or by [[How do I use tabs on mobile?|creating a new tab]]. Then follow the instructions in the sections below.<br><br>
[[Image:Awesome Screen]]

==Using the All Pages tab==
When you first open the Awesome Screen you''ll see a list of your most visited sites. Simply tap on the one you want to go to that site. If you don''t see what you want right away, use the keyboard to type the name or address of the site you want. The Awesome Screen will instantly search through your bookmarks, history, and desktop tabs to find a match. Just tap on one of the results to go to that page.<br><br>
[[Image:Awesome Screen1]]
{note}For more about bookmarks and tags see, [[How do I use bookmarks on mobile?]]{/note}

==Using the Bookmarks, History and Desktop tabs==
You can also browse through your bookmarks, history and desktop tabs by selecting their tabs in the Awesome Screen.<br><br>
[[Image:Awesome Screen2]]

==Searching the web==
If you type something in the Awesome Screen and it doesn''t find any results, just tap on the type of search you''d like to do and Firefox will take you directly to the results.<br><br>
[[Image:Awesome Screen3]]
{/for}
{for m14}
=How do I search?=
Firefox makes searching easy by bringing your web pages to the top of the list as-you-type.

#Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by tapping the plus + on the Tab. <br><br>
#:[[Image:title_bar_and_tab]]
#Type what you are looking for. In this example, typing ''fast'' in the Awesome screen brings up a Youtube video with the word ''fast'' in the title from the history followed by the Google, Amazon, Twitter and Wikipedia search options.{for m23} ''''''Note'''''':The first search option displayed is your current default search engine. If you wish, you can [[Search and Find tools in Firefox for Android#w_how-do-i-change-the-default-search-engine|change the default search engine]].{/for}<br><br>
#:[[Image:search_bar]]
#Tap Google to search the web for your term.<br><br>
#:[[Image:google_search]]
#Tap a result in the list to go to the website.

=How do I browse by Bookmarks and History?=
#Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by tapping the plus + on the Tab. <br><br>
#:[[Image:title_bar_and_tab]]<br><br>
#Tap the Bookmarks tab to view your Bookmarks.<br><br>
#:[[Image:bookmarks_native]]
#:The Desktop Bookmarks folder appears at the top if you have [[How do I sync Firefox between my desktop and mobile?|set up a Firefox Sync account on your computer and paired your mobile device]]. Tap the Desktop Bookmarks folder to see the synced bookmark folders from your desktop Firefox.<br><br>
#:[[Image:desktop_bookmarks]]
#Tap the History tab to go to the list of your recently viewed sites.<br><br>
#:[[Image:history_native]]
#:The top 100 sites in your history appear.

{note}For more about bookmarks, see [[How do I use bookmarks on mobile?]]{/note}
{/for}

{for m23}
=How to set Firefox to always show the URL in the address bar?=
You can turn this feature on or off at any time in your Settings:
#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]] and then tap {button Settings} (on some phones you may need to tap {button More} first).
#Change the ''''''Show Page Title'''''' pref to ''''''Show page address'''''' in the Privacy & Security section of your Firefox Settings.<br><br>
#:[[Image:titlesettings]]

=How to quickly type in the domain name of previously visited websites?=
Firefox will also complete URLs of websites that you''ve been to before. For example, if you type "aw" Firefox may autocomplete "awesomefoundation.org" if you''ve visited that site in the past. Tapping {button Go} in this case would take you directly to that address. 
{/for}

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/LnnpCM]]','<div class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><p>The Awesome Screen gets you where you want to go quickly by giving you a list of your most often visited sites along with the ability to browse through your bookmarks, history and desktop Firefox tabs. Just tap on the site you want to visit. No typing involved! 
</p>
<div class="note">This article talks about accessing bookmarks, history and tabs from your desktop computer. In order to do that you need to set up Firefox Sync. <strong><a href="/en-US/kb/use-sync-share-bookmarks-and-more-with-firefox-mobile">Use Sync to share your Firefox bookmarks, passwords and more with Firefox for mobile</a></strong> will show you how.</div>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m14"><p>The Awesome Screen gets you where you want to go quickly by giving you a list of your most often visited sites along with the ability to browse through your bookmarks and history. Just tap on the site you want to visit. No typing involved! 
</p></div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-quickly-find-the-site-i-want"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How do I quickly find the site I want?</span></a><ul><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_using-the-all-pages-tab"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Using the All Pages tab</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_using-the-bookmarks-history-and-desktop-tabs"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Using the Bookmarks, History and Desktop tabs</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_searching-the-web"><span class="tocnumber">1.3</span> <span class="toctext">Searching the web</span></a></li></span></ul></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-search"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How do I search?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m14"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-browse-by-bookmarks-and-history"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">How do I browse by Bookmarks and History?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m23"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-set-firefox-to-always-show-the-url-in-the-address-bar"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">How to set Firefox to always show the URL in the address bar?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="m23"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-quickly-type-in-the-domain-name-of-previously-visited-websites"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">How to quickly type in the domain name of previously visited websites?</span></a></li></span></ul></div>
<div class="for" data-for="not m14" style="display: none;">
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-quickly-find-the-site-i-want">How do I quickly find the site I want?</h1>
<p>First, open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the <strong>location bar</strong> at the top of any page or by <a href="/en-US/kb/manage-tabs-firefox-android">creating a new tab</a>. Then follow the instructions in the sections below.<br><br>
<img alt="Awesome Screen" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-07-06-55-be1217.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h2 id="w_using-the-all-pages-tab">Using the All Pages tab</h2>
<p>When you first open the Awesome Screen you''ll see a list of your most visited sites. Simply tap on the one you want to go to that site. If you don''t see what you want right away, use the keyboard to type the name or address of the site you want. The Awesome Screen will instantly search through your bookmarks, history, and desktop tabs to find a match. Just tap on one of the results to go to that page.<br><br>
<img alt="Awesome Screen1" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-06-32-34-dd2d9f.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note">For more about bookmarks and tags see, <a href="/en-US/kb/add-delete-and-view-bookmarked-webpages-firefox-android">Add, delete and view bookmarked webpages in Firefox for Android</a></div>
<h2 id="w_using-the-bookmarks-history-and-desktop-tabs">Using the Bookmarks, History and Desktop tabs</h2>
<p>You can also browse through your bookmarks, history and desktop tabs by selecting their tabs in the Awesome Screen.<br><br>
<img alt="Awesome Screen2" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-06-33-03-93db0e.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<h2 id="w_searching-the-web">Searching the web</h2>
<p>If you type something in the Awesome Screen and it doesn''t find any results, just tap on the type of search you''d like to do and Firefox will take you directly to the results.<br><br>
<img alt="Awesome Screen3" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-03-27-07-08-26-9eae1e.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m14">
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-search">How do I search?</h1>
<p>Firefox makes searching easy by bringing your web pages to the top of the list as-you-type.
</p>
<ol><li>Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by tapping the plus + on the Tab. <br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="title_bar_and_tab" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-12-49-51-7effcb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Type what you are looking for. In this example, typing ''fast'' in the Awesome screen brings up a Youtube video with the word ''fast'' in the title from the history followed by the Google, Amazon, Twitter and Wikipedia search options.<span class="for" data-for="m23"> <strong>Note</strong>:The first search option displayed is your current default search engine. If you wish, you can <a href="/en-US/kb/search-and-find-tools-firefox-android#w_how-do-i-change-the-default-search-engine">change the default search engine</a>.</span><br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="search_bar" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-13-17-17-0a0507.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Tap Google to search the web for your term.<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="google_search" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-13-23-15-15c01b.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Tap a result in the list to go to the website.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-browse-by-bookmarks-and-history">How do I browse by Bookmarks and History?</h1>
<ol><li>Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by tapping the plus + on the Tab. <br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="title_bar_and_tab" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-12-49-51-7effcb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""><br><br>
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Tap the Bookmarks tab to view your Bookmarks.<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="bookmarks_native" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-13-44-41-1a7795.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd><dd>The Desktop Bookmarks folder appears at the top if you have <a href="/en-US/kb/use-sync-share-bookmarks-and-more-with-firefox-mobile">set up a Firefox Sync account on your computer and paired your mobile device</a>. Tap the Desktop Bookmarks folder to see the synced bookmark folders from your desktop Firefox.<br><br>
</dd><dd><img alt="desktop_bookmarks" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-13-55-59-43a7b5.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li>Tap the History tab to go to the list of your recently viewed sites.<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="history_native" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-19-14-09-14-3cd15f.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd><dd>The top 100 sites in your history appear.
</dd></dl>
</li></ol>
<div class="note">For more about bookmarks, see <a href="/en-US/kb/add-delete-and-view-bookmarked-webpages-firefox-android">Add, delete and view bookmarked webpages in Firefox for Android</a></div>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m23">
<h1 id="w_how-to-set-firefox-to-always-show-the-url-in-the-address-bar">How to set Firefox to always show the URL in the address bar?</h1>
<p>You can turn this feature on or off at any time in your Settings:
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
 and then tap <span class="button">Settings</span> (on some phones you may need to tap <span class="button">More</span> first).
</li><li>Change the <strong>Show Page Title</strong> pref to <strong>Show page address</strong> in the Privacy &amp; Security section of your Firefox Settings.<br><br>
<dl><dd><img alt="titlesettings" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-07-24-06-44-36-6ebdbb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-to-quickly-type-in-the-domain-name-of-previously-visited-websites">How to quickly type in the domain name of previously visited websites?</h1>
<p>Firefox will also complete URLs of websites that you''ve been to before. For example, if you type "aw" Firefox may autocomplete "<a href="http://awesomefoundation.org">awesomefoundation.org</a>" if you''ve visited that site in the past. Tapping <span class="button">Go</span> in this case would take you directly to that address. 
</p></div><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44177", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 1, 2013, 2:42:20 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-01T14:42:20-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add a link to how to change the default search engine", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 1, 2013, 2:43:25 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-01T14:43:25-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:17+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44411,'en-US','firefox-health-report-understand-your-android-browser-perf','Firefox Health Report - understand your Android browser performance','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-health-report-understand-your-android-browser-perf','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-health-report-understand-your-android-browser-perf/revision/44411',43160,'2013-08-06T01:33:49-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','firefox 23 is no longer beta so remove all refernces to beta',1,'2013-08-06T01:35:20-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2013-08-06T01:35:20-07:00','rtanglao','approved','The Firefox Health Report (FHR) provides insights and performance information about your browser.  By analysing your browser’s performance information, FHR is able to provide you with useful tips that help you get the best from Firefox. For more information about how we handle your data, see [https://www.mozilla.org/legal/privacy/firefox.html our privacy policy]. 

__TOC__
=How to view your Firefox Health Report=
#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]].
#Tap {button Settings}.
#Tap {button Data choices}.
#Tap on the {button Firefox Health Report} link to view the Firefox Health Report.
<!--
{note}''''''Note:'''''' If you have just installed Firefox, the information in the Health Report may not be accurate. It typically takes 14 days of browser use to see any trends.{/note}
-->

=How to turn data sharing on or off=
Data sharing is on by default but you can always turn it on or off:
#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]].
#Tap {button Settings}.
#Tap {button Data choices}.
#Check or uncheck the box next to ''''''Firefox Health Report''''''


When you turn sharing off, Firefox will stop sending information about your browser to Mozilla servers. Firefox will send a request to the Mozilla servers to delete the previously submitted information.  This request is processed immediately after being successfully received.  If the browser does not receive a response that the request was successfully processed (due to lack of internet connectivity, for instance), the browser will continue to send the delete request periodically until it is successfully received.

If  you do not turn sharing off, but the browser is no longer sending data (due to being uninstalled or no longer being used), the previously sent data from your browser will be deleted after 180 days.

Even if you choose not to share data with Mozilla, you will still be able to see information about your browser when you go to the Firefox Health Report page, and you can view the comparison data from other browsers that are sharing their data.  The comparison data will not be based on the data from your browser since it was not shared with Mozilla.

<!--
=What is the Startup Time graph?=
The ''''''Startup Time by Day'''''' graph shows how long it took your browser to start on any given day. The default view (Average), shows the median startup time for that day. Clicking on the “All” toggle shows all the startup times for the day. You can see up to 90 days of data on the graph.

=How do I view the raw data collected?=
You can view a text file of the data that Firefox Health Report collects by clicking on the ''''''Raw Data'''''' tab. This display shows the exact data that is being sent to Mozilla (if sharing is on).
-->
<!-- =Who owns the data collected?=
You own all data collected by FHR. You can delete it anytime by going to _____ and by pressing the delete button. After information is sent to Mozilla’s servers, it stays there for 180 days and is automatically deleted after that. -->
=What data is shared with Mozilla?=

The ''''''Important Metrics'''''' section in the Firefox Health Report has all the data that is shared with Mozilla. To look at the exact data being shared with Mozilla, tap on the {button see the information we record}{/for} link under the ''''''Important Metrics'''''' section.

<!-- commenting this out for now because the url might change
[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/171LPjo]]
-->','<p>The Firefox Health Report (FHR) provides insights and performance information about your browser.  By analysing your browser’s performance information, FHR is able to provide you with useful tips that help you get the best from Firefox. For more information about how we handle your data, see <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/legal/privacy/firefox.html">our privacy policy</a>. 
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-view-your-firefox-health-report"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How to view your Firefox Health Report</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-turn-data-sharing-on-or-off"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How to turn data sharing on or off</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_what-data-is-shared-with-mozilla"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">What data is shared with Mozilla?</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_how-to-view-your-firefox-health-report">How to view your Firefox Health Report</h1>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Settings</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Data choices</span>.
</li><li>Tap on the <span class="button">Firefox Health Report</span> link to view the Firefox Health Report.
</li></ol>
<p>
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-to-turn-data-sharing-on-or-off">How to turn data sharing on or off</h1>
<p>Data sharing is on by default but you can always turn it on or off:
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Settings</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Data choices</span>.
</li><li>Check or uncheck the box next to <strong>Firefox Health Report</strong>
</li></ol>
<p><br>
When you turn sharing off, Firefox will stop sending information about your browser to Mozilla servers. Firefox will send a request to the Mozilla servers to delete the previously submitted information.  This request is processed immediately after being successfully received.  If the browser does not receive a response that the request was successfully processed (due to lack of internet connectivity, for instance), the browser will continue to send the delete request periodically until it is successfully received.
</p><p>If  you do not turn sharing off, but the browser is no longer sending data (due to being uninstalled or no longer being used), the previously sent data from your browser will be deleted after 180 days.
</p><p>Even if you choose not to share data with Mozilla, you will still be able to see information about your browser when you go to the Firefox Health Report page, and you can view the comparison data from other browsers that are sharing their data.  The comparison data will not be based on the data from your browser since it was not shared with Mozilla.
</p><p>

</p>
<h1 id="w_what-data-is-shared-with-mozilla">What data is shared with Mozilla?</h1>
<p>The <strong>Important Metrics</strong> section in the Firefox Health Report has all the data that is shared with Mozilla. To look at the exact data being shared with Mozilla, tap on the <span class="button">see the information we record</span> link under the <strong>Important Metrics</strong> section.
</p><p>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44411", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 6, 2013, 1:33:49 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-06T01:33:49-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "firefox 23 is no longer beta so remove all refernces to beta", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 6, 2013, 1:35:20 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-06T01:35:20-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Aug 6, 2013, 1:35:20 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-06T01:35:20-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:15+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44439,'en-US','firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','Firefox issues with Nexus 10 and Android 4.3','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43/revision/44439',NULL,'2013-08-06T13:17:07-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','DO NOT APPROVE! WORK IN PROGRESS - needs feedback from Tyler',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.
* Title Bar Menu missing after long tap.
* Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like CNN.com.
* Title bar disappears on bing.com.
=Title Bar Menu missing after long tap=
Some users may not be able to see the menu when they long tap (tap and hold for about 1 second) on the title bar.

The workaround for this issue is to make sure you haven''t selected anything in the title bar and then to long tap  on the title bar.

Developers are working on this problem and we will revise this article and update [https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629
 this forum thread as necessary].
=Crashes and rendering issues=
Firefox may crash or render web pages incorrectly. For example cnn.com might display only a portion of the content and may not display the complete sidebar.

To workaround this issue, disable auto-rotation and use landscape orientation (longest edge is horizonal) as follows:
# Make sure your device is in landscape orientation.
# In the Google Settings app, tap {button Accessibility}.
# Un-check "Auto-rotate screen".
Developers are working on this problem [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=900020 in bug 900020].
= Cannot search with the bing search engine=
If you scroll down when at http://bing.com in landscape-orientation you see the title bar disappear and you may not be able to make it re-appear by scrolling back up as expected.

There is no workaround at the moment but developers are working on it in 
[https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=902138 bug 902138].','<p>If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.
</p>
<ul><li> Title Bar Menu missing after long tap.
</li><li> Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like <a href="http://CNN.com">CNN.com</a>.
</li><li> Title bar disappears on <a href="http://bing.com">bing.com</a>.
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_title-bar-menu-missing-after-long-tap">Title Bar Menu missing after long tap</h1>
<p>Some users may not be able to see the menu when they long tap (tap and hold for about 1 second) on the title bar.
</p><p>The workaround for this issue is to make sure you haven''t selected anything in the title bar and then to long tap  on the title bar.
</p><p>Developers are working on this problem and we will revise this article and update <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629">this forum thread as necessary</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_crashes-and-rendering-issues">Crashes and rendering issues</h1>
<p>Firefox may crash or render web pages incorrectly. For example <a href="http://cnn.com">cnn.com</a> might display only a portion of the content and may not display the complete sidebar.
</p><p>To workaround this issue, disable auto-rotation and use landscape orientation (longest edge is horizonal) as follows:
</p>
<ol><li> Make sure your device is in landscape orientation.
</li><li> In the Google Settings app, tap <span class="button">Accessibility</span>.
</li><li> Un-check "Auto-rotate screen".
</li></ol>
<p>Developers are working on this problem <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=900020">in bug 900020</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_cannot-search-with-the-bing-search-engine">Cannot search with the bing search engine</h1>
<p>If you scroll down when at <a href="http://bing.com">http://bing.com</a> in landscape-orientation you see the title bar disappear and you may not be able to make it re-appear by scrolling back up as expected.
</p><p>There is no workaround at the moment but developers are working on it in 
<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=902138">bug 902138</a>.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44439", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 6, 2013, 1:17:07 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-06T13:17:07-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "DO NOT APPROVE! WORK IN PROGRESS - needs feedback from Tyler", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:13+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44461,'en-US','firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','Firefox issues with Nexus 10 and Android 4.3','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43/revision/44461',NULL,'2013-08-06T23:01:01-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','DO NOT APPROVE! WORK IN PROGRESS - needs feedback from Tyler Downer',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.
* Title Bar Menu missing after long tap.
* Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like CNN.com.
* Title bar disappears on bing.com.

Developers are working on these problems and we will revise this article and update [https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629
 this forum thread as necessary].
 
=Title Bar Menu missing after long tap=
Some users may not be able to see the menu when they long tap (tap and hold for about 1 second) on the title bar.

The workaround for this issue is to make sure you haven''t selected anything in the title bar and then to long tap  on the title bar.

=Crashes and rendering issues=
Firefox may crash or render web pages incorrectly. For example cnn.com might display only a portion of the content and may not display the complete sidebar.

To workaround this issue, disable auto-rotation and use landscape orientation (ensure your tablet''s longest edge is horizonal) as follows:
# Make sure your device is in landscape orientation.
# In the Google Settings app, tap {button Accessibility}.
# Un-check "Auto-rotate screen".
Developers are working on this problem [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=900020 in bug 900020].
= Cannot search with the bing search engine=
If you scroll down when at http://bing.com in landscape-orientation you may see the title bar disappear and you may not be able to make it re-appear by scrolling back up as expected.

There is no workaround at the moment but developers are working on it in 
[https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=902138 bug 902138]. Until a workaround is found or the problem is fixed, you can use another search engine.','<p>If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.
</p>
<ul><li> Title Bar Menu missing after long tap.
</li><li> Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like <a href="http://CNN.com">CNN.com</a>.
</li><li> Title bar disappears on <a href="http://bing.com">bing.com</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>Developers are working on these problems and we will revise this article and update <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629">this forum thread as necessary</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_title-bar-menu-missing-after-long-tap">Title Bar Menu missing after long tap</h1>
<p>Some users may not be able to see the menu when they long tap (tap and hold for about 1 second) on the title bar.
</p><p>The workaround for this issue is to make sure you haven''t selected anything in the title bar and then to long tap  on the title bar.
</p>
<h1 id="w_crashes-and-rendering-issues">Crashes and rendering issues</h1>
<p>Firefox may crash or render web pages incorrectly. For example <a href="http://cnn.com">cnn.com</a> might display only a portion of the content and may not display the complete sidebar.
</p><p>To workaround this issue, disable auto-rotation and use landscape orientation (ensure your tablet''s longest edge is horizonal) as follows:
</p>
<ol><li> Make sure your device is in landscape orientation.
</li><li> In the Google Settings app, tap <span class="button">Accessibility</span>.
</li><li> Un-check "Auto-rotate screen".
</li></ol>
<p>Developers are working on this problem <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=900020">in bug 900020</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_cannot-search-with-the-bing-search-engine">Cannot search with the bing search engine</h1>
<p>If you scroll down when at <a href="http://bing.com">http://bing.com</a> in landscape-orientation you may see the title bar disappear and you may not be able to make it re-appear by scrolling back up as expected.
</p><p>There is no workaround at the moment but developers are working on it in 
<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=902138">bug 902138</a>. Until a workaround is found or the problem is fixed, you can use another search engine.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44461", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 6, 2013, 11:01:01 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-06T23:01:01-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "DO NOT APPROVE! WORK IN PROGRESS - needs feedback from Tyler Downer", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:10+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44463,'en-US','firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','Firefox issues with Nexus 10 and Android 4.3','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43/revision/44463',NULL,'2013-08-07T00:06:14-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','DO NOT APPROVE! WORK IN PROGRESS - needs feedback from Tyler Downer',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.
* Title Bar Menu missing after long tap.
* Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like CNN.com.
* Title bar disappears on bing.com.

Developers are working on these problems and we will revise this article and update [https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629
 this forum thread as necessary].
 
=Title Bar Menu missing after long tap=
Some users may not be able to see the menu when they long tap (tap and hold for about 1 second) on the title bar.

The workaround for this issue is to make sure you haven''t selected anything in the title bar and then to long tap  on the title bar.

Developers are working on this problem [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=889562 in bug 889562].

=Crashes and rendering issues=
Firefox may crash or render web pages incorrectly. For example cnn.com might display only a portion of the content and may not display the complete sidebar.

To workaround this issue, disable auto-rotation and use landscape orientation (ensure your tablet''s longest edge is horizonal) as follows:
# Make sure your device is in landscape orientation.
# In the Google Settings app, tap {button Accessibility}.
# Un-check "Auto-rotate screen".
Developers are working on this problem [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=900020 in bug 900020].
= Cannot search with the bing search engine=
If you scroll down when at http://bing.com in landscape-orientation you may see the title bar disappear and you may not be able to make it re-appear by scrolling back up.

There is no workaround at the moment but developers are working on it in 
[https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=902138 bug 902138]. Until a workaround is found or the problem is fixed, tap on the magnifying glass [[Image:bing magnifying glass ff230 nexus 10 android 43]] to get the title bar back and then use another search engine.','<p>If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.
</p>
<ul><li> Title Bar Menu missing after long tap.
</li><li> Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like <a href="http://CNN.com">CNN.com</a>.
</li><li> Title bar disappears on <a href="http://bing.com">bing.com</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>Developers are working on these problems and we will revise this article and update <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629">this forum thread as necessary</a>.
</p>
