On longer web pages, the title bar (which includes the open tab counter) automatically hides itself. To access it again, pull down.','<div class="for" data-for="not m23"><div class="note"><strong>Note</strong>: This feature is only available in version 23 of Firefox and higher.</div></div>
<p>On longer web pages, the title bar (which includes the open tab counter) automatically hides itself. To access it again, pull down.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44530", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 8, 2013, 6:16:31 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-08T06:16:31-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "reword to indicate the tab counter gets hidden too", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 8, 2013, 1:23:33 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-08T13:23:33-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "feer56", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Aug 19, 2014, 11:03:49 AM", "datetime": "2014-08-19T11:03:49-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "user917725", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:03+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (44569,'en-US','how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests','How does Firefox for Android use the permissions it requests?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests/revision/44569',30574,'2013-08-08T23:30:37-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','DO NOT APPROVE UNTIL FF24 Beta is available in the Google Play Store',1,'2013-08-09T11:30:27-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','This article describes how Firefox uses the permissions it requests, while respecting your privacy and personal data. Mozilla is committed to your privacy: [http://www.mozilla.org/legal/privacy/firefox.html Firefox Privacy Policy]

Firefox for Android currently uses these permissions:

* ''''''Your location'''''' - Fine (GPS) location.  GPS location is used only when you choose to share your location with a website. Firefox never uses your location itself or shares it with a website without your permission. [http://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/geolocation/ Learn more about Firefox''s location controls].

* ''''''Storage'''''' - Modify/delete SD card contents.  Firefox uses this permission to save downloaded files to the SD card.  {for m10}Firefox will also store its own settings and history on the SD card if you use the Android Settings app to move Firefox to SD storage.{/for}

* ''''''Hardware controls'''''' - Take pictures and videos.  When a web page requests an image file to upload, you may choose to take a picture with your device''s built-in camera.  Firefox never takes a picture or video unless you ask it to.  For more information, see this article about [http://hacks.mozilla.org/2011/09/introducing-aurora-9/ what''s new for web developers in Firefox 9].

* ''''''Network communication'''''' - Full Internet access, view network state.  Firefox uses these permissions to download web pages, add-ons, and other content over the Internet.

* ''''''System Tools'''''' - Install shortcuts.  This permission is used by Firefox to allow you to add bookmarks or web app shortcuts to your device home screen.

* ''''''System Tools'''''' - Prevent phone from sleeping, prevent tablet from sleeping. The Adobe Flash plug-in uses this permission in versions of Firefox that include Flash support.

* ''''''System Tools'''''' - Modify global system settings. Firefox uses this permission to enable or disable your Firefox Sync account when you change your sync settings.

* ''''''Your accounts'''''' - Act as an account authenticator, manage the accounts list, use the authentication credentials of an account.  If you set up Firefox Sync, then Firefox uses these permissions to add your sync account to the Android sync settings.

{for m15}
* ''''''Your personal information'''''' - Read and write Browser''s history and bookmarks.  Firefox uses this permission if you choose to import history and bookmarks from the default browser on your Android device.
{/for}

* ''''''Control Near Field Communication (NFC)'''''' - Allows the use of the NFC chip on the device. Firefox uses this permission to share tabs by tapping two devices with NFC together. This permission is only required for the Firefox for Android beta.

* ''''''Record audio'''''' - Record audio from the device''s microphone. Firefox uses this permission for WebRTC (real-time communication). This feature is still in development and is currently available only to developers. This permission is only required for the Firefox for Android beta.

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/LHhqLV]]','<p>This article describes how Firefox uses the permissions it requests, while respecting your privacy and personal data. Mozilla is committed to your privacy: <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/legal/privacy/firefox.html">Firefox Privacy Policy</a>
</p><p>Firefox for Android currently uses these permissions:
</p>
<ul><li> <strong>Your location</strong> - Fine (GPS) location.  GPS location is used only when you choose to share your location with a website. Firefox never uses your location itself or shares it with a website without your permission. <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/geolocation/">Learn more about Firefox''s location controls</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Storage</strong> - Modify/delete SD card contents.  Firefox uses this permission to save downloaded files to the SD card.  <span class="for" data-for="m10">Firefox will also store its own settings and history on the SD card if you use the Android Settings app to move Firefox to SD storage.</span>
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Hardware controls</strong> - Take pictures and videos.  When a web page requests an image file to upload, you may choose to take a picture with your device''s built-in camera.  Firefox never takes a picture or video unless you ask it to.  For more information, see this article about <a href="http://hacks.mozilla.org/2011/09/introducing-aurora-9/">what''s new for web developers in Firefox 9</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Network communication</strong> - Full Internet access, view network state.  Firefox uses these permissions to download web pages, add-ons, and other content over the Internet.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>System Tools</strong> - Install shortcuts.  This permission is used by Firefox to allow you to add bookmarks or web app shortcuts to your device home screen.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>System Tools</strong> - Prevent phone from sleeping, prevent tablet from sleeping. The Adobe Flash plug-in uses this permission in versions of Firefox that include Flash support.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>System Tools</strong> - Modify global system settings. Firefox uses this permission to enable or disable your Firefox Sync account when you change your sync settings.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Your accounts</strong> - Act as an account authenticator, manage the accounts list, use the authentication credentials of an account.  If you set up Firefox Sync, then Firefox uses these permissions to add your sync account to the Android sync settings.
</li></ul>
<div class="for" data-for="m15">
<ul><li> <strong>Your personal information</strong> - Read and write Browser''s history and bookmarks.  Firefox uses this permission if you choose to import history and bookmarks from the default browser on your Android device.
</li></ul>
</div>
<ul><li> <strong>Control Near Field Communication (NFC)</strong> - Allows the use of the NFC chip on the device. Firefox uses this permission to share tabs by tapping two devices with NFC together. This permission is only required for the Firefox for Android beta.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Record audio</strong> - Record audio from the device''s microphone. Firefox uses this permission for WebRTC (real-time communication). This feature is still in development and is currently available only to developers. This permission is only required for the Firefox for Android beta.
</li></ul>
<p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "44569", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 8, 2013, 11:30:37 PM", "datetime": "2013-08-08T23:30:37-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "DO NOT APPROVE UNTIL FF24 Beta is available in the Google Play Store", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 9, 2013, 11:30:27 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-09T11:30:27-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:47:01+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (45449,'en-US','how-do-i-share-things-firefox-android','How do I share things from Firefox for Android?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-share-things-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-share-things-firefox-android/revision/45449',NULL,'2013-08-23T08:46:08-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','DO NOT APPROVE - WORK IN PROGRESS - fixed typos, use template for menu and use screenshot without graphic next to share',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','Firefox for Android makes it easy to share things you find on web. This article explains how it works. 
{for not m24}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=for Android Beta|slug=mobile/beta]]
<!-- When Fx24 is released, change the template above to [[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=for Android Release|slug=mobile]] -->
{/for}

To share things you find on web, go to that website and: 

#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]] and then tap {button Settings} (on some phones you may need to tap {button More} first).
#Tap the {button Share} button to share. <br><br> [[Image:FF24 Share Menu Jelly Bean 300px wide]] 

=How do I Share Things in Reader Mode?=

To share things in Reader mode: 

