</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "45455", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 23, 2013, 9:19:44 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-23T09:19:44-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "minor copy edits, ready for l10n", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 23, 2013, 9:20:57 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-23T09:20:57-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:46:49+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (45468,'en-US','how-do-i-share-things-firefox-android','How do I share things from Firefox for Android?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-share-things-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-do-i-share-things-firefox-android/revision/45468',45455,'2013-08-24T00:17:16-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','clarify NFC must be enabled on sending and receiving advice and remove awkward ''to''  and ''from'' wording',1,'2013-08-24T00:17:36-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','Firefox for Android makes it easy to share things on the web using the share menu item, reader mode and by bumping together two devices that support NFC. This article explains how it works. 
__TOC__
{for not m24}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=for Android Beta|slug=mobile/beta]]
<!-- When Fx24 is released, change the template above to [[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=for Android Release|slug=mobile]] -->
{/for}

=How do I Share using the menu?=
To share things you find on the web, go to that website and: 

#Tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]] and then tap {button Settings} (on some phones you may need to tap {button More} first).
#Tap the {button Share} button to share. <br><br> [[Image:FF24 Share Menu Jelly Bean 300px wide]] 

=How do I Share in Reader Mode?=

To share things in Reader mode: 

#Tap the [[Image:readinglist4]] icon and choose the app that you want to share with.

=How do I share using NFC?=
{note}Only a few newer Andoid devices support NFC. Both the sending and receiving devices must support NFC for this feature to work.{/note}
# On both the sending and receiving devices, ensure NFC is on: In Android settings, under {button Wireless & Network} tap {button More...} and then check the box next to "NFC".
# To share a URL from Firefox, touch the ''''back'''' of the sending device to the ''''back'''' of the receiving device and then tap {button Touch to beam} on the sending device. 
<br><br>[[Image:ff24 touch to beam jelly bean 300px wide]] 

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/18bVEMZ]]','<p>Firefox for Android makes it easy to share things on the web using the share menu item, reader mode and by bumping together two devices that support NFC. This article explains how it works. 
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-share-using-the-menu"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How do I Share using the menu?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-share-in-reader-mode"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How do I Share in Reader Mode?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-share-using-nfc"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">How do I share using NFC?</span></a></li></ul></div>
<div class="for" data-for="not m24" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox for Android Beta version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile/beta">mozilla.org/mobile/beta</a>.</div>

<p></p></div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-share-using-the-menu">How do I Share using the menu?</h1>
<p>To share things you find on the web, go to that website and: 
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
 and then tap <span class="button">Settings</span> (on some phones you may need to tap <span class="button">More</span> first).
</li><li>Tap the <span class="button">Share</span> button to share. <br><br> <img alt="FF24 Share Menu Jelly Bean 300px wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-08-23-15-41-11-9fe933.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-share-in-reader-mode">How do I Share in Reader Mode?</h1>
<p>To share things in Reader mode: 
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <img alt="readinglist4" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-08-04-11-19-33-a87ff6.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> icon and choose the app that you want to share with.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-share-using-nfc">How do I share using NFC?</h1>
<div class="note">Only a few newer Andoid devices support NFC. Both the sending and receiving devices must support NFC for this feature to work.</div>
<ol><li> On both the sending and receiving devices, ensure NFC is on: In Android settings, under <span class="button">Wireless &amp; Network</span> tap <span class="button">More...</span> and then check the box next to "NFC".
</li><li> To share a URL from Firefox, touch the <em>back</em> of the sending device to the <em>back</em> of the receiving device and then tap <span class="button">Touch to beam</span> on the sending device. 
</li></ol>
<p><br><br><img alt="ff24 touch to beam jelly bean 300px wide" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-08-23-16-05-31-3f03da.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</p><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "45468", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 24, 2013, 12:17:16 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-24T00:17:16-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "clarify NFC must be enabled on sending and receiving advice and remove awkward ''to''  and ''from'' wording", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 24, 2013, 12:17:36 AM", "datetime": "2013-08-24T00:17:36-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:46:46+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (46239,'en-US','how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests','How does Firefox for Android use the permissions it requests?','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests/revision/46239',44718,'2013-09-15T23:42:04-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','dummy update to set it ready for l10n - not sure why i didn''t set this ready for l10n before, my apologies',1,'2013-09-15T23:42:35-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2013-09-15T23:42:35-07:00','rtanglao','approved','This article describes how Firefox uses the permissions it requests, while respecting your privacy and personal data. Mozilla is committed to your privacy: [http://www.mozilla.org/legal/privacy/firefox.html Firefox Privacy Policy]

Firefox for Android currently uses these permissions:

* ''''''Your location'''''' - Fine (GPS) location.  GPS location is used only when you choose to share your location with a website. Firefox never uses your location itself or shares it with a website without your permission. [http://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/geolocation/ Learn more about Firefox''s location controls].

* ''''''Storage'''''' - Modify/delete SD card contents.  Firefox uses this permission to save downloaded files to the SD card.  {for m10}Firefox will also store its own settings and history on the SD card if you use the Android Settings app to move Firefox to SD storage.{/for}

* ''''''Hardware controls'''''' - Take pictures and videos.  When a web page requests an image file to upload, you may choose to take a picture with your device''s built-in camera.  Firefox never takes a picture or video unless you ask it to.  For more information, see this article about [http://hacks.mozilla.org/2011/09/introducing-aurora-9/ what''s new for web developers in Firefox 9].

* ''''''Network communication'''''' - Full Internet access, view network state.  Firefox uses these permissions to download web pages, add-ons, and other content over the Internet.

* ''''''System Tools'''''' - Install shortcuts.  This permission is used by Firefox to allow you to add bookmarks or web app shortcuts to your device home screen.

* ''''''System Tools'''''' - Prevent phone from sleeping, prevent tablet from sleeping. The Adobe Flash plug-in uses this permission in versions of Firefox that include Flash support.

* ''''''System Tools'''''' - Modify global system settings. Firefox uses this permission to enable or disable your Firefox Sync account when you change your sync settings.

* ''''''Your accounts'''''' - Act as an account authenticator, manage the accounts list, use the authentication credentials of an account.  If you set up Firefox Sync, then Firefox uses these permissions to add your sync account to the Android sync settings.

{for m15}
* ''''''Your personal information'''''' - Read and write Browser''s history and bookmarks.  Firefox uses this permission if you choose to import history and bookmarks from the default browser on your Android device.
{/for}

{for m24}
* ''''''Control Near Field Communication (NFC)'''''' - Allows the use of the NFC chip on the device. Firefox uses this permission to share tabs by tapping two devices with NFC together.

* ''''''Record audio'''''' - Record audio from the device''s microphone. Firefox uses this permission for WebRTC (real-time communication). This feature is still in development and is currently available only to developers.
{/for}

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/LHhqLV]]','<p>This article describes how Firefox uses the permissions it requests, while respecting your privacy and personal data. Mozilla is committed to your privacy: <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/legal/privacy/firefox.html">Firefox Privacy Policy</a>
</p><p>Firefox for Android currently uses these permissions:
</p>
<ul><li> <strong>Your location</strong> - Fine (GPS) location.  GPS location is used only when you choose to share your location with a website. Firefox never uses your location itself or shares it with a website without your permission. <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/geolocation/">Learn more about Firefox''s location controls</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Storage</strong> - Modify/delete SD card contents.  Firefox uses this permission to save downloaded files to the SD card.  <span class="for" data-for="m10">Firefox will also store its own settings and history on the SD card if you use the Android Settings app to move Firefox to SD storage.</span>
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Hardware controls</strong> - Take pictures and videos.  When a web page requests an image file to upload, you may choose to take a picture with your device''s built-in camera.  Firefox never takes a picture or video unless you ask it to.  For more information, see this article about <a href="http://hacks.mozilla.org/2011/09/introducing-aurora-9/">what''s new for web developers in Firefox 9</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Network communication</strong> - Full Internet access, view network state.  Firefox uses these permissions to download web pages, add-ons, and other content over the Internet.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>System Tools</strong> - Install shortcuts.  This permission is used by Firefox to allow you to add bookmarks or web app shortcuts to your device home screen.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>System Tools</strong> - Prevent phone from sleeping, prevent tablet from sleeping. The Adobe Flash plug-in uses this permission in versions of Firefox that include Flash support.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>System Tools</strong> - Modify global system settings. Firefox uses this permission to enable or disable your Firefox Sync account when you change your sync settings.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Your accounts</strong> - Act as an account authenticator, manage the accounts list, use the authentication credentials of an account.  If you set up Firefox Sync, then Firefox uses these permissions to add your sync account to the Android sync settings.
</li></ul>
<div class="for" data-for="m15">
<ul><li> <strong>Your personal information</strong> - Read and write Browser''s history and bookmarks.  Firefox uses this permission if you choose to import history and bookmarks from the default browser on your Android device.
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m24">
<ul><li> <strong>Control Near Field Communication (NFC)</strong> - Allows the use of the NFC chip on the device. Firefox uses this permission to share tabs by tapping two devices with NFC together.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> <strong>Record audio</strong> - Record audio from the device''s microphone. Firefox uses this permission for WebRTC (real-time communication). This feature is still in development and is currently available only to developers.
</li></ul>
</div><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "46239", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Sep 15, 2013, 11:42:04 PM", "datetime": "2013-09-15T23:42:04-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "dummy update to set it ready for l10n - not sure why i didn''t set this ready for l10n before, my apologies", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Sep 15, 2013, 11:42:35 PM", "datetime": "2013-09-15T23:42:35-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Sep 15, 2013, 11:42:35 PM", "datetime": "2013-09-15T23:42:35-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:46:44+00:00');
