To use this feature, start a guest session and hand the device to somebody you trust. This person will be able to browse without seeing your personal browsing data. Once finished, you end the guest session and resume browsing with your personal browsing data intact and unaffected by the other person.


__TOC__
{for not m25}
[[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=for Android Beta|slug=beta]]
<!-- USE THIS VERSION OF THE TEMPLATE AFTER RELEASE - [[Template:ApplytoFx|channel=release|slug=/]] -->
{/for}
=How do I start a Firefox Guest Session?=
#Tap the Firefox {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {menu Tools} and finally tap {menu New Guest Session}.<br /><br />[[Image:New Guest Session]] 
#Tap  {key Continue} to start a guest session without any of your personal browsing data.
=How do I end a Firefox Guest Session?=
#Tap the Firefox {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {menu Exit Guest Session}.<br /><br />[[Image:Exit Guest Session]] 
#Tap {key Continue} to delete all the browsing data from this guest session and return to a regular session with your personal browsing data.

=How can I tell if I am in a Guest Session?=
*Tap the Firefox {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]]. If you see {menu Exit Guest Session}, then you are using a Firefox Guest Session, otherwise you are in a regular Firefox session.','<p>A Firefox guest session allows you to share your browser with somebody else and not have their browsing affect your personal browsing data like saved passwords, history or bookmarks.
</p><p>To use this feature, start a guest session and hand the device to somebody you trust. This person will be able to browse without seeing your personal browsing data. Once finished, you end the guest session and resume browsing with your personal browsing data intact and unaffected by the other person.
</p><p><br>
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-start-a-firefox-guest-session"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How do I start a Firefox Guest Session?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-end-a-firefox-guest-session"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How do I end a Firefox Guest Session?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-can-i-tell-if-i-am-in-a-guest-session"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">How can I tell if I am in a Guest Session?</span></a></li></ul></div>
<div class="for" data-for="not m25" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox for Android Beta version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/beta">mozilla.org/beta</a>.</div>

<p></p></div>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-start-a-firefox-guest-session">How do I start a Firefox Guest Session?</h1>
<ol><li>Tap the Firefox <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="menu">Tools</span> and finally tap <span class="menu">New Guest Session</span>.<br><br><img alt="New Guest Session" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-10-24-18-31-39-084e03.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li><li>Tap  <span class="key">Continue</span> to start a guest session without any of your personal browsing data.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-do-i-end-a-firefox-guest-session">How do I end a Firefox Guest Session?</h1>
<ol><li>Tap the Firefox <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="menu">Exit Guest Session</span>.<br><br><img alt="Exit Guest Session" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-10-24-18-32-48-1b1256.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</li><li>Tap <span class="key">Continue</span> to delete all the browsing data from this guest session and return to a regular session with your personal browsing data.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_how-can-i-tell-if-i-am-in-a-guest-session">How can I tell if I am in a Guest Session?</h1>
<ul><li>Tap the Firefox <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
. If you see <span class="menu">Exit Guest Session</span>, then you are using a Firefox Guest Session, otherwise you are in a regular Firefox session.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "48221", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 17, 2013, 1:51:25 PM", "datetime": "2013-10-17T13:51:25-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "as per verdi''s feedback modified it to make it clear your friend can''t see your personal browsing data", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Oct 20, 2013, 1:44:14 AM", "datetime": "2013-10-20T01:44:14-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:46:21+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (48246,'en-US','firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','Firefox issues with Nexus 10 and Android 4.3','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/firefox-issues-nexus-10-and-android-43/revision/48246',44540,'2013-10-18T04:20:08-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','update to say that these issues were fixed in ff25',1,'2013-10-18T04:20:47-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.
<!-- fixed in FF24
* Title Bar Menu missing after long tap.
-->
* Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like CNN.com. 
* Title bar disappears on bing.com.

These problems were fixed in Firefox 25 for Android which will be released on Tuesday October 29, 2013 and is currently in [http://www.mozilla.org/en-US/mobile/beta/ beta]. We encourage you to try the beta and see if it solves your issues.

We will revise this article and update [https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629
 this forum thread as necessary].

<!-- this was fixed in FF24 
=Title Bar Menu missing after long tap=
Some users may not be able to see the menu when they long tap (tap and hold for about 1 second) on the title bar.

The workaround for this issue is to make sure you haven''t selected anything in the title bar and then to long tap  on the title bar.

Developers are working on this problem [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=889562 in bug 889562].
-->

=Crashes and rendering issues=
Firefox may crash or render web pages incorrectly. For example cnn.com might display only a portion of the content and may not display the complete sidebar.

To workaround this issue, disable auto-rotation and use landscape orientation (ensure your tablet''s longest edge is horizonal) as follows:
# Make sure your device is in landscape orientation.
# In the Google Settings app, tap {button Accessibility}.
# Un-check "Auto-rotate screen".
Developers are working on this problem [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=900020 in bug 900020].
= Cannot search with the bing search engine=
If you scroll down when at http://bing.com in landscape-orientation you may see the title bar disappear and you may not be able to make it re-appear by scrolling back up.

There is no workaround at the moment but developers are working on it in 
[https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=902138 bug 902138]. Until a workaround is found or the problem is fixed,  close Firefox from the app switch screen by using the app switching button  [[Image:app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean]], restart Firefox and then use another search engine.

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/18f7amY]]','<p>If you have upgraded your Nexus 10 tablet to the latest of version of Android, 4.3,  you may experience the following issues with Firefox.

</p>
<ul><li> Crashes and rendering issues with certain sites like <a href="http://CNN.com">CNN.com</a>. 
</li><li> Title bar disappears on <a href="http://bing.com">bing.com</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>These problems were fixed in Firefox 25 for Android which will be released on Tuesday October 29, 2013 and is currently in <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/en-US/mobile/beta/">beta</a>. We encourage you to try the beta and see if it solves your issues.
</p><p>We will revise this article and update <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/questions/966629">this forum thread as necessary</a>.
</p><p>
</p>
<h1 id="w_crashes-and-rendering-issues">Crashes and rendering issues</h1>
<p>Firefox may crash or render web pages incorrectly. For example <a href="http://cnn.com">cnn.com</a> might display only a portion of the content and may not display the complete sidebar.
</p><p>To workaround this issue, disable auto-rotation and use landscape orientation (ensure your tablet''s longest edge is horizonal) as follows:
</p>
<ol><li> Make sure your device is in landscape orientation.
</li><li> In the Google Settings app, tap <span class="button">Accessibility</span>.
</li><li> Un-check "Auto-rotate screen".
</li></ol>
<p>Developers are working on this problem <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=900020">in bug 900020</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_cannot-search-with-the-bing-search-engine">Cannot search with the bing search engine</h1>
<p>If you scroll down when at <a href="http://bing.com">http://bing.com</a> in landscape-orientation you may see the title bar disappear and you may not be able to make it re-appear by scrolling back up.
</p><p>There is no workaround at the moment but developers are working on it in 
<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=902138">bug 902138</a>. Until a workaround is found or the problem is fixed,  close Firefox from the app switch screen by using the app switching button  <img alt="app switch button 25px - Android Jelly Bean" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-04-05-15-11-37-747d89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">, restart Firefox and then use another search engine.
</p><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "48246", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 18, 2013, 4:20:08 AM", "datetime": "2013-10-18T04:20:08-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "update to say that these issues were fixed in ff25", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Oct 18, 2013, 4:20:47 AM", "datetime": "2013-10-18T04:20:47-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:46:19+00:00');
