</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "50774", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 18, 2013, 7:17:35 AM", "datetime": "2013-11-18T07:17:35-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "as per https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=939785 need to change directory listing urls  to use the ftp server - part 2", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 18, 2013, 7:23:51 AM", "datetime": "2013-11-18T07:23:51-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Nov 18, 2013, 7:23:51 AM", "datetime": "2013-11-18T07:23:51-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:45:45+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (51859,'en-US','clearing-cookies-private-data-history-and-settings','Clearing cookies, private data, history, and settings in Firefox for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clearing-cookies-private-data-history-and-settings','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clearing-cookies-private-data-history-and-settings/revision/51859',35770,'2013-12-13T16:22:29-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix some minor stylistic typos',1,'2013-12-13T16:23:29-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','{for m14}
Firefox for Android provides a basic level of control over privacy-related data. You can easily clear ''''''ALL'''''' private data, but unlike the desktop version of firefox you cannot delete cookies for an individual website.

The following tutorial demonstrates how to clear all private and historical data from your browser.

{for =m16,=m17,=m18,=m19,=m20,=m21,=m22,=m23,=m24}
[[Video:clear_history]]
{/for}{/for}

{for =m16,=m17,=m18,=m19,=m20,=m21,=m22,=m23,=m24}
#To clear private data, cookies, history and settings in Firefox for Android, tap the {button Main menu} > {button More} > {button Settings}.
#Select {button Clear private data} from the Privacy & Security section of the Settings screen.
#Choose the data you want to keep or clear by enabling the check boxes.
#Tap {button Clear data}.
A notification appears confirming your data was cleared.
{/for}

{for m25}
#To clear private data, cookies, history and settings in Firefox for Android, tap the {button Menu} button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]], then tap {button Settings} (on some devices you may have to tap {button More} first).
#Tap {button Privacy} and then tap {button Clear private data}.
#Choose the data you want to keep or clear by enabling the check boxes.
#Tap {button Clear data}.
A notification appears confirming your data was cleared.
{/for}

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/LEjDDl]]','<div class="for" data-for="m14"><p>Firefox for Android provides a basic level of control over privacy-related data. You can easily clear <strong>ALL</strong> private data, but unlike the desktop version of firefox you cannot delete cookies for an individual website.
</p><p>The following tutorial demonstrates how to clear all private and historical data from your browser.
</p><div class="for" data-for="=m16,=m17,=m18,=m19,=m20,=m21,=m22,=m23,=m24" style="display: none;"><p>The video "clear_history" does not exist.

</p><div class="for" data-for="=m16,=m17,=m18,=m19,=m20,=m21,=m22,=m23,=m24" style="display: none;">
<ol><li>To clear private data, cookies, history and settings in Firefox for Android, tap the <span class="button">Main menu</span> &gt; <span class="button">More</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span>.
</li><li>Select <span class="button">Clear private data</span> from the Privacy &amp; Security section of the Settings screen.
</li><li>Choose the data you want to keep or clear by enabling the check boxes.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Clear data</span>.
</li></ol>
<p>A notification appears confirming your data was cleared.
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m25">
<ol><li>To clear private data, cookies, history and settings in Firefox for Android, tap the <span class="button">Menu</span> button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)
, then tap <span class="button">Settings</span> (on some devices you may have to tap <span class="button">More</span> first).
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Privacy</span> and then tap <span class="button">Clear private data</span>.
</li><li>Choose the data you want to keep or clear by enabling the check boxes.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Clear data</span>.
</li></ol>
<p>A notification appears confirming your data was cleared.
</p></div><p>&nbsp;

</p></div></div>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "51859", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Dec 13, 2013, 4:22:29 PM", "datetime": "2013-12-13T16:22:29-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix some minor stylistic typos", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Dec 13, 2013, 4:23:29 PM", "datetime": "2013-12-13T16:23:29-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:45:42+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (52004,'en-US','getting-started-firefox-android-tablet-browser','Get started with Firefox for Android on tablets','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-firefox-android-tablet-browser','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-firefox-android-tablet-browser/revision/52004',30702,'2013-12-18T05:31:26-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','small update to make it clear that 7" tablets get the tablet user experience',1,'2013-12-18T05:32:14-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','This article describes how to get started with the Firefox for Android tablet browser.

{for not m9}
[[T:ApplytoFx|version=9 for mobile|slug=mobile]]
{/for}
{for =m14}
[[T:ApplytoFx|version=15 for Android|slug=mobile]]
{/for}

{note} ''''''Note:'''''' Tablets with screens smaller than 7" do not use the tablet browser by default. For those tablets including phablets like the Samsung Galaxy Note I, II and III, see [[Getting started with Firefox for mobile]]. {/note}

{for =m10, m15}
__TOC__

==How do I know if my device is supported?==
To install the Firefox for Android tablet browser, refer to the following articles:
*[[Will Firefox work on my mobile device?]] 
*[[How do I install Firefox on a mobile device?]]

The following image shows the Firefox mobile tablet interface in landscape mode.
{for =m10}
[[Image:tablet_ui]]
{/for}
{for m15}
[[Image:tablet_m15]]
{/for}
The following image shows the Firefox mobile tablet interface in portrait mode.
{for =m10}
[[Image:tablet_portrait]]
{/for}
{for m15}
[[Image:tablet_portrait_small_m15]]
{/for}

==Where are the tablet navigation controls?==
The navigation and menus are across the top of the screen, from left to right, as shown in the following screenshot:
{for =m10}
[[Image:tablet controls]]
{/for}
{for m15}
[[Image:tablet_menu_m15]]
{/for}
*Tabs icon - Displays the number of open tabs, tap to show tabs in the sidebar. To hide the tabs in landscape mode, swipe left across the black tab margin.
*Location bar - Tap the location bar to access your history and bookmarks. Or type an address or search term, then press Enter on the soft keyboard to go.
{for m15}
*Reload page - Tap to reload the page.
{/for}
*Bookmark site - Tap the star to add a site to your bookmarks list.
{for =m10}
*Main Menu - Tap to access Preferences, Add-ons, Downloads, Quit, Site Options, Save as PDF, Share Page and Find in Page, as shown in the following image.
[[Image:main menu2]]
{/for}
{for m15}
*Main Menu - Tap to access Share, Save as PDF, Find in Page, Request Desktop Site, Clear Site Settings, Add-ons, Downloads, Settings, and Quit.
{/for}

{for =m10}
==Why can''t I watch animated or video Flash content on my tablet?==
Flash is not yet supported on Firefox for Android, see
[[Firefox for Mobile doesn''t support Flash]].
{/for}

{for m15}
==How do I watch videos on my tablet?==
See [[How do I watch Flash videos with Firefox for Android?]].
{/for}

==How do I find my bookmarks and history?==
{for =m10}
#Tap the Location Bar. <br>Three buttons appear for Bookmarks, History and Desktop.
*Tap the Bookmarks button to view bookmarks. Long-tap a bookmark to modify or share it.
*Tap the History button to view history. Long-tap a link to share it or open in a new tab.
*Tap the Desktop button to set up or access synced tabs. See [[How do I sync Firefox between my desktop and mobile?]]
{/for}
{for m15}
#Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by tapping the plus + on the Tab.
*Tap the Bookmarks tab to view your Bookmarks.
*Tap the History tab to go to the list of your recently viewed sites.
{/for}

==How do I clear the recent history on my tablet?==
{for =m10}
''''The Clear Mobile History add-on adds a {button Clear History} button to your Preferences.''''
#Tap the {button Main Menu} button in the upper-right corner of the screen and select {menu Add-ons} to open the Add-ons screen.
#Tap in the Add-ons search box and type "Clear Mobile History" to search for the add-on.
#Tap the Clear Mobile History listing to expand it and select {button Add to Firefox}. A progress bar appears while the add-on is being downloaded and installed. When it''s done, Clear Mobile History should appear in your list of add-ons at the top of the screen.<br>
#To clear items from the All Pages and History, tap the Main Menu button in the upper-right of the screen and select Preferences. Scroll down and tap the Clear History button to remove all results from the All Pages and History screens.<br>[[Image:clear history]]
{/for}
{for =m15}
#Tap {button Menu} > {button Settings} > {button Clear private data}.
#Select the Browsing and download history check box.
#Tap {button Clear data}.
A notification appears confirming deletion of your data.
{/for}

{for =m10}
==How do I get the text to reformat when I zoom?==
#To reformat text on zoom, tap the Main Menu button in the upper-right of the screen and select Preferences. Scroll down and tap the Reformat text on zoom checkbox.<br>[[Image:text reformat]]
{/for}

==How do I view the Desktop version of web pages?==
{for =m10}
''''Installing the add-on "Phony" will let you disguise Firefox for Mobile as a desktop browser so websites will serve you the desktop version of their pages.
#Tap the {button Main Menu} button in the upper-right corner of the screen and select {menu Add-ons} to open the Add-ons screen.
#Tap in the Add-ons search box and type "Phony" to search for the add-on.
#Tap the Phony listing to expand it and select {button Add to Firefox}. A progress bar appears while the add-on is being downloaded and installed. When it''s done, Phony should appear in your list of add-ons at the top of the screen.<br>[[Image: phony tablet]]
#Next, tap the {menu Preferences} menu item at the top left to switch to the Preferences screen.
#Finally, tab the {button Default} button in the ''''''User Agent'''''' row and select {menu Desktop Firefox} as your new user agent. Now websites appear as just as they do on your desktop!<br>[[Image:Phony User Agent]]

===Troubleshooting User Agent Setup===
*The menus and search bar in Firefox at the top, right, and left can appear and disappear if you swipe up, left, or right. So, try swiping to find them if they aren''t viewable.
*If you installed Phony but you don''t see the User Agent item on the Preferences list, try going back to the Add-ons menu, tap the Phony Add-on and then tap Disable and then tap Enable. Then, go back to the Preferences to see if you have the User Agent item. 
{/for}
{for m15}
#Tap {button Menu} > {button Settings} > {button Request Desktop Site}.
The page reloads as it would appear on your desktop.
{/for}

{for =m10}
==How do I customize my tablet browser look and feel with Personas?==
''''The Personas add-on makes it easy to customize the look of Firefox.''''
#Tap the {button Main Menu} button in the upper-right corner of the screen and select {menu Add-ons} to open the Add-ons screen.
#Tap in the Add-ons search box and type "Personas" to search for the add-on.
#Tap the Personas listing to expand it and select {button Add to Firefox}. A progress bar appears while the add-on is being downloaded and installed. When it''s done, a {button Restart} button will appear.<br>[[Image: Install Personas]]
#Tap Restart to complete the installation. 
#Once Firefox restarts, go to getpersonas.com
#Tap a Persona to try it out and then tap {button Wear this Persona} to skin your browser with the new look.[[Image:Mobile Persona]]
{/for}

==Need more help?==
Refer to the following articles for additional how-to instructions for mobile features. 
{for =m10}
{note} Note that the method for accessing items in the main menu on your tablet is different than on Firefox for mobile phones. So, you''ll use the Main Menu button instead of the Gear button to complete equivalent steps. {/note}
{/for}
*[[How do I copy and paste text on mobile?]]
*[[How do I change my language on mobile?]]
*[[How do I use bookmarks on mobile?]]
*[[Protecting stored passwords on mobile]]
*[[How do I stop websites from tracking me on mobile?]]
*[[How does Firefox for Android use the permissions it requests?]]
*[[How do I find and install Add-ons?]]
{/for}

[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/MvRNi6]]','<p>This article describes how to get started with the Firefox for Android tablet browser.
</p><div class="for" data-for="not m9" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox  version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile">mozilla.org/mobile</a>.</div>
<p></p></div><div class="for" data-for="=m14" style="display: none;"><p></p><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This applies to the latest Firefox  version which can be downloaded from <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/mobile">mozilla.org/mobile</a>.</div>
<p></p></div>
<div class="note"> <strong>Note:</strong> Tablets with screens smaller than 7" do not use the tablet browser by default. For those tablets including phablets like the Samsung Galaxy Note I, II and III, see <a href="/en-US/kb/get-started-firefox-android">Get started with Firefox for Android</a>. </div>
<div class="for" data-for="=m10,m15">
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-know-if-my-device-is-supported"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How do I know if my device is supported?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_where-are-the-tablet-navigation-controls"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Where are the tablet navigation controls?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_why-cant-i-watch-animated-or-video-flash-content-on-my-tablet"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Why can''t I watch animated or video Flash content on my tablet?</span></a></li></span></span><span class="for" data-for="m15"><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-watch-videos-on-my-tablet"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">How do I watch videos on my tablet?</span></a></li></span></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-find-my-bookmarks-and-history"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">How do I find my bookmarks and history?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-clear-the-recent-history-on-my-tablet"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">How do I clear the recent history on my tablet?</span></a></li></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-get-the-text-to-reformat-when-i-zoom"><span class="tocnumber">7</span> <span class="toctext">How do I get the text to reformat when I zoom?</span></a></li></span></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-view-the-desktop-version-of-web-pages"><span class="tocnumber">8</span> <span class="toctext">How do I view the Desktop version of web pages?</span></a><ul><span class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_troubleshooting-user-agent-setup"><span class="tocnumber">8.1</span> <span class="toctext">Troubleshooting User Agent Setup</span></a></li></span></span></ul></li></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-customize-my-tablet-browser-look-and-feel-with-personas"><span class="tocnumber">9</span> <span class="toctext">How do I customize my tablet browser look and feel with Personas?</span></a></li></span></span><span class="for" data-for="=m10,m15"><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_need-more-help"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">Need more help?</span></a></li></span></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-know-if-my-device-is-supported">How do I know if my device is supported?</h2>
<p>To install the Firefox for Android tablet browser, refer to the following articles:
</p>
<ul><li><a href="/en-US/kb/will-firefox-work-my-mobile-device">Will Firefox work on my mobile device?</a> 
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/install-firefox-android-device-using-google-play">Install Firefox on an Android device using Google Play</a>
</li></ul>
<p>The following image shows the Firefox mobile tablet interface in landscape mode.
</p><div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><p><img alt="tablet_ui" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-06-15-53-20-30334c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m15"><p><img alt="tablet_m15" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-08-22-16-07-17-04d8d6.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div><p>The following image shows the Firefox mobile tablet interface in portrait mode.
</p><div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><p><img alt="tablet_portrait" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-04-06-15-53-42-a25431.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m15"><p><img alt="tablet_portrait_small_m15" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-08-25-09-53-11-cfa605.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div>
<h2 id="w_where-are-the-tablet-navigation-controls">Where are the tablet navigation controls?</h2>
<p>The navigation and menus are across the top of the screen, from left to right, as shown in the following screenshot:
</p><div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><p><img alt="tablet controls" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-11-18-14-39-03-512027.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m15"><p><img alt="tablet_menu_m15" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-08-22-16-12-30-8c4462.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div>
<ul><li>Tabs icon - Displays the number of open tabs, tap to show tabs in the sidebar. To hide the tabs in landscape mode, swipe left across the black tab margin.
</li><li>Location bar - Tap the location bar to access your history and bookmarks. Or type an address or search term, then press Enter on the soft keyboard to go.
</li></ul>
<div class="for" data-for="m15">
<ul><li>Reload page - Tap to reload the page.
</li></ul>
</div>
<ul><li>Bookmark site - Tap the star to add a site to your bookmarks list.
</li></ul>
<div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;">
<ul><li>Main Menu - Tap to access Preferences, Add-ons, Downloads, Quit, Site Options, Save as PDF, Share Page and Find in Page, as shown in the following image.
</li></ul>
<p><img alt="main menu2" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-12-02-13-16-46-8d6ab8.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m15">
<ul><li>Main Menu - Tap to access Share, Save as PDF, Find in Page, Request Desktop Site, Clear Site Settings, Add-ons, Downloads, Settings, and Quit.
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;">
<h2 id="w_why-cant-i-watch-animated-or-video-flash-content-on-my-tablet">Why can''t I watch animated or video Flash content on my tablet?</h2>
<p>Flash is not yet supported on Firefox for Android, see
<a class="new" href="/en-US/kb/new?title=Firefox+for+Mobile+doesn%27t+support+Flash" title="Page does not exist.">Firefox for Mobile doesn''t support Flash</a>.
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="m15">
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-watch-videos-on-my-tablet">How do I watch videos on my tablet?</h2>
<p>See <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-watch-flash-videos-firefox-android">How do I watch Flash videos with Firefox for Android?</a>.
</p></div>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-find-my-bookmarks-and-history">How do I find my bookmarks and history?</h2>
<div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;">
<ol><li>Tap the Location Bar. <br>Three buttons appear for Bookmarks, History and Desktop.
</li></ol>
<ul><li>Tap the Bookmarks button to view bookmarks. Long-tap a bookmark to modify or share it.
</li><li>Tap the History button to view history. Long-tap a link to share it or open in a new tab.
</li><li>Tap the Desktop button to set up or access synced tabs. See <a href="/en-US/kb/use-sync-share-bookmarks-and-more-with-firefox-mobile">Use Sync to share your Firefox bookmarks, passwords and more with Firefox for mobile</a>
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m15">
<ol><li>Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by tapping the plus + on the Tab.
</li></ol>
<ul><li>Tap the Bookmarks tab to view your Bookmarks.
</li><li>Tap the History tab to go to the list of your recently viewed sites.
</li></ul>
</div>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-clear-the-recent-history-on-my-tablet">How do I clear the recent history on my tablet?</h2>
<div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><p><em>The Clear Mobile History add-on adds a <span class="button">Clear History</span> button to your Preferences.</em>
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Main Menu</span> button in the upper-right corner of the screen and select <span class="menu">Add-ons</span> to open the Add-ons screen.
</li><li>Tap in the Add-ons search box and type "Clear Mobile History" to search for the add-on.
</li><li>Tap the Clear Mobile History listing to expand it and select <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span>. A progress bar appears while the add-on is being downloaded and installed. When it''s done, Clear Mobile History should appear in your list of add-ons at the top of the screen.<br>
</li><li>To clear items from the All Pages and History, tap the Main Menu button in the upper-right of the screen and select Preferences. Scroll down and tap the Clear History button to remove all results from the All Pages and History screens.<br><img alt="clear history" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-12-02-13-05-46-5ec05b.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
</div><div class="for" data-for="=m15" style="display: none;">
<ol><li>Tap <span class="button">Menu</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="button">Clear private data</span>.
</li><li>Select the Browsing and download history check box.
</li><li>Tap <span class="button">Clear data</span>.
</li></ol>
<p>A notification appears confirming deletion of your data.
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;">
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-get-the-text-to-reformat-when-i-zoom">How do I get the text to reformat when I zoom?</h2>
<ol><li>To reformat text on zoom, tap the Main Menu button in the upper-right of the screen and select Preferences. Scroll down and tap the Reformat text on zoom checkbox.<br><img alt="text reformat" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-12-02-13-06-17-21c3cb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
</div>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-view-the-desktop-version-of-web-pages">How do I view the Desktop version of web pages?</h2>
<div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;"><p><em>Installing the add-on "Phony" will let you disguise Firefox for Mobile as a desktop browser so websites will serve you the desktop version of their pages.
</em>
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Main Menu</span> button in the upper-right corner of the screen and select <span class="menu">Add-ons</span> to open the Add-ons screen.
</li><li>Tap in the Add-ons search box and type "Phony" to search for the add-on.
</li><li>Tap the Phony listing to expand it and select <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span>. A progress bar appears while the add-on is being downloaded and installed. When it''s done, Phony should appear in your list of add-ons at the top of the screen.<br><img alt="phony tablet" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-12-02-12-49-48-0dcb42.jpg" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>Next, tap the <span class="menu">Preferences</span> menu item at the top left to switch to the Preferences screen.
</li><li>Finally, tab the <span class="button">Default</span> button in the <strong>User Agent</strong> row and select <span class="menu">Desktop Firefox</span> as your new user agent. Now websites appear as just as they do on your desktop!<br><img alt="Phony User Agent" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-12-02-15-51-27-c21f96.jpg" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
<h3 id="w_troubleshooting-user-agent-setup">Troubleshooting User Agent Setup</h3>
<ul><li>The menus and search bar in Firefox at the top, right, and left can appear and disappear if you swipe up, left, or right. So, try swiping to find them if they aren''t viewable.
</li><li>If you installed Phony but you don''t see the User Agent item on the Preferences list, try going back to the Add-ons menu, tap the Phony Add-on and then tap Disable and then tap Enable. Then, go back to the Preferences to see if you have the User Agent item. 
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="m15">
<ol><li>Tap <span class="button">Menu</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="button">Request Desktop Site</span>.
</li></ol>
<p>The page reloads as it would appear on your desktop.
</p></div><div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;">
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-customize-my-tablet-browser-look-and-feel-with-personas">How do I customize my tablet browser look and feel with Personas?</h2>
<p><em>The Personas add-on makes it easy to customize the look of Firefox.</em>
</p>
<ol><li>Tap the <span class="button">Main Menu</span> button in the upper-right corner of the screen and select <span class="menu">Add-ons</span> to open the Add-ons screen.
</li><li>Tap in the Add-ons search box and type "Personas" to search for the add-on.
</li><li>Tap the Personas listing to expand it and select <span class="button">Add to Firefox</span>. A progress bar appears while the add-on is being downloaded and installed. When it''s done, a <span class="button">Restart</span> button will appear.<br><img alt="Install Personas" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-12-02-16-14-02-2aa988.jpg" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li><li>Tap Restart to complete the installation. 
</li><li>Once Firefox restarts, go to <a href="http://getpersonas.com">getpersonas.com</a>
</li><li>Tap a Persona to try it out and then tap <span class="button">Wear this Persona</span> to skin your browser with the new look.<img alt="Mobile Persona" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2011-12-02-16-14-41-7fa686.jpg" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</li></ol>
</div>
<h2 id="w_need-more-help">Need more help?</h2>
<p>Refer to the following articles for additional how-to instructions for mobile features. 
</p><div class="for" data-for="=m10" style="display: none;">
<div class="note"> Note that the method for accessing items in the main menu on your tablet is different than on Firefox for mobile phones. So, you''ll use the Main Menu button instead of the Gear button to complete equivalent steps. </div>
</div>
<ul><li><a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-copy-and-paste-text-android">How do I copy and paste text on Android?</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/change-default-language-firefox-android">Change the default language of Firefox for Android</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/add-delete-and-view-bookmarked-webpages-firefox-android">Add, delete and view bookmarked webpages in Firefox for Android</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/using-master-password-firefox-android">Using Master Password on Firefox for Android</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-use-do-not-track-firefox-android">How do I use Do-not-track on Firefox for Android?</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/how-firefox-android-use-permissions-it-requests">How does Firefox for Android use the permissions it requests?</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/find-and-install-add-ons-firefox-android">Find and install extensions on Firefox for Android</a>
</li></ul>
</div><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "52004", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Dec 18, 2013, 5:31:26 AM", "datetime": "2013-12-18T05:31:26-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "small update to make it clear that 7\" tablets get the tablet user experience", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Dec 18, 2013, 5:32:14 AM", "datetime": "2013-12-18T05:32:14-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:45:40+00:00');
