[[Template:ShareArticle|link=http://mzl.la/MvRNi6]]','<p>This article describes how to get started with the Firefox for Android tablet browser.
</p>
<div class="note"> <strong>Note:</strong> Tablets with screens smaller than 7" do not use the tablet browser by default. For those tablets including phablets like the Samsung Galaxy Note I, II and III, see <a href="/en-US/kb/get-started-firefox-android">Get started with Firefox for Android</a>. </div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-know-if-my-device-is-supported"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">How do I know if my device is supported?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_where-are-the-tablet-navigation-controls"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Where are the tablet navigation controls?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-watch-videos-on-my-tablet"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">How do I watch videos on my tablet?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-find-my-bookmarks-and-history"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">How do I find my bookmarks and history?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-do-i-view-the-desktop-version-of-web-pages"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">How do I view the Desktop version of web pages?</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-know-if-my-device-is-supported">How do I know if my device is supported?</h2>
<p>To install the Firefox for Android tablet browser, refer to the following articles:
</p>
<ul><li><a href="/en-US/kb/will-firefox-work-my-mobile-device">Will Firefox work on my mobile device?</a> 
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/install-firefox-android-device-using-google-play">Install Firefox on an Android device using Google Play</a>
</li></ul>
<p>The following image shows the Firefox mobile tablet interface in landscape mode.
</p><p><img alt="tablet landscape m26" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-12-19-11-15-45-880830.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p><p>The following image shows the Firefox mobile tablet interface in portrait mode.
</p><p><img alt="tablet portrait m26" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-12-19-11-17-10-da0edd.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h2 id="w_where-are-the-tablet-navigation-controls">Where are the tablet navigation controls?</h2>
<p>The navigation and menus are across the top of the screen, from left to right, as shown in the following screenshot:
</p><p><br>
<img alt="tablet landscape menu m26" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-12-19-11-18-50-957aa3.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
}
</p>
<ul><li>Tabs icon - Displays the number of open tabs, tap to show tabs in the sidebar. To hide the tabs in landscape mode, swipe left across the black tab margin.
</li><li>Location bar - Tap the location bar to access your history and bookmarks. Or type an address or search term, then press Enter on the soft keyboard to go.
</li><li>Reload page - Tap to reload the page.
</li><li>Bookmark site - Tap the star to add a site to your bookmarks list.
</li><li>Main Menu - Tap to access Share, Save as PDF, Find in Page, Request Desktop Site, Clear Site Settings, Add-ons, Downloads, Settings, and Quit.
</li></ul>
<p><br>
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-watch-videos-on-my-tablet">How do I watch videos on my tablet?</h2>
<p>See <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-watch-flash-videos-firefox-android">How do I watch Flash videos with Firefox for Android?</a>.
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-find-my-bookmarks-and-history">How do I find my bookmarks and history?</h2>
<ol><li>Open the Awesome Screen by tapping in the Title bar at the top of any page or by tapping the plus + on the Tab.
</li></ol>
<ul><li>Tap the Bookmarks tab to view your Bookmarks.
</li><li>Tap the History tab to go to the list of your recently viewed sites.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_how-do-i-view-the-desktop-version-of-web-pages">How do I view the Desktop version of web pages?</h2>
<ol><li>Tap <span class="button">Menu</span>  and then tap <span class="button">Request Desktop Site</span>.
</li></ol>
<p>The page reloads as it would appear on your desktop.
</p><p>&nbsp;

</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "52027", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Dec 19, 2013, 3:26:45 AM", "datetime": "2013-12-19T03:26:45-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "DO NOT APPROVE! WORK IN PROGRESS - needs feedback from :verdi", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:45:37+00:00');
