</p>
<ol><li> Completely close Thunderbird, as explained above.
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Use the Thunderbird Profile Manager to create a new profile</a> in your desired location, then exit the Profile Manager. <div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> If you just installed Thunderbird on a new computer, you can use the default profile that is automatically created when you first run Thunderbird, instead of creating a new profile.</div>
</li><li>Locate the backed up profile folder on your hard drive or backup medium (e.g., your USB-stick).
</li><li>Open the profile folder backup (e.g., the <span class="filepath">xxxxxxxx.default</span> backup).
</li><li>Copy the entire <em>contents</em> of the profile folder backup, such as the <span class="filepath">mimeTypes.rdf</span> file, <span class="filepath">prefs.js</span> file, <span class="filepath">bookmarkbackups</span> folder, etc.
</li><li>Locate and open the new profile folder as explained above and then close Thunderbird (if open).
</li><li>Paste the contents of the backed up profile folder into the new profile folder, overwriting existing files of the same name.
</li><li>Start Thunderbird.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_moving-a-profile">Moving a profile</h1>
<p>Occasionally, you might want to move a profile or tell Thunderbird to use a profile stored in another location. 
</p>
<ol><li>Shut down Thunderbird.
</li><li>Move the profile folder to the desired location.<span class="for" data-for="winxp" style="display: none;"> For example, on Windows XP, move the profile from <span class="filepath">C:\Documents and Settings\[username]\Application Data\Thunderbird\Profiles\xxxxxxxx.default</span> to <span class="filepath">D:\Stuff\MyMailProfile</span></span>. (If you are reverting to a  backed up profile, this step isn''t necessary. Just note the current location of the profile you want to restore.)
</li><li>Open up the profiles.ini file in a text editor. The file is located in the application data folder for Thunderbird:
<ul><li> The path is <span class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;"><span class="filepath">%AppData%\Thunderbird\</span>&nbsp;for Windows</span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;"><span class="filepath">~/.thunderbird/</span>&nbsp;for Linux</span><span class="for" data-for="mac"><span class="filepath">~/Library/Thunderbird/</span>&nbsp;for Mac OS X</span>.
</li></ul>
</li><li>In the <span class="filepath">profiles.ini</span> file, locate the entry for the profile you''ve just moved. Change the Path= line to the new location. 
</li><li>If you switch from a relative path to a non-relative path, the direction of the slashes may need to change. For example, in Windows, non-relative paths use backslashes, whereas relative ones use forward slashes. Change IsRelative=1 to IsRelative=0.
</li><li>Save <span class="filepath">profiles.ini</span> and restart Thunderbird.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_see-also">See Also</h1>
<ul><li><a href="http://kb.mozillazine.org/Profile_Manager">Profile Manager Article</a> on MozillaZine
</li><li><a href="http://kb.mozillazine.org/Profile_backup">Profile Backup Article</a> on MozillaZine
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "82955", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 23, 2014, 2:15:54 PM", "datetime": "2014-11-23T14:15:54-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "nit: fix link to Using Multiple Profiles", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 23, 2014, 2:16:41 PM", "datetime": "2014-11-23T14:16:41-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:44:10+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (87308,'en-US','view-webpages-on-tv-roku-and-firefox-android','View webpages on your TV with Roku and Firefox for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/view-webpages-on-tv-roku-and-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/view-webpages-on-tv-roku-and-firefox-android/revision/87308',86550,'2015-01-13T13:04:16-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','my apologies to localizers! i found out today this feature is in FF36 not FF35',1,'2015-01-13T13:04:36-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2015-01-13T13:04:36-08:00','rtanglao','approved','{for not m36}[[Template:updateandroid]]{/for}

<!--L10N contributors: If you don''t have access to a Roku device, please contact jsavage@mozilla.com and ask me for localized screenshots-->

View your favorite webpages on a bigger screen with Roku and Firefox for Android. Just set up your Roku on the same WiFi network as your Android device, and follow these easy instructions:

#Launch Firefox on your Android device and open the webpage you want to mirror.
#Tap on the menu button [[Template:androidmenulocation]], select {menu Tools}, and then {menu Mirror Tab}.
#;[[Image:tab mirror chromecast]]
#On the ''''Send to Device'''' prompt, choose your Roku device.
#;[[Image:send to device roku]]
#To stop mirroring the tab, tap on the menu button and select {menu Stop Mirroring}.

{note}''''''Videos:'''''' Firefox for Android also makes it possible to view Web videos on your TV. See [[Use Firefox for Android to send videos to your Roku]] to get started.{/note}','<div class="for" data-for="not m36" style="display: none;"><div class="warning">This article applies to the latest version of Firefox for Android. Please <a href="/en-US/kb/update-latest-version-firefox-android">update your version</a> first to enjoy these features.</div></div>
<p></p><p>
</p><p>View your favorite webpages on a bigger screen with Roku and Firefox for Android. Just set up your Roku on the same WiFi network as your Android device, and follow these easy instructions:
</p>
<ol><li>Launch Firefox on your Android device and open the webpage you want to mirror.
</li><li>Tap on the menu button The template "androidmenulocation" does not exist or has no approved revision., select <span class="menu">Tools</span>, and then <span class="menu">Mirror Tab</span>.
<dl><dt><img alt="tab mirror chromecast" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-10-20-08-53-56-c75904.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li>On the <em>Send to Device</em> prompt, choose your Roku device.
<dl><dt><img alt="send to device roku" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-10-20-11-11-45-12482b.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li>To stop mirroring the tab, tap on the menu button and select <span class="menu">Stop Mirroring</span>.
</li></ol>
<div class="note"><strong>Videos:</strong> Firefox for Android also makes it possible to view Web videos on your TV. See <a href="/en-US/kb/use-firefox-android-send-videos-your-roku">Use Firefox for Android to send videos to your Roku</a> to get started.</div>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "87308", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jan 13, 2015, 1:04:16 PM", "datetime": "2015-01-13T13:04:16-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "my apologies to localizers! i found out today this feature is in FF36 not FF35", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jan 13, 2015, 1:04:36 PM", "datetime": "2015-01-13T13:04:36-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jan 13, 2015, 1:04:36 PM", "datetime": "2015-01-13T13:04:36-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:44:08+00:00');
