<h1 id="w_calendar-integration">Calendar integration</h1>
<p>Starting in Thunderbird 38, the <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/projects/calendar/">Lightning</a> calendar add-on is bundled with Thunderbird.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "95118", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 22, 2015, 7:44:27 AM", "datetime": "2015-05-22T07:44:27-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "enough content to approve, probably more user facing features to document (won''t document maildir until the ui is usable by non geeks)", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 22, 2015, 7:45:22 AM", "datetime": "2015-05-22T07:45:22-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:43:29+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (95121,'en-US','new-thunderbird-38','New in Thunderbird 38.0','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-38','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-38/revision/95121',95118,'2015-05-22T07:49:52-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','add yahoo messenger chat',1,'2015-05-22T07:50:03-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','This article describes the major changes that are visible to users in Thunderbird version 38. Full details of all the changes can be found in the Thunderbird 38 release notes.

__TOC__

=Chat supports Yahoo Messenger=
Thunderbird chat now supports [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=955574 Yahoo Messenger].
=Filtering sent/archived messages = 
You can finally filter on [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=11039 sent] and [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=479823 archived] messages.
=Search multiple address books =
You can now [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=170270 search multiple address books]!
=Expanded Folder Pane columns=
In the  folder pane (the list of folders on the left), you can now show expanded options (Unread, Total and Size) {menu View|Layout|Folder Pane Columns}.
=Google OAuth2=
[https://developers.google.com/gmail/oauth_overview The Gmail IMAP and SMTP servers have been "extended" in a non-standard way to support authorization via the industry-standard OAuth 2.0 protocol]. Thunderbird 38 supports this [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=849540 OAuth] "extension".

=Calendar integration=
Starting in Thunderbird 38, the [https://www.mozilla.org/projects/calendar/ Lightning] calendar add-on is bundled with Thunderbird.','<p>This article describes the major changes that are visible to users in Thunderbird version 38. Full details of all the changes can be found in the Thunderbird 38 release notes.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_chat-supports-yahoo-messenger"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Chat supports Yahoo Messenger</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_filtering-sentarchived-messages"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Filtering sent/archived messages</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_search-multiple-address-books"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Search multiple address books</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_expanded-folder-pane-columns"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Expanded Folder Pane columns</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_google-oauth2"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Google OAuth2</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_calendar-integration"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">Calendar integration</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_chat-supports-yahoo-messenger">Chat supports Yahoo Messenger</h1>
<p>Thunderbird chat now supports <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=955574">Yahoo Messenger</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_filtering-sentarchived-messages">Filtering sent/archived messages</h1>
<p>You can finally filter on <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=11039">sent</a> and <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=479823">archived</a> messages.
</p>
<h1 id="w_search-multiple-address-books">Search multiple address books</h1>
<p>You can now <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=170270">search multiple address books</a>!
</p>
<h1 id="w_expanded-folder-pane-columns">Expanded Folder Pane columns</h1>
<p>In the  folder pane (the list of folders on the left), you can now show expanded options (Unread, Total and Size) <span class="menu">View|Layout|Folder Pane Columns</span>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_google-oauth2">Google OAuth2</h1>
<p><a href="https://developers.google.com/gmail/oauth_overview">The Gmail IMAP and SMTP servers have been "extended" in a non-standard way to support authorization via the industry-standard OAuth 2.0 protocol</a>. Thunderbird 38 supports this <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=849540">OAuth</a> "extension".
</p>
<h1 id="w_calendar-integration">Calendar integration</h1>
<p>Starting in Thunderbird 38, the <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/projects/calendar/">Lightning</a> calendar add-on is bundled with Thunderbird.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "95121", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 22, 2015, 7:49:52 AM", "datetime": "2015-05-22T07:49:52-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add yahoo messenger chat", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 22, 2015, 7:50:03 AM", "datetime": "2015-05-22T07:50:03-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:43:27+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (96954,'en-US','maildir-thunderbird','Maildir in Thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/maildir-thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/maildir-thunderbird/revision/96954',NULL,'2015-06-12T09:24:23-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP do not approve, a better stub',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','Thunderbird has had hidden support (Maildir is disabled by default) for the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maildir Maildir] mail storage format for several years but Maildir is still not 100% ready for users. This article explains the format change. 

{warning}WARNING:Unless you are advanced and know how to backup your email before turning on Maildir and how to restore it if you run into problems, we suggest you leave Maildir disabled.{/warning}

Maildir is a single file per email ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Email#Filename_extensions EML]) unlike the current default monolithic single file format  which is one file per folder (known a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mbox mbox]). This storage format has significant benefits:
* Backups are easier because amount of data needed to be backed up is reduced to just those emails that have changed since the last backup.
* It is easier for anti-virus to scan emails in individual files and infected mails can be removed without the loss of all the other mail in the folder as often occurs today with anti-virus software which cannot handle multiple emails in one file.

This is a major change for Thunderbird because it changes the mail storage mechanism. The development team have spent a significant amount of time developing maildir
<!--
but one last software change is still missing and that an option in the user interface to enable maildir globally
-->. However due to a lack of time, and testers, before Thunderbird 38 was released the actual underlying changes have not had the extensive manual testing that would normally occur for such a major change.

While you are encouraged to try the format and report [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/ bugs]. 
= How to turn on Maildir =
{warning}WARNING: Again this feature is experimental and we recommend that you know how to backup and restore your email before turning on Maildir.{/warning}
Turn on mail dir as follows:
# Backup your email.
#','<p>Thunderbird has had hidden support (Maildir is disabled by default) for the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maildir">Maildir</a> mail storage format for several years but Maildir is still not 100% ready for users. This article explains the format change. 
