</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "96961", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 9:55:43 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T09:55:43-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "oops missed some typos!", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 9:55:57 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T09:55:57-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 9:56:28 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T09:56:28-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:43:08+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (96962,'en-US','launch-android-app-using-firefox','Launch an Android app using Firefox','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/launch-android-app-using-firefox','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/launch-android-app-using-firefox/revision/96962',NULL,'2015-06-12T09:58:26-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','typo - remove repetition of title',1,'2015-06-12T09:58:50-07:00','rtanglao',1,1,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','If an app is available for a web page you''re on (for example, YouTube.<!--removing link-->com or maps.google.<!--removing active url-->com), Firefox gives you the option to open that app for a better experience.

#If an Android app is available for the content you''re viewing, the Android icon will appear in the address bar:
#;[[Image:app url android]]
#Tap on the Android icon to launch the app.','<p>If an app is available for a web page you''re on (for example, YouTube.com or maps.google.com), Firefox gives you the option to open that app for a better experience.
</p>
<ol><li>If an Android app is available for the content you''re viewing, the Android icon will appear in the address bar:
<dl><dt><img alt="app url android" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2015-05-14-18-38-12-ba9bf0.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li>Tap on the Android icon to launch the app.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "96962", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 9:58:26 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T09:58:26-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "typo - remove repetition of title", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 9:58:50 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T09:58:50-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:43:05+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (96963,'en-US','maildir-thunderbird','Maildir in Thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/maildir-thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/maildir-thunderbird/revision/96963',96961,'2015-06-12T10:11:40-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','add that it''s only availalbe in tb38 and above',1,'2015-06-12T10:11:57-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2015-06-12T10:11:57-07:00','rtanglao','approved','Thunderbird has had hidden support (Maildir is disabled by default) for the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maildir Maildir] mail storage format for several years but Maildir is still not 100% ready for users. This article explains the format change and how to test Maildir starting in Thunderbird 38 (Maildir is not ready for testing prior to version 38). 

{warning}WARNING:Unless you are advanced and know how to backup your email before turning on Maildir and how to restore it if you run into problems, we suggest you leave Maildir disabled.{/warning}

Maildir is a single file per email ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Email#Filename_extensions EML]) unlike the current default monolithic single file format  which is one file per folder (known a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mbox mbox]). This storage format has significant benefits:
* Backups are easier because amount of data needed to be backed up is reduced to just those emails that have changed since the last backup.
* It is easier for anti-virus to scan emails in individual files and infected mails can be removed without the loss of all the other mail in the folder as often occurs today with anti-virus software which cannot handle multiple emails in one file.

This is a major change for Thunderbird because it changes the mail storage mechanism. The development team have spent a significant amount of time developing maildir
<!--
but one last software change is still missing and that an option in the user interface to enable maildir globally
-->. 

However due to a lack of time, and testers, before Thunderbird 38 was released the actual underlying changes have not had the extensive manual testing that would normally occur for such a major change.

= How to turn on Maildir =
{warning}WARNING: Again, this feature is experimental and we recommend that you know how to file bugs and how to backup and restore your email before turning on Maildir.{/warning}
Here''s how to turn on Maildir:
# Backup your email. ''''''If you don''t know how to backup your email, then you are not qualified to test Maildir.''''''
# Click the Application menu button [[Image:New Fx Menu]].
# Click {menu Preferences} and then {for win,linux}{menu Options}{/for}{for mac}{menu Preferences}{/for}.
# Click {menu Advanced} and then click {menu General}.
# Next to "Message Store Type for new accounts", select {button File per message, (maildir)}.
# Any email account created from now on will use Maildir (existing accounts will continue to use mbox). Please [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird file a bug] if you encounter any Maildir issues.','<p>Thunderbird has had hidden support (Maildir is disabled by default) for the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maildir">Maildir</a> mail storage format for several years but Maildir is still not 100% ready for users. This article explains the format change and how to test Maildir starting in Thunderbird 38 (Maildir is not ready for testing prior to version 38). 
</p>
<div class="warning">WARNING:Unless you are advanced and know how to backup your email before turning on Maildir and how to restore it if you run into problems, we suggest you leave Maildir disabled.</div>
<p>Maildir is a single file per email (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Email#Filename_extensions">EML</a>) unlike the current default monolithic single file format  which is one file per folder (known a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mbox">mbox</a>). This storage format has significant benefits:
</p>
<ul><li> Backups are easier because amount of data needed to be backed up is reduced to just those emails that have changed since the last backup.
</li><li> It is easier for anti-virus to scan emails in individual files and infected mails can be removed without the loss of all the other mail in the folder as often occurs today with anti-virus software which cannot handle multiple emails in one file.
</li></ul>
<p>This is a major change for Thunderbird because it changes the mail storage mechanism. The development team have spent a significant amount of time developing maildir
. 
</p><p>However due to a lack of time, and testers, before Thunderbird 38 was released the actual underlying changes have not had the extensive manual testing that would normally occur for such a major change.
</p>
<h1 id="w_how-to-turn-on-maildir">How to turn on Maildir</h1>
<div class="warning">WARNING: Again, this feature is experimental and we recommend that you know how to file bugs and how to backup and restore your email before turning on Maildir.</div>
<p>Here''s how to turn on Maildir:
</p>
<ol><li> Backup your email. <strong>If you don''t know how to backup your email, then you are not qualified to test Maildir.</strong>
</li><li> Click the Application menu button <img alt="New Fx Menu" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-01-10-13-08-08-f52b8c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">.
</li><li> Click <span class="menu">Preferences</span> and then <span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;"><span class="menu">Options</span></span><span class="for" data-for="mac"><span class="menu">Preferences</span></span>.
</li><li> Click <span class="menu">Advanced</span> and then click <span class="menu">General</span>.
</li><li> Next to "Message Store Type for new accounts", select <span class="button">File per message, (maildir)</span>.
</li><li> Any email account created from now on will use Maildir (existing accounts will continue to use mbox). Please <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird">file a bug</a> if you encounter any Maildir issues.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "96963", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 10:11:40 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T10:11:40-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add that it''s only availalbe in tb38 and above", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 10:11:57 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T10:11:57-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jun 12, 2015, 10:11:57 AM", "datetime": "2015-06-12T10:11:57-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:43:03+00:00');
