</p>
<ol><li> Tap the menu button at the bottom of the screen. (You might need to <a href="/en-US/kb/navigation-bar-firefox-ios">scroll all the way to the top of the page</a> for the menu button to appear).
</li><li>Tap the <strong>Scan QR Code</strong> icon in the menu panel at the bottom of the screen. (You might need to swipe to the next panel first.)
</li></ol>
<div class="note"><strong>Don''t see a menu button?</strong> You might be on an older version of Firefox. Please update to the latest version through the App Store.<br></div>
<p>Firefox for iOS will automatically open the iOS camera for scanning QR codes.
</p><p>After scanning, if the QR code is a web address the page will be opened.
</p><p>If words instead of a web address show up after scanning, Firefox for iOS will search for those words using your default search engine.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "141390", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jul 14, 2017, 8:01:59 AM", "datetime": "2017-07-14T08:01:59-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP: PLEASE DON''T set RFL until Joni has taken a look", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jul 14, 2017, 8:02:32 AM", "datetime": "2017-07-14T08:02:32-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:40:54+00:00');
