Firefox for iOS has a QR code reader to allow a user to load a webpage or search for words from a QR code. This article will show you how to scan a QR code.

#[[Template:iosmenu]](You might need to [[Navigation bar in Firefox for iOS|scroll all the way to the top of the page]] for the menu button to appear).
#Tap the ''''''Scan QR Code'''''' icon in the menu panel at the bottom of the screen. (You might need to swipe to the next panel first.)
;[[Image:ffios8-scan-qr-code]] 
{note}''''''Don''t see a menu button?'''''' You might be on an older version of Firefox. Please update to the latest version through the App Store.<br>{/note}

Firefox for iOS will automatically open the iOS camera for scanning QR codes.
Please position your QR code so that it is aligned within the frame outlined by the four blue guidelines. Firefox will automatically scan the QR code once it detects proper alignment.
[[Image:ffios-ios-camera-qr-code-scanner]]

* After scanning, if the QR code is a web address the page will be opened.
* If words instead of a web address show up after scanning, Firefox for iOS will search for those words using your default search engine.','<p></p><div class="note">These features are available on Firefox version 8.0 or later. See <a href="/en-US/kb/what-version-firefox-do-i-have-ios">Which version of Firefox am I using?</a> to find your version number.</div>
<p></p><p>Firefox for iOS has a QR code reader to allow a user to load a webpage or search for words from a QR code. This article will show you how to scan a QR code.
</p>
<ol><li><p>At the bottom of the screen, tap the menu button (the menu will be at the top right if you''re using an iPad): 
</p>
<dl><dt><img alt="firefoxiosnewmenu" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-04-01-07-47-28-9ccefb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="400">
</dt></dl>(You might need to <a href="/en-US/kb/navigation-bar-firefox-ios">scroll all the way to the top of the page</a> for the menu button to appear).
</li><li>Tap the <strong>Scan QR Code</strong> icon in the menu panel at the bottom of the screen. (You might need to swipe to the next panel first.)
</li></ol>
<dl><dt><img alt="ffios8-scan-qr-code" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2017-07-16-21-59-43-113b25.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
<div class="note"><strong>Don''t see a menu button?</strong> You might be on an older version of Firefox. Please update to the latest version through the App Store.<br></div>
<p>Firefox for iOS will automatically open the iOS camera for scanning QR codes.
Please position your QR code so that it is aligned within the frame outlined by the four blue guidelines. Firefox will automatically scan the QR code once it detects proper alignment.
<img alt="ffios-ios-camera-qr-code-scanner" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2017-07-16-22-12-05-448916.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<ul><li> After scanning, if the QR code is a web address the page will be opened.
</li><li> If words instead of a web address show up after scanning, Firefox for iOS will search for those words using your default search engine.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "141489", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jul 17, 2017, 10:33:24 AM", "datetime": "2017-07-17T10:33:24-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add [[Template:iosmenu]]", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jul 17, 2017, 10:34:23 AM", "datetime": "2017-07-17T10:34:23-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:40:27+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (141490,'en-US','night-mode-firefox-ios','Website Dark Mode in Firefox for iOS','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/night-mode-firefox-ios','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/night-mode-firefox-ios/revision/141490',141457,'2017-07-17T10:35:36-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','add [[Template:iosmenu]]',1,'2017-07-17T10:35:46-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2017-07-17T19:17:39-07:00','heyjoni','approved','[[Template:ios8.0]]

Firefox for iOS has a night mode to reduce webpage brightness while browsing. Perfect for those late night surfing sessions!

#[[Template:iosmenu]](You might need to [[Navigation bar in Firefox for iOS|scroll all the way to the top of the page]] for the menu button to appear).
#Tap the ''''''Night Mode'''''' icon to reduce the brightness. (You might need to swipe to the next panel first.)
To set Firefox for iOS back to normal brightness, repeat the above two steps.
;[[Image:ffios8-night-mode]] 
{note}''''''Don''t see a menu button?'''''' You might be on an older version of Firefox. Please update to the latest version through the App Store.<br>{/note}','<p></p><div class="note">These features are available on Firefox version 8.0 or later. See <a href="/en-US/kb/what-version-firefox-do-i-have-ios">Which version of Firefox am I using?</a> to find your version number.</div>
<p></p><p>Firefox for iOS has a night mode to reduce webpage brightness while browsing. Perfect for those late night surfing sessions!
</p>
<ol><li><p>At the bottom of the screen, tap the menu button (the menu will be at the top right if you''re using an iPad): 
</p>
<dl><dt><img alt="firefoxiosnewmenu" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-04-01-07-47-28-9ccefb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="400">
</dt></dl>(You might need to <a href="/en-US/kb/navigation-bar-firefox-ios">scroll all the way to the top of the page</a> for the menu button to appear).
</li><li>Tap the <strong>Night Mode</strong> icon to reduce the brightness. (You might need to swipe to the next panel first.)
</li></ol>
<p>To set Firefox for iOS back to normal brightness, repeat the above two steps.
</p>
<dl><dt><img alt="ffios8-night-mode" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2017-07-16-23-03-29-91ab40.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
<div class="note"><strong>Don''t see a menu button?</strong> You might be on an older version of Firefox. Please update to the latest version through the App Store.<br></div>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "141490", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jul 17, 2017, 10:35:36 AM", "datetime": "2017-07-17T10:35:36-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add [[Template:iosmenu]]", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jul 17, 2017, 10:35:46 AM", "datetime": "2017-07-17T10:35:46-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jul 17, 2017, 7:17:39 PM", "datetime": "2017-07-17T19:17:39-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "heyjoni", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:40:24+00:00');
