[[Template:androidversion]]
Here''s how to do it for your version of Android:

=Android version 7 and Android version 8=

#Tap the menu button at the top right corner
#;[[Image:focus menu android]]
#Tap {menu Settings}.
#Tap the switch next to ''''Make default browser'''' to turn it on (blue means on).
#This will open up the ''''Default apps'''' screen.
#Tap {menu Browser app}.
#Tap ''''''Firefox Focus'''''' to select it.

=Android version 6=
#In the Settings menu on your phone, tap ''''''Apps & notifications'''''' (it may be called ''''''Apps'''''' on some versions of Android).
#Tap {menu Advanced} (you may have to tap on the {button Gear} icon first on some versions of Android).
#Tap {menu Default apps}.
#Tap {menu Browser app} to open a list of choices.
#Tap ''''''Firefox Focus'''''' to select it.

=Android version 5 and older=

==Step 1: Clear the current browser that opens links==
# Open the Settings application and tap on {button Apps}. (On some versions of Android this button is labelled ''''''Applications'''''' or ''''''Application manager'''''' and you may have to tap on {button Manage applications} before the next step.)
# Tap on the {button All} tab.
#;[[Image:Android ICS Manage Apps - Cropped just showing stock]]
# Tap on the current browser that opens links. This is usually the default browser which is called "Browser" or "Internet".
# Tap on {button Clear defaults} to prevent this browser from opening links by default. If "Clear defaults" is greyed out, then either you have not installed another browser or you have installed another browser like Opera and it is set to be the default browser. If you have installed another browser, go back to the previous step and repeat with the default browser.
#;[[Image:Android ICS Clear defaults - Cropped]]

==Step 2: Set Firefox Focus to be the default browser for opening links==
# Open a link in an Android application like the Mail application.
# Tap on {button Firefox Focus} and then tap on {button Always}.','<p>Set Firefox Focus as your default browser if you want it to open links by default. The instructions vary depending on your version of Android:
</p><p>
</p>
<div class="note">To find your version of Android, open the Settings app, tap <strong>About phone</strong>, <strong>About tablet</strong> or <strong>About device</strong> (you may have to tap on the <strong>More</strong> tab on some versions of Android) and if your Android version is not shown, tap <strong>Android version</strong> (or <strong>Software information</strong> on some versions of Android).</div>
Here''s how to do it for your version of Android:
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_android-version-7-and-android-version-8">Android version 7 and Android version 8</h1>
<ol><li>Tap the menu button at the top right corner
<dl><dt><img alt="focus menu android" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2017-05-18-06-44-43-c75311.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Settings</span>.
</li><li>Tap the switch next to <em>Make default browser</em> to turn it on (blue means on).
</li><li>This will open up the <em>Default apps</em> screen.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Browser app</span>.
</li><li>Tap <strong>Firefox Focus</strong> to select it.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_android-version-6">Android version 6</h1>
<ol><li>In the Settings menu on your phone, tap <strong>Apps &amp; notifications</strong> (it may be called <strong>Apps</strong> on some versions of Android).
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Advanced</span> (you may have to tap on the <span class="button">Gear</span> icon first on some versions of Android).
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Default apps</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Browser app</span> to open a list of choices.
</li><li>Tap <strong>Firefox Focus</strong> to select it.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_android-version-5-and-older">Android version 5 and older</h1>
<h2 id="w_step-1-clear-the-current-browser-that-opens-links">Step 1: Clear the current browser that opens links</h2>
<ol><li> Open the Settings application and tap on <span class="button">Apps</span>. (On some versions of Android this button is labelled <strong>Applications</strong> or <strong>Application manager</strong> and you may have to tap on <span class="button">Manage applications</span> before the next step.)
</li><li> Tap on the <span class="button">All</span> tab.
<dl><dt><img alt="Android ICS Manage Apps - Cropped just showing stock" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-12-11-59-02-8caa08.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Tap on the current browser that opens links. This is usually the default browser which is called "Browser" or "Internet".
</li><li> Tap on <span class="button">Clear defaults</span> to prevent this browser from opening links by default. If "Clear defaults" is greyed out, then either you have not installed another browser or you have installed another browser like Opera and it is set to be the default browser. If you have installed another browser, go back to the previous step and repeat with the default browser.
<dl><dt><img alt="Android ICS Clear defaults - Cropped" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2013-02-03-22-30-33-ca626d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_step-2-set-firefox-focus-to-be-the-default-browser-for-opening-links">Step 2: Set Firefox Focus to be the default browser for opening links</h2>
<ol><li> Open a link in an Android application like the Mail application.
</li><li> Tap on <span class="button">Firefox Focus</span> and then tap on <span class="button">Always</span>.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "149063", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 25, 2017, 4:01:54 AM", "datetime": "2017-10-25T04:01:54-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Application manager on Samsung S2 4.1.2", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Oct 25, 2017, 4:02:15 AM", "datetime": "2017-10-25T04:02:15-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Oct 25, 2017, 4:02:15 AM", "datetime": "2017-10-25T04:02:15-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:40:04+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (149099,'en-US','templateandroidversion','Template:androidversion','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/templateandroidversion','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/templateandroidversion/revision/149099',149061,'2017-10-25T07:27:09-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','s3 Android 4.4.2 tap on ''More'' tab',1,'2017-10-25T07:27:27-07:00','rtanglao',1,1,1,'2017-10-25T07:27:27-07:00','rtanglao','approved','<!--
Samsung Note 8, Android 7.1.1 Settings->About phone->Software information
Samsung S3, Android 4.4.2 Settings->tap on ''More'' tab->About device
Samsung SII, Android 4.1.2 Settings->About device
-->
{note}To find your version of Android, open the Settings app, tap ''''''About phone'''''', ''''''About tablet'''''' or ''''''About device'''''' (you may have to tap on the ''''''More'''''' tab on some versions of Android) and if your Android version is not shown, tap ''''''Android version'''''' (or ''''''Software information'''''' on some versions of Android).{/note}','<p>
</p>
<div class="note">To find your version of Android, open the Settings app, tap <strong>About phone</strong>, <strong>About tablet</strong> or <strong>About device</strong> (you may have to tap on the <strong>More</strong> tab on some versions of Android) and if your Android version is not shown, tap <strong>Android version</strong> (or <strong>Software information</strong> on some versions of Android).</div>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "149099", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 25, 2017, 7:27:09 AM", "datetime": "2017-10-25T07:27:09-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "s3 Android 4.4.2 tap on ''More'' tab", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Oct 25, 2017, 7:27:27 AM", "datetime": "2017-10-25T07:27:27-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Oct 25, 2017, 7:27:27 AM", "datetime": "2017-10-25T07:27:27-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:40:02+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (152466,'en-US','forum-response-tabs-below-url-bar','Forum Response - Tabs below the URL bar','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/forum-response-tabs-below-url-bar','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/forum-response-tabs-below-url-bar/revision/152466',NULL,'2017-11-15T13:47:16-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','added warning that it doesn''t work on OSX , moved disclaimer note to the top',1,'2017-11-16T00:17:24-08:00','heyjoni',1,0,1,'2017-11-16T00:17:29-08:00','heyjoni','approved','Firefox''s style or appearance can be modified by creating a custom style rule to override the default styles in Firefox. 

{note}Custom style rules might not work every time because of other factors (e.g. compatibility with other custom style rules) beyond the Mozilla community''s control. Your custom style rule might also stop working each time a new Firefox release comes out.{/note}

{warning}The following  "moving tabs below the url bar" procedure only works on Linux and Windows. ''''''It does not work on Mac OS X.''''''{/warning}
Here''s how to do it:

#Create a userChrome.css file (following the steps below or see our [https://vimeo.com/242513527 community member''s video (starts at 8:45)]. The rules you put in this file will override the default styles in Firefox.
#*Open your currently active profile folder: Type in ''''''about:profiles'''''' in the address bar, then click ''''''Open Folder'''''' (Windows) or ''''''Show in Finder'''''' (Mac).
#*Create a new folder named ''''''chrome''''''.
#*Create a desktop shortcut to the ''''chrome'''' folder for easier future access.
#*Make sure Windows is set to show you file extensions like .txt and .css
#*Create a new text file inside the chrome folder named userChrome.css
#Paste the CSS rules found in the third example [https://www.userchrome.org/what-is-userchrome-css.html here] into the userChrome.css file and save your changes.
#Reopen Firefox.
(''''''Tip:'''''' Turn on your title bar or menu bar after you''ve made these changes.)','<p>Firefox''s style or appearance can be modified by creating a custom style rule to override the default styles in Firefox. 
</p>
<div class="note">Custom style rules might not work every time because of other factors (e.g. compatibility with other custom style rules) beyond the Mozilla community''s control. Your custom style rule might also stop working each time a new Firefox release comes out.</div>
<div class="warning">The following  "moving tabs below the url bar" procedure only works on Linux and Windows. <strong>It does not work on Mac OS X.</strong></div>
<p>Here''s how to do it:
</p>
<ol><li>Create a userChrome.css file (following the steps below or see our <a href="https://vimeo.com/242513527">community member''s video (starts at 8:45)</a>. The rules you put in this file will override the default styles in Firefox.
<ul><li>Open your currently active profile folder: Type in <strong>about:profiles</strong> in the address bar, then click <strong>Open Folder</strong> (Windows) or <strong>Show in Finder</strong> (Mac).
</li><li>Create a new folder named <strong>chrome</strong>.
</li><li>Create a desktop shortcut to the <em>chrome</em> folder for easier future access.
</li><li>Make sure Windows is set to show you file extensions like .txt and .css
</li><li>Create a new text file inside the chrome folder named userChrome.css
</li></ul>
</li><li>Paste the CSS rules found in the third example <a href="https://www.userchrome.org/what-is-userchrome-css.html">here</a> into the userChrome.css file and save your changes.
</li><li>Reopen Firefox.
</li></ol>
<p>(<strong>Tip:</strong> Turn on your title bar or menu bar after you''ve made these changes.)
