</li></ul>
</div></span><span class="for" data-for="=fx57" style="display: none;"><div class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;">
<ul><li><a href="https://download-installer.cdn.mozilla.net/pub/firefox/releases/56.0.2/win32/en-US/Firefox%20Setup%2056.0.2.exe">Firefox 56.0.2</a> <strong>32-bit</strong> (US English)
</li><li><a href="https://download-installer.cdn.mozilla.net/pub/firefox/releases/56.0.2/win64/en-US/Firefox%20Setup%2056.0.2.exe">Firefox 56.0.2</a> <strong>64-bit</strong> (US English)
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="mac">
<ul><li><a href="https://download-installer.cdn.mozilla.net/pub/firefox/releases/56.0.2/mac/en-US/Firefox%2056.0.2.dmg">Firefox 56.0.2</a> (US English)
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;">
<ul><li><a href="https://download-installer.cdn.mozilla.net/pub/firefox/releases/56.0.2/linux-i686/en-US/firefox-56.0.2.tar.bz2">Firefox 56.0.2</a> (US English)
</li></ul>
</div></span>
<ul><li><a href="https://ftp.mozilla.org/pub/mozilla.org/firefox/releases/">Directory of other versions and languages</a>
</li></ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Important</strong>: By default, Firefox is set for automatic updates. To prevent Firefox from automatically updating itself after you install an older version, you''ll need to change your Firefox update settings: <span class="for" data-for="mac">In the Menu bar at the top of the screen, click <span class="menu">Firefox</span> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span> (or <span class="menu">Preferences</span>, in some cases).</span><span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Click the menu button <img alt="Fx89menuButton" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-05-15-11-18-38-e5b736.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span>.</span>
 <span class="for" data-for="fx56">In the <span class="menu">General</span> panel, go to the <em>Firefox Updates</em> section. <span class="for" data-for="=fx56" style="display: none;"> (In <a href="/en-US/kb/find-what-version-firefox-you-are-using">Firefox version</a> 55 and below, you would go to the <span class="menu"><a href="/en-US/kb/advanced-panel-settings-in-firefox">Advanced</a></span> panel and choose the <span class="menu">Update</span> tab.)</span></span><span class="for" data-for="not fx56" style="display: none;">Go to the <span class="menu">Advanced</span> panel and choose the <span class="menu">Update</span> tab (see <a href="/en-US/kb/advanced-panel-settings-in-firefox#w_update-tab">this article</a> for details).</span></div>
<h1 id="w_downgrade-alternatives">Downgrade alternatives</h1>
<p>Instead of downgrading to an older, insecure version of Firefox and changing your update settings, you should consider these alternatives:
</p><p><strong>Install Firefox Extended Support Release.</strong> <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/firefox/organizations/">Firefox Extended Support Release (ESR)</a> is an official version of Firefox developed for large organizations like universities and businesses. Firefox ESR does not come with the latest features but it has the latest security and stability fixes. For more information, see the article <a href="/en-US/kb/switch-to-firefox-extended-support-release-esr">Switch to Firefox Extended Support Release (ESR) for personal use</a>.
</p><p><strong>Use the latest version of another browser:</strong>  
</p><div class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;"><div class="for" data-for="win10" style="display: none;">
<ul><li><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=48126">Microsoft Edge</a>
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="not win10">
<ul><li><a href="http://windows.microsoft.com/en-us/internet-explorer/download-ie">Internet Explorer</a>
</li></ul>
</div>
<ul><li><a href="https://www.google.com/chrome">Google Chrome</a>
</li><li><a href="http://www.opera.com/">Opera</a>
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="mac">
<ul><li><a href="http://www.apple.com/safari/">Safari</a>
</li><li><a href="https://www.google.com/chrome">Google Chrome</a>
</li><li><a href="http://www.opera.com/">Opera</a>
</li></ul>
</div><div class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;">
<ul><li><a href="https://www.google.com/chrome">Google Chrome</a>
</li><li><a href="http://www.opera.com/">Opera</a>
</li></ul>
</div>
<h1 id="w_help-us-make-firefox-better">Help us make Firefox better</h1>
<p>If the <a href="http://www.mozilla.org/firefox/all.html">latest version of Firefox</a> is causing problems for you or you just don''t like something about it, please give us feedback about it here:
</p>
<ul><li><span class="button"><a href="http://input.mozilla.org/feedback/">Submit your feedback and suggestions about Firefox</a></span>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "155968", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jan 19, 2018, 8:00:15 AM", "datetime": "2018-01-19T08:00:15-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "no need to mention test versions of nightly or bet as per Alice", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jan 19, 2018, 8:00:39 AM", "datetime": "2018-01-19T08:00:39-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jan 19, 2018, 8:00:39 AM", "datetime": "2018-01-19T08:00:39-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:39:49+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (157553,'en-US','install-firefox-your-phone-or-tablet','Install Firefox on your phone or tablet','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/install-firefox-your-phone-or-tablet','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/install-firefox-your-phone-or-tablet/revision/157553',99120,'2018-03-04T14:23:28-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','implemented Alice''s suggestions :-) thanksAlice',1,'2018-03-04T14:24:02-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2018-03-04T14:24:02-08:00','rtanglao','approved','Firefox brings your favorite features and security to your Android <!--and iOS - save this for later--> devices. Learn how to install it on your phone or tablet so you can browse the Web quickly and privately.

=Install through your phone''s marketplace=
Install Firefox through your phone''s official marketplace to ensure that you get the best version of Firefox for your device. Most marketplaces will also automatically keep Firefox up to date.

*[[Install Firefox on an Android device using Google Play | Google Play]]
*[https://www.tstore.co.kr/userpoc/main T store]
*[https://m.store.yandex.com/ Yandex]

<!--Localizers, if you have support articles for your specific marketplace, please link them here.-->
<!--*iOS *Partner 11 - waiting until official --> 

{note}''''''Tip:'''''' Use [[How do I set up Firefox Sync?| Sync]] to share your bookmarks, passwords and site preferences on all your devices.{/note}

=Install from Mozilla''s download server=
Visit Mozilla''s [https://download.mozilla.org/?product=fennec-latest&os=android&lang=multi server] and download the latest version of Firefox in your language. 

{warning}Firefox will need to be updated manually if you install it using this method. See [[Update to the latest version of Firefox for Android]].{/warning}','<p>Firefox brings your favorite features and security to your Android  devices. Learn how to install it on your phone or tablet so you can browse the Web quickly and privately.
</p>
<h1 id="w_install-through-your-phones-marketplace">Install through your phone''s marketplace</h1>
<p>Install Firefox through your phone''s official marketplace to ensure that you get the best version of Firefox for your device. Most marketplaces will also automatically keep Firefox up to date.
</p>
<ul><li><a href="/en-US/kb/install-firefox-android-device-using-google-play"> Google Play</a>
</li><li><a href="https://www.tstore.co.kr/userpoc/main">T store</a>
</li><li><a href="https://m.store.yandex.com/">Yandex</a>
</li></ul>
<p>
 
</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Tip:</strong> Use <a href="/en-US/kb/how-do-i-set-sync-my-computer"> Sync</a> to share your bookmarks, passwords and site preferences on all your devices.</div>
<h1 id="w_install-from-mozillas-download-server">Install from Mozilla''s download server</h1>
<p>Visit Mozilla''s <a href="https://download.mozilla.org/?product=fennec-latest&amp;os=android&amp;lang=multi">server</a> and download the latest version of Firefox in your language. 
</p>
<div class="warning">Firefox will need to be updated manually if you install it using this method. See <a href="/en-US/kb/update-latest-version-firefox-android">Update to the latest version of Firefox for Android</a>.</div>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "157553", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Mar 4, 2018, 2:23:28 PM", "datetime": "2018-03-04T14:23:28-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "implemented Alice''s suggestions :-) thanksAlice", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Mar 4, 2018, 2:24:02 PM", "datetime": "2018-03-04T14:24:02-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Mar 4, 2018, 2:24:02 PM", "datetime": "2018-03-04T14:24:02-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:39:46+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (158506,'en-US','how-replace-google-assistant-firefox-search','How to replace Google Assistant with a Firefox search','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-replace-google-assistant-firefox-search','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/how-replace-google-assistant-firefox-search/revision/158506',158442,'2018-03-21T06:38:20-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','only works with Android 6 and newer',1,'2018-03-21T06:38:43-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','{for not m59}[[Template:updateandroid]]{/for}

Follow these steps to set up Firefox to work with Android Assist, so that a Firefox search replaces Google Assistant when you long-press the home button. This feature only works with Android 6 Marshmallow and newer. 

=On Pixel XL and Android 8.1=
#Open the Settings app on your phone.
#Tap {menu Apps & Notifications}.
#Tap {menu Advanced}.
#Tap {menu Default Apps}.
#Tap {menu Assist & voice input}.
#Tap {menu Firefox}.

You can now long-tap the home button to search with Firefox.

=On Note 8 and Android 7.1.1=
#Open the Settings app on your phone.
#Tap the menu on the top right.
#Tap {menu Default Apps}.
#Tap {menu Device assistance app}.
#Tap {menu Firefox}.

You can now long-tap the home button to search with Firefox.','<div class="for" data-for="not m59" style="display: none;"><div class="warning">This article applies to the latest version of Firefox for Android. Please <a href="/en-US/kb/update-latest-version-firefox-android">update your version</a> first to enjoy these features.</div></div>
<p></p><p>Follow these steps to set up Firefox to work with Android Assist, so that a Firefox search replaces Google Assistant when you long-press the home button. This feature only works with Android 6 Marshmallow and newer. 
</p>
<h1 id="w_on-pixel-xl-and-android-8-1">On Pixel XL and Android 8.1</h1>
<ol><li>Open the Settings app on your phone.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Apps &amp; Notifications</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Advanced</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Default Apps</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Assist &amp; voice input</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Firefox</span>.
</li></ol>
<p>You can now long-tap the home button to search with Firefox.
</p>
<h1 id="w_on-note-8-and-android-7-1-1">On Note 8 and Android 7.1.1</h1>
<ol><li>Open the Settings app on your phone.
</li><li>Tap the menu on the top right.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Default Apps</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Device assistance app</span>.
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Firefox</span>.
</li></ol>
<p>You can now long-tap the home button to search with Firefox.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "158506", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Mar 21, 2018, 6:38:20 AM", "datetime": "2018-03-21T06:38:20-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "only works with Android 6 and newer", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Mar 21, 2018, 6:38:43 AM", "datetime": "2018-03-21T06:38:43-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:39:44+00:00');
