<ul><li>For a list of <a href="/groups/forum-helpers">Support Forum helpers, click here</a>. Contributors to the Support Forum in the last 90 days <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/community/top-contributors/questions/">are listed here</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li>For a list of <a href="/groups/forum-moderators">Support Forum moderators, click here</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li>For a list of <a href="/groups/accessibility">people involved in Accessibility, click here</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>SUMO Localizers are members of the community who make SUMO available in many languages used around the world. We bring meaning to everyone!
</p>
<ul><li> Find a list of all languages and <a href="/kb/locales">meet the translators for your language here</a>.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> You can also see <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/community/top-contributors/l10n/">the leading localizers for all the locales here</a> (use the <em>Select by Locale</em> dropdown to choose a language).
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "180322", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 23, 2019, 4:00:14 AM", "datetime": "2019-04-23T04:00:14-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "my job has changed a wee bit :-)", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 23, 2019, 4:00:54 AM", "datetime": "2019-04-23T04:00:54-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Apr 23, 2019, 4:00:54 AM", "datetime": "2019-04-23T04:00:54-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:39:32+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (181020,'en-US','add-ons-disabled-or-fail-to-install-firefox','Add-ons disabled or fail to install on Firefox','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/add-ons-disabled-or-fail-to-install-firefox','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/add-ons-disabled-or-fail-to-install-firefox/revision/181020',181017,'2019-05-07T11:43:41-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix typo',1,'2019-05-07T11:43:56-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2019-05-07T11:43:56-07:00','rtanglao','approved','On late Friday, May 3rd, 2019, we became aware of an issue with Firefox that prevented existing and new add-ons from running or being installed. We are very sorry for the inconvenience caused to people who use Firefox.

A fix has been released starting with Firefox version 66.0.4. An update will be rolled out automatically with the latest fixes, or you can download the most recent version (currently 66.0.5):
*[https://www.mozilla.org/firefox/new/ Firefox desktop]
*[https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.mozilla.firefox&hl Firefox for Android on Google Play] (or see your device''s app download site).

Please see the [https://www.mozilla.org/firefox/66.0.5/releasenotes/ Firefox 66.0.5 release notes] for more information.

Below are known issues and workarounds for things that may not be restored automatically.

__TOC__

=Add-ons appearing as ''''unsupported'''' or disappeared from your ''''about:addons'''' page.=

Under certain circumstances, users updating to Firefox 66.0.4+ may see some of their add-ons disappear ([https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1549718 Bug 1549718]). The data for those add-ons is not lost, however. Re-installing the affected add-ons should restore the previous state:
#Go to https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/.
#Search for your add-ons and install them individually.

=Master password=
{note}This is fixed with Firefox 66.0.5. This section applies only if you have 66.0.4. [[Find what version of Firefox you are using]].{/note}
If you have a master password that has not been used for a while, the fix in 66.0.4 might not take effect. You can work around this by entering or resetting your master password.

If you know your master password:
#[[Template:optionspreferences]]
#Select the {menu Privacy & Security} panel.
#Under ''''Logins and Passwords'''' section, click on {button Saved logins…}. This will prompt for your master password.
#After you have entered your master password successfully, restart Firefox.

If you don’t know your master password:
#Follow the instructions at [[Reset your Master Password if you''ve forgotten it]].
#Once you have reset the master password, Firefox will restart.
{warning}''''''Resetting your master password will remove all of your saved usernames and passwords.''''''{/warning}

=Container add-ons=
Containers add-ons may reset to their default state. If add-ons that use the Containers functionality, like Multi-Account Containers and Facebook Container, were disabled as part of this problem, any lost site data for containers, as well as deleted custom containers you may have configured, will not be recovered by this new release.

Data that may be lost for Container add-ons include configuration data, for which containers to enable or disable, and container names and icons. Locally-stored data for the container (cookies and permissions) are also affected ([https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1549204 Bug 1549204]).

See [[Multi-Account Containers]] to set them up again.

=Themes will need to be re-enabled=
Settings for themes will default back and will need to be re-enabled:
#Visit [https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/themes/].
#Click on the theme you want to install.
#Click the {button Install theme} button. Click {button Remove} if you change your mind. Your changes will apply automatically.

See [[Use themes to change the look of Firefox]] or [[Built-in themes in Firefox - alternative to complete themes]] to learn more about themes.

=Home page and search=
If your home page or search settings are set by an add-on, they will be reset to their default settings ([https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1549192 Bug 1549192]). To change them back:

==Home page==
#[[Template:optionspreferences]]
#Select the {menu Home} panel.
#Choose your desired settings for the ''''Home page and new windows'''' and ''''New tabs'''' by clicking the drop-down menu next to each one.
;See [[How to set the home page]] for more information.

==Search==
#[[Template:optionspreferences]]
#Select the {menu Search} panel.
#Choose a default search engine and additional search engines.
;See [[Change your default search settings in Firefox]] for more information.','<p>On late Friday, May 3rd, 2019, we became aware of an issue with Firefox that prevented existing and new add-ons from running or being installed. We are very sorry for the inconvenience caused to people who use Firefox.
</p><p>A fix has been released starting with Firefox version 66.0.4. An update will be rolled out automatically with the latest fixes, or you can download the most recent version (currently 66.0.5):
</p>
<ul><li><a href="https://www.mozilla.org/firefox/new/">Firefox desktop</a>
</li><li><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.mozilla.firefox&amp;hl">Firefox for Android on Google Play</a> (or see your device''s app download site).
</li></ul>
<p>Please see the <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/firefox/66.0.5/releasenotes/">Firefox 66.0.5 release notes</a> for more information.
</p><p>Below are known issues and workarounds for things that may not be restored automatically.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_add-ons-appearing-as-unsupported-or-disappeared-from-your-aboutaddons-page"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Add-ons appearing as unsupported or disappeared from your about:addons page.</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_master-password"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Master password</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_container-add-ons"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Container add-ons</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_themes-will-need-to-be-re-enabled"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Themes will need to be re-enabled</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_home-page-and-search"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Home page and search</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_home-page"><span class="tocnumber">5.1</span> <span class="toctext">Home page</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_search"><span class="tocnumber">5.2</span> <span class="toctext">Search</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_add-ons-appearing-as-unsupported-or-disappeared-from-your-aboutaddons-page">Add-ons appearing as <em>unsupported</em> or disappeared from your <em>about:addons</em> page.</h1>
<p>Under certain circumstances, users updating to Firefox 66.0.4+ may see some of their add-ons disappear (<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1549718">Bug 1549718</a>). The data for those add-ons is not lost, however. Re-installing the affected add-ons should restore the previous state:
</p>
<ol><li>Go to <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/">https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/</a>.
</li><li>Search for your add-ons and install them individually.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_master-password">Master password</h1>
<div class="note">This is fixed with Firefox 66.0.5. This section applies only if you have 66.0.4. <a href="/en-US/kb/find-what-version-firefox-you-are-using">Find what version of Firefox you are using</a>.</div>
<p>If you have a master password that has not been used for a while, the fix in 66.0.4 might not take effect. You can work around this by entering or resetting your master password.
</p><p>If you know your master password:
</p>
<ol><li><span class="for" data-for="mac">In the Menu bar at the top of the screen, click <span class="menu">Firefox</span> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span> (or <span class="menu">Preferences</span>, in some cases).</span><span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Click the menu button <img alt="Fx89menuButton" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-05-15-11-18-38-e5b736.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span>.</span>

</li><li>Select the <span class="menu">Privacy &amp; Security</span> panel.
</li><li>Under <em>Logins and Passwords</em> section, click on <span class="button">Saved logins…</span>. This will prompt for your master password.
</li><li>After you have entered your master password successfully, restart Firefox.
</li></ol>
<p>If you don’t know your master password:
</p>
<ol><li>Follow the instructions at <a href="/en-US/kb/reset-your-primary-password-if-youve-forgotten-it">Reset your Primary Password if you''ve forgotten it</a>.
</li><li>Once you have reset the master password, Firefox will restart.
</li></ol>
<div class="warning"><strong>Resetting your master password will remove all of your saved usernames and passwords.</strong></div>
<h1 id="w_container-add-ons">Container add-ons</h1>
<p>Containers add-ons may reset to their default state. If add-ons that use the Containers functionality, like Multi-Account Containers and Facebook Container, were disabled as part of this problem, any lost site data for containers, as well as deleted custom containers you may have configured, will not be recovered by this new release.
</p><p>Data that may be lost for Container add-ons include configuration data, for which containers to enable or disable, and container names and icons. Locally-stored data for the container (cookies and permissions) are also affected (<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1549204">Bug 1549204</a>).
</p><p>See <a href="/en-US/kb/containers">Multi-Account Containers</a> to set them up again.
</p>
<h1 id="w_themes-will-need-to-be-re-enabled">Themes will need to be re-enabled</h1>
<p>Settings for themes will default back and will need to be re-enabled:
</p>
<ol><li>Visit <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/themes/">https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/themes/</a>.
</li><li>Click on the theme you want to install.
</li><li>Click the <span class="button">Install theme</span> button. Click <span class="button">Remove</span> if you change your mind. Your changes will apply automatically.
</li></ol>
<p>See <a href="/en-US/kb/use-themes-change-look-of-firefox">Use themes to change the look of Firefox</a> or <a href="/en-US/kb/built-themes-firefox-alternative-complete-themes">Built-in themes in Firefox - alternative to complete themes</a> to learn more about themes.
</p>
<h1 id="w_home-page-and-search">Home page and search</h1>
<p>If your home page or search settings are set by an add-on, they will be reset to their default settings (<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1549192">Bug 1549192</a>). To change them back:
</p>
<h2 id="w_home-page">Home page</h2>
<ol><li><span class="for" data-for="mac">In the Menu bar at the top of the screen, click <span class="menu">Firefox</span> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span> (or <span class="menu">Preferences</span>, in some cases).</span><span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Click the menu button <img alt="Fx89menuButton" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-05-15-11-18-38-e5b736.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span>.</span>

</li><li>Select the <span class="menu">Home</span> panel.
</li><li>Choose your desired settings for the <em>Home page and new windows</em> and <em>New tabs</em> by clicking the drop-down menu next to each one.
</li></ol>
<dl><dt>See <a href="/en-US/kb/how-to-set-the-home-page">How to set the home page</a> for more information.
</dt></dl>
<h2 id="w_search">Search</h2>
<ol><li><span class="for" data-for="mac">In the Menu bar at the top of the screen, click <span class="menu">Firefox</span> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span> (or <span class="menu">Preferences</span>, in some cases).</span><span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Click the menu button <img alt="Fx89menuButton" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-05-15-11-18-38-e5b736.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> and select <span class="menu">Settings</span>.</span>

</li><li>Select the <span class="menu">Search</span> panel.
</li><li>Choose a default search engine and additional search engines.
</li></ol>
<dl><dt>See <a href="/en-US/kb/change-your-default-search-settings-firefox">Manage Firefox search settings</a> for more information.
</dt></dl>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "181020", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 7, 2019, 11:43:41 AM", "datetime": "2019-05-07T11:43:41-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix typo", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 7, 2019, 11:43:56 AM", "datetime": "2019-05-07T11:43:56-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "May 7, 2019, 11:43:56 AM", "datetime": "2019-05-07T11:43:56-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:39:29+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (200015,'en-US','make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above','Workaround to make Estonian Smartcards work in Firefox 76+','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above/revision/200015',NULL,'2020-05-08T07:26:47-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','first draft',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','{for not win}{warning}This workaround has been tested on Windows computers only. It might not be needed on Linux and macOS. {/warning}{/for}

#Type in ''''''about:config'''''' in your address bar. (Click the {button Accept the Risk and Continue} button to pass the warning screen).
#Look for the ''''security.osclientcerts.autoload'''' preference and change its value to ''''''true''''''.','<div class="for" data-for="not win"><div class="warning">This workaround has been tested on Windows computers only. It might not be needed on Linux and macOS. </div></div>
<ol><li>Type in <strong>about:config</strong> in your address bar. (Click the <span class="button">Accept the Risk and Continue</span> button to pass the warning screen).
</li><li>Look for the <em>security.osclientcerts.autoload</em> preference and change its value to <strong>true</strong>.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "200015", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 8, 2020, 7:26:47 AM", "datetime": "2020-05-08T07:26:47-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "first draft", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:39:27+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (200016,'en-US','make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above','Workaround to make Estonian Smartcards work in Firefox 76+','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above/revision/200016',NULL,'2020-05-08T07:30:25-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','link to about:config article, https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1636100',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','{for not win}{warning}This workaround has been tested on Windows computers only. It might not be needed on Linux and macOS. {/warning}{/for}

#Type in ''''''about:config'''''' (more info about this in [[Configuration Editor for Firefox]]) in your address bar. (Click the {button Accept the Risk and Continue} button to pass the warning screen).
#Look for the ''''security.osclientcerts.autoload'''' preference and change its value to ''''''true''''''.','<div class="for" data-for="not win"><div class="warning">This workaround has been tested on Windows computers only. It might not be needed on Linux and macOS. </div></div>
<ol><li>Type in <strong>about:config</strong> (more info about this in <a href="/en-US/kb/about-config-editor-firefox">Configuration Editor for Firefox</a>) in your address bar. (Click the <span class="button">Accept the Risk and Continue</span> button to pass the warning screen).
</li><li>Look for the <em>security.osclientcerts.autoload</em> preference and change its value to <strong>true</strong>.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "200016", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 8, 2020, 7:30:25 AM", "datetime": "2020-05-08T07:30:25-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "link to about:config article, https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1636100", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:39:24+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (200021,'en-US','make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above','Workaround to make Estonian Smartcards work in Firefox 76+','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/make-estonian-smartcards-work-firefox-76-and-above/revision/200021',NULL,'2020-05-08T07:54:03-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','link to bug1636100',1,'2020-05-08T07:54:57-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2020-05-08T07:54:57-07:00','rtanglao','approved','{for not win}{warning}This workaround has been tested on Windows computers only. It might not be needed on Linux and macOS. {/warning}{/for}

#Type in ''''''about:config'''''' (more info about this in [[Configuration Editor for Firefox]]) in your address bar. (Click the {button Accept the Risk and Continue} button to pass the warning screen).
#Look for the ''''security.osclientcerts.autoload'''' preference and change its value to ''''''true''''''.

[More technical details about this can be found in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1636100 bug1636100].]','<div class="for" data-for="not win"><div class="warning">This workaround has been tested on Windows computers only. It might not be needed on Linux and macOS. </div></div>
<ol><li>Type in <strong>about:config</strong> (more info about this in <a href="/en-US/kb/about-config-editor-firefox">Configuration Editor for Firefox</a>) in your address bar. (Click the <span class="button">Accept the Risk and Continue</span> button to pass the warning screen).
</li><li>Look for the <em>security.osclientcerts.autoload</em> preference and change its value to <strong>true</strong>.
</li></ol>
