<h2 id="w_keyboard-support">Keyboard Support</h2>
<p>Thunderbird has extensive keyboard shortcuts to allow you to perform tasks inside Thunderbird faster. See the <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/keyboard-shortcuts-thunderbird">Keyboard Shortcuts</a> support page for more information.
</p><p>If you use a screen reader, there are specific keyboard actions that work with your screen reader. We are updating our support documentation to list these keyboard actions for screen readers. 
</p>
<h2 id="w_screen-readers">Screen Readers</h2>
<p>Documentation for keyboard actions that can be used within our
</p>
<h3 id="w_supported-screen-readers-by-operating-system">Supported Screen Readers By Operating System</h3>
<h4 id="w_windows">Windows</h4>
<p>On Windows, the following screen readers have been tested to work with Thunderbird.
</p>
<ul><li><a href="http://www.nvaccess.org/">NVDA</a> (free, donation-based)
</li><li><a href="https://www.freedomscientific.com/products/software/jaws/">Jaws</a>  (commercial)
</li></ul>
<p>The following screen readers have not been thoroughly tested with Thunderbird, but are available on Windows.
</p>
<ul><li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/complete-guide-to-narrator-e4397a0d-ef4f-b386-d8ae-c172f109bdb1">Narrator</a> (Windows default)
</li><li><a href="http://www.gwmicro.com/Window-Eyes/">Windows Eyes</a> (commercial)
</li></ul>
<h4 id="w_mac">Mac</h4>
<p>On macOS, the following screen readers have not been thoroughly tested with Thunderbird, but are available on macOS.
</p>
<ul><li><a href="https://www.apple.com/accessibility/vision/">VoiceOver</a> (macOS default)
</li></ul>
<h4 id="w_linux">Linux</h4>
<p>On Linux, the following screen readers have not been thoroughly tested with Thunderbird, but are available on Linux operating systems.
</p>
<ul><li><a href="https://help.gnome.org/users/orca/stable/">Orca</a> (GNOME default)
</li></ul>
<p><br>
</p>
<h2 id="w_font-size">Font Size</h2>
<h2 id="w_115-and-greater">115 and greater</h2>
<p>There have been significant updates in 115 to improve the ability to adjust the font size throughout the application.
</p><p>Here''s how to change the font size:
</p>
<ul><li> Click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Font Size</span> and then click the <span class="button">+</span> icon to increase the font size or click the <span class="button">-</span> icon to decrease the font size. 
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_102">102</h2>
<p>In older versions, the following add-on was recommended for increasing the font size.
</p>
<ul><li><a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/theme-font-size-changer-fixed/">Theme Font &amp; Size Changer (fixed) add-on</a>
</li></ul>
<p>For instructions on how to install add-ons, see <a href="/en-US/kb/installing-addon-thunderbird">Installing an Add-on in Thunderbird</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_accessibility-features-specific-for-firefox-and-firefox-for-android">Accessibility features specific for Firefox and Firefox for Android</h2>
<p>To find out about Accessibility features specific to <strong>Firefox</strong>, see
<a href="/en-US/kb/accessibility-features-firefox">Accessibility features in Firefox - Make Firefox and web content work for all users</a>.
</p><p>To find out more Accessibility Features for <strong>Firefox for Android</strong>, see <a href="/en-US/kb/mobile-accessibility-features">Mobile Accessibility Features</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_display-options">Display Options</h2>
<p>In Thunderbird, you have the option to change your display options.
</p>
<ul><li> Click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="button">General</span> and then scroll down to "Language &amp; Appearance"
</li><li> The following screen will display:
</li></ul>
