</td></tr></tbody></table>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "269261", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 2, 2023, 1:37:09 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-02T01:37:09-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "developer tools on macOS is Command+Option+I", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 2, 2023, 1:37:49 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-02T01:37:49-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:36:00+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (269798,'en-US','unable-install-add-on-extension-theme-thunderbird','Unable to install add-ons (extensions or themes) in Thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/unable-install-add-on-extension-theme-thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/unable-install-add-on-extension-theme-thunderbird/revision/269798',170356,'2023-11-06T08:08:24-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','remove obsolete warnings and fix menu button',1,'2023-11-06T08:08:57-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','An inability to install an extension can be the result of problems with the extension or the version of Thunderbird you are using. This article describes various causes of install problems and what you can do to address them.

__TOC__

= Add-on is not compatible =
A file in each add-on indicates the range of Thunderbird versions with which it is compatible. At [https://addons.thunderbird.net/ Thunderbird Add-ons] you can find and review the version compatibility information for each add-on. If your installed version of Thunderbird does not fit within the specified range, then installing the add-on or starting Thunderbird will fail or indicate the add-on is not compatible. 

''''''A published add-on is the responsibility of its respective add-on author.''''''
If an add-on does not work or is not compatible, you have these choices:
* Update to the latest version of Thunderbird. For more information, see [[Updating Thunderbird]].
* Find a version of the add-on that is compatible with your version of Thunderbird. The [https://addons.thunderbird.net/ Thunderbird Add-ons] website usually has the most up to date version.
* Use a different add-on. You can often find other add-ons with similar functionality at [https://addons.thunderbird.net/ Thunderbird Add-ons].
* Contact the author of the add-on at the support site listed on its add-on page. (Note: posting a review is not effective and will not reach the author.)

= Trouble installing Themes =
Starting with beta version 61, Thunderbird supports only lightweight themes, and you can therefore no longer install "complete themes".  [[Install themes to change the look of Thunderbird]] describes the purpose and installation process.  

= You are asked to download the add-on, rather than allowed to install it =
Some websites serve add-ons as downloads, requiring you to download the file to your computer, before installing it. 
* These files are usually {filepath [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XPInstall .xpi]} or {filepath [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JAR_%28file_format%29 .jar]} files. 
# Download the file to your local computer.
# Click {menu ≡} > {menu Add-ons and Themes}. The Add-ons Manager tab will open.
#In the Add-ons Manager tab, select the {menu Extensions} panel.
# To add the downloaded add-on to the list of available add-ons, drag and drop the file into the Add-ons window. The add-on is added to the list.
#  The installation process should begin.
''''''An add-on will not work if incompatible.''''''

= Corrupt extension files =
Corrupt extension configuration files can cause problems when trying to install an add-on. Deleting these files will make Thunderbird recreate them the next time it starts. You won''t lose your extensions or their settings by deleting these files.

# Open your profile folder:
#* [[T:openProfileFolderTB]]
# Delete the following files:
#* {filepath extensions.sqlite}
#* {filepath extensions.sqlite-journal} (if found) 
#* {filepath extensions.ini}
#* {filepath extensions.json}
# Restart Thunderbird.

= Conflict with another add-on =
An already installed add-on may interfere with the installation of a new one. Install the new extension in Thunderbird [[Safe Mode Thunderbird|Safe Mode]] as a workaround. 

= Add-on has a high risk of causing stability or security problems and can''t be installed =
Certain add-ons have been blocklisted for being unsafe.  For more information, see [[Add-ons that cause stability or security issues are put on a blocklist]].

<!-- MZ credit -->
<br><br>
''''''''''Based on information from
* [[Unable to install add-ons (extensions or themes)]]
* [http://kb.mozillazine.org/Unable_to_install_themes_or_extensions_-_Firefox Unable to install themes or extensions - Firefox (mozillaZine KB)]''''''''''','<p>An inability to install an extension can be the result of problems with the extension or the version of Thunderbird you are using. This article describes various causes of install problems and what you can do to address them.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_add-on-is-not-compatible"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Add-on is not compatible</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_trouble-installing-themes"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Trouble installing Themes</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_you-are-asked-to-download-the-add-on-rather-than-allowed-to-install-it"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">You are asked to download the add-on, rather than allowed to install it</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_corrupt-extension-files"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Corrupt extension files</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_conflict-with-another-add-on"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Conflict with another add-on</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_add-on-has-a-high-risk-of-causing-stability-or-security-problems-and-cant-be-installed"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">Add-on has a high risk of causing stability or security problems and can''t be installed</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_add-on-is-not-compatible">Add-on is not compatible</h1>
<p>A file in each add-on indicates the range of Thunderbird versions with which it is compatible. At <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/">Thunderbird Add-ons</a> you can find and review the version compatibility information for each add-on. If your installed version of Thunderbird does not fit within the specified range, then installing the add-on or starting Thunderbird will fail or indicate the add-on is not compatible. 
</p><p><strong>A published add-on is the responsibility of its respective add-on author.</strong>
If an add-on does not work or is not compatible, you have these choices:
</p>
<ul><li> Update to the latest version of Thunderbird. For more information, see <a href="/en-US/kb/updating-thunderbird">Update Thunderbird to the latest version</a>.
</li><li> Find a version of the add-on that is compatible with your version of Thunderbird. The <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/">Thunderbird Add-ons</a> website usually has the most up to date version.
</li><li> Use a different add-on. You can often find other add-ons with similar functionality at <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/">Thunderbird Add-ons</a>.
</li><li> Contact the author of the add-on at the support site listed on its add-on page. (Note: posting a review is not effective and will not reach the author.)
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_trouble-installing-themes">Trouble installing Themes</h1>
<p>Starting with beta version 61, Thunderbird supports only lightweight themes, and you can therefore no longer install "complete themes".  <a href="/en-US/kb/install-themes-change-look-thunderbird">Install themes to change the look of Thunderbird</a> describes the purpose and installation process.  
</p>
<h1 id="w_you-are-asked-to-download-the-add-on-rather-than-allowed-to-install-it">You are asked to download the add-on, rather than allowed to install it</h1>
<p>Some websites serve add-ons as downloads, requiring you to download the file to your computer, before installing it. 
</p>
<ul><li> These files are usually <span class="filepath"><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XPInstall">.xpi</a></span> or <span class="filepath"><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JAR_%28file_format%29">.jar</a></span> files. 
</li></ul>
<ol><li> Download the file to your local computer.
</li><li> Click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add-ons and Themes</span>. The Add-ons Manager tab will open.
</li><li>In the Add-ons Manager tab, select the <span class="menu">Extensions</span> panel.
</li><li> To add the downloaded add-on to the list of available add-ons, drag and drop the file into the Add-ons window. The add-on is added to the list.
</li><li>  The installation process should begin.
</li></ol>
<p><strong>An add-on will not work if incompatible.</strong>
</p>
<h1 id="w_corrupt-extension-files">Corrupt extension files</h1>
<p>Corrupt extension configuration files can cause problems when trying to install an add-on. Deleting these files will make Thunderbird recreate them the next time it starts. You won''t lose your extensions or their settings by deleting these files.
</p>
<ol><li> Open your profile folder:
<ul><li> <ul><li> Click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Help</span> and select <span class="menu">Troubleshooting Information</span>. The <strong>Troubleshooting Information</strong> tab will open.
</li><li> Under the <strong>Application Basics</strong> section, find the <span class="for" data-for="win,mac"><em>Profile Folder</em></span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;"><em>Profile Directory</em></span> row, then click on <span class="button"><span class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;">Open Folder</span><span class="for" data-for="mac">Show in Finder</span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;">Open Directory</span></span>. <span class="for" data-for="mac">A window will open that contains your profile folder.</span><span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Your profile folder will open.</span>
</li></ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> If you are unable to open or use Thunderbird, follow the instructions in <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data#w_finding-your-profile-without-opening-thunderbird">Finding your profile without opening Thunderbird</a>.</div>
</li></ul>
</li><li> Delete the following files:
<ul><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.sqlite</span>
</li><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.sqlite-journal</span> (if found) 
</li><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.ini</span>
</li><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.json</span>
</li></ul>
</li><li> Restart Thunderbird.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_conflict-with-another-add-on">Conflict with another add-on</h1>
<p>An already installed add-on may interfere with the installation of a new one. Install the new extension in Thunderbird <a href="/en-US/kb/troubleshoot-mode-thunderbird">Safe Mode</a> as a workaround. 
</p>
<h1 id="w_add-on-has-a-high-risk-of-causing-stability-or-security-problems-and-cant-be-installed">Add-on has a high risk of causing stability or security problems and can''t be installed</h1>
<p>Certain add-ons have been blocklisted for being unsafe.  For more information, see <a href="/en-US/kb/add-ons-cause-issues-are-on-blocklist">Why does Mozilla disable some add-ons from running in Firefox?</a>.
</p><p>
<br><br>
<em><strong>Based on information from
</strong></em>
</p>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/unable-install-add-ons-extensions-or-themes">Unable to install add-ons (extensions or themes)</a>
</li><li> <a href="http://kb.mozillazine.org/Unable_to_install_themes_or_extensions_-_Firefox">Unable to install themes or extensions - Firefox (mozillaZine KB)</a><em><strong></strong></em>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "269798", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 6, 2023, 8:08:24 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-06T08:08:24-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "remove obsolete warnings and fix menu button", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 6, 2023, 8:08:57 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-06T08:08:57-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:35:57+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (269799,'en-US','templateopenProfileFolderTB','Template:openProfileFolderTB','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/templateopenProfileFolderTB','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/templateopenProfileFolderTB/revision/269799',246636,'2023-11-06T08:12:37-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','update to 115',1,'2023-11-06T08:12:50-08:00','rtanglao',1,1,1,'2023-11-06T08:12:50-08:00','rtanglao','approved','* Click {menu ≡} > {menu Help} and select {menu Troubleshooting Information}. The ''''''Troubleshooting Information'''''' tab will open.
* Under the ''''''Application Basics'''''' section, find the {for win,mac}''''Profile Folder''''{/for}{for linux}''''Profile Directory''''{/for} row, then click on {button {for win}Open Folder{/for}{for mac}Show in Finder{/for}{for linux}Open Directory{/for}}. {for mac}A window will open that contains your profile folder.{/for}{for win,linux}Your profile folder will open.{/for}
{note}''''''Note:'''''' If you are unable to open or use Thunderbird, follow the instructions in [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data#w_finding-your-profile-without-opening-thunderbird|Finding your profile without opening Thunderbird]].{/note}','<ul><li> Click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Help</span> and select <span class="menu">Troubleshooting Information</span>. The <strong>Troubleshooting Information</strong> tab will open.
</li><li> Under the <strong>Application Basics</strong> section, find the <span class="for" data-for="win,mac"><em>Profile Folder</em></span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;"><em>Profile Directory</em></span> row, then click on <span class="button"><span class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;">Open Folder</span><span class="for" data-for="mac">Show in Finder</span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;">Open Directory</span></span>. <span class="for" data-for="mac">A window will open that contains your profile folder.</span><span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Your profile folder will open.</span>
</li></ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> If you are unable to open or use Thunderbird, follow the instructions in <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data#w_finding-your-profile-without-opening-thunderbird">Finding your profile without opening Thunderbird</a>.</div>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "269799", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 6, 2023, 8:12:37 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-06T08:12:37-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "update to 115", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 6, 2023, 8:12:50 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-06T08:12:50-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Nov 6, 2023, 8:12:50 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-06T08:12:50-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:35:54+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (269800,'en-US','unable-install-add-on-extension-theme-thunderbird','Unable to install add-ons (extensions or themes) in Thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/unable-install-add-on-extension-theme-thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/unable-install-add-on-extension-theme-thunderbird/revision/269800',269798,'2023-11-06T08:16:10-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix formatting error that causeds 2 bullets to show up for opening the profile folder',1,'2023-11-06T08:16:28-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','An inability to install an extension can be the result of problems with the extension or the version of Thunderbird you are using. This article describes various causes of install problems and what you can do to address them.

__TOC__

= Add-on is not compatible =
A file in each add-on indicates the range of Thunderbird versions with which it is compatible. At [https://addons.thunderbird.net/ Thunderbird Add-ons] you can find and review the version compatibility information for each add-on. If your installed version of Thunderbird does not fit within the specified range, then installing the add-on or starting Thunderbird will fail or indicate the add-on is not compatible. 

''''''A published add-on is the responsibility of its respective add-on author.''''''
If an add-on does not work or is not compatible, you have these choices:
* Update to the latest version of Thunderbird. For more information, see [[Updating Thunderbird]].
* Find a version of the add-on that is compatible with your version of Thunderbird. The [https://addons.thunderbird.net/ Thunderbird Add-ons] website usually has the most up to date version.
* Use a different add-on. You can often find other add-ons with similar functionality at [https://addons.thunderbird.net/ Thunderbird Add-ons].
* Contact the author of the add-on at the support site listed on its add-on page. (Note: posting a review is not effective and will not reach the author.)

= Trouble installing Themes =
Starting with beta version 61, Thunderbird supports only lightweight themes, and you can therefore no longer install "complete themes".  [[Install themes to change the look of Thunderbird]] describes the purpose and installation process.  

= You are asked to download the add-on, rather than allowed to install it =
Some websites serve add-ons as downloads, requiring you to download the file to your computer, before installing it. 
* These files are usually {filepath [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XPInstall .xpi]} or {filepath [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JAR_%28file_format%29 .jar]} files. 
# Download the file to your local computer.
# Click {menu ≡} > {menu Add-ons and Themes}. The Add-ons Manager tab will open.
#In the Add-ons Manager tab, select the {menu Extensions} panel.
# To add the downloaded add-on to the list of available add-ons, drag and drop the file into the Add-ons window. The add-on is added to the list.
#  The installation process should begin.
''''''An add-on will not work if incompatible.''''''

= Corrupt extension files =
Corrupt extension configuration files can cause problems when trying to install an add-on. Deleting these files will make Thunderbird recreate them the next time it starts. You won''t lose your extensions or their settings by deleting these files.

# Open your profile folder:<br />[[T:openProfileFolderTB]]
# Delete the following files:
#* {filepath extensions.sqlite}
#* {filepath extensions.sqlite-journal} (if found) 
#* {filepath extensions.ini}
#* {filepath extensions.json}
# Restart Thunderbird.

= Conflict with another add-on =
An already installed add-on may interfere with the installation of a new one. Install the new extension in Thunderbird [[Safe Mode Thunderbird|Safe Mode]] as a workaround. 

= Add-on has a high risk of causing stability or security problems and can''t be installed =
Certain add-ons have been blocklisted for being unsafe.  For more information, see [[Add-ons that cause stability or security issues are put on a blocklist]].

<!-- MZ credit -->
<br><br>
''''''''''Based on information from
* [[Unable to install add-ons (extensions or themes)]]
* [http://kb.mozillazine.org/Unable_to_install_themes_or_extensions_-_Firefox Unable to install themes or extensions - Firefox (mozillaZine KB)]''''''''''','<p>An inability to install an extension can be the result of problems with the extension or the version of Thunderbird you are using. This article describes various causes of install problems and what you can do to address them.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_add-on-is-not-compatible"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Add-on is not compatible</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_trouble-installing-themes"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Trouble installing Themes</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_you-are-asked-to-download-the-add-on-rather-than-allowed-to-install-it"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">You are asked to download the add-on, rather than allowed to install it</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_corrupt-extension-files"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Corrupt extension files</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_conflict-with-another-add-on"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Conflict with another add-on</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_add-on-has-a-high-risk-of-causing-stability-or-security-problems-and-cant-be-installed"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">Add-on has a high risk of causing stability or security problems and can''t be installed</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_add-on-is-not-compatible">Add-on is not compatible</h1>
<p>A file in each add-on indicates the range of Thunderbird versions with which it is compatible. At <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/">Thunderbird Add-ons</a> you can find and review the version compatibility information for each add-on. If your installed version of Thunderbird does not fit within the specified range, then installing the add-on or starting Thunderbird will fail or indicate the add-on is not compatible. 
</p><p><strong>A published add-on is the responsibility of its respective add-on author.</strong>
If an add-on does not work or is not compatible, you have these choices:
</p>
<ul><li> Update to the latest version of Thunderbird. For more information, see <a href="/en-US/kb/updating-thunderbird">Update Thunderbird to the latest version</a>.
</li><li> Find a version of the add-on that is compatible with your version of Thunderbird. The <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/">Thunderbird Add-ons</a> website usually has the most up to date version.
</li><li> Use a different add-on. You can often find other add-ons with similar functionality at <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/">Thunderbird Add-ons</a>.
</li><li> Contact the author of the add-on at the support site listed on its add-on page. (Note: posting a review is not effective and will not reach the author.)
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_trouble-installing-themes">Trouble installing Themes</h1>
<p>Starting with beta version 61, Thunderbird supports only lightweight themes, and you can therefore no longer install "complete themes".  <a href="/en-US/kb/install-themes-change-look-thunderbird">Install themes to change the look of Thunderbird</a> describes the purpose and installation process.  
</p>
<h1 id="w_you-are-asked-to-download-the-add-on-rather-than-allowed-to-install-it">You are asked to download the add-on, rather than allowed to install it</h1>
<p>Some websites serve add-ons as downloads, requiring you to download the file to your computer, before installing it. 
</p>
<ul><li> These files are usually <span class="filepath"><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XPInstall">.xpi</a></span> or <span class="filepath"><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JAR_%28file_format%29">.jar</a></span> files. 
</li></ul>
<ol><li> Download the file to your local computer.
</li><li> Click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add-ons and Themes</span>. The Add-ons Manager tab will open.
</li><li>In the Add-ons Manager tab, select the <span class="menu">Extensions</span> panel.
</li><li> To add the downloaded add-on to the list of available add-ons, drag and drop the file into the Add-ons window. The add-on is added to the list.
</li><li>  The installation process should begin.
</li></ol>
<p><strong>An add-on will not work if incompatible.</strong>
</p>
<h1 id="w_corrupt-extension-files">Corrupt extension files</h1>
<p>Corrupt extension configuration files can cause problems when trying to install an add-on. Deleting these files will make Thunderbird recreate them the next time it starts. You won''t lose your extensions or their settings by deleting these files.
</p>
<ol><li> Open your profile folder:<br><ul><li> Click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Help</span> and select <span class="menu">Troubleshooting Information</span>. The <strong>Troubleshooting Information</strong> tab will open.
</li><li> Under the <strong>Application Basics</strong> section, find the <span class="for" data-for="win,mac"><em>Profile Folder</em></span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;"><em>Profile Directory</em></span> row, then click on <span class="button"><span class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;">Open Folder</span><span class="for" data-for="mac">Show in Finder</span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;">Open Directory</span></span>. <span class="for" data-for="mac">A window will open that contains your profile folder.</span><span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Your profile folder will open.</span>
</li></ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> If you are unable to open or use Thunderbird, follow the instructions in <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data#w_finding-your-profile-without-opening-thunderbird">Finding your profile without opening Thunderbird</a>.</div>
</li><li> Delete the following files:
<ul><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.sqlite</span>
</li><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.sqlite-journal</span> (if found) 
</li><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.ini</span>
</li><li> <span class="filepath">extensions.json</span>
</li></ul>
</li><li> Restart Thunderbird.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_conflict-with-another-add-on">Conflict with another add-on</h1>
<p>An already installed add-on may interfere with the installation of a new one. Install the new extension in Thunderbird <a href="/en-US/kb/troubleshoot-mode-thunderbird">Safe Mode</a> as a workaround. 
</p>
<h1 id="w_add-on-has-a-high-risk-of-causing-stability-or-security-problems-and-cant-be-installed">Add-on has a high risk of causing stability or security problems and can''t be installed</h1>
<p>Certain add-ons have been blocklisted for being unsafe.  For more information, see <a href="/en-US/kb/add-ons-cause-issues-are-on-blocklist">Why does Mozilla disable some add-ons from running in Firefox?</a>.
</p><p>
<br><br>
<em><strong>Based on information from
</strong></em>
</p>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/unable-install-add-ons-extensions-or-themes">Unable to install add-ons (extensions or themes)</a>
</li><li> <a href="http://kb.mozillazine.org/Unable_to_install_themes_or_extensions_-_Firefox">Unable to install themes or extensions - Firefox (mozillaZine KB)</a><em><strong></strong></em>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "269800", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 6, 2023, 8:16:10 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-06T08:16:10-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix formatting error that causeds 2 bullets to show up for opening the profile folder", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 6, 2023, 8:16:28 AM", "datetime": "2023-11-06T08:16:28-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:35:52+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (269882,'en-US','keyboard-shortcuts-thunderbird','Keyboard shortcuts - perform common Thunderbird tasks quickly','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/keyboard-shortcuts-thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/keyboard-shortcuts-thunderbird/revision/269882',269261,'2023-11-07T03:58:43-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','message list columns moving is not fully working on macOS',1,'2023-11-07T03:59:00-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','Keyboard shortcuts are quick key combinations that let you perform certain tasks in Thunderbird faster. For example, if you want to [[Archived Messages|archive a message]], you can simply strike the "A" key rather than using the mouse to click the option in a menu. Some shortcuts can be customized or disabled with the use of an add-on.

__TOC__

= About keyboard shortcuts =

In Thunderbird, keyboard shortcuts are context sensitive. That is, they vary according to the area of the Thunderbird interface that is currently "active". For example, when a message is selected in the message list, the Cut, Copy and Paste keyboard shortcuts are disabled (because it doesn''t make sense to cut and paste text into the message list). Similarly, if you select text while you are reading a message, the Copy shortcut is available, but not the Cut or Paste shortcuts (because while it makes sense to copy text from a message you are reading, it doesn''t make sense to paste text into or cut text from a message you are reading).

Sometimes the keyboard shortcut functions themselves vary depending on the part of the Thunderbird interface that is active. For example, if you are writing a message, the {for win,linux}{key Ctrl+A}{/for}{for mac}{key Command+A}{/for} keyboard shortcut selects all the text in the message. However, if a message is highlighted in the message list, {for win,linux}{key Ctrl+A}{/for}{for mac}{key Command+A}{/for} selects all the messages in the message list.

= Shortcut keys and operating systems =

*On Windows and Linux, the shortcut accelerator key is usually the {key Ctrl} key.
*On macOS, the shortcut accelerator key is usually the {key Command} key.
*On macOS laptops, you must hold down the {key fn} key to enable a function key.

= List of keyboard shortcuts =

View Keyboard Shortcuts for:
* [[#w_message-functions|Message functions]]
* [[#w_search-and-filter-functions|Search and filter functions]]
* [[#w_moving-around-thunderbird|Moving around Thunderbird]]
* [[#w_writing-messages|Writing messages]]
* [[#w_address-book|Address Book]]
* [[#w_calendar|Calendar]]
* [[#w_miscellaneous|Miscellaneous]]

== Message functions ==

[[#w_list-of-keyboard-shortcuts|  ← ]] | [[#w_list-of-keyboard-shortcuts|  ↑  ]] | [[#w_search-and-filter-functions|  → ]]

{| 
