</p><p>For the moment, the only workaround we can offer is to customize the accent colors and memorize them.
</p>
<h2 id="w_im-not-getting-notifications-for-my-email-or-they-are-not-arriving-unless-i-check-manually">I''m not getting notifications for my email or they are not arriving unless I check manually</h2>
<p>You might have acceidentally skipped over this in the first time user experience. Make sure you grant notification permissions to the application in your Android settings.
</p><p>We''ve also changed the way the former "folder classes" work. If you are not getting notifications for the folders that are important to you, double check that you have either sync or push enabled in the folder settings for that folder.
</p>
<h2 id="w_what-is-happening-with-exchange-support">What is happening with Exchange Support?</h2>
<p>Thunderbird for Android currently supports the following protocols: IMAP, POP and SMTP. Support for Exchange is being planned for future releases. Please keep an eye on our <a href="https://blog.thunderbird.net/category/mobile-news/">blog</a> for news.
</p>
<h2 id="w_what-is-happening-with-thunderbird-sync">What is happening with Thunderbird Sync?</h2>
<ul><li> We are building our own sync storage server and it is taking some time to set it up and test. We will let you know when it is available for public pre-release testing.
</li><li> In the meantime, you can reuse your email account settings from Thunderbird Desktop via a QR code or import your settings from K-9 or from a file. Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a> for full details.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_what-about-calendering">What about calendering?</h2>
<ul><li> Thunderbird for Android does not have calendar functionality. It is not on the near term roadmap, but will be evaluated in the future.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "287788", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 30, 2024, 5:00:43 PM", "datetime": "2024-10-30T17:00:43.846593-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/2#issuecomment-2447806551", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Oct 30, 2024, 8:36:14 PM", "datetime": "2024-10-30T20:36:14.235071-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "wsmwk", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Oct 30, 2024, 8:36:14 PM", "datetime": "2024-10-30T20:36:14.235071-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "wsmwk", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:31:07+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (288490,'en-US','manage-notifications-firefox-android','Manage notifications in Firefox for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/manage-notifications-firefox-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/manage-notifications-firefox-android/revision/288490',206550,'2024-11-11T10:51:46.008236-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','[[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]] instead of androidmenulocation',1,'2024-11-11T10:53:03.526393-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2024-11-11T10:53:03.526393-08:00','rtanglao','approved','In Firefox for Android you can customize which notifications you receive from the app.

#Open Firefox for Android. 
#Tap the three-dot menu button [[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]]
#Tap {menu Settings}
#Tap {menu Site permissions}.
#Select {menu Notification}.
#Choose {menu Ask to allow} to be prompted when notifications are available or {menu Blocked} to not see notifications at all.','<p>In Firefox for Android you can customize which notifications you receive from the app.
</p>
<ol><li>Open Firefox for Android. 
</li><li>Tap the three-dot menu button (either <a href="/en-US/kb/firefox-menu-icon-missing-android-how-access-menu"> at the bottom right on some devices</a> or in the upper right of the browser)

</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Settings</span>
</li><li>Tap <span class="menu">Site permissions</span>.
</li><li>Select <span class="menu">Notification</span>.
</li><li>Choose <span class="menu">Ask to allow</span> to be prompted when notifications are available or <span class="menu">Blocked</span> to not see notifications at all.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "288490", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 11, 2024, 10:51:46 AM", "datetime": "2024-11-11T10:51:46.008236-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "[[Template:AndroidMenuLocation]] instead of androidmenulocation", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 11, 2024, 10:53:03 AM", "datetime": "2024-11-11T10:53:03.526393-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Nov 11, 2024, 10:53:03 AM", "datetime": "2024-11-11T10:53:03.526393-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:31:05+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (288510,'en-US','configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','Configure push email for Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android/revision/288510',NULL,'2024-11-11T21:02:04.679807-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP, needs screenshots, do not approve, do not translate',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.
__TOC__
==Turn on push email for a folder==
{warning}WARNING: The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu ≡ > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}  > ''''''your email account'''''' > {menu Fetching mail} > {menu Advanced} > {menu Max folders to check with push}. Thunderbird does not enforce this limit. Please ensure you do not go over this limit.{/warning}
# Tap {button ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account e.g. your gmail account  > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap ''''''Inbox''''''''  to enable push email for your Inbox.
#;[[Image:enable push-pixel7a]]
# Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable Push''''''. 
# Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable sync''''''.
{note}The ''''''Enable sync'''''' setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.{/note}
Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled and working.
[[Image:bell-system-bar-pixel7a]] 
If you do not see the bell icon, please stop Thunderbird for Android and open it again.
===Alarms & Reminders Permission for Android 13 and above===
{note}This section is not applicable to you if your Android version is older than Android 13.{/note}
# On Android 13 and above, a notification will let you  know you need to grant the ''''''Alarms & reminders''''''  permission. Proceed to the permissions screen by tapping the notification.
#;[[Image: missing permission notification]]
# Add this permission by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Allow setting alarms and reminders''''''.  If you do not grant this permission, then push mail will not work.
#;[[Image:alarm-and-reminders-permission-screen]]
== How to control the push mail notification==
Once you enable push mail, Thunderbird for Android will display a notification. You change  this notification or turn it off by tapping on the notification or via app menu ≡ > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}  > {menu Notifications} > {menu Messages} under ''''''Notification categories''''''
#;[[Image:notification-settings]]
=== Do not display the push mail notification ===
* Slide ''''''Show notifications'''''' to the left. 
=== Change the push mail notification ===
If you choose to display the push mail notification, Android offers several display options. Here are the most important:
* ''''''Default'''''': ring or vibrate depending on your Android settings or ''''''Silent''''''.
* ''''''Sound'''''': the default notification sound.
* ''''''Vibration'''''': whether or not to vibrate.
* ''''''Show notification dot'''''': whether or not to display a notification dot in the Android system bar. 

==Turn off push email for a folder==
# Tap {button ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account e.g. your gmail account  > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example, tap ''''''Inbox''''''  to disable push email for your Inbox.
# Turn off push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable Push''''''. 
# Turn on sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable sync''''''. 
===Learn more===
* Wikipedia: [https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Push_email Push email]
* Google: [https://support.google.com/android/answer/9079661 Control notifications on Android]','<p>By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Turn on push email for a folder</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_alarms-reminders-permission-for-android-13-and-above"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Alarms &amp; Reminders Permission for Android 13 and above</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_how-to-control-the-push-mail-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">How to control the push mail notification</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_do-not-display-the-push-mail-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Do not display the push mail notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_change-the-push-mail-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Change the push mail notification</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-off-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Turn off push email for a folder</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_learn-more"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Learn more</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder">Turn on push email for a folder</h2>
<div class="warning">WARNING: The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu ≡ &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>  &gt; <strong>your email account</strong> &gt; <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Advanced</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Max folders to check with push</span>. Thunderbird does not enforce this limit. Please ensure you do not go over this limit.</div>
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap <span class="button">Show accounts</span> at the bottom of the screen.
</li><li> Tap account e.g. your gmail account  &gt; tap <span class="button">Manage folders</span>.
</li><li> Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap <strong>Inbox''</strong>  to enable push email for your Inbox.
<dl><dt>The image "enable push-pixel7a" does not exist.
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Enable Push</strong>. 
</li><li> Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for <strong>Enable sync</strong>.
</li></ol>
<div class="note">The <strong>Enable sync</strong> setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.</div>
<p>Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled and working.
The image "bell-system-bar-pixel7a" does not exist. 
If you do not see the bell icon, please stop Thunderbird for Android and open it again.
</p>
<h3 id="w_alarms-reminders-permission-for-android-13-and-above">Alarms &amp; Reminders Permission for Android 13 and above</h3>
<div class="note">This section is not applicable to you if your Android version is older than Android 13.</div>
<ol><li> On Android 13 and above, a notification will let you  know you need to grant the <strong>Alarms &amp; reminders</strong>  permission. Proceed to the permissions screen by tapping the notification.
<dl><dt>The image "missing permission notification" does not exist.
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Add this permission by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Allow setting alarms and reminders</strong>.  If you do not grant this permission, then push mail will not work.
<dl><dt>The image "alarm-and-reminders-permission-screen" does not exist.
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_how-to-control-the-push-mail-notification">How to control the push mail notification</h2>
<p>Once you enable push mail, Thunderbird for Android will display a notification. You change  this notification or turn it off by tapping on the notification or via app menu ≡ &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>  &gt; <span class="menu">Notifications</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Messages</span> under <strong>Notification categories</strong>
</p>
<ol><li><dl><dt>The image "notification-settings" does not exist.
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h3 id="w_do-not-display-the-push-mail-notification">Do not display the push mail notification</h3>
<ul><li> Slide <strong>Show notifications</strong> to the left. 
</li></ul>
<h3 id="w_change-the-push-mail-notification">Change the push mail notification</h3>
<p>If you choose to display the push mail notification, Android offers several display options. Here are the most important:
</p>
<ul><li> <strong>Default</strong>: ring or vibrate depending on your Android settings or <strong>Silent</strong>.
</li><li> <strong>Sound</strong>: the default notification sound.
</li><li> <strong>Vibration</strong>: whether or not to vibrate.
</li><li> <strong>Show notification dot</strong>: whether or not to display a notification dot in the Android system bar. 
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_turn-off-push-email-for-a-folder">Turn off push email for a folder</h2>
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap <span class="button">Show accounts</span> at the bottom of the screen.
</li><li> Tap account e.g. your gmail account  &gt; tap <span class="button">Manage folders</span>.
</li><li> Tap your folder of choice. For example, tap <strong>Inbox</strong>  to disable push email for your Inbox.
</li><li> Turn off push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for <strong>Enable Push</strong>. 
</li><li> Turn on sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Enable sync</strong>. 
</li></ol>
<h3 id="w_learn-more">Learn more</h3>
<ul><li> Wikipedia: <a href="https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Push_email">Push email</a>
</li><li> Google: <a href="https://support.google.com/android/answer/9079661">Control notifications on Android</a>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "288510", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 11, 2024, 9:02:04 PM", "datetime": "2024-11-11T21:02:04.679807-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, needs screenshots, do not approve, do not translate", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:30:57+00:00');
