<h2 id="w_display-remote-content-for-a-particular-message-sender-or-website">Display remote content for a particular message, sender or website</h2>
<p>If you trust the sender, you can allow remote content to be downloaded. Emails look much better with images and stylesheets turned on. To load remote content, click <span class="button"><span class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;">Options</span><span class="for" data-for="mac,linux">Preferences</span></span> in the notification bar and select one of the following options:
</p><p><span class="for" data-for="tb115"><span class="for" data-for="mac,linux"><img alt="Remote Content Exceptions" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-01-23-02-30-41-a058d8.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span></span>
<span class="for" data-for="not tb45" style="display: none;"><span class="for" data-for="win" style="display: none;"><img alt="Remote content blocking options Win" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2015-10-24-02-48-19-998820.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span><span class="for" data-for="not tb115" style="display: none;">
