= 2. Unified Toolbar = 
There is a new “Unified Toolbar” on top of the Tab Bar, which is fully screenreader and keyboard accessible.  This toolbar is used for all  “Spaces” of the Spaces Toolbar, which are  Mail, Address Book, Calendar, Tasks, Chat and Settings. More details at [[Unified Toolbar]].

= 3. Tab Bar = 
In Supernova,  the Tab Bar is only displayed if you have two or more tabs. For example, if you have a Mail tab and a Calendar Tab, the Tab Bar is visible. If you just have one tab like the Mail tab, the Tab Bar automatically disappears.

= 4. Message List Header = 
The Message List Header is new for 115. It shows the current folder name, number of messages, "Quick Filter", and “Message list display options” icon [[Image:tb115-display-options-icon-offical-from-micah]]. If you are not seeing the Message List Header, click {menu ≡} > {menu View} > {menu Layout} > {menu Message List Header}.

= 5. Folder Pane = 
The Folder Pane is where your accounts and folders will appear. It will show the account name(s) specified in the [[Configuration Options for Accounts|account settings window]], with default account first, and any additional accounts listed in the order you added them. If you are not seeing the Message List Header, click {menu ≡} > {menu View} > {menu Layout} > {menu Folder Pane}.

Within each account, special folders ({filepath Inbox}, {filepath Sent}, {filepath Trash}) will be listed first with unique icons, while other folders will appear in alphabetical order. 

Sub-folders will appear underneath the parent folder. To expand or collapse an account or parent folder, click on the arrow beside the account or parent folder, or double  click on the name.

You can [[Switching the folder pane view|choose your preferred view(s) of the Folder Pane]]. 

= 6. Quick Filter Bar = 
The Quick Filter Bar helps you sort your message list based on specific criteria.  See [[Quick Filter Toolbar|Quick Filter Bar]].

= 7. Message List Pane = 
In table view, the Message List Pane displays the list of messages of the selected folder as columns, with details like date/time, subject, sender, and more. To pick which details are displayed, and how wide each column is, see [[Message List Columns]]. To change to cards view, click on the "Message list display options" icon [[Image:tb115-display-options-icon-offical-from-micah]] > {menu Cards View}.

= 8. Message Header Pane = 
The Message ''''''Header'''''' Pane (just above the message pane) will show you information about the selected message, such as the ''''From'''', ''''To'''', and ''''Subject'''' headers, as well as the date/time of the message. 

You can also take actions on the message, such as reply, forward, archive, mark as junk or as read and delete. 

''''More actions'''' are available under down arrow, such as redirect, tag, mark as read,  save, print, convert to event or task, view source, repair text encoding, and message body. The last action is ''''Customize'''' message header settings, where you can choose how the message header is displayed. 

Click on the avatar beside a contact to add that person to your address book, and the avatar will change to blue. If the contact is in your address book, the avatar color will be blue and you can edit or delete the address book entry.

= 9. Message Pane =
The Message Pane is where you see the content of the selected message. To show/hide the Message Pane, press {key F8}, or click {menu ≡} > {menu View} > {menu Layout} > {menu Message Pane}.

= 10. Today Pane = 
The Today Pane will display information from your calendar, such as any events scheduled for today, tomorrow, and upcoming events (by default within the next 5 days).
Click on the arrows at the top of the Today Pane to switch to the ''''Events and Tasks'''' view, which will include your calendar tasks as well as events, or the ''''Tasks'''' view which will only include your calendar tasks, not events.

To hide the Today Pane, click on the {button X} beside the arrows. To bring it back, click on {menu Today Pane} in the Status Bar. You can also show/hide the Today Pane, by pressing {key F11}.

= 11. Status Bar =

The Status Bar from left to right:
* A button to switch back and forth from online to offline and vice versa.
* An area to display status messages about operations like downloading email, compacting folders etc.
* A button to switch back and forth between displaying the "Today Pane" and not displaying it.

The goal over time is remove the Status Bar and move its functions to more contextually relevant places. For example, the Unread and Total counts that used to be in the Status Bar in pre Supernova releases have been moved to the individual folders.

= Vertical View Layout with Card View =

The following screenshot shows the Vertical View Layout with Card View. To see this view: 
# select "Vertical View" as follows: click {menu ≡} > {menu View} > {menu Layout} > {menu Vertical View} and then 
# select "Card View": (to the right of {button Quick Filter}) click on the "Message list display options" icon [[Image:tb115-display-options-icon-offical-from-micah]] > {menu Cards View}.

[[Image:tb115-vertical-card-view]] 

This configuration has most of the same components with the same features as their counterparts in "Classic View Layout with Table View":
* 1. Spaces Toolbar  
* 2. Unified Toolbar  
* 3. Tab Bar 
* 4. Message List Header 
* 5. Folder Pane 
* 6. Quick Filter Bar 
* 7. Message List Pane  
* 8. Message Pane
* 9. Today Pane  
* 10. Status Bar 
* 11. One of the cards in Card View
Card view (one of the cards is highlighted in red, see #11), is a multi-line, non-column alternative view of the message list. Version 115 has a two line "card" for each message in the Message List Pane. The first line has the sender''s display name (not the actual email address), time and at the top right the ''''Message Actions'''' menu, {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''''kebab'''''' menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab). The second line displays the subject. 

Version 128 and newer has a three line "card" for each message in the Message List Pane. The third line adds information about the message thread (if there is more than one message in that thread), tags and starred status.','<div class="note"> For versions of Thunderbird prior to Thunderbird 115 Supernova, please refer to: <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-main-window">Getting started with the Thunderbird main window</a>.</div>
<p>This article describes Thunderbird''s main window for Thunderbird 115 Supernova and newer versions.
</p><p>There are many ways to configure Thunderbird''s main window. This article describes two popular configurations:
</p>
<ul><li> Classic View Layout with Table View for the Message List Pane
</li><li> Vertical View Layout with Card View for the Message List Pane
</li></ul>
<p>Refer also to the many <a href="/en-US/kb/keyboard-shortcuts-thunderbird">keyboard shortcuts</a> available in the main window to help you quickly perform functions, such as message actions and navigation, searching and calendar actions. 
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_classic-view-layout-with-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Classic View Layout with Table View</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_1-spaces-toolbar"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">1. Spaces Toolbar</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_2-unified-toolbar"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">2. Unified Toolbar</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_3-tab-bar"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">3. Tab Bar</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_4-message-list-header"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">4. Message List Header</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_5-folder-pane"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">5. Folder Pane</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_6-quick-filter-bar"><span class="tocnumber">7</span> <span class="toctext">6. Quick Filter Bar</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_7-message-list-pane"><span class="tocnumber">8</span> <span class="toctext">7. Message List Pane</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_8-message-header-pane"><span class="tocnumber">9</span> <span class="toctext">8. Message Header Pane</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_9-message-pane"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">9. Message Pane</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_10-today-pane"><span class="tocnumber">11</span> <span class="toctext">10. Today Pane</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_11-status-bar"><span class="tocnumber">12</span> <span class="toctext">11. Status Bar</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_vertical-view-layout-with-card-view"><span class="tocnumber">13</span> <span class="toctext">Vertical View Layout with Card View</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_classic-view-layout-with-table-view">Classic View Layout with Table View</h1>
<p>The following screenshot shows the Classic View Layout with Table View. To see this view: 
</p>
<ol><li> select "Classic View" as follows: click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">View</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Layout</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Classic View</span> and then 
</li><li> select "Table View": (to the right of <span class="button">Quick Filter</span>) click on the "Message list display options" icon <img alt="tb115-display-options-icon-offical-from-micah" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2023-07-09-20-04-06-4a2c27.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> &gt; <span class="menu">Table View</span>
</li></ol>
<p><img alt="tb115-classic-table-view" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2023-07-06-21-21-08-fb78b9.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</p>
<h1 id="w_1-spaces-toolbar">1. Spaces Toolbar</h1>
<p>Since version 102, Thunderbird has had a central Spaces Toolbar for fast and easy access to your most important activities. Click on the buttons to move between the various "Spaces": Mail, Address Book, Calendar, Tasks, Chat, and your  add-ons. At the bottom of the Spaces Toolbar, there is a button for hiding the Spaces Toolbar. Above this, is a button to change Settings. More details at <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-102">New in Thunderbird 102</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_2-unified-toolbar">2. Unified Toolbar</h1>
<p>There is a new “Unified Toolbar” on top of the Tab Bar, which is fully screenreader and keyboard accessible.  This toolbar is used for all  “Spaces” of the Spaces Toolbar, which are  Mail, Address Book, Calendar, Tasks, Chat and Settings. More details at <a href="/en-US/kb/unified-toolbar">Unified Toolbar</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_3-tab-bar">3. Tab Bar</h1>
<p>In Supernova,  the Tab Bar is only displayed if you have two or more tabs. For example, if you have a Mail tab and a Calendar Tab, the Tab Bar is visible. If you just have one tab like the Mail tab, the Tab Bar automatically disappears.
</p>
<h1 id="w_4-message-list-header">4. Message List Header</h1>
<p>The Message List Header is new for 115. It shows the current folder name, number of messages, "Quick Filter", and “Message list display options” icon <img alt="tb115-display-options-icon-offical-from-micah" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2023-07-09-20-04-06-4a2c27.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">. If you are not seeing the Message List Header, click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">View</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Layout</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Message List Header</span>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_5-folder-pane">5. Folder Pane</h1>
<p>The Folder Pane is where your accounts and folders will appear. It will show the account name(s) specified in the <a href="/en-US/kb/configuration-options-accounts">account settings window</a>, with default account first, and any additional accounts listed in the order you added them. If you are not seeing the Message List Header, click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">View</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Layout</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Folder Pane</span>.
</p><p>Within each account, special folders (<span class="filepath">Inbox</span>, <span class="filepath">Sent</span>, <span class="filepath">Trash</span>) will be listed first with unique icons, while other folders will appear in alphabetical order. 
</p><p>Sub-folders will appear underneath the parent folder. To expand or collapse an account or parent folder, click on the arrow beside the account or parent folder, or double  click on the name.
</p><p>You can <a href="/en-US/kb/switching-folder-pane-view">choose your preferred view(s) of the Folder Pane</a>. 
</p>
<h1 id="w_6-quick-filter-bar">6. Quick Filter Bar</h1>
<p>The Quick Filter Bar helps you sort your message list based on specific criteria.  See <a href="/en-US/kb/quick-filter-toolbar">Quick Filter Bar</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_7-message-list-pane">7. Message List Pane</h1>
<p>In table view, the Message List Pane displays the list of messages of the selected folder as columns, with details like date/time, subject, sender, and more. To pick which details are displayed, and how wide each column is, see <a href="/en-US/kb/message-list-columns">Message List Columns</a>. To change to cards view, click on the "Message list display options" icon <img alt="tb115-display-options-icon-offical-from-micah" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2023-07-09-20-04-06-4a2c27.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> &gt; <span class="menu">Cards View</span>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_8-message-header-pane">8. Message Header Pane</h1>
<p>The Message <strong>Header</strong> Pane (just above the message pane) will show you information about the selected message, such as the <em>From</em>, <em>To</em>, and <em>Subject</em> headers, as well as the date/time of the message. 
</p><p>You can also take actions on the message, such as reply, forward, archive, mark as junk or as read and delete. 
</p><p><em>More actions</em> are available under down arrow, such as redirect, tag, mark as read,  save, print, convert to event or task, view source, repair text encoding, and message body. The last action is <em>Customize</em> message header settings, where you can choose how the message header is displayed. 
</p><p>Click on the avatar beside a contact to add that person to your address book, and the avatar will change to blue. If the contact is in your address book, the avatar color will be blue and you can edit or delete the address book entry.
</p>
<h1 id="w_9-message-pane">9. Message Pane</h1>
<p>The Message Pane is where you see the content of the selected message. To show/hide the Message Pane, press <span class="key">F8</span>, or click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">View</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Layout</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Message Pane</span>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_10-today-pane">10. Today Pane</h1>
<p>The Today Pane will display information from your calendar, such as any events scheduled for today, tomorrow, and upcoming events (by default within the next 5 days).
Click on the arrows at the top of the Today Pane to switch to the <em>Events and Tasks</em> view, which will include your calendar tasks as well as events, or the <em>Tasks</em> view which will only include your calendar tasks, not events.
</p><p>To hide the Today Pane, click on the <span class="button">X</span> beside the arrows. To bring it back, click on <span class="menu">Today Pane</span> in the Status Bar. You can also show/hide the Today Pane, by pressing <span class="key">F11</span>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_11-status-bar">11. Status Bar</h1>
<p>The Status Bar from left to right:
</p>
<ul><li> A button to switch back and forth from online to offline and vice versa.
</li><li> An area to display status messages about operations like downloading email, compacting folders etc.
</li><li> A button to switch back and forth between displaying the "Today Pane" and not displaying it.
</li></ul>
<p>The goal over time is remove the Status Bar and move its functions to more contextually relevant places. For example, the Unread and Total counts that used to be in the Status Bar in pre Supernova releases have been moved to the individual folders.
</p>
<h1 id="w_vertical-view-layout-with-card-view">Vertical View Layout with Card View</h1>
<p>The following screenshot shows the Vertical View Layout with Card View. To see this view: 
</p>
<ol><li> select "Vertical View" as follows: click <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">View</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Layout</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Vertical View</span> and then 
</li><li> select "Card View": (to the right of <span class="button">Quick Filter</span>) click on the "Message list display options" icon <img alt="tb115-display-options-icon-offical-from-micah" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2023-07-09-20-04-06-4a2c27.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> &gt; <span class="menu">Cards View</span>.
</li></ol>
<p><img alt="tb115-vertical-card-view" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2023-07-06-22-49-37-2dd39c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</p><p>This configuration has most of the same components with the same features as their counterparts in "Classic View Layout with Table View":
</p>
<ul><li> 1. Spaces Toolbar  
</li><li> 2. Unified Toolbar  
</li><li> 3. Tab Bar 
</li><li> 4. Message List Header 
</li><li> 5. Folder Pane 
</li><li> 6. Quick Filter Bar 
</li><li> 7. Message List Pane  
</li><li> 8. Message Pane
</li><li> 9. Today Pane  
</li><li> 10. Status Bar 
</li><li> 11. One of the cards in Card View
</li></ul>
<p>Card view (one of the cards is highlighted in red, see #11), is a multi-line, non-column alternative view of the message list. Version 115 has a two line "card" for each message in the Message List Pane. The first line has the sender''s display name (not the actual email address), time and at the top right the <em>Message Actions</em> menu, <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <strong>kebab</strong> menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab). The second line displays the subject. 
</p><p>Version 128 and newer has a three line "card" for each message in the Message List Pane. The third line adds information about the message thread (if there is more than one message in that thread), tags and starred status.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "291154", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jan 6, 2025, 8:49:27 PM", "datetime": "2025-01-06T20:49:27.176754-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Please do not localize needs Wayne''s approval. see https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/74#issuecomment-2574055401", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jan 6, 2025, 8:50:47 PM", "datetime": "2025-01-06T20:50:47.064675-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:29:42+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (291196,'en-US','configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','Configure push email for Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android/revision/291196',288703,'2025-01-07T21:30:56.967520-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/8#issuecomment-2576784521',1,'2025-01-07T21:31:26.139625-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2025-01-15T08:12:47.499469-08:00','rtanglao','approved','By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.
__TOC__
==Turn on push email for a folder==
{warning}WARNING: The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu ≡ > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}  > ''''''your email account'''''' > {menu Fetching mail} > {menu Advanced} > {menu Max folders to check with push}. Thunderbird does not warn you when this limit is exceeded. Exceeding this limit will result in push email not working on some of the folders you configured for push.{/warning}
# Tap {button ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account e.g. your ''''''Gmail'''''' account  > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap ''''''Inbox''''''  to enable push email for your Inbox.
#;[[Image:enable-push-tb-android-8]]
# Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable Push''''''. 
# Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable sync''''''.
{note}The ''''''Enable sync'''''' setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.{/note}
Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled.
;[[Image:bell-icon-android-system-bar-tb8-pushmail-notification]] 
===Alarms & Reminders Permission for Android 13 and above===
{note}This section is not applicable to you if your Android version is older than Android 13.{/note}
# On Android 13 and above, a notification will let you know you need to grant the ''''''Alarms & reminders''''''  permission. Proceed to the permissions screen by tapping the {button Missing permission to schedule alarms} notification.
#;[[Image:missing-permission-tb8-android-pushmail]]
# Add this permission by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Allow setting alarms and reminders''''''.  If you do not grant this permission, then push email will not work.
#;[[Image:allow-setting-alarms-reminders-tb8-android-pushmail]]
== The push email service notification==
* Once the permission is granted (or right after enabling push on older Android versions), Thunderbird for Android will display a push email service notification entitled ''''''Waiting for new emails'''''':
*;[[Image:notification-waiting-for-new-emails]]
* Tapping on the {button Waiting for new emails} notification will allow you to configure the notification itself ({button Configure notification}) or to disable push email altogether ({button Disable Push}):
*;[[Image:configure-notification-or-disable-push]]
[[UI:details_start]] 
==Configure the push email service notification using "Configure notification"==
You can change the display of this notification or hide it by tapping {button Configure notification}.
;[[Image:notification-settings-tb8-android-pushmail]]
==== Hide the push email service notification ====
Hiding the push email service notification does not turn off push email. 
* Slide ''''''Show notifications'''''' to the left. 
==== Change the push email service notification ====
Minimizing the notification will hide the bell icon from the Android status bar, but still keep the notification in the notification shade.  You will still be able to see the status of your push email service (e.g. ''''''Waiting for new emails'''''' or ''''''Sleeping until network is available'''''').
[[UI:details_end]] 
[[UI:details_start]] 
==Disable Push email from the push email service notification using "Disable Push"==
Tap {button Disable Push} to disable push email altogether.
[[UI:details_end]] 
[[UI:details_start]] 
==Turn off push email for a folder==
# Tap {button ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account e.g. your Gmail account  > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example, tap ''''''Inbox''''''  to disable push email for your Inbox.
# Turn off push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable Push''''''. 
# Turn on sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable sync''''''. 
[[UI:details_end]] 
== New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification ==
The notifications for new email messages are configured separately from the push email service notification. New email notifications are configured as follows: 
* Tap the application menu {button ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > {menu Notifications} > {menu Messages} under ''''''Notification categories''''''.
==Learn more==
* Wikipedia: [https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Push_email Push email]
* Google: [https://support.google.com/android/answer/9079661 Control notifications on Android]','<p>By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Turn on push email for a folder</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_alarms-reminders-permission-for-android-13-and-above"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Alarms &amp; Reminders Permission for Android 13 and above</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">The push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_configure-the-push-email-service-notification-using-configure-notification"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Configure the push email service notification using "Configure notification"</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_hide-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Hide the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_change-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">3.2</span> <span class="toctext">Change the push email service notification</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_disable-push-email-from-the-push-email-service-notification-using-disable-push"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Disable Push email from the push email service notification using "Disable Push"</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-off-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Turn off push email for a folder</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_new-email-notifications-are-completely-separate-from-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_learn-more"><span class="tocnumber">7</span> <span class="toctext">Learn more</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder">Turn on push email for a folder</h2>
<div class="warning">WARNING: The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu ≡ &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>  &gt; <strong>your email account</strong> &gt; <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Advanced</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Max folders to check with push</span>. Thunderbird does not warn you when this limit is exceeded. Exceeding this limit will result in push email not working on some of the folders you configured for push.</div>
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap <span class="button">Show accounts</span> at the bottom of the screen.
</li><li> Tap account e.g. your <strong>Gmail</strong> account  &gt; tap <span class="button">Manage folders</span>.
</li><li> Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap <strong>Inbox</strong>  to enable push email for your Inbox.
<dl><dt><img alt="enable-push-tb-android-8" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-10-00-62ddea.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Enable Push</strong>. 
</li><li> Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for <strong>Enable sync</strong>.
</li></ol>
<div class="note">The <strong>Enable sync</strong> setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.</div>
<p>Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled.
</p>
<dl><dt><img alt="bell-icon-android-system-bar-tb8-pushmail-notification" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-15-19-df30c1.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
<h3 id="w_alarms-reminders-permission-for-android-13-and-above">Alarms &amp; Reminders Permission for Android 13 and above</h3>
<div class="note">This section is not applicable to you if your Android version is older than Android 13.</div>
<ol><li> On Android 13 and above, a notification will let you know you need to grant the <strong>Alarms &amp; reminders</strong>  permission. Proceed to the permissions screen by tapping the <span class="button">Missing permission to schedule alarms</span> notification.
<dl><dt><img alt="missing-permission-tb8-android-pushmail" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-21-43-416308.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Add this permission by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Allow setting alarms and reminders</strong>.  If you do not grant this permission, then push email will not work.
<dl><dt><img alt="allow-setting-alarms-reminders-tb8-android-pushmail" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-29-13-66fbe3.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_the-push-email-service-notification">The push email service notification</h2>
<ul><li> Once the permission is granted (or right after enabling push on older Android versions), Thunderbird for Android will display a push email service notification entitled <strong>Waiting for new emails</strong>:
<dl><dt><img alt="notification-waiting-for-new-emails" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-15-14-39-10-32ff52.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Tapping on the <span class="button">Waiting for new emails</span> notification will allow you to configure the notification itself (<span class="button">Configure notification</span>) or to disable push email altogether (<span class="button">Disable Push</span>):
<dl><dt><img alt="configure-notification-or-disable-push" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-15-13-50-14-2997ea.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ul>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details"> 
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_configure-the-push-email-service-notification-using-configure-notification" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Configure the push email service notification using "Configure notification"</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>You can change the display of this notification or hide it by tapping <span class="button">Configure notification</span>.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="notification-settings-tb8-android-pushmail" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-34-51-59f0a4.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl><h4 id="w_hide-the-push-email-service-notification">Hide the push email service notification</h4><p>Hiding the push email service notification does not turn off push email. 
</p><ul><li> Slide <strong>Show notifications</strong> to the left. 
</li></ul><h4 id="w_change-the-push-email-service-notification">Change the push email service notification</h4><p>Minimizing the notification will hide the bell icon from the Android status bar, but still keep the notification in the notification shade.  You will still be able to see the status of your push email service (e.g. <strong>Waiting for new emails</strong> or <strong>Sleeping until network is available</strong>).
</p></div>






</section> 
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details"> 
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_disable-push-email-from-the-push-email-service-notification-using-disable-push" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Disable Push email from the push email service notification using "Disable Push"</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true">Tap <span class="button">Disable Push</span> to disable push email altogether.
</p></section> 
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details"> 
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_turn-off-push-email-for-a-folder" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Turn off push email for a folder</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap <span class="button">Show accounts</span> at the bottom of the screen.
</li><li> Tap account e.g. your Gmail account  &gt; tap <span class="button">Manage folders</span>.
</li><li> Tap your folder of choice. For example, tap <strong>Inbox</strong>  to disable push email for your Inbox.
</li><li> Turn off push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for <strong>Enable Push</strong>. 
</li><li> Turn on sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Enable sync</strong>. 
</li></ol><p></p></div>

</section> 
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_new-email-notifications-are-completely-separate-from-the-push-email-service-notification">New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification</h2>
<p>The notifications for new email messages are configured separately from the push email service notification. New email notifications are configured as follows: 
</p>
<ul><li> Tap the application menu <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Notifications</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Messages</span> under <strong>Notification categories</strong>.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_learn-more">Learn more</h2>
<ul><li> Wikipedia: <a href="https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Push_email">Push email</a>
</li><li> Google: <a href="https://support.google.com/android/answer/9079661">Control notifications on Android</a>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "291196", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jan 7, 2025, 9:30:56 PM", "datetime": "2025-01-07T21:30:56.967520-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/8#issuecomment-2576784521", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jan 7, 2025, 9:31:26 PM", "datetime": "2025-01-07T21:31:26.139625-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jan 15, 2025, 8:12:47 AM", "datetime": "2025-01-15T08:12:47.499469-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:29:39+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (291395,'en-US','thunderbird-android-import','Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import/revision/291395',287770,'2025-01-13T08:29:59.421145-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','wrap in note tag',1,'2025-01-13T08:30:48.242620-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','{note}The transfer process supports account settings and account passwords. Emails and other data are not transfered.{/note}

{warning}This feature is still being developed as part of Thunderbird for Android and Thunderbird for Desktop. [https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=net.thunderbird.android.beta Upgrade to the latest version of Thunderbird for Android beta] for the latest version on Android.{/warning}

