</li><li> Ask and help with <strong>Daily</strong>-specific questions in the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/daily">Thunderbird Daily topicbox community mailing list</a>.
</li><li> <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird">Report bugs</a> that you find. Report performance issues by <a href="/en-US/kb/profiling-thunderbird-performance">creating a performance profile</a> and adding it to your bug report or support posting.
</li><li> <strong>Daily</strong> does not have Release Notes. But you can get a sense, after the fact, by looking at  <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/notes/beta">Beta release notes</a>.  Or following <a href="https://hg.mozilla.org/comm-central/">comm-central checkings via the web page</a> or subscribing to the <a href="https://hg.mozilla.org/comm-central/rss-log">comm-central RSS feed</a>.
</li><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/mozilla-crash-reporter-tb">Please submit <strong>all</strong> crash reports</a>.
</li><li> Backup your profile with <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Tools</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Export</span>.
</li><li> Review the <strong>Daily</strong> Start Page which has handy information, accessed in Thunderbird with <span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;"> <span class="key">ALT</span> &gt; </span><span class="menu">Go</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Mail Start Page</span> (<a href="/en-US/kb/keyboard-shortcuts-thunderbird#w_moving-around-thunderbird">keyboard shortcuts</a>), or  <a href="https://start.thunderbird.net/en-US/daily/">in your browser</a>.  
</li><li> Join us in <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">other ways to contribute to the project.</a>
