<h1 id="w_channel-details">Channel Details</h1>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-release-channel-default">Thunderbird Release Channel (Default)</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Users who want a Thunderbird that is stable and regularly updated<br>
<strong>Update frequency:</strong> Every four weeks<br>
<strong>Download:</strong> <a href="https://thunderbird.net/download/release">https://thunderbird.net/download/release</a><br>
</p><p>Thunderbird Release, introduced in 2025, is the default channel of Thunderbird that most users should download and use. It receives updates every four weeks that include new features, improvements, bug fixes, and security patches. This channel represents the best balance between new functionality and stability.
</p><p>Learn more in our <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release">Thunderbird Release</a> support article.  Want to know why we made this our default? Check out our <a href="https://blog.thunderbird.net/2025/02/thunderbird-desktop-release-channel-default-download/">blog post on the new default release</a> and <a href="https://blog.thunderbird.net/2025/03/thunderbird-release-channel-update/">more details on the channel update</a>. 
</p>
<div class="note">May not be compatible with all add-ons.  Please <a class="new" href="/en-US/kb/new?title=ensure+your+Thunderbird+add-on+is+supported" title="Page does not exist.">ensure your Thunderbird add-on is supported</a> before downloading.</div>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-extended-support-release-channel-esr">Thunderbird Extended Support Release Channel (ESR)</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Users or organizations that prioritize long-term stability over new features<br>
<strong>Update frequency:</strong> Once per year (with occasional security updates)<br>
<strong>Download:</strong> <a href="https://thunderbird.net/download/esr">https://thunderbird.net/download/esr</a><br>
</p><p>The ESR channel of Thunderbird is ideal for users who prefer minimal changes to their software during most of the year. It receives important security updates but fewer feature changes over time. This is a great option for managed environments, like businesses or schools, where consistent behavior and low maintenance are key. Learn more in our <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-esr">Thunderbird ESR</a> support article.
</p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-beta-channel">Thunderbird Beta Channel</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Users who want to test upcoming features and help improve Thunderbird<br>
Update frequency: Frequent updates, before they reach the Thunderbird Release Channel<br>
Download: <a href="https://thunderbird.net/download/beta">https://thunderbird.net/download/beta</a><br>
</p><p>Thunderbird Beta gives you early access to new features before they become part of the Thunderbird Release Channel. It is more stable than Daily but still in active testing. You might encounter occasional bugs, and your reports of these bugs to our team is important for improving Thunderbird. Learn more in our <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> support article.
</p>
<div class="warning">May not be compatible with all add-ons.  Please <a class="new" href="/en-US/kb/new?title=ensure+your+Thunderbird+add-on+is+supported" title="Page does not exist.">ensure your Thunderbird add-on is supported</a> before downloading.</div>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-daily-channel">Thunderbird Daily Channel</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Adventurous users who want the absolute latest and don’t mind risk<br>
<strong>Update frequency:</strong> Daily<br>
<strong>Download:</strong> <a href="https://thunderbird.net/download/daily">https://thunderbird.net/download/daily</a><br>
</p><p>This is the cutting edge of Thunderbird development. The Daily Channel is where new code lands first, and it can be unstable or break entirely. It’s meant for contributors and experienced testers who are comfortable troubleshooting issues, and data loss is possible. If that sounds like you, check out our <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-daily">Thunderbird Daily</a> support article.
</p>
<div class="warning">May not be compatible with all add-ons.  Please <a class="new" href="/en-US/kb/new?title=ensure+your+Thunderbird+add-on+is+supported" title="Page does not exist.">ensure your Thunderbird add-on is supported</a> before downloading.</div>
<p><br>
<strong>Still unsure which channel to use? Start with the Thunderbird Release Channel. You can always switch later if your needs change.
</strong>
<strong></strong>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "296368", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 1, 2025, 9:06:14 AM", "datetime": "2025-05-01T09:06:14.048699-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "remove Standard, \"channel\" is a made up jargony word so quote it in the first citation", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:29:04+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (296516,'en-US','thunderbird-smtp-ehlo','How Thunderbird for Android avoids leaking your IP address to SMTP servers','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-smtp-ehlo','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-smtp-ehlo/revision/296516',NULL,'2025-05-07T08:24:27.545761-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','typos and some formatting changes',1,'2025-05-08T07:57:13.418042-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2025-05-12T11:42:02.248435-07:00','rtanglao','approved','Thunderbird sends email using the Internet standard [http://wikipedia.org/wiki/Simple_Mail_Transfer_Protocol SMTP] protocol. As part of this, the ''''''EHLO'''''' (or ''''''HELO'''''') command is used to identify the client to the mail server. This step typically includes a hostname or IP address.

If Thunderbird were to send your real IP address during this handshake, it could reveal information about your location or network. This can happen even if you''re using privacy tools like a VPN or proxy. In some cases, the server you’re sending mail through may include the ''''''EHLO'''''' information in the ''''''Received'''''' header of the message. This means the recipient could potentially see your original IP address.

To protect your privacy, Thunderbird uses a generic hostname: ''''''ehlo.thunderbird.net''''''. This address is only used as an identifier in the SMTP conversation. There is no mail server behind it. No emails are ever sent through this hostname.

Using ''''''ehlo.thunderbird.net'''''' helps maintain protocol compliance while avoiding exposure of your real IP address. Thunderbird does not collect or store any information through this mechanism. Your email content, connections, and metadata remain private. Please see https://www.thunderbird.net/privacy for more details.','<p>Thunderbird sends email using the Internet standard <a href="http://wikipedia.org/wiki/Simple_Mail_Transfer_Protocol">SMTP</a> protocol. As part of this, the <strong>EHLO</strong> (or <strong>HELO</strong>) command is used to identify the client to the mail server. This step typically includes a hostname or IP address.
</p><p>If Thunderbird were to send your real IP address during this handshake, it could reveal information about your location or network. This can happen even if you''re using privacy tools like a VPN or proxy. In some cases, the server you’re sending mail through may include the <strong>EHLO</strong> information in the <strong>Received</strong> header of the message. This means the recipient could potentially see your original IP address.
</p><p>To protect your privacy, Thunderbird uses a generic hostname: <strong><a href="http://ehlo.thunderbird.net">ehlo.thunderbird.net</a></strong>. This address is only used as an identifier in the SMTP conversation. There is no mail server behind it. No emails are ever sent through this hostname.
</p><p>Using <strong><a href="http://ehlo.thunderbird.net">ehlo.thunderbird.net</a></strong> helps maintain protocol compliance while avoiding exposure of your real IP address. Thunderbird does not collect or store any information through this mechanism. Your email content, connections, and metadata remain private. Please see <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/privacy">https://www.thunderbird.net/privacy</a> for more details.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "296516", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 7, 2025, 8:24:27 AM", "datetime": "2025-05-07T08:24:27.545761-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "typos and some formatting changes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 8, 2025, 7:57:13 AM", "datetime": "2025-05-08T07:57:13.418042-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "May 12, 2025, 11:42:02 AM", "datetime": "2025-05-12T11:42:02.248435-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:29:02+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (296544,'en-US','thunderbird-smtp-ehlo-redirect-1','Protecting your privacy when sending email using SMTP and EHLO','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-smtp-ehlo-redirect-1','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-smtp-ehlo-redirect-1/revision/296544',NULL,'2025-05-08T12:57:10.291702-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','REDIRECT [[How Thunderbird for Android avoids leaking your IP address to SMTP servers]]','<p>REDIRECT <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-smtp-ehlo">How Thunderbird for Android avoids leaking your IP address to SMTP servers</a>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "296544", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 8, 2025, 12:57:10 PM", "datetime": "2025-05-08T12:57:10.291702-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:29:00+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (297629,'en-US','configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','Configure push email for Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android/revision/297629',293371,'2025-05-29T16:08:41.477596-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','for some reason "New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification" and "Learn more" were in a super large font. Not sure why. Deleted a blank line and that fixed it by luck?!?',1,'2025-05-29T16:09:59.825967-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.

__TOC__

=Turn on push email for a folder=
{warning}
WARNING:
* If you kill the Thunderbird for Android app, for example by swiping up on the recent task window, push email will stop working. Thunderbird needs to be running, and it needs network access for push email to work.
* The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu ≡ > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > ''''''your email account'''''' > {menu Fetching mail} > {menu Advanced} > {menu Max folders to check with push}. Thunderbird does not warn you when this limit is exceeded. Exceeding this limit will result in push email not working on some of the folders you configured for push.
{/warning}
# Tap {button ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account, for example your Gmail account > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap ''''''Inbox'''''' to enable push email for your Inbox.
#;[[Image:enable-push-tb-android-8]]
# Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable Push''''''.
# Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable sync''''''.
{note}The ''''''Enable sync'''''' setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.{/note}
Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled.
;[[Image:bell-icon-android-system-bar-tb8-pushmail-notification]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Alarms & reminders permission for Android 13 and above==
{note}This section is not applicable to you if your Android version is older than Android 13.{/note}
# On Android 13 and above, a notification will let you know you need to grant the ''''Alarms & reminders'''' permission. Proceed to the permissions screen by tapping the {button Missing permission to schedule alarms} notification.
#;[[Image:missing-permission-tb8-android-pushmail]]
# Add this permission by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Allow setting alarms and reminders''''''. If you do not grant this permission, then push email will not work.
#;[[Image:allow-setting-alarms-reminders-tb8-android-pushmail]]

=The push email service notification=
* Once the permission is granted (or right after enabling push on older Android versions), Thunderbird for Android will display a push email service notification entitled ''''''Waiting for new emails'''''':
*;[[Image:notification-waiting-for-new-emails]]
* Tapping on the {button Waiting for new emails} notification will allow you to configure the notification itself ({button Configure notification}) or to disable push email altogether ({button Disable Push}):
*;[[Image:configure-notification-or-disable-push]]

==Configure the push email service notification using “Configure notification”==
You can change the display of this notification or hide it by tapping {button Configure notification}.
;[[Image:notification-settings-tb8-android-pushmail]]

===Hide the push email service notification===
Hiding the push email service notification does not turn off push email.
* Slide ''''''Show notifications'''''' to the left.

===Change the push email service notification===
Minimizing the notification will hide the bell icon from the Android status bar, but still keep the notification in the notification shade. You will still be able to see the status of your push email service (for example, ''''''Waiting for new emails'''''' or ''''''Sleeping until network is available'''''').

===Disable Push email from the push email service notification using “Disable Push”===
Tap {button Disable Push} to disable push email altogether.
[[UI:details_end]]

=Turn off push email for a folder=
# Tap {button ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account, for example, your Gmail account > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example, tap ''''''Inbox'''''' to disable push email for your Inbox.
# Turn off push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable Push''''''.
# Turn on sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable sync''''''.
[[UI:details_end]]

=New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification=
The notifications for new email messages are configured separately from the push email service notification. New email notifications are configured as follows:
* Tap the application menu {button ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > {menu Notifications} > {menu Messages} under ''''Notification categories''''.

=Learn more=
* Wikipedia: [https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Push_email Push email]
* Google: [https://support.google.com/android/answer/9079661 Control notifications on Android]','<p>By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Turn on push email for a folder</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_alarms-reminders-permission-for-android-13-and-above"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Alarms &amp; reminders permission for Android 13 and above</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">The push email service notification</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_configure-the-push-email-service-notification-using-configure-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Configure the push email service notification using “Configure notification”</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_hide-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Hide the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_change-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Change the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_disable-push-email-from-the-push-email-service-notification-using-disable-push"><span class="tocnumber">2.1.3</span> <span class="toctext">Disable Push email from the push email service notification using “Disable Push”</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-off-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Turn off push email for a folder</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_new-email-notifications-are-completely-separate-from-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_learn-more"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Learn more</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder">Turn on push email for a folder</h1>
<div class="warning">
<p>WARNING:
</p>
<ul><li> If you kill the Thunderbird for Android app, for example by swiping up on the recent task window, push email will stop working. Thunderbird needs to be running, and it needs network access for push email to work.
</li><li> The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu ≡ &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <strong>your email account</strong> &gt; <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Advanced</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Max folders to check with push</span>. Thunderbird does not warn you when this limit is exceeded. Exceeding this limit will result in push email not working on some of the folders you configured for push.
</li></ul>
</div>
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap <span class="button">Show accounts</span> at the bottom of the screen.
</li><li> Tap account, for example your Gmail account &gt; tap <span class="button">Manage folders</span>.
</li><li> Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap <strong>Inbox</strong> to enable push email for your Inbox.
<dl><dt><img alt="enable-push-tb-android-8" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-10-00-62ddea.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Enable Push</strong>.
</li><li> Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for <strong>Enable sync</strong>.
</li></ol>
<div class="note">The <strong>Enable sync</strong> setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.</div>
<p>Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled.
</p>
<dl><dt><img alt="bell-icon-android-system-bar-tb8-pushmail-notification" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-15-19-df30c1.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_alarms-reminders-permission-for-android-13-and-above" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Alarms &amp; reminders permission for Android 13 and above</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><div class="note">This section is not applicable to you if your Android version is older than Android 13.</div><ol><li> On Android 13 and above, a notification will let you know you need to grant the <em>Alarms &amp; reminders</em> permission. Proceed to the permissions screen by tapping the <span class="button">Missing permission to schedule alarms</span> notification.
<dl><dt><img alt="missing-permission-tb8-android-pushmail" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-21-43-416308.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Add this permission by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Allow setting alarms and reminders</strong>. If you do not grant this permission, then push email will not work.
<dl><dt><img alt="allow-setting-alarms-reminders-tb8-android-pushmail" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-29-13-66fbe3.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol><h1 id="w_the-push-email-service-notification">The push email service notification</h1><ul><li> Once the permission is granted (or right after enabling push on older Android versions), Thunderbird for Android will display a push email service notification entitled <strong>Waiting for new emails</strong>:
<dl><dt><img alt="notification-waiting-for-new-emails" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-15-14-39-10-32ff52.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Tapping on the <span class="button">Waiting for new emails</span> notification will allow you to configure the notification itself (<span class="button">Configure notification</span>) or to disable push email altogether (<span class="button">Disable Push</span>):
<dl><dt><img alt="configure-notification-or-disable-push" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-15-13-50-14-2997ea.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ul></div>




<h2 id="w_configure-the-push-email-service-notification-using-configure-notification" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Configure the push email service notification using “Configure notification”</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><p>You can change the display of this notification or hide it by tapping <span class="button">Configure notification</span>.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="notification-settings-tb8-android-pushmail" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-34-51-59f0a4.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl><h3 id="w_hide-the-push-email-service-notification">Hide the push email service notification</h3><p>Hiding the push email service notification does not turn off push email.
</p><ul><li> Slide <strong>Show notifications</strong> to the left.
</li></ul><h3 id="w_change-the-push-email-service-notification">Change the push email service notification</h3><p>Minimizing the notification will hide the bell icon from the Android status bar, but still keep the notification in the notification shade. You will still be able to see the status of your push email service (for example, <strong>Waiting for new emails</strong> or <strong>Sleeping until network is available</strong>).
</p><h3 id="w_disable-push-email-from-the-push-email-service-notification-using-disable-push">Disable Push email from the push email service notification using “Disable Push”</h3><p>Tap <span class="button">Disable Push</span> to disable push email altogether.
</p></div>








</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_turn-off-push-email-for-a-folder">Turn off push email for a folder</h1>
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap <span class="button">Show accounts</span> at the bottom of the screen.
</li><li> Tap account, for example, your Gmail account &gt; tap <span class="button">Manage folders</span>.
</li><li> Tap your folder of choice. For example, tap <strong>Inbox</strong> to disable push email for your Inbox.
</li><li> Turn off push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for <strong>Enable Push</strong>.
</li><li> Turn on sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Enable sync</strong>.
</li></ol>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_new-email-notifications-are-completely-separate-from-the-push-email-service-notification">New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification</h1>
<p>The notifications for new email messages are configured separately from the push email service notification. New email notifications are configured as follows:
</p>
<ul><li> Tap the application menu <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Notifications</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Messages</span> under <em>Notification categories</em>.
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_learn-more">Learn more</h1>
<ul><li> Wikipedia: <a href="https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Push_email">Push email</a>
</li><li> Google: <a href="https://support.google.com/android/answer/9079661">Control notifications on Android</a>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "297629", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 29, 2025, 4:08:41 PM", "datetime": "2025-05-29T16:08:41.477596-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "for some reason \"New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification\" and \"Learn more\" were in a super large font. Not sure why. Deleted a blank line and that fixed it by luck?!?", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 29, 2025, 4:09:59 PM", "datetime": "2025-05-29T16:09:59.825967-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:28:57+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (297632,'en-US','configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','Configure push email for Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/configure-push-email-thunderbird-android/revision/297632',297629,'2025-05-29T16:22:21.316078-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','change app menu to be consistently "to the app menu {menu ≡}"',1,'2025-05-29T16:23:28.200515-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.

__TOC__

=Turn on push email for a folder=
{warning}
WARNING:
* If you kill the Thunderbird for Android app, for example by swiping up on the recent task window, push email will stop working. Thunderbird needs to be running, and it needs network access for push email to work.
* The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > ''''''your email account'''''' > {menu Fetching mail} > {menu Advanced} > {menu Max folders to check with push}. Thunderbird does not warn you when this limit is exceeded. Exceeding this limit will result in push email not working on some of the folders you configured for push.
{/warning}
# Tap the app menu {menu ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account, for example your Gmail account > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap ''''''Inbox'''''' to enable push email for your Inbox.
#;[[Image:enable-push-tb-android-8]]
# Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable Push''''''.
# Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable sync''''''.
{note}The ''''''Enable sync'''''' setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.{/note}
Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled.
;[[Image:bell-icon-android-system-bar-tb8-pushmail-notification]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Alarms & reminders permission for Android 13 and above==
{note}This section is not applicable to you if your Android version is older than Android 13.{/note}
# On Android 13 and above, a notification will let you know you need to grant the ''''Alarms & reminders'''' permission. Proceed to the permissions screen by tapping the {button Missing permission to schedule alarms} notification.
#;[[Image:missing-permission-tb8-android-pushmail]]
# Add this permission by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Allow setting alarms and reminders''''''. If you do not grant this permission, then push email will not work.
#;[[Image:allow-setting-alarms-reminders-tb8-android-pushmail]]

=The push email service notification=
* Once the permission is granted (or right after enabling push on older Android versions), Thunderbird for Android will display a push email service notification entitled ''''''Waiting for new emails'''''':
*;[[Image:notification-waiting-for-new-emails]]
* Tapping on the {button Waiting for new emails} notification will allow you to configure the notification itself ({button Configure notification}) or to disable push email altogether ({button Disable Push}):
*;[[Image:configure-notification-or-disable-push]]

==Configure the push email service notification using “Configure notification”==
You can change the display of this notification or hide it by tapping {button Configure notification}.
;[[Image:notification-settings-tb8-android-pushmail]]

===Hide the push email service notification===
Hiding the push email service notification does not turn off push email.
* Slide ''''''Show notifications'''''' to the left.

===Change the push email service notification===
Minimizing the notification will hide the bell icon from the Android status bar, but still keep the notification in the notification shade. You will still be able to see the status of your push email service (for example, ''''''Waiting for new emails'''''' or ''''''Sleeping until network is available'''''').

===Disable Push email from the push email service notification using “Disable Push”===
Tap {button Disable Push} to disable push email altogether.
[[UI:details_end]]

=Turn off push email for a folder=
# Tap the app menu {menu ≡} at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap {button Show accounts} at the bottom of the screen.
# Tap account, for example, your Gmail account > tap {button Manage folders}.
# Tap your folder of choice. For example, tap ''''''Inbox'''''' to disable push email for your Inbox.
# Turn off push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for ''''''Enable Push''''''.
# Turn on sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for ''''''Enable sync''''''.

[[UI:details_end]]

=New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification=
The notifications for new email messages are configured separately from the push email service notification. New email notifications are configured as follows:
* Tap the app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > {menu Notifications} > {menu Messages} under ''''Notification categories''''.

=Learn more=
* Wikipedia: [https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Push_email Push email]
* Google: [https://support.google.com/android/answer/9079661 Control notifications on Android]','<p>By default, push email is off for all folders. Thunderbird for Android allows you to configure a limited number of folders (IMAP only; POP is not supported.) for push email so that you can see incoming email messages immediately.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Turn on push email for a folder</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_alarms-reminders-permission-for-android-13-and-above"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Alarms &amp; reminders permission for Android 13 and above</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">The push email service notification</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_configure-the-push-email-service-notification-using-configure-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Configure the push email service notification using “Configure notification”</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_hide-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Hide the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_change-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">2.1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Change the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_disable-push-email-from-the-push-email-service-notification-using-disable-push"><span class="tocnumber">2.1.3</span> <span class="toctext">Disable Push email from the push email service notification using “Disable Push”</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-off-push-email-for-a-folder"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Turn off push email for a folder</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_new-email-notifications-are-completely-separate-from-the-push-email-service-notification"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">New Email notifications are completely separate from the push email service notification</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_learn-more"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Learn more</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_turn-on-push-email-for-a-folder">Turn on push email for a folder</h1>
<div class="warning">
<p>WARNING:
</p>
<ul><li> If you kill the Thunderbird for Android app, for example by swiping up on the recent task window, push email will stop working. Thunderbird needs to be running, and it needs network access for push email to work.
</li><li> The maximum number of push folders for an account is set in the app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <strong>your email account</strong> &gt; <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Advanced</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Max folders to check with push</span>. Thunderbird does not warn you when this limit is exceeded. Exceeding this limit will result in push email not working on some of the folders you configured for push.
</li></ul>
</div>
<ol><li> Tap the app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> at the top left. If your email accounts are hidden, tap <span class="button">Show accounts</span> at the bottom of the screen.
</li><li> Tap account, for example your Gmail account &gt; tap <span class="button">Manage folders</span>.
</li><li> Tap your folder of choice. For example: tap <strong>Inbox</strong> to enable push email for your Inbox.
<dl><dt><img alt="enable-push-tb-android-8" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-10-00-62ddea.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Turn on push email for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the right for <strong>Enable Push</strong>.
</li><li> Turn off sync for this folder by tapping until the slider is on the left for <strong>Enable sync</strong>.
</li></ol>
<div class="note">The <strong>Enable sync</strong> setting is for periodic syncs and should be disabled once push is enabled.</div>
<p>Once push email is enabled for at least one folder, you should see a bell icon in the Android system bar. The bell icon indicates that push email is enabled.
</p>
<dl><dt><img alt="bell-icon-android-system-bar-tb8-pushmail-notification" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2024-11-11-21-15-19-df30c1.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
