</p>
<h1 id="w_1-card-or-table-view-for-the-message-list">1. Card or Table view for the message list</h1>
<p>Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-main-window-supernova">Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)</a> for more information on Card and Table view.
</p>
<h2 id="w_card-view">Card view</h2>
<ul><li> Click <span class="button">Card view</span> to select <strong>Card view</strong> and then 
<ul><li> Click <span class="button">2 rows</span>  The first row has the sender''s display name (not the actual email address), time and at the top right the <em>Message Actions</em> menu, <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <strong>kebab</strong> menu because the three vertical dots resemble a kebab). The second row displays the subject. 
</li><li> OR <span class="button">3 rows</span> to get a 3rd row. which adds information about the message thread (if there is more than one message in that thread), tags and starred status.
</li></ul>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_table-view">Table view</h2>
<ul><li> Click <span class="button">Table view</span> to select <strong>Table view</strong> and then:
<ul><li> Tick ✓ <span class="button">allow horizontal scroll</span> if you would like horizontal scrolling for wide content like tables.
</li></ul>
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_2-select-default-threading-for-new-folders-unthreaded-threaded-or-grouped-by-sort">2. Select default threading for new folders: Unthreaded, Threaded or Grouped by Sort</h1>
<ul><li> Click <span class="button">Threaded</span> to to make all new folders threaded by default.
</li><li> OR Click <span class="button">Unthreaded</span> to to make all new folders unthreaded by default.
</li><li> OR Click <span class="button">Grouped by Sort</span> to to sort by groups.
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_3-default-sort-field-date-subject-from-and-so-on">3. Default Sort field: Date, Subject, From, and so on</h1>
<p>There are many options for default sort order for new folders. The most popular optons for <strong>Default Sort by:</strong> are:
</p>
<ul><li> <span class="menu">Date</span>
</li><li> <span class="menu">Subject</span>
</li><li> <span class="menu">From</span>
</li></ul>
<p>Once you have picked a Default sort field, you can then choose <span class="button">Ascending</span> or <span class="button">Descending</span>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_4-select-folders-to-apply-new-settings-to-to">4. Select folders to apply new settings to to</h1>
<p>You choose to apply the new settings to your current folders as follows:
</p>
<ul><li> Click <span class="button">All existing folders</span> to apply the new settings to all folders not just the new ones. Don''t worry you will be given a chance to cancel applying the changes.
</li><li> OR click <span class="button">Choose....</span> to apply the new settings to a particular folder, click <span class="button">Folder...</span>, or a paricular folder and its subfolders, <span class="button">Folder and its children...</span>. Again, you can cancel.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "299823", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jun 30, 2025, 12:26:34 AM", "datetime": "2025-06-30T00:26:34.112447-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "added explanation of all options WIP, do not localize please :-) For discussion please leave comments in https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/79", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jun 30, 2025, 12:28:16 AM", "datetime": "2025-06-30T00:28:16.342220-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:28:08+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (299824,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/299824',299814,'2025-06-30T00:32:47.493991-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','linked to New Appearance panel article, do not localize or approv please :-) For discussion please leave comments in https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/79',1,'2025-06-30T00:33:05.876562-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details,  please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]]

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=
==Dark Message Mode==
* Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
*;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]] 
==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance},  allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details please refer to: [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]]
==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux, or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults at Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub''''''.
==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try.  Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email - account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in an test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to: [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]]

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages. For example data in a table with many columns.

=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]

[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]

[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]

[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
<p></p><p>This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release">Thunderbird Release for Desktop</a>. For full details,  please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>
</p>
