n class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode">Dark Message Mode</h2>
<ul><li> Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
<dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings">New Appearance Panel in Settings</h2>
<p>The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>,  allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details please refer to: <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications">Native OS Notifications</h2>
<p>Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux, or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub">Redesigned Account hub</h2>
<p>The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults at Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting">Manual Folder Sorting</h2>
<p>Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</h2>
<p>Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try.  Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email - account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>We recommend you try this in an test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p>
<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile">Export for Mobile</h2>
<p>Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to: <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</h2>
<p>Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages. For example data in a table with many columns.
</p>
