This article describes the ''''''Appearance'''''' panel (Thunderbird 140 and newer) which can be found at Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}. It allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, change the view''s settings, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options.

__TOC__

[[Image:tb-140-appearances-panel]]

=1. Card or Table view for the message list=
Please refer to [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] for more information on Card and Table view.
==Card view ==
* Click {button Card view} to select ''''''Card view'''''' and then 
** Click {button 2 rows}  The first row has the sender''s display name (not the actual email address), time and at the top right the ''''Message Actions'''' menu, {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''''kebab'''''' menu because the three vertical dots resemble a kebab). The second row displays the subject. 
** OR {button 3 rows} to get a 3rd row. which adds information about the message thread (if there is more than one message in that thread), tags and starred status.
== Table view==
* Click {button Table view} to select ''''''Table view'''''' and then:
** Tick ✓ {button allow horizontal scroll} if you would like horizontal scrolling for wide content like tables.

=2. Select default threading for new folders: Unthreaded, Threaded or Grouped by Sort=
* Click {button Threaded} to to make all new folders threaded by default.
* OR Click {button Unthreaded} to to make all new folders unthreaded by default.
* OR Click {button Grouped by Sort} to to sort by groups.

=3. Default Sort field: Date, Subject, From, and so on=
There are many options for default sort order for new folders. The most popular optons for ''''''Default Sort by:'''''' are:
* {menu Date}
* {menu Subject}
* {menu From}

Once you have picked a Default sort field, you can then choose {button Ascending} or {button Descending}.

=4. Select folders to apply new settings to to=
You choose to apply the new settings to your current folders as follows:
* Click {button All existing folders} to apply the new settings to all folders not just the new ones. Don''t worry you will be given a chance to cancel applying the changes.
* OR click {button Choose....} to apply the new settings to a particular folder, click {button Folder...}, or a paricular folder and its subfolders, {button Folder and its children...}. Again, you can cancel.','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
