</li><li> OR Click <span class="button">Grouped by Sort</span> to to sort by groups.
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_3-default-sort-field-date-subject-from-and-so-on">3. Default Sort field: Date, Subject, From, and so on</h1>
<p>There are many options for default sort order for new folders. The most popular optons for <strong>Default Sort by:</strong> are:
</p>
<ul><li> <span class="menu">Date</span>
</li><li> <span class="menu">Subject</span>
</li><li> <span class="menu">From</span>
</li></ul>
<p>Once you have picked a Default sort field, you can then choose <span class="button">Ascending</span> or <span class="button">Descending</span>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_4-select-folders-to-apply-new-settings-to-to">4. Select folders to apply new settings to to</h1>
<p>You choose to apply the new settings to your current folders as follows:
</p>
<ul><li> Click <span class="button">All existing folders</span> to apply the new settings to all folders not just the new ones. Don''t worry you will be given a chance to cancel applying the changes.
</li><li> OR click <span class="button">Choose....</span> to apply the new settings to a particular folder, click <span class="button">Folder...</span>, or a paricular folder and its subfolders, <span class="button">Folder and its children...</span>. Again, you can cancel.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "299825", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jun 30, 2025, 12:34:18 AM", "datetime": "2025-06-30T00:34:18.560952-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add [[T:TBMore]]", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jun 30, 2025, 12:34:35 AM", "datetime": "2025-06-30T00:34:35.155594-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:28:03+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (299826,'en-US','appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab','Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab/revision/299826',299825,'2025-06-30T00:35:53.510578-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix title  WIP, do not localize please :-) For discussion please leave comments in https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/79',1,'2025-06-30T00:36:02.454070-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[T:TBMore]]

This article describes the ''''''Appearance'''''' panel (Thunderbird 140 and newer) which can be found at Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}. It allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, change the view''s settings, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options.

__TOC__

[[Image:tb-140-appearances-panel]]

=1. Card or Table view for the message list=
Please refer to [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] for more information on Card and Table view.
==Card view ==
* Click {button Card view} to select ''''''Card view'''''' and then 
** Click {button 2 rows}  The first row has the sender''s display name (not the actual email address), time and at the top right the ''''Message Actions'''' menu, {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''''kebab'''''' menu because the three vertical dots resemble a kebab). The second row displays the subject. 
** OR {button 3 rows} to get a 3rd row. which adds information about the message thread (if there is more than one message in that thread), tags and starred status.
== Table view==
* Click {button Table view} to select ''''''Table view'''''' and then:
** Tick ✓ {button allow horizontal scroll} if you would like horizontal scrolling for wide content like tables.

=2. Select default threading for new folders: Unthreaded, Threaded or Grouped by Sort=
* Click {button Threaded} to to make all new folders threaded by default.
* OR Click {button Unthreaded} to to make all new folders unthreaded by default.
* OR Click {button Grouped by Sort} to to sort by groups.

=3. Default Sort field: Date, Subject, From, and so on=
There are many options for default sort order for new folders. The most popular optons for ''''''Default Sort by:'''''' are:
* {menu Date}
* {menu Subject}
* {menu From}

Once you have picked a Default sort field, you can then choose {button Ascending} or {button Descending}.

=4. Select folders to apply new settings to=
You choose to apply the new settings to your current folders as follows:
* Click {button All existing folders} to apply the new settings to all folders not just the new ones. Don''t worry you will be given a chance to cancel applying the changes.
* OR click {button Choose....} to apply the new settings to a particular folder, click {button Folder...}, or a paricular folder and its subfolders, {button Folder and its children...}. Again, you can cancel.','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
