INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (301115,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/301115',299991,'2025-07-21T23:24:29.068224-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','Added link to New email notifications in Thunderbird WIP, do not localize or approve please :-) For discussion please leave comments in https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/92',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}.  Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.
==Better Exchange support==
Building on the software in 140, we have improved it to the point where anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth (password authentication for on premise is supported in this release)

This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=

==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]

==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].

==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.

==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub''''''.

==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.

==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
<p></p><p>This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release">Thunderbird Release for Desktop</a>. For full details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-141"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 141</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Archive action added to new email notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_better-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Better Exchange support</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry"><span class="tocnumber">1.3</span> <span class="toctext">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_dark-message-mode"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Dark Message Mode</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">New Appearance Panel in Settings</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_native-os-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Native OS Notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_redesigned-account-hub"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Redesigned Account hub</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manual-folder-sorting"><span class="tocnumber">2.5</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Folder Sorting</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users"><span class="tocnumber">2.6</span> <span class="toctext">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_export-for-mobile"><span class="tocnumber">2.7</span> <span class="toctext">Export for Mobile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">2.8</span> <span class="toctext">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">3.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">3.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">3.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-141">Thunderbird 141</h1>
<h2 id="w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications">Archive action added to new email notifications</h2>
<ul><li> You can now <span class="button">Archive</span> email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to <span class="button">Mark as Read</span>, <span class="button">Delete</span>, <span class="button">Mark as Starred</span> and <span class="button">Mark as Spam</span>.  Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird">New email notifications in Thunderbird</a> for further information.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_better-exchange-support">Better Exchange support</h2>
<p>Building on the software in 140, we have improved it to the point where anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth (password authentication for on premise is supported in this release)
</p><p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p>
<h2 id="w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</h2>
<p>If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.
</p><p>More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in <a href="/en-US/kb/introduction-to-e2e-encryption">Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird</a> and <a href="/en-US/kb/openpgp-thunderbird-howto-and-faq">OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ</a>.
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Dark Message Mode</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl></div>


<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true"><p>Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
