<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><p>Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-139" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 139</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-138" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 138</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-137" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 137</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-136" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 136</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "302707", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 19, 2025, 12:26:50 AM", "datetime": "2025-08-19T00:26:50.726604-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, do not localize or approve please :-) For discussion please comment in: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/97", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 19, 2025, 8:46:03 AM", "datetime": "2025-08-19T08:46:03.007242-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:27:06+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (302709,'en-US','new-email-notifications-thunderbird','New email notifications in Thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird/revision/302709',301669,'2025-08-19T00:45:26.169148-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','document windows notification settings WIP, do not localize or approve please :-) For discussion please leave comments in https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/89',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','In order for this feature to work, you have to enable and configure notifications both in Thunderbird and in your operating system.
__TOC__
=1. Turn on native notifications in Thunderbird=

# Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''When new messages arrive''''''. {for win, linux}Ensure ''''''Use the system notification'''''' is ticked "✓" {/for}
# Click {button Customize...}
# Ensure the fields and actions you would like to display in your new email notifications are ticked "✓" (''''''Archive'''''' is only available in 141 and newer releases).
#;[[Image:borderless customize new mail alert]]
{warning}Some operating systems have limits on how many action buttons are displayed in a notification. Windows 11 for example will only display 4 action buttons even if you have selected 5 or more actions.{/warning}
=2. Configure your operating system''s native notifications=
Please follow your operating system''s documentation to enable and configure notifications native to your operating system.
==Windows==
==Turn on Thunderbird email notifications==
(Refer to Microsoft''s Knowledge Base Article for more details:  [https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/notifications-and-do-not-disturb-in-windows-feeca47f-0baf-5680-16f0-8801db1a8466 Notifications and Do Not Disturb in Windows].)
# Enable notifications globally: In the Settings app  on your Windows device, open System > {menu Notifications} and then toggle the switch next to {menu Notifications} to {button On}.
# Under {menu Notifications from apps and other senders}, scroll down to {menu Mozilla Thunderbird} and then toggle the switch to {button On}.
# Click on the chevron {button >} to configure more options.

==macOS==

==Linux==','<p>In order for this feature to work, you have to enable and configure notifications both in Thunderbird and in your operating system.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_1-turn-on-native-notifications-in-thunderbird"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">1. Turn on native notifications in Thunderbird</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_2-configure-your-operating-systems-native-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">2. Configure your operating system''s native notifications</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_windows"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Windows</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_turn-on-thunderbird-email-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Turn on Thunderbird email notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_macos"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">macOS</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_linux"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Linux</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_1-turn-on-native-notifications-in-thunderbird">1. Turn on native notifications in Thunderbird</h1>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>When new messages arrive</strong>. <span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;">Ensure <strong>Use the system notification</strong> is ticked "✓" </span>
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Customize...</span>
</li><li> Ensure the fields and actions you would like to display in your new email notifications are ticked "✓" (<strong>Archive</strong> is only available in 141 and newer releases).
<dl><dt><img alt="borderless customize new mail alert" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-07-21-23-13-12-298a52.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<div class="warning">Some operating systems have limits on how many action buttons are displayed in a notification. Windows 11 for example will only display 4 action buttons even if you have selected 5 or more actions.</div>
<h1 id="w_2-configure-your-operating-systems-native-notifications">2. Configure your operating system''s native notifications</h1>
<p>Please follow your operating system''s documentation to enable and configure notifications native to your operating system.
</p>
<h2 id="w_windows">Windows</h2>
<h2 id="w_turn-on-thunderbird-email-notifications">Turn on Thunderbird email notifications</h2>
<p>(Refer to Microsoft''s Knowledge Base Article for more details:  <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/notifications-and-do-not-disturb-in-windows-feeca47f-0baf-5680-16f0-8801db1a8466">Notifications and Do Not Disturb in Windows</a>.)
</p>
<ol><li> Enable notifications globally: In the Settings app  on your Windows device, open System &gt; <span class="menu">Notifications</span> and then toggle the switch next to <span class="menu">Notifications</span> to <span class="button">On</span>.
</li><li> Under <span class="menu">Notifications from apps and other senders</span>, scroll down to <span class="menu">Mozilla Thunderbird</span> and then toggle the switch to <span class="button">On</span>.
</li><li> Click on the chevron <span class="button">&gt;</span> to configure more options.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_macos">macOS</h2>
<h2 id="w_linux">Linux</h2>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "302709", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 19, 2025, 12:45:26 AM", "datetime": "2025-08-19T00:45:26.169148-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "document windows notification settings WIP, do not localize or approve please :-) For discussion please leave comments in https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/89", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:27:03+00:00');
