</li></ol>
<div class="warning">Some operating systems have limits on how many action buttons are displayed in a notification. Windows 11 for example will only display 4 action buttons even if you have selected 5 or more actions.</div>
<h1 id="w_2-configure-your-operating-systems-native-notifications">2. Configure your operating system''s native notifications</h1>
<p>Please follow your operating system''s documentation to enable and configure notifications native to your operating system.
</p>
<h2 id="w_windows">Windows</h2>
<h2 id="w_turn-on-thunderbird-email-notifications">Turn on Thunderbird email notifications</h2>
<p>(Refer to Microsoft''s Knowledge Base Article for more details:  <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/notifications-and-do-not-disturb-in-windows-feeca47f-0baf-5680-16f0-8801db1a8466">Notifications and Do Not Disturb in Windows</a>.)
</p>
<ol><li> Enable notifications globally: In the Settings app  on your Windows device, open System &gt; <span class="menu">Notifications</span> and then toggle the switch next to <span class="menu">Notifications</span> to <span class="button">On</span>.
</li><li> Under <span class="menu">Notifications from apps and other senders</span>, scroll down to <span class="menu">Mozilla Thunderbird</span> and then toggle the switch to <span class="button">On</span>.
</li><li> Click on the chevron <span class="button">&gt;</span> to configure more options.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_example-windows-11-notification">Example: Windows 11 notification</h2>
