<h2 id="w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Archive action added to new email notifications</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true"><li> You can now <span class="button">Archive</span> email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to <span class="button">Mark as Read</span>, <span class="button">Delete</span>, <span class="button">Mark as Starred</span> and <span class="button">Mark as Spam</span>. Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird">New email notifications in Thunderbird</a> for further information.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_better-exchange-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Better Exchange support</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true"><p>Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
</p><p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true"><p>If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.
</p><p>More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in <a href="/en-US/kb/introduction-to-e2e-encryption">Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird</a> and <a href="/en-US/kb/openpgp-thunderbird-howto-and-faq">OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ</a>.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true">This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511">bug 1979511</a>.
</p></section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Dark Message Mode</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><p>Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl></div>


<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true"><p>Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-139" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 139</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-138" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-18" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 138</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-18" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-137" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-19" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 137</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-19" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-136" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-20" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 136</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-20" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "305720", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Sep 19, 2025, 6:05:24 PM", "datetime": "2025-09-19T18:05:24.946092-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "143 is a bug fix release, nothing user facing of note :-) for discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/104", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Sep 19, 2025, 6:07:28 PM", "datetime": "2025-09-19T18:07:28.495526-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Sep 19, 2025, 6:07:28 PM", "datetime": "2025-09-19T18:07:28.495526-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:26:05+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (306029,'en-US','profiling-thunderbird-performance','Profiling Thunderbird Performance','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/profiling-thunderbird-performance','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/profiling-thunderbird-performance/revision/306029',304962,'2025-09-22T17:27:26.638260-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','for sumo event :-)',1,'2025-09-22T17:29:27.709700-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','Creating a performance profile can be useful for developers to find the causes of high CPU load, slowness or memory usage in Thunderbird. But first, check if the problem goes away in [[Troubleshoot Mode Thunderbird|Troubleshoot Mode]]. You may also find it useful to go through the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Testing:Memory_Usage_Problems performance checklist].

Some types of profiling will require using development build which you can obtain from [https://www.thunderbird.net/download/daily/ Thunderbird Daily download].

We will be using Firefox''s performance profiler, so you may see references to Firefox in the profiler dialogs. [https://profiler.firefox.com/docs/#/ Firefox profiler documentation] is excellent, but you will only need to refer to it if you have trouble or want to do something special, such as profiling startup performance. In the documentation, anywhere ''Firefox'' is mentioned, think ''Thunderbird''.

{note}''''''Note:'''''' There is an opportunity to remove personally identifiable information before sharing data.{/note}

__TOC__

= Step 1 - Preparing performance recording in Thunderbird =

The performance recorder is part of the ''''Developer Toolbox'''' in Thunderbird. 

Before you start your recording, prepare as much as possible the scenario to be tested in Thunderbird.

# In Thunderbird’s main window, open the ''''Developer Toolbox'''': Press {for win,linux}{key Ctrl+Shift+I}{/for}{for mac}{key Command+Shift+I}{/for}, ''''''''''or'''''''''' click on {menu ≡} > {menu Tools} > {menu Developer Tools}.
#;{warning}''''''Important:'''''' Confirm the warning prompt ''''Incoming Connection ... Allow connection?'''' with {key OK} so that the toolbox can connect to your Thunderbird application.<br> <br>Note: The prompt might be hidden behind other Thunderbird windows.{/warning}
# The ''''Developer Tools'''' window is shown.
# Current versions of Thunderbird will show the ''''''Performance'''''' tab with {button Start recording} shown.  If you do not see that tab, then press {key F1}, or click on the {button •••} button in the top-right corner, then click on {menu Settings}. Ensure that {menu [✓] Performance} is checked. Then click on the {menu Performance} tab that has appeared at the top of the toolbox.
# If you see "Failed to get the active browserId while starting the profiler" this may be ignored.
# ''''''Configure profiler settings:''''''
## Click ''''''Edit Settings...'''''' which is the last item in the Developer Tools window. 
## The ''''about:profiling'''' window is shown.
## Select the {button Thunderbird} preset, if it isn''t already. After this point, when you mark any other settings, the preset will change to "Custom" which is normal. (If you are using nightly/trunk builds, select the "Daily" preset.)
## If you have any privacy concerns, or to save memory, unmark the checkbox for {button Screenshots}.
## Scroll down and also mark the checkbox for {button All File IO}. 
## Change any other settings that might be needed, for example, {button Native Allocations} (for high memory issues. (''''''Native Allocations'''''' requires using Thunderbird daily builds.)
## If you need more than a minute to capture the problem you are profiling, or added certain additional collections, then you may need to adjust some ''''''Buffer Settings'''''' such increase the ''''''Buffer size''''''from 1GB to 2GB, and increase the ''''''Sampling interval'''''' from the default 1 ms.
## Close the ''''about:profiling'''' using the window controls.  (there is no {button OK} or {button Save} button)
# Important: Before starting your performance recording, go back to the main Thunderbird window, and finish preparing the performance scenario to be recorded.

= Step 2 - Recording a performance profile =

You are now ready to record and save the performance profile of your scenario. Unless told otherwise, try to keep your recording as short as possible by recording only the exact set of actions which are suspected to cause the problem. 

# In the {menu Performance} tab of the ''''Developer Tools'''' window, click on the {button Start recording} button.
# Without delay, go back to the main Thunderbird window and perform the set of actions you want to record.
# Once finished, immediately select {button Capture recording} in the ''''Developer Tools'''' window.

= Step 3 - Saving and sharing a performance profile =

# Click {button Capture recording} to finish the collection process and you will briefly see ''''''Capturing profile'''''', ending with a Firefox Profiler window "https://profiler.firefox.com/from-browser/". If you did not see the capture button then you are using an older version of Thunderbird ad profiler. Skip to the section on [[#w_old-versions-of-thunderbird|Old Versions of Thunderbird]]. 
# Click {button Upload Local Profile}. For the profile which you are preparing to share there is a list of items under "Include additional data that may be identifiable" - uncheck the boxes for any private information items which you wish to not share. 
# Scroll down to the choices for saving the data. Use {button Download} for saving a local json file which you may then privately email to someone else or attach to a bug report.  Use {button Upload} to send the profile to a repository at https://profiler.firefox.com/. ''''''Upload'''''' will provide a permalink in the form of https://share.firefox.dev/ which you can copy and share with developers and others who might help you with your problem.
# Close the Performance Profiler window.
# Close the Developers Tools window.

== Old versions of Thunderbird == 

Older versions of Thunderbird require some manual steps to save the profile.

# On the left side, right next to the new ''''Recording #1'''' item, click the ''''''Save'''''' link and save the file to somewhere on your computer. The file extension must be ''''.json''''.
# Go to https://profiler.firefox.com/ (yes, on firefox.com).
# Select {button Load a profile from file} and select the ''''.json'''' file which you just saved for upload.
# ''''''Important: Near the top-right, select the green {button Publish} button'''''', then in the ''''Share Performance Profile'''' panel, select the (blue) {button Publish} button again.
# Copy the link (e.g. https://share.firefox.dev/1XYZXYz) which pops up in the top-right corner under the new {button permalink} button and paste it into an appropriate [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird new bug] or existing bug on [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org Bugzilla (BMO)].
# Finally, back in the ''''Developer Tools'''' {menu Performance} tab, you can delete the performance profile using the ''''''trash-icon'''''' just above the profile list in the left-top corner (where you saved the profile), and then close the ''''Developer Tools'''' window. ⚡

= Profiling Thunderbird startup and shutdown =

Profiling startup or shutdown involves [https://profiler.firefox.com/docs/#/./guide-startup-shutdown special, but very simple instructions].  Again, where ''Firefox'' is mentioned, think ''Thunderbird''.','<p>Creating a performance profile can be useful for developers to find the causes of high CPU load, slowness or memory usage in Thunderbird. But first, check if the problem goes away in <a href="/en-US/kb/troubleshoot-mode-thunderbird">Troubleshoot Mode</a>. You may also find it useful to go through the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Testing:Memory_Usage_Problems">performance checklist</a>.
</p><p>Some types of profiling will require using development build which you can obtain from <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/download/daily/">Thunderbird Daily download</a>.
</p><p>We will be using Firefox''s performance profiler, so you may see references to Firefox in the profiler dialogs. <a href="https://profiler.firefox.com/docs/#/">Firefox profiler documentation</a> is excellent, but you will only need to refer to it if you have trouble or want to do something special, such as profiling startup performance. In the documentation, anywhere ''Firefox'' is mentioned, think ''Thunderbird''.
</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> There is an opportunity to remove personally identifiable information before sharing data.</div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_step-1-preparing-performance-recording-in-thunderbird"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Step 1 - Preparing performance recording in Thunderbird</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_step-2-recording-a-performance-profile"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Step 2 - Recording a performance profile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_step-3-saving-and-sharing-a-performance-profile"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Step 3 - Saving and sharing a performance profile</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_old-versions-of-thunderbird"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Old versions of Thunderbird</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_profiling-thunderbird-startup-and-shutdown"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Profiling Thunderbird startup and shutdown</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_step-1-preparing-performance-recording-in-thunderbird">Step 1 - Preparing performance recording in Thunderbird</h1>
<p>The performance recorder is part of the <em>Developer Toolbox</em> in Thunderbird. 
</p><p>Before you start your recording, prepare as much as possible the scenario to be tested in Thunderbird.
</p>
<ol><li> In Thunderbird’s main window, open the <em>Developer Toolbox</em>: Press <span class="for" data-for="win,linux" style="display: none;"><span class="key">Ctrl</span> + <span class="key">Shift</span> + <span class="key">I</span></span><span class="for" data-for="mac"><span class="key">Command</span> + <span class="key">Shift</span> + <span class="key">I</span></span>, <em><strong>or</strong></em> click on <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Tools</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Developer Tools</span>.
<dl><dt><div class="warning"><strong>Important:</strong> Confirm the warning prompt <em>Incoming Connection ... Allow connection?</em> with <span class="key">OK</span> so that the toolbox can connect to your Thunderbird application.<br> <br>Note: The prompt might be hidden behind other Thunderbird windows.</div>
</dt></dl>
</li><li> The <em>Developer Tools</em> window is shown.
</li><li> Current versions of Thunderbird will show the <strong>Performance</strong> tab with <span class="button">Start recording</span> shown.  If you do not see that tab, then press <span class="key">F1</span>, or click on the <span class="button">•••</span> button in the top-right corner, then click on <span class="menu">Settings</span>. Ensure that <span class="menu">[✓] Performance</span> is checked. Then click on the <span class="menu">Performance</span> tab that has appeared at the top of the toolbox.
</li><li> If you see "Failed to get the active browserId while starting the profiler" this may be ignored.
</li><li> <strong>Configure profiler settings:</strong>
<ol><li> Click <strong>Edit Settings...</strong> which is the last item in the Developer Tools window. 
</li><li> The <em>about:profiling</em> window is shown.
</li><li> Select the <span class="button">Thunderbird</span> preset, if it isn''t already. After this point, when you mark any other settings, the preset will change to "Custom" which is normal. (If you are using nightly/trunk builds, select the "Daily" preset.)
</li><li> If you have any privacy concerns, or to save memory, unmark the checkbox for <span class="button">Screenshots</span>.
</li><li> Scroll down and also mark the checkbox for <span class="button">All File IO</span>. 
</li><li> Change any other settings that might be needed, for example, <span class="button">Native Allocations</span> (for high memory issues. (<strong>Native Allocations</strong> requires using Thunderbird daily builds.)
</li><li> If you need more than a minute to capture the problem you are profiling, or added certain additional collections, then you may need to adjust some <strong>Buffer Settings</strong> such increase the <strong>Buffer size</strong>from 1GB to 2GB, and increase the <strong>Sampling interval</strong> from the default 1 ms.
</li><li> Close the <em>about:profiling</em> using the window controls.  (there is no <span class="button">OK</span> or <span class="button">Save</span> button)
</li></ol>
</li><li> Important: Before starting your performance recording, go back to the main Thunderbird window, and finish preparing the performance scenario to be recorded.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_step-2-recording-a-performance-profile">Step 2 - Recording a performance profile</h1>
<p>You are now ready to record and save the performance profile of your scenario. Unless told otherwise, try to keep your recording as short as possible by recording only the exact set of actions which are suspected to cause the problem. 
</p>
<ol><li> In the <span class="menu">Performance</span> tab of the <em>Developer Tools</em> window, click on the <span class="button">Start recording</span> button.
</li><li> Without delay, go back to the main Thunderbird window and perform the set of actions you want to record.
</li><li> Once finished, immediately select <span class="button">Capture recording</span> in the <em>Developer Tools</em> window.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_step-3-saving-and-sharing-a-performance-profile">Step 3 - Saving and sharing a performance profile</h1>
<ol><li> Click <span class="button">Capture recording</span> to finish the collection process and you will briefly see <strong>Capturing profile</strong>, ending with a Firefox Profiler window "<a href="https://profiler.firefox.com/from-browser/">https://profiler.firefox.com/from-browser/</a>". If you did not see the capture button then you are using an older version of Thunderbird ad profiler. Skip to the section on <a href="#w_old-versions-of-thunderbird">Old Versions of Thunderbird</a>. 
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Upload Local Profile</span>. For the profile which you are preparing to share there is a list of items under "Include additional data that may be identifiable" - uncheck the boxes for any private information items which you wish to not share. 
</li><li> Scroll down to the choices for saving the data. Use <span class="button">Download</span> for saving a local json file which you may then privately email to someone else or attach to a bug report.  Use <span class="button">Upload</span> to send the profile to a repository at <a href="https://profiler.firefox.com/">https://profiler.firefox.com/</a>. <strong>Upload</strong> will provide a permalink in the form of <a href="https://share.firefox.dev/">https://share.firefox.dev/</a> which you can copy and share with developers and others who might help you with your problem.
</li><li> Close the Performance Profiler window.
</li><li> Close the Developers Tools window.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_old-versions-of-thunderbird">Old versions of Thunderbird</h2>
<p>Older versions of Thunderbird require some manual steps to save the profile.
</p>
<ol><li> On the left side, right next to the new <em>Recording #1</em> item, click the <strong>Save</strong> link and save the file to somewhere on your computer. The file extension must be <em>.json</em>.
</li><li> Go to <a href="https://profiler.firefox.com/">https://profiler.firefox.com/</a> (yes, on <a href="http://firefox.com">firefox.com</a>).
</li><li> Select <span class="button">Load a profile from file</span> and select the <em>.json</em> file which you just saved for upload.
</li><li> <strong>Important: Near the top-right, select the green <span class="button">Publish</span> button</strong>, then in the <em>Share Performance Profile</em> panel, select the (blue) <span class="button">Publish</span> button again.
</li><li> Copy the link (e.g. <a href="https://share.firefox.dev/1XYZXYz">https://share.firefox.dev/1XYZXYz</a>) which pops up in the top-right corner under the new <span class="button">permalink</span> button and paste it into an appropriate <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird">new bug</a> or existing bug on <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org">Bugzilla (BMO)</a>.
</li><li> Finally, back in the <em>Developer Tools</em> <span class="menu">Performance</span> tab, you can delete the performance profile using the <strong>trash-icon</strong> just above the profile list in the left-top corner (where you saved the profile), and then close the <em>Developer Tools</em> window. ⚡
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_profiling-thunderbird-startup-and-shutdown">Profiling Thunderbird startup and shutdown</h1>
<p>Profiling startup or shutdown involves <a href="https://profiler.firefox.com/docs/#/./guide-startup-shutdown">special, but very simple instructions</a>.  Again, where ''Firefox'' is mentioned, think ''Thunderbird''.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "306029", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Sep 22, 2025, 5:27:26 PM", "datetime": "2025-09-22T17:27:26.638260-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "for sumo event :-)", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Sep 22, 2025, 5:29:27 PM", "datetime": "2025-09-22T17:29:27.709700-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:26:02+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (306174,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/306174',305923,'2025-09-24T09:29:13.118837-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix spelling mistake :-)',1,'2025-09-24T09:29:29.228347-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2025-09-24T09:29:29.228347-07:00','rtanglao','approved','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 143=
* Bug fixes.
* Various Exchange Support fixes. This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 142=
==Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues with Hotmail and outlook.com accounts==
If you see: ''''''Exchange auth error'''''' or ''''''Authentication failed. Please check the username and password'''''' when adding a ''''''Hotmail'''''' or ''''''outlook.com'''''' account, here''s how to switch to the old ''''''Account Setup'''''' flow to fix the problem:
* Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings} > {menu General} and untick ''''''Create accounts in the new Account Hub'''''':
*;[[Image:tb142-disable-account-hub|width=350]]
* Please try adding the email account again. If you still have issues, please [https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form file a support request on SUMO].
This will be fixed in a future Thunderbird release.

==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key Control}+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order|width=350]]

==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]].

==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.

==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}. Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.

==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).

This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].

== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=
==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]

==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].

==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.

==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub''''''.

==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.

==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
