<p>Here are some specific tips that will allow you to find the relevant settings for screen dimming on your device: Look for Android settings under sections with words like: 
</p>
<ul><li> <strong>Eye comfort shield</strong>: Turn off.
</li><li> <strong>Power saving</strong>: Turn off or increase timeout before it starts.
</li><li> <strong>Battery saver</strong>: Turn off or increase timeout to prevent dimming.
</li><li> <strong>High contrast text</strong> or <strong>High contrast mode</strong>: See if changing these settings makes your screen more readable.
</li><li> <strong>Accessibility</strong> and <strong>Display</strong>: Look for settings related to screen dimming, screen timeouts and lock settings - turn off all automatic screen dimming, extra screen dimming (often found in <span class="menu">Android Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Accessibility</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Extra dim</span>) and increase timeouts for screen locking.
</li></ul>
