<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "313625", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 12, 2025, 11:58:49 PM", "datetime": "2025-11-12T23:58:49.560709-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "MANUAL CONFIGURATION supports EWS, IMAP and POP3. Discussion please in : https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/108#issuecomment-3525817994", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 13, 2025, 12:18:54 AM", "datetime": "2025-11-13T00:18:54.126114-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:24:47+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (313631,'en-US','thunderbird-and-exchange','Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange/revision/313631',311882,'2025-11-13T00:11:41.320736-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','Change "Graph API" to "Microsoft Graph" Discussion please at: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/109',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','{warning}
Thunderbird Version 145 implements Exchange via the EWS API (Exchange Web Services), ''''''currently limited to email''''''. 

Calendar and address book using the EWS API will follow at a later date. Also in the future is Exchange via ''''''Microsoft Graph'''''', so please do not file bug reports for these items at this time. 

Exchange is new, so we very much welcome your [[#w_feedback-and-bug-reports|feedback and bug reports]]. For more technical detail, as well as things to test and look for, see the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page]. {/warning}

__TOC__

=Setup=
When creating a new account using classic account creation, choose the "Exchange Web Services" option. Or if using the new Account Hub, when providing an exchange email address, "Exchange" should be automatically detected. If exchange is not detected, choose the first "Exchange" option.

==1. Configure your Exchange account==
===Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird ''''''Account Hub'''''' flow:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email}.
# Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account.{note}''''''Note:'''''' You do not need to enter your password in the ''''''Password'''''' field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note}Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#;[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11]]
# Click the {button Exchange} button (not the one labelled {button Exchange  REQUIRES ADD-ON}) in the ''''''Choose your email account type'''''' dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.{note}''''''Note:'''''' The {button Exchange} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
#;[[Image:tb142-beta-exchange-support-button]]
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.

[[UI:details_start]]
===Thunderbird profile with no accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with no accounts, you will see the older, ''''''Set Up Your Existing Email Address'''''' flow:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email}.
# Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account.{note}''''''Note:'''''' You do not need to enter your password in the ''''''Password'''''' field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note}Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#;[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11]]
# Click the {button Exchange Web Services} button (not the one labelled {button Exchange/Office365}) in the ''''''Choose your email account type'''''' dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange implementation.{note}''''''Note:'''''' The {button Exchange Web Services} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
#;[[Image:tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button]]
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
[[UI:details_end]]

==2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account==
Once you have configured your Exchange Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|send and receive emails]] just like an IMAP or POP account.

=Limitations=
Not yet supported:
* Address book
* Calendar
* Filters (Phase 5)
* Folder quotas (Phase 5)
* Folder subscription (Phase 5)
* Message retention policies (Phase 5)
* Message download sync for offline use (Phase 5)
* Message tagging (Phase 5)
* NTLM authentication (Phase 5)
* OAuth authentication with on-premise instances (Phase 5)
* Shared mailboxes (Phase 5)
* Star message (Phase 5)
"Phase 5" items are on the near term road map, expected to by available/resolved by 1Q2026. The full list of phase 5 is [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/showdependencytree.cgi?id=1995377&hide_resolved=1 this bug list].

=Feedback and Bug Reports=
To report a problem when using version 145 or newer, please [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&component=Networking:%20Exchange&short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&blocked=1847846&bug_type=defect file a bug report]. To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].

You may use topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta beta group] or the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise enterprise group].

=Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers=
Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].','<div class="warning">
<p>Thunderbird Version 145 implements Exchange via the EWS API (Exchange Web Services), <strong>currently limited to email</strong>. 
</p><p>Calendar and address book using the EWS API will follow at a later date. Also in the future is Exchange via <strong>Microsoft Graph</strong>, so please do not file bug reports for these items at this time. 
</p>
Exchange is new, so we very much welcome your <a href="#w_feedback-and-bug-reports">feedback and bug reports</a>. For more technical detail, as well as things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>. </div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_setup"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Setup</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_1-configure-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">1. Configure your Exchange account</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_2-send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_limitations"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Limitations</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_feedback-and-bug-reports"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Feedback and Bug Reports</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_setup">Setup</h1>
<p>When creating a new account using classic account creation, choose the "Exchange Web Services" option. Or if using the new Account Hub, when providing an exchange email address, "Exchange" should be automatically detected. If exchange is not detected, choose the first "Exchange" option.
</p>
<h2 id="w_1-configure-your-exchange-account">1. Configure your Exchange account</h2>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</h3>
<p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird <strong>Account Hub</strong> flow:
</p>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>.
</li><li> Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> You do not need to enter your password in the <strong>Password</strong> field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div>Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Exchange</span> button (not the one labelled <span class="button">Exchange  REQUIRES ADD-ON</span>) in the <strong>Choose your email account type</strong> dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The <span class="button">Exchange</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div>
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-beta-exchange-support-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-03-20-2802fd.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</button></h3><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with no accounts, you will see the older, <strong>Set Up Your Existing Email Address</strong> flow:
</p><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>.
</li><li> Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> You do not need to enter your password in the <strong>Password</strong> field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div>Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button (not the one labelled <span class="button">Exchange/Office365</span>) in the <strong>Choose your email account type</strong> dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange implementation.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div>
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-23-12-9340ff.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_2-send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account">2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</h2>
<p>Once you have configured your Exchange Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">send and receive emails</a> just like an IMAP or POP account.
</p>
<h1 id="w_limitations">Limitations</h1>
<p>Not yet supported:
</p>
<ul><li> Address book
</li><li> Calendar
</li><li> Filters (Phase 5)
</li><li> Folder quotas (Phase 5)
</li><li> Folder subscription (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message retention policies (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message download sync for offline use (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message tagging (Phase 5)
</li><li> NTLM authentication (Phase 5)
</li><li> OAuth authentication with on-premise instances (Phase 5)
</li><li> Shared mailboxes (Phase 5)
</li><li> Star message (Phase 5)
</li></ul>
<p>"Phase 5" items are on the near term road map, expected to by available/resolved by 1Q2026. The full list of phase 5 is <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/showdependencytree.cgi?id=1995377&amp;hide_resolved=1">this bug list</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_feedback-and-bug-reports">Feedback and Bug Reports</h1>
<p>To report a problem when using version 145 or newer, please <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&amp;component=Networking:%20Exchange&amp;short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&amp;blocked=1847846&amp;bug_type=defect">file a bug report</a>. To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p><p>You may use topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta">beta group</a> or the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise">enterprise group</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</h1>
<p>Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "313631", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 13, 2025, 12:11:41 AM", "datetime": "2025-11-13T00:11:41.320736-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Change \"Graph API\" to \"Microsoft Graph\" Discussion please at: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/109", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:24:44+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (313635,'en-US','thunderbird-and-exchange','Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange/revision/313635',311882,'2025-11-13T00:30:43.312607-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','Manual configuration of EWS Servers. discussion please: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/109#issuecomment-3526259890',1,'2025-11-13T00:32:10.455658-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','{warning}
For the best Exchange experience, we recommend Thunderbird 145 or newer.

Thunderbird implements Exchange via the EWS API (Exchange Web Services), ''''''currently limited to email''''''. 

Calendar and address book using the EWS API will follow at a later date. Also in the future is Exchange via ''''''Microsoft Graph'''''', so please do not file bug reports for these items at this time. 

Exchange is new, so we very much welcome your [[#w_feedback-and-bug-reports|feedback and bug reports]]. For more technical detail, as well as things to test and look for, see the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page]. {/warning}

__TOC__

=Setup=
When creating a new account using classic account creation, choose the "Exchange Web Services" option. Or if using the new Account Hub, when providing an exchange email address, "Exchange" should be automatically detected. If exchange is not detected, choose the first "Exchange" option.

==1. Configure your Exchange account==
===Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird ''''''Account Hub'''''' flow:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email}.
# Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account.{note}''''''Note:'''''' You do not need to enter your password in the ''''''Password'''''' field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note}Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#;[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11]]
# Click the {button Exchange} button (not the one labelled {button Exchange  REQUIRES ADD-ON}) in the ''''''Choose your email account type'''''' dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.{note}''''''Note:'''''' The {button Exchange} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
#;[[Image:tb142-beta-exchange-support-button]]
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
[[UI:details_start]]
====Manual EWS Configuration====
There are a diversity of EWS servers which could cause auto configuration of your EWS email account to fail. Here''s a potential workaround for that situation:
# In [[New in Thunderbird Desktop|145]] and newer once you enter a valid email address, you can now manually configure your email settings by clicking MANUAL CONFIGURATION.  Please consult your Exhchange administrator for the exact manual settings.
# Under ''''''Protocol'''''' select {menu EWS}.
# Follow the prompts and fill in the settings from your Exchange administrator.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
===Thunderbird profile with no accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with no accounts, you will see the older, ''''''Set Up Your Existing Email Address'''''' flow:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email}.
# Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account.{note}''''''Note:'''''' You do not need to enter your password in the ''''''Password'''''' field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note}Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#;[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11]]
# Click the {button Exchange Web Services} button (not the one labelled {button Exchange/Office365}) in the ''''''Choose your email account type'''''' dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange implementation.{note}''''''Note:'''''' The {button Exchange Web Services} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
#;[[Image:tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button]]
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
[[UI:details_end]]

==2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account==
Once you have configured your Exchange Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|send and receive emails]] just like an IMAP or POP account.

=Limitations=
Not yet supported:
* Address book
* Calendar
* Filters (Phase 5)
* Folder quotas (Phase 5)
* Folder subscription (Phase 5)
* Message retention policies (Phase 5)
* Message download sync for offline use (Phase 5)
* Message tagging (Phase 5)
* NTLM authentication (Phase 5)
* OAuth authentication with on-premise instances (Phase 5)
* Shared mailboxes (Phase 5)
* Star message (Phase 5)
"Phase 5" items are on the near term road map, expected to by available/resolved by 1Q2026. The full list of phase 5 is [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/showdependencytree.cgi?id=1995377&hide_resolved=1 this bug list].

=Feedback and Bug Reports=
To report a problem when using version 145 or newer, please [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&component=Networking:%20Exchange&short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&blocked=1847846&bug_type=defect file a bug report]. To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].

You may use topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta beta group] or the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise enterprise group].

=Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers=
Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].','<div class="warning">
<p>For the best Exchange experience, we recommend Thunderbird 145 or newer.
</p><p>Thunderbird implements Exchange via the EWS API (Exchange Web Services), <strong>currently limited to email</strong>. 
</p><p>Calendar and address book using the EWS API will follow at a later date. Also in the future is Exchange via <strong>Microsoft Graph</strong>, so please do not file bug reports for these items at this time. 
</p>
Exchange is new, so we very much welcome your <a href="#w_feedback-and-bug-reports">feedback and bug reports</a>. For more technical detail, as well as things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>. </div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_setup"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Setup</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_1-configure-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">1. Configure your Exchange account</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-4"><a href="#w_manual-ews-configuration"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Manual EWS Configuration</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_2-send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_limitations"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Limitations</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_feedback-and-bug-reports"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Feedback and Bug Reports</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_setup">Setup</h1>
<p>When creating a new account using classic account creation, choose the "Exchange Web Services" option. Or if using the new Account Hub, when providing an exchange email address, "Exchange" should be automatically detected. If exchange is not detected, choose the first "Exchange" option.
</p>
<h2 id="w_1-configure-your-exchange-account">1. Configure your Exchange account</h2>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</h3>
<p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird <strong>Account Hub</strong> flow:
</p>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>.
</li><li> Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> You do not need to enter your password in the <strong>Password</strong> field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div>Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Exchange</span> button (not the one labelled <span class="button">Exchange  REQUIRES ADD-ON</span>) in the <strong>Choose your email account type</strong> dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The <span class="button">Exchange</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div>
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-beta-exchange-support-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-03-20-2802fd.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h4 id="w_manual-ews-configuration" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Manual EWS Configuration</button></h4><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><p>There are a diversity of EWS servers which could cause auto configuration of your EWS email account to fail. Here''s a potential workaround for that situation:
</p><ol><li> In <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop">145</a> and newer once you enter a valid email address, you can now manually configure your email settings by clicking MANUAL CONFIGURATION.  Please consult your Exhchange administrator for the exact manual settings.
</li><li> Under <strong>Protocol</strong> select <span class="menu">EWS</span>.
</li><li> Follow the prompts and fill in the settings from your Exchange administrator.
</li></ol><p></p></div>


</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</button></h3><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with no accounts, you will see the older, <strong>Set Up Your Existing Email Address</strong> flow:
</p><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>.
</li><li> Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> You do not need to enter your password in the <strong>Password</strong> field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div>Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button (not the one labelled <span class="button">Exchange/Office365</span>) in the <strong>Choose your email account type</strong> dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange implementation.<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div>
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-23-12-9340ff.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_2-send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account">2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</h2>
<p>Once you have configured your Exchange Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">send and receive emails</a> just like an IMAP or POP account.
</p>
<h1 id="w_limitations">Limitations</h1>
<p>Not yet supported:
</p>
<ul><li> Address book
</li><li> Calendar
</li><li> Filters (Phase 5)
</li><li> Folder quotas (Phase 5)
</li><li> Folder subscription (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message retention policies (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message download sync for offline use (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message tagging (Phase 5)
</li><li> NTLM authentication (Phase 5)
</li><li> OAuth authentication with on-premise instances (Phase 5)
</li><li> Shared mailboxes (Phase 5)
</li><li> Star message (Phase 5)
</li></ul>
<p>"Phase 5" items are on the near term road map, expected to by available/resolved by 1Q2026. The full list of phase 5 is <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/showdependencytree.cgi?id=1995377&amp;hide_resolved=1">this bug list</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_feedback-and-bug-reports">Feedback and Bug Reports</h1>
<p>To report a problem when using version 145 or newer, please <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&amp;component=Networking:%20Exchange&amp;short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&amp;blocked=1847846&amp;bug_type=defect">file a bug report</a>. To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p><p>You may use topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta">beta group</a> or the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise">enterprise group</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</h1>
<p>Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "313635", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 13, 2025, 12:30:43 AM", "datetime": "2025-11-13T00:30:43.312607-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Manual configuration of EWS Servers. discussion please: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/109#issuecomment-3526259890", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 13, 2025, 12:32:10 AM", "datetime": "2025-11-13T00:32:10.455658-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:24:36+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (313667,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/313667',313625,'2025-11-13T12:42:23.527912-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','[[Thunderbird and Exchange#w_manual-ews-configuration|Manual EWS configuration section of our Thunderbird and Exchange article]]',1,'2025-11-13T12:43:05.949752-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2025-11-19T14:15:21.950120-08:00','rtanglao','approved','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__
=Thunderbird 145=
* Thunderbird now supports DNS over HTTPS.
* In the ''''''Account Hub'''''', once you enter a valid email address, you can now manually configure your email settings by clicking {menu MANUAL CONFIGURATION}. 
*;[[Image:tb145-account-hub-manual-configuration]]
* ''''''MANUAL CONFIGURATION'''''' in the ''''''Account Hub'''''' supports manual configuration of {menu EWS}, {menu IMAP} and {menu POP3} accounts.
*;[[Image:tb145-ews-imap-pop-account-hub-manual-configuration]]
* Manual configuration of EWS accounts is now supported as per the screenshots in the above two bullet points. For more details, please see the [[Thunderbird and Exchange#w_manual-ews-configuration|Manual EWS configuration section of our Thunderbird and Exchange article]].
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 144=
==Exchange enhancements and bug fixes==
* Another bug fix release.
* Various Exchange Support fixes. This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions. We are planning a promotional splash in one of the next few releases. Getting closer!
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 143=
==Exchange Support enhancements and bug fixes==
* Bug fixes.
* Various Exchange Support fixes. This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 142=
==Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues with Hotmail and outlook.com accounts==
If you see: ''''''Exchange auth error'''''' or ''''''Authentication failed. Please check the username and password'''''' when adding a ''''''Hotmail'''''' or ''''''outlook.com'''''' account, here''s how to switch to the old ''''''Account Setup'''''' flow to fix the problem:
* Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings} > {menu General} and untick ''''''Create accounts in the new Account Hub'''''':
*;[[Image:tb142-disable-account-hub|width=350]]
* Please try adding the email account again. If you still have issues, please [https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form file a support request on SUMO].
This will be fixed in a future Thunderbird release.
==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key Control}+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder which will be fixed in a future release. You can follow along in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979880 bug 1979880].
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order|width=350]]
==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]].
==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.
==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}. Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.
==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].
== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=
==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]
==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].
==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub'''''' (not enabled in ESR, we recommend the latest monthly release for the best experience).
==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].
==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
<p></p><p>This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release">Thunderbird Release for Desktop</a>. For full details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>.
</p>
