<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-142">Thunderbird 142</h1>
<h2 id="w_switch-to-the-old-account-setup-flow-to-fix-issues-with-hotmail-and-outlook-com-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues with Hotmail and <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> accounts</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><p>If you see: <strong>Exchange auth error</strong> or <strong>Authentication failed. Please check the username and password</strong> when adding a <strong>Hotmail</strong> or <strong><a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a></strong> account, here''s how to switch to the old <strong>Account Setup</strong> flow to fix the problem:
</p><ul><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> and untick <strong>Create accounts in the new Account Hub</strong>:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-disable-account-hub" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-27-10-54-39-2636ed.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="350">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Please try adding the email account again. If you still have issues, please <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">file a support request on SUMO</a>.
</li></ul><p>This will be fixed in a future Thunderbird release.
</p></div>



<h2 id="w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Reset manual folder sorting order</button></h2>
<ol class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><li> Right click (<span class="key">Control</span>+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. <strong><a href="mailto:nemo@thunderbird.net">nemo@thunderbird.net</a></strong> in the <strong>Folder Pane</strong> (more details: <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-main-window-supernova">Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)</a> and then:
</li><li> Click the menu item <span class="menu">Reset Folder Order</span> to clear any previously defined manual sorting. <strong>NOTE</strong>: This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder which will be fixed in a future release. You can follow along in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979880">bug 1979880</a>.
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-reset-folder-order" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-00-23-24-8d62b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="350">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Add a visual signature to a PDF</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true">Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: <a href="/en-US/kb/view-pdf-files-firefox-or-choose-another-viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf">View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true">See the 141 section for more details.
</p>
<h2 id="w_more-stable-exchange-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">More stable Exchange support</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true">This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange">Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)</a> and our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-141">Thunderbird 141</h1>
<h2 id="w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Archive action added to new email notifications</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true"><li> You can now <span class="button">Archive</span> email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to <span class="button">Mark as Read</span>, <span class="button">Delete</span>, <span class="button">Mark as Starred</span> and <span class="button">Mark as Spam</span>. Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird">New email notifications in Thunderbird</a> for further information.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_better-exchange-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Better Exchange support</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true">Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p>
<h2 id="w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><p>If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.
</p><p>More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in <a href="/en-US/kb/introduction-to-e2e-encryption">Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird</a> and <a href="/en-US/kb/openpgp-thunderbird-howto-and-faq">OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ</a>.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true">This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511">bug 1979511</a>.
</p></section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Dark Message Mode</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true"><p>Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl></div>


<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong> (not enabled in ESR, we recommend the latest monthly release for the best experience).
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-hidden="true">Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p>
<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-18" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-18" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-139" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-19" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 139</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-19" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-138" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-20" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 138</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-20" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-137" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-21" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 137</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-21" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-136" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-22" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 136</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-22" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "313667", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 13, 2025, 12:42:23 PM", "datetime": "2025-11-13T12:42:23.527912-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "[[Thunderbird and Exchange#w_manual-ews-configuration|Manual EWS configuration section of our Thunderbird and Exchange article]]", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Nov 13, 2025, 12:43:05 PM", "datetime": "2025-11-13T12:43:05.949752-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Nov 19, 2025, 2:15:21 PM", "datetime": "2025-11-19T14:15:21.950120-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:24:34+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (313932,'en-US','thunderbird-and-exchange','Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange/revision/313932',313635,'2025-11-17T13:04:40.506317-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','EWS instead of "EWS API"  and  "Microsoft Graph" instead of Graph API as agreed by MZLA staff;  Repeat the 145 disclaimer discussion please at: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/109#issuecomment-3543776874',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','{warning}
For the best Exchange experience, we recommend Thunderbird 145 or newer.
Thunderbird implements Exchange via EWS (Exchange Web Services), ''''''currently limited to email''''''.

Calendar and address book using EWS will follow at a later date. Also in the future, is Exchange via ''''''''Microsoft Graph'''''', so please do not file bug reports for these items at this time.

Exchange is new, so we very much welcome your [[#w_feedback-and-bug-reports|feedback and bug reports]]. For more technical detail, as well as things to test and look for, see the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].{/warning}

__TOC__

=Setup=
When creating a new account using classic account creation, choose the ''''''Exchange Web Services'''''' option. Or if using the new Account Hub, when providing an exchange email address, ''''''Exchange'''''' should be automatically detected. If Exchange is not detected, choose the first ''''''Exchange'''''' option.
==Configure your Exchange account==
Again, for the best experience, we recommend Thunderbird 145 or newer.
[[UI:details_start]]
===Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird ''''''Account Hub''''''.
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email}. The ''''''Account Hub'''''' window will appear.
# Enter your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account.
# Click the {button Continue} button. The password entry window will appear.<br><br>{note}''''''Note:'''''' In the first dialog box, you do not enter your account password. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note} Screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#:[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11|width=450]]
# Enter your password and click {button Sign in}. The account type selection window will appear.
#:[[Image:tb142-beta-exchange-support-button|width=450]]
# Select the {button Exchange} radio button and click {button Continue} to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
{note}''''''Note:'''''' The {button Exchange} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
====Manual EWS Configuration====
There are a diversity of EWS servers which could cause auto configuration of your EWS email account to fail. Here''s a potential workaround for that situation:
# In [[New in Thunderbird Desktop|145]] and newer once you enter a valid email address, you can now manually configure your email settings by clicking {menu MANUAL CONFIGURATION}. Please consult your Exchange administrator for the exact manual settings.
# Under ''''''Protocol'''''', select {menu EWS}.
# Follow the prompts and fill in the settings from your Exchange administrator.
[[UI:details_end]]

[[UI:details_start]]
===Thunderbird profile with no accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with no accounts, you will see the older add account wizard.
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email}. The ''''''Account Hub'''''' window will appear.
# Enter your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account.
# Click the {button Continue} button. The password entry window will appear.<br><br>{note}''''''Note:'''''' In the first dialog box, you do not enter your account password. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note} Screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#:[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11|width=450]]
# Enter your password and click {button Sign in}. The account settings window will appear.
#:[[Image:tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button]]
# Select the {button Exchange Web Services} radio button and click {button Continue} to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
{note}''''''Note:'''''' The {button Exchange Web Services} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
[[UI:details_end]]
=Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account=
Once you have configured your Exchange Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|send and receive emails]] just like an IMAP or POP account.
=Limitations=
Not yet supported:
* Address book
* Calendar
* Filters (Phase 5)
* Folder quotas (Phase 5)
* Folder subscription (Phase 5)
* Message retention policies (Phase 5)
* Message download sync for offline use (Phase 5)
* Message tagging (Phase 5)
* NTLM authentication (Phase 5)
* OAuth authentication with on-premise instances (Phase 5)
* Shared mailboxes (Phase 5)
* Star message (Phase 5)
"Phase 5" items are on the near term road map, expected to by available/resolved by 1Q2026. The full list of phase 5 is [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/showdependencytree.cgi?id=1995377&hide_resolved=1 this bug list].
=Feedback and Bug Reports=
To report a problem when using version 145 or newer, please [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&component=Networking:%20Exchange&short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&blocked=1847846&bug_type=defect file a bug report]. 

To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].

You may use Topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta beta group] or the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise enterprise group].
= Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers=
Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].','<div class="warning">
<p>For the best Exchange experience, we recommend Thunderbird 145 or newer.
Thunderbird implements Exchange via EWS (Exchange Web Services), <strong>currently limited to email</strong>.
</p><p>Calendar and address book using EWS will follow at a later date. Also in the future, is Exchange via ''<strong>Microsoft Graph</strong>, so please do not file bug reports for these items at this time.
</p>
Exchange is new, so we very much welcome your <a href="#w_feedback-and-bug-reports">feedback and bug reports</a>. For more technical detail, as well as things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.</div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_setup"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Setup</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_configure-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Configure your Exchange account</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-4"><a href="#w_manual-ews-configuration"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Manual EWS Configuration</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_limitations"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Limitations</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_feedback-and-bug-reports"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Feedback and Bug Reports</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_setup">Setup</h1>
<p>When creating a new account using classic account creation, choose the <strong>Exchange Web Services</strong> option. Or if using the new Account Hub, when providing an exchange email address, <strong>Exchange</strong> should be automatically detected. If Exchange is not detected, choose the first <strong>Exchange</strong> option.
</p>
<h2 id="w_configure-your-exchange-account">Configure your Exchange account</h2>
<p>Again, for the best experience, we recommend Thunderbird 145 or newer.
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</button></h3><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird <strong>Account Hub</strong>.
</p><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>. The <strong>Account Hub</strong> window will appear.
</li><li> Enter your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Continue</span> button. The password entry window will appear.<br><br><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> In the first dialog box, you do not enter your account password. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div> Screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dd><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="450">
</dd></dl>
</li><li> Enter your password and click <span class="button">Sign in</span>. The account type selection window will appear.
<dl><dd><img alt="tb142-beta-exchange-support-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-03-20-2802fd.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="450">
</dd></dl>
</li><li> Select the <span class="button">Exchange</span> radio button and click <span class="button">Continue</span> to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The <span class="button">Exchange</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div><h4 id="w_manual-ews-configuration">Manual EWS Configuration</h4><p>There are a diversity of EWS servers which could cause auto configuration of your EWS email account to fail. Here''s a potential workaround for that situation:
</p><ol><li> In <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop">145</a> and newer once you enter a valid email address, you can now manually configure your email settings by clicking <span class="menu">MANUAL CONFIGURATION</span>. Please consult your Exchange administrator for the exact manual settings.
</li><li> Under <strong>Protocol</strong>, select <span class="menu">EWS</span>.
</li><li> Follow the prompts and fill in the settings from your Exchange administrator.
</li></ol><p></p></div>






</section>
<p></p><p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</button></h3><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with no accounts, you will see the older add account wizard.
</p><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>. The <strong>Account Hub</strong> window will appear.
</li><li> Enter your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Continue</span> button. The password entry window will appear.<br><br><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> In the first dialog box, you do not enter your account password. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div> Screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dd><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="450">
</dd></dl>
</li><li> Enter your password and click <span class="button">Sign in</span>. The account settings window will appear.
<dl><dd><img alt="tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-23-12-9340ff.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dd></dl>
</li><li> Select the <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> radio button and click <span class="button">Continue</span> to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div><p></p></div>



</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account">Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</h1>
<p>Once you have configured your Exchange Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">send and receive emails</a> just like an IMAP or POP account.
</p>
<h1 id="w_limitations">Limitations</h1>
<p>Not yet supported:
</p>
<ul><li> Address book
</li><li> Calendar
</li><li> Filters (Phase 5)
</li><li> Folder quotas (Phase 5)
</li><li> Folder subscription (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message retention policies (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message download sync for offline use (Phase 5)
</li><li> Message tagging (Phase 5)
</li><li> NTLM authentication (Phase 5)
</li><li> OAuth authentication with on-premise instances (Phase 5)
</li><li> Shared mailboxes (Phase 5)
</li><li> Star message (Phase 5)
</li></ul>
<p>"Phase 5" items are on the near term road map, expected to by available/resolved by 1Q2026. The full list of phase 5 is <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/showdependencytree.cgi?id=1995377&amp;hide_resolved=1">this bug list</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_feedback-and-bug-reports">Feedback and Bug Reports</h1>
<p>To report a problem when using version 145 or newer, please <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&amp;component=Networking:%20Exchange&amp;short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&amp;blocked=1847846&amp;bug_type=defect">file a bug report</a>. 
</p><p>To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p><p>You may use Topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta">beta group</a> or the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise">enterprise group</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</h1>
<p>Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "313932", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 17, 2025, 1:04:40 PM", "datetime": "2025-11-17T13:04:40.506317-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "EWS instead of \"EWS API\"  and  \"Microsoft Graph\" instead of Graph API as agreed by MZLA staff;  Repeat the 145 disclaimer discussion please at: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/109#issuecomment-3543776874", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:24:31+00:00');
