INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (318552,'en-US','thunderbird-128-nebula-faq','Thunderbird 128 Nebula FAQ','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-128-nebula-faq','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-128-nebula-faq/revision/318552',288401,'2026-01-19T11:42:25.375087-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix exchange section',1,'2026-01-19T11:42:51.879249-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2026-01-19T11:42:51.879249-08:00','rtanglao','approved','[[T:TBMore]]
This article answers questions for new users of Thunderbird 128 (Nebula), in particular users who have upgraded from a previous version.

Nebula is constantly evolving. Throughout the next year, we will deliver many improvements to existing Nebula features and introduce brand new ones. Upgrade to version 128 and experience the future of Thunderbird!

__TOC__

== What is happening with Thunderbird Sync? ==
We are building our own sync storage server and it is taking some time to set it up and test. We will let you know when it is available for public pre-release testing.

== What is happening with Exchange Support? ==

We recommend you use Exchange in Thunderbird for Desktop 147 or newer. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] for more details including current limitations.

== Why is Thunderbird 128 labeled as 128.0esr when previous versions were not called ESR? ==

''''''In short: Thunderbird 128.0esr is the same release channel as Thunderbird 115, only the name has changed''''''. This channel gets a yearly major feature release as always.

For 128, we added “ESR”(which stands for Extended Support Release) to the name because we’re introducing a new monthly feature release channel similar to the [[Choose a Firefox update channel|Firefox Rapid Release channel]]. So we needed to distinguish between that and the yearly channel. Since Firefox calls their yearly release “ESR”, we opted to do the same.

For many years, due to lack of development resources, Thunderbird had no monthly feature release at all. There was only Beta. During that time, it wasn’t necessary to use the “ESR” label.

Going forward, there will be four Thunderbird channels:
* ''''''Daily'''''': Updates every day with the latest changes directly from development branches, for bleeding edge testers.
* ''''''Beta'''''': Major updates every 4 weeks, after testing on Daily. Provides testing for final release branches.
* ''''''Release'''''': Major updates every 4 weeks, containing everything that was tested on Beta the previous month.
* ''''''Extended Support Release (ESR)'''''': Major updates once per year, minor and security updates the rest of the time, with support extending for ~15 months after a major update.

''''The new monthly feature release channel will be available for testing and use later this year.''''
== Why are my Thunderbird customizations broken in 128? ==
If your customization required changes to userChrome.css, userContent.css, or other related files, then these [[userChrome.css and .js and userContent are unsupported|userChrome* customizations are still unsupported in 128]] (they were also unsupported in 115 and all previous releases). There may be [https://support.mozilla.org/questions/thunderbird?tagged=unsupporteduserchromecss&show=all solutions in the forums] but please remember these are unofficial; unsupported solutions and could break at any time.','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
This article answers questions for new users of Thunderbird 128 (Nebula), in particular users who have upgraded from a previous version.
<p></p><p>Nebula is constantly evolving. Throughout the next year, we will deliver many improvements to existing Nebula features and introduce brand new ones. Upgrade to version 128 and experience the future of Thunderbird!
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_what-is-happening-with-thunderbird-sync"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">What is happening with Thunderbird Sync?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_what-is-happening-with-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">What is happening with Exchange Support?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_why-is-thunderbird-128-labeled-as-128-0esr-when-previous-versions-were-not-called-esr"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Why is Thunderbird 128 labeled as 128.0esr when previous versions were not called ESR?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_why-are-my-thunderbird-customizations-broken-in-128"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Why are my Thunderbird customizations broken in 128?</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_what-is-happening-with-thunderbird-sync">What is happening with Thunderbird Sync?</h2>
<p>We are building our own sync storage server and it is taking some time to set it up and test. We will let you know when it is available for public pre-release testing.
</p>
<h2 id="w_what-is-happening-with-exchange-support">What is happening with Exchange Support?</h2>
<p>We recommend you use Exchange in Thunderbird for Desktop 147 or newer. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange">Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)</a> for more details including current limitations.
</p>
<h2 id="w_why-is-thunderbird-128-labeled-as-128-0esr-when-previous-versions-were-not-called-esr">Why is Thunderbird 128 labeled as 128.0esr when previous versions were not called ESR?</h2>
<p><strong>In short: Thunderbird 128.0esr is the same release channel as Thunderbird 115, only the name has changed</strong>. This channel gets a yearly major feature release as always.
</p><p>For 128, we added “ESR”(which stands for Extended Support Release) to the name because we’re introducing a new monthly feature release channel similar to the <a href="/en-US/kb/choosing-firefox-update-channel">Firefox Rapid Release channel</a>. So we needed to distinguish between that and the yearly channel. Since Firefox calls their yearly release “ESR”, we opted to do the same.
</p><p>For many years, due to lack of development resources, Thunderbird had no monthly feature release at all. There was only Beta. During that time, it wasn’t necessary to use the “ESR” label.
</p><p>Going forward, there will be four Thunderbird channels:
</p>
<ul><li> <strong>Daily</strong>: Updates every day with the latest changes directly from development branches, for bleeding edge testers.
</li><li> <strong>Beta</strong>: Major updates every 4 weeks, after testing on Daily. Provides testing for final release branches.
</li><li> <strong>Release</strong>: Major updates every 4 weeks, containing everything that was tested on Beta the previous month.
</li><li> <strong>Extended Support Release (ESR)</strong>: Major updates once per year, minor and security updates the rest of the time, with support extending for ~15 months after a major update.
</li></ul>
<p><em>The new monthly feature release channel will be available for testing and use later this year.</em>
</p>
<h2 id="w_why-are-my-thunderbird-customizations-broken-in-128">Why are my Thunderbird customizations broken in 128?</h2>
<p>If your customization required changes to userChrome.css, userContent.css, or other related files, then these <a href="/en-US/kb/userchromecss-js-usercontent-unsupported">userChrome* customizations are still unsupported in 128</a> (they were also unsupported in 115 and all previous releases). There may be <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/thunderbird?tagged=unsupporteduserchromecss&amp;show=all">solutions in the forums</a> but please remember these are unofficial; unsupported solutions and could break at any time.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "318552", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jan 19, 2026, 11:42:25 AM", "datetime": "2026-01-19T11:42:25.375087-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix exchange section", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jan 19, 2026, 11:42:51 AM", "datetime": "2026-01-19T11:42:51.879249-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jan 19, 2026, 11:42:51 AM", "datetime": "2026-01-19T11:42:51.879249-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:24:04+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (319608,'en-US','new-thunderbird-android','New in Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android/revision/319608',318066,'2026-02-09T00:00:14.830759-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','dicussion please: https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/32',1,'2026-02-09T00:00:35.536265-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[T:TBAndroidMore]]
This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in Thunderbird for Android. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__
=Thunderbird 16=
* The SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com have been fixed in [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312 #10312].
* Known Issue: Deleted/read messages in your unified inbox may not update until you manually refresh. We hope to have a fix soon. you can can follow along on issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10243 #10243]


=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 15==
* There are further SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com and the team is testing a fix. You can follow along on issue [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312 #10312]. It looks like this will fixed in the next release, TB 16.
==Thunderbird 14==
* SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com have been fixed.
==Thunderbird 13==
* The notification in status bar re-appearing multiple times a day issue (github issue [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/8049 #8049]) has been fixed.
* Special folders (Trash, Sent, Drafts, Archives, etc) not appearing after updating from TB11 to TB12 (github issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9771 #9771]) was fixed.
* The bug with outgoing email not working for certain educational and enterprise accounts is scheduled to be fixed in the next release, Thunderbird 14 for Android (github issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9160 #9160]).
==Thunderbird 12==
<!--
for discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/22
see: https://matrix.to/#/!xPTYfLywxFMryjbnJl:mozilla.org/$okoHEWLX71BqfNVgYgNggAYMLJgg1-xGW4gq9BUs4Dg?via=mozilla.org&via=matrix.org&via=chat.rhaalovely.net
* You can now add your avatar in Account Settings <-- commented out until I can figure out 
how to make this work
-->
* If you use a password manager, Android will now use it to automatically fill in your password when you add a new account.
==Thunderbird 11==
* Mail folders are easier to navigate.
* Algorithmic darkening makes reading emails easier in dark mode.
* Thunderbird 11.1 : Selected/read/unread message states are now easier to distinguish visually.
* You can still see font settings if you search for ''''''font'''''' in Settings. This will be removed in a future Thunderbird release. Please use the Android operating system font size settings instead.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 10==
* You can now empty your Spam folder by tapping {menu Empty Spam} in the Spam folder''s menu {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''''kebab'''''' menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab).
* On Android 10 or older, you now have an option to use the system theme.
*# Tap {button ≡} at the top left > tap the gear icon:{button [[Image:gear icon]]} at the bottom left.
*# Tap {button General settings} > tap {menu Display} > tap {button Use system default} under ''''''Theme''''''
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 9==
* Initial Android 15 support.
* Thunderbird attempts to use your email provider''s auto configuration database. If it fails it, it uses Mozilla''s database.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 8==
* Refer to [[New in Thunderbird for Android version 8]] please.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird for Android: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird%20android">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird-android/form">Get Support</a></div>
