</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "319693", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 10, 2026, 12:12:17 PM", "datetime": "2026-02-10T12:12:17.245301-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "works on k-9 too of course! english only for now, so do not translate please! Discussion please https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/23", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Feb 10, 2026, 12:12:32 PM", "datetime": "2026-02-10T12:12:32.426434-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:23:21+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (319788,'en-US','thundermail-and-thunderbird-android','Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android/revision/319788',319693,'2026-02-11T08:31:09.458637-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix support link and formatting. english only for now, so do not translate please! Discussion please https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/23',1,'2026-02-11T08:31:43.220278-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[Template:TBproEarlyBirdInviteOnly]]
Here’s how to get started with Mozilla’s Thundermail service. 

=Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird for Android=
''''''NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires Thunderbird (and of course K-9 as well) 15 for Android or newer. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird for Android, which is documented in [[New in Thunderbird for Android]].

# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > {menu Add account}.
# Enter your Thundermail email address (for example [mailto:nemo@thundermail.com nemo@thundermail.com]) 
# Click {button Next}.
# The next screen will prompt you to ''''''Please specify the special folders for your account'''''' along with some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click {button Next}. 
# On the next screen, configure your user name under ''''''Your name'''''' and optionally your signature and {button Next}.
# The next screen will give you some sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click {button Next} .

=Manual settings=

Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your [https://accounts.tb.pro/self-serve/connection-info TB Pro accounts page]. If it doesn’t, please try manually changing the receiving email and sending email settings as per the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new
[[UI:details_start]]

==Receiving Email==
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}
# Under ''''''Accounts'''''', tap on your Thundermail email account. (For example: [mailto:nemo@thundermail.com nemo@thundermail.com])
# Tap {menu Fetching mail} > {menu Incoming Server} and set the following values:
*''''''Server:'''''' [http://mail.thundermail.com mail.thundermail.com] ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS ''''''Port:'''''' 993
*''''''Authentication:'''''' OAuth 2.0
*''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address e.g. [mailto:nemo@thundermail.com nemo@thundermail.com]

==Sending Email==
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}
# Under ''''''Accounts'''''', tap on your Thundermail email account. (For example: [mailto:nemo@thundermail.com nemo@thundermail.com])
# Tap {menu Sending mail} > {menu Outgoing server} and set the following values:
* ''''''Server Name:'''''' [http://mail.thundermail.com mail.thundermail.com] ''''''Connection'''''' ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS ''''''Port:'''''' 465
* ''''''Authentication:'''''' OAuth 2.0
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address For example: nemo@thundermail.com

[[UI:details_end]]

=Send and receive email and have some fun!=
* Send and receive email with Thundermail.
* New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out [[Getting started with Thunderbird for Android]].
<!--
* If you have large files, you can send them with FIXME because Send on Mobile needs some polish: add link to Thunderbird Send which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
-->','<p></p><div class="warning">NOTE: Thundermail (formerly known as Thunderbird Pro) is currently in its Early Bird release and available  by invitation only. To learn more and join the waitlist, visit <a href="https://tb.pro/">our website</a>. We’ll be opening Thundermail to the public once the Early Bird release concludes.</div>
Here’s how to get started with Mozilla’s Thundermail service. 
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-for-android">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird for Android</h1>
<p><strong>NOTE</strong>: Thunderbird Pro requires Thunderbird (and of course K-9 as well) 15 for Android or newer. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird for Android, which is documented in <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android">New in Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add account</span>.
</li><li> Enter your Thundermail email address (for example <a href="mailto:nemo@thundermail.com">nemo@thundermail.com</a>) 
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen will prompt you to <strong>Please specify the special folders for your account</strong> along with some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span>. 
</li><li> On the next screen, configure your user name under <strong>Your name</strong> and optionally your signature and <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen will give you some sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span> .
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_manual-settings">Manual settings</h1>
<p>Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/self-serve/connection-info">TB Pro accounts page</a>. If it doesn’t, please try manually changing the receiving email and sending email settings as per the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new</a>
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_receiving-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Receiving Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. (For example: <a href="mailto:nemo@thundermail.com">nemo@thundermail.com</a>)
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Incoming Server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li><strong>Server:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 993
</li><li><strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li><strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address e.g.&nbsp;<a href="mailto:nemo@thundermail.com">nemo@thundermail.com</a>
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. (For example: <a href="mailto:nemo@thundermail.com">nemo@thundermail.com</a>)
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Sending mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Outgoing server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a> <strong>Connection</strong> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 465
</li><li> <strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address For example: <a href="mailto:nemo@thundermail.com">nemo@thundermail.com</a>
</li></ul><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_send-and-receive-email-and-have-some-fun">Send and receive email and have some fun!</h1>
<ul><li> Send and receive email with Thundermail.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-android">Getting started with Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "319788", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 11, 2026, 8:31:09 AM", "datetime": "2026-02-11T08:31:09.458637-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix support link and formatting. english only for now, so do not translate please! Discussion please https://github.com/thunderbird/android-knowledgebase-issues/issues/23", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Feb 11, 2026, 8:31:43 AM", "datetime": "2026-02-11T08:31:43.220278-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:23:18+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (319789,'en-US','getting-started-thunderbird-pro','Getting Started with Thunderbird Pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro/revision/319789',319691,'2026-02-11T08:36:34.834307-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix support link and formatting. english only for now, so do not translate please! Discussion please https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/118',1,'2026-02-11T08:36:47.533457-08:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','For the best experience, we recommend that you start off with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari.

* If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, install the Thunderbird Pro add-on as per [[Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop]]. If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
* Login. You''ll have to enter a credit card number even though you may have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code (have problems with a code that you received? please [https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new ask for support]). Currently, only credit cards  are accepted. Apple Pay, Paypal and other 3rd party services are not currently supported. 
* Configure Thunderbird for Desktop for Thundermail as per the article [[Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail]].
* Configure Thunderbird for Android for Thundermail as per the article: [[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android]].
* Configure Appointment as per [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907 our Appointment articles].
* Configure Send as per [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 our Send articles].

Go forth, set up some office hours with Appointment, send some files with Send and send and receive email with Thundermail!','<p>For the best experience, we recommend that you start off with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari.
</p>
<ul><li> If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, install the Thunderbird Pro add-on as per <a href="/en-US/kb/install-thunderbird-pro-add-thunderbird-desktop">Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop</a>. If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
</li><li> Login. You''ll have to enter a credit card number even though you may have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code (have problems with a code that you received? please <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">ask for support</a>). Currently, only credit cards  are accepted. Apple Pay, Paypal and other 3rd party services are not currently supported. 
</li><li> Configure Thunderbird for Desktop for Thundermail as per the article <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail">Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail</a>.
</li><li> Configure Thunderbird for Android for Thundermail as per the article: <a href="/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android">Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li><li> Configure Appointment as per <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907">our Appointment articles</a>.
</li><li> Configure Send as per <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235">our Send articles</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>Go forth, set up some office hours with Appointment, send some files with Send and send and receive email with Thundermail!
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "319789", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 11, 2026, 8:36:34 AM", "datetime": "2026-02-11T08:36:34.834307-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix support link and formatting. english only for now, so do not translate please! Discussion please https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/118", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Feb 11, 2026, 8:36:47 AM", "datetime": "2026-02-11T08:36:47.533457-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:23:16+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (319793,'en-US','install-thunderbird-pro-add-thunderbird-desktop','Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/install-thunderbird-pro-add-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/install-thunderbird-pro-add-thunderbird-desktop/revision/319793',319686,'2026-02-11T12:42:38.931090-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','recommend latest ESR or newer, discussion please: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/111',1,'2026-02-11T12:43:30.958167-08:00','rtanglao',1,1,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[Template:TBproEarlyBirdInviteOnly]]

{note}''''''PLEASE NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires the latest [[Thunderbird ESR]] release or newer. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird, which is documented here: [[New in Thunderbird Desktop]].{/note}

= Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on =

The [https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/pro/ ''''''Thunderbird Pro add-on''''''] is [[Installing an Add-on in Thunderbird|installed]] like any other Thunderbird add-on:

# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > {menu Add-ons and Themes}.
# Enter “''''''Thunderbird Pro''''''” in ''''''Find more add-ons''''''.
# Click {button Add to Thunderbird} and then {button Add} in the dialogue that pops up. Follow the prompts to complete the process.
#;[[Image:2026-02-10 how install tb pro add-on]] 

= Explore the Power of Thunderbird Pro! =

* [[Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail|Add your Thundermail account to Thunderbird Desktop]] and send some messages!
* If you have an Android phone, [[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android|add your Thundermail account to Thunderbird for Android]] and send some email while on the go.

* Configure [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 Thunderbird Send''''''] for sending large files.
* Have folks book time on your calendar by setting up [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907 ''''''Thunderbird Appointment''''''].

And more!','<p></p><div class="warning">NOTE: Thundermail (formerly known as Thunderbird Pro) is currently in its Early Bird release and available  by invitation only. To learn more and join the waitlist, visit <a href="https://tb.pro/">our website</a>. We’ll be opening Thundermail to the public once the Early Bird release concludes.</div>
<p></p>
<div class="note"><strong>PLEASE NOTE</strong>: Thunderbird Pro requires the latest <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-esr">Thunderbird ESR</a> release or newer. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird, which is documented here: <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop">New in Thunderbird Desktop</a>.</div>
<h1 id="w_install-the-thunderbird-pro-add-on">Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on</h1>
<p>The <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/pro/"><strong>Thunderbird Pro add-on</strong></a> is <a href="/en-US/kb/installing-addon-thunderbird">installed</a> like any other Thunderbird add-on:
</p>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add-ons and Themes</span>.
</li><li> Enter “<strong>Thunderbird Pro</strong>” in <strong>Find more add-ons</strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Add to Thunderbird</span> and then <span class="button">Add</span> in the dialogue that pops up. Follow the prompts to complete the process.
<dl><dt><img alt="2026-02-10 how install tb pro add-on" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-02-10-10-02-25-efe500.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_explore-the-power-of-thunderbird-pro">Explore the Power of Thunderbird Pro!</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail">Add your Thundermail account to Thunderbird Desktop</a> and send some messages!
</li><li> If you have an Android phone, <a href="/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android">add your Thundermail account to Thunderbird for Android</a> and send some email while on the go.
</li></ul>
<ul><li> Configure <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235">Thunderbird Send<strong></strong></a><strong> for sending large files.
</strong>
</li><li> Have folks book time on your calendar by setting up <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907"><strong>Thunderbird Appointment</strong></a>.
</li></ul>
<p>And more!
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "319793", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 11, 2026, 12:42:38 PM", "datetime": "2026-02-11T12:42:38.931090-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "recommend latest ESR or newer, discussion please: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/111", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Feb 11, 2026, 12:43:30 PM", "datetime": "2026-02-11T12:43:30.958167-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:23:14+00:00');
