 work?</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbirds-filelink-feature">Thunderbird''s Filelink feature</h1>
<p>Many email servers do not accept messages with large file attachments. The file size restriction varies depending on the mail server configuration. While you might be able to send a message with a large attachment, the receiving mail server might refuse to accept a message with a large attachment. This is all beyond the control of Thunderbird.
</p><p>Thunderbird’s Filelink feature eliminates this problem by providing support for online storage services. It allows you to upload attachments to an online storage service, and then replaces the attachment in the message with a link to that online storage. The message recipient clicks the link to download the attachment. As additional benefits, sending and receiving large files is much faster and both you and the recipient will save disk space.
</p><p>Note that you can use Thunderbird Filelink in addition to <a href="/en-US/kb/how-use-attachments">regular attachments</a>. For example, you can attach small files directly to a message and use Filelink for large attachments in the same message.
</p><p>The Thunderbird community has made available a number of <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/tag/filelink">Filelink provider add-ons</a> for various providers (<a href="#w_what-storage-services-are-currently-supported">more details below</a>).
</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The previously inbuilt support for the <em>WeTransfer</em> FileLink provider has been removed.</div>
<h1 id="w_adding-filelink">Adding Filelink</h1>
<p>To use this feature, you need to install one of the <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/tag/filelink">Filelink provider add-ons</a> first, as described below. For some online storage service providers, you may have to first create a new account or configure an existing account with them.
</p>
<ul><li> Click <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Composition</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Attachments</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Find more providers...</span>
</li><li> Choose a Filelink Provider add-on, and click <span class="button">＋ Add to Thunderbird</span>.
</li><li> Confirm add-on permissions from the popup panel with <span class="button">Add</span>.
</li><li> In the <span class="menu">Attachments</span> section of the <em>Settings</em> (see above), click on the button <span class="button">Add [Your Filelink provider]</span>.
</li><li> Add information as requested by the addon.
</li><li> Thunderbird will suggest using Filelink for attachments larger than 5 MB (you can change the threshold in the same section), or you can right-click on a regular attachment to convert it.
</li></ul>
<div class="note">
<ul><li> If you want to be prompted to use Filelink when a message attachment exceeds a certain size, tick the following option:
</li></ul>
<p><strong>[✓] Offer to share for files larger than [5] MB</strong>
</p>
<ul><li> You may also change the threshold file size as required.</li></ul></div>

<h1 id="w_using-filelink">Using Filelink</h1>
<p>When you attach a file to a message, and the file size exceeds the size you have specified above, Thunderbird will automatically offer to use Filelink:
</p><p><img alt="Proton-FileLink-LargeFileNotification" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-05-10-14-54-16-912351.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<ul><li> Click the <span class="button">Link</span> button to upload the file to the online storage service provider.
</li><li> If you prefer to attach the file as a <a href="/en-US/kb/how-use-attachments">regular attachment</a>, choose <span class="button">Ignore</span>.
</li></ul>
<p>After choosing <span class="button">Link</span>, your file will be uploaded in the background and the displayed message will update to:
</p><p><img alt="Proton-FileLink-UploadingFileNotification" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-05-10-14-51-18-5d2e96.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note"> Regardless of the file size and the Filelink notification, you can always force a file to be attached using Filelink:
<ul><li> Choose the down arrow of the <span class="button">Attach | v</span> button on the composition toolbar to access the <span class="menu">Filelink</span> submenu.
</li><li> Right-click on a regular attachment and from the context menu, choose <span class="menu">Convert to...</span> &gt; <span class="menu">[Your FileLink provider]</span>. You can choose from a list of your enabled providers.</li></ul></div>

<p>When the linking is complete – that is, your attachment has been uploaded to the service provider – Thunderbird will automatically add a section in the message with a link to the online copy of your file  as shown below:
</p><p><img alt="TB78-filelink-linked-anonymous" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-08-29-10-09-54-3855ee.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The link section will appear in plain text, if <strong>Compose messages in HTML format</strong> is turned off in Account Settings.</div>
<p>When your recipients receive the message, they will see the same information and clicking the link in the message will take them to a page where they can download the attachment.
</p>
<hr>
<h1 id="w_filelink-faq">Filelink FAQ</h1>
<p>Attachments that you send via Filelink are not stored on Thunderbird servers. Each file storage service provider has its own privacy policy and terms of service. The file storage service provider has reviewed the Filelink feature to ensure that it is consistent with their policies.
</p>
<h2 id="w_does-thunderbird-know-which-provider-the-user-has-picked">Does Thunderbird know which provider the user has picked?</h2>
<p>No. Thunderbird is unaware of which provider has been selected by a user. Provider configuration is stored on the local machine.
</p>
<h2 id="w_what-storage-services-are-currently-supported">What storage services are currently supported?</h2>
<ul><li> A number of popular file storage providers are supported through <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/tag/filelink">Filelink provider add-ons</a>.
</li><li> You can also use Filelink with your preferred WebDAV server with the <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/filelink-provider-for-webdav/">Filelink provider for WebDAV</a> add-on.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>
<h2 id="w_can-the-storage-service-view-my-attachments">Can the storage service view my attachments?</h2>
<p>Unless you encrypt the file before uploading, the storage services will be able to view the file, as will anyone who obtains the link to the attachment. Users must decide on their own which service provider they trust with that responsibility. Service providers will generally explain your privacy rights in their terms of service. 
</p><p>Note that standard attachment functionality is also not encrypted. When you send an attachment the "normal" way, without using Thunderbird’s OpenPGP or SMIME features, the file can be accessed by anyone that can access the message between your system and the recipients system (such as your email service provider). Filelink adds some security as file uploads to the storage service provider are sent via HTTPS, a secure protocol. We recommend using Thunderbird''s OpenPGP or SMIME features for maximum security of your communications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_how-long-will-my-file-be-available-on-the-storage-service-providers-site">How long will my file be available on the storage service provider''s site?</h2>
<p>Depending on the terms and conditions of your third-party storage service provider and your service agreement with them, the file may remain available on the provider’s site for a limited period, a certain number of downloads, or until you explicitly delete it. You will need to log in to the provider’s website to view and delete the files in your personal storage space.
</p>
<h2 id="w_can-you-support-service-provider-x-or-protocol-y">Can you support service provider X or protocol Y?</h2>
<p>Please check if the Thunderbird community has provided a <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/tag/filelink">Filelink provider add-on</a> for the service provider you are looking for.
<a href="https://webextension-api.thunderbird.net/en/stable/cloudFile.html">Developer documentation for the Filelink API</a> is available.
</p>
<h2 id="w_i-dont-like-the-idea-of-storing-my-files-with-third-parties-like-this-do-regular-attachments-still-work">I don''t like the idea of storing my files with third-parties like this. Do regular attachments still work?</h2>
<p>Regular email attachments still work the same as they always have. We are just offering you an option to upload large attachments somewhere else if you wish. Thunderbird''s notion of a large file defaults to 5 MB, but can be customized in Thunderbird’s Settings:
</p>
<ol><li> Click <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Composition</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Attachments</span>
</li><li> <strong>[✓] Offer to share for files larger than [5] MB</strong>
</li></ol>
<p>Removing the checkmark will prevent the automatical Filelink notification when you attach big files, but the Filelink feature will still be available from the <span class="button">Attach | v</span> button dropdown as well as other attachment menus and context menus.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "320486", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Feb 23, 2026, 11:41:54 PM", "datetime": "2026-02-23T23:41:54.695892-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "link to Send articles. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/120", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Feb 23, 2026, 11:43:09 PM", "datetime": "2026-02-23T23:43:09.334468-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:23:04+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (320901,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/320901',318403,'2026-02-27T16:14:02.325948-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/123',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 148=
* [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NTLM NTLM authentication] is now supported.
* Thunderbird switched to a more secure authorization protocol called ''''''PKCE'''''' for Yahoo, AT&T and AOL accounts. This switch adds support for Yahoo/AOL calendars and adddress books. Full details: [[Thunderbird and Yahoo]]
* Known issue: Dark mode link colors might be hard to read. Workaround: switch to a different theme. A fix has been developed for a future release; you can follow along in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2018015 bug 2018015].

[[UI:details_start]]

=Thunderbird 147=
==Reset Folder Order==
* {menu Reset Folder Order} has been fixed (see the 142 section). It now restores the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
==Localization of folder names==
* All outstanding issues with localization of folder names have been fixed. If you notice any other issues, please [https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird file a Thunderbird desktop support request].

=Thunderbird 146=
==Drag and Drop on macOS==
* Drag and Drop for attachments on macOS is working again.
==OpenPGP Keyserver==
* You can now add your own OpenPGP Keyserver:
** Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings} >{menu Privacy & Security} > Under ''''''OpenPGP Keyservers'''''' {menu Add...}. Screenshot:
[[Image:tb146-add-open-pgp-keyserver]]
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 145=
==DNS over HTTPS==
* Thunderbird now supports DNS over HTTPS.
==Account Hub supports manual configuration for EWS, IMAP and POP3 accounts==
* In the ''''''Account Hub'''''', once you enter a valid email address, you can now manually configure your email settings by clicking {menu MANUAL CONFIGURATION}. 
*;[[Image:tb145-account-hub-manual-configuration]]
* ''''''MANUAL CONFIGURATION'''''' in the ''''''Account Hub'''''' supports manual configuration of {menu EWS}, {menu IMAP} and {menu POP3} accounts.
*;[[Image:tb145-ews-imap-pop-account-hub-manual-configuration]]
* Manual configuration of EWS accounts is now supported as per the screenshots in the above two bullet points. For more details, please see the [[Thunderbird and Exchange#w_manual-ews-configuration|Manual EWS configuration section of our Thunderbird and Exchange article]].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 144=
==Exchange enhancements and bug fixes==
* Another bug fix release.
* Various Exchange Support fixes. This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions. We are planning a promotional splash in one of the next few releases. Getting closer!
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 143=
==Exchange Support enhancements and bug fixes==
* Bug fixes.
* Various Exchange Support fixes. This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 142=
==Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues with Hotmail and outlook.com accounts==
If you see: ''''''Exchange auth error'''''' or ''''''Authentication failed. Please check the username and password'''''' when adding a ''''''Hotmail'''''' or ''''''outlook.com'''''' account, here''s how to switch to the old ''''''Account Setup'''''' flow to fix the problem:
* Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings} > {menu General} and untick ''''''Create accounts in the new Account Hub'''''':
*;[[Image:tb142-disable-account-hub|width=350]]
* Please try adding the email account again. If you still have issues, please [https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form file a support request on SUMO].
This will be fixed in a future Thunderbird release.
==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key Control}+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder which will be fixed in a future release. You can follow along in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979880 bug 1979880].
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order|width=350]]
==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]].
==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.
==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}. Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.
==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].
== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=
==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]
==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].
==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub'''''' (not enabled in ESR, we recommend the latest monthly release for the best experience).
==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].
==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
