This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in Thunderbird for Android. For full details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>.
<p></p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-18"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 18</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-17"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 17</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-16"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 16</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-15"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 15</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-14"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 14</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-13"><span class="tocnumber">2.5</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 13</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-12"><span class="tocnumber">2.6</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 12</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-11"><span class="tocnumber">2.7</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 11</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-10"><span class="tocnumber">2.8</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 10</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-9"><span class="tocnumber">2.9</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 9</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-8"><span class="tocnumber">2.10</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 8</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-18">Thunderbird 18</h2>
<ul><li> PNG custom avatars are now supported (as well as JPEGs and stylized letter monograms as per the Thunderbird 17 section).
</li><li> There is a new setting to display times in ISO 8601 format <em>(YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm)</em> in the message list.
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; tap the gear icon:<span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">General settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Display</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Date/Time Format</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">ISO</span>.
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-17" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 17</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><li> Custom avatars for email accounts are now available. JPEGs only for now. PNGs will be supported in a future release. Upload yours as follows: 
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the gear icon:<span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap your email account that you want to customize e.g. <em><a href="mailto:nemo@thunderbird.net">nemo@thunderbird.net</a></em> &gt; tap <span class="menu">General settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Image</span> to upload your custom JPEG. You can also use a stylized letter monogram by tapping <span class="menu">Monogram</span> or pick one of the built-in icons by tapping <span class="menu">Icon</span>.
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-16" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 16</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><li> The SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> have been fixed in <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312">#10312</a>.
</li><li> The following issue was fixed in TB 16.1 which was released one week after Thunderbird 16.0. <del>Known Issue: Deleted/read messages in your unified inbox may not update until you manually refresh. We hope to have a fix soon. you can can follow along on issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10243">#10243</a></del>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-15" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 15</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><li> There are further SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> and the team is testing a fix. You can follow along on issue <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312">#10312</a>. It looks like this will fixed in the next release, TB 16.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-14" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 14</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><li> SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> have been fixed.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-13" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 13</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true"><li> The notification in status bar re-appearing multiple times a day issue (github issue <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/8049">#8049</a>) has been fixed.
</li><li> Special folders (Trash, Sent, Drafts, Archives, etc) not appearing after updating from TB11 to TB12 (github issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9771">#9771</a>) was fixed.
</li><li> The bug with outgoing email not working for certain educational and enterprise accounts is scheduled to be fixed in the next release, Thunderbird 14 for Android (github issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9160">#9160</a>).
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-12" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 12</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true"><li> If you use a password manager, Android will now use it to automatically fill in your password when you add a new account.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-11" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 11</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Mail folders are easier to navigate.
</li><li> Algorithmic darkening makes reading emails easier in dark mode.
</li><li> Thunderbird 11.1&nbsp;: Selected/read/unread message states are now easier to distinguish visually.
</li><li> You can still see font settings if you search for <strong>font</strong> in Settings. This will be removed in a future Thunderbird release. Please use the Android operating system font size settings instead.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-10" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 10</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now empty your Spam folder by tapping <span class="menu">Empty Spam</span> in the Spam folder''s menu <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <strong>kebab</strong> menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab).
</li><li> On Android 10 or older, you now have an option to use the system theme.
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the gear icon:<span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">General settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Display</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">Use system default</span> under <strong>Theme</strong>
</li></ol>
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-9" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 9</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Initial Android 15 support.
</li><li> Thunderbird attempts to use your email provider''s auto configuration database. If it fails it, it uses Mozilla''s database.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-8" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 8</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android-version-8">New in Thunderbird for Android version 8</a> please.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "326867", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 23, 2026, 8:14:20 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-23T20:14:20.335687-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix typos", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 23, 2026, 8:14:31 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-23T20:14:31.183216-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:22:23+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (326868,'en-US','new-thunderbird-android','New in Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android/revision/326868',326867,'2026-04-23T20:18:34.082433-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','add "under Message lists"',1,'2026-04-23T20:19:53.200727-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[T:TBAndroidMore]]
This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in Thunderbird for Android. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__
==Thunderbird 18==
* PNG custom avatars are now supported (as well as JPEGs and stylized letter monograms as per the Thunderbird 17 section).
* There is a new setting to display times in ISO 8601 format ''''(YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm)'''' in the message list.
*# Tap {button ≡} > tap the gear icon:{button [[Image:gear icon]]}.
*# Tap {button General settings} > tap {menu Display} > under ''''''Messsage lists'''''', tap {menu Date/Time Format} > tap {button ISO}.
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 17==
* Custom avatars for email accounts are now available. JPEGs only for now. PNGs will be supported in a future release. Upload yours as follows: 
*# Tap {button ≡} at the top left > tap the gear icon:{button [[Image:gear icon]]} at the bottom left.
*# Tap your email account that you want to customize e.g. ''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''' > tap {menu General settings} > tap {menu Image} to upload your custom JPEG. You can also use a stylized letter monogram by tapping {menu Monogram} or pick one of the built-in icons by tapping {menu Icon}.
==Thunderbird 16==
* The SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com have been fixed in [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312 #10312].
* The following issue was fixed in TB 16.1 which was released one week after Thunderbird 16.0. <del>Known Issue: Deleted/read messages in your unified inbox may not update until you manually refresh. We hope to have a fix soon. you can can follow along on issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10243 #10243]</del>
==Thunderbird 15==
* There are further SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com and the team is testing a fix. You can follow along on issue [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312 #10312]. It looks like this will fixed in the next release, TB 16.
==Thunderbird 14==
* SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com have been fixed.
==Thunderbird 13==
* The notification in status bar re-appearing multiple times a day issue (github issue [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/8049 #8049]) has been fixed.
* Special folders (Trash, Sent, Drafts, Archives, etc) not appearing after updating from TB11 to TB12 (github issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9771 #9771]) was fixed.
* The bug with outgoing email not working for certain educational and enterprise accounts is scheduled to be fixed in the next release, Thunderbird 14 for Android (github issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9160 #9160]).
==Thunderbird 12==
* If you use a password manager, Android will now use it to automatically fill in your password when you add a new account.
==Thunderbird 11==
* Mail folders are easier to navigate.
* Algorithmic darkening makes reading emails easier in dark mode.
* Thunderbird 11.1 : Selected/read/unread message states are now easier to distinguish visually.
* You can still see font settings if you search for ''''''font'''''' in Settings. This will be removed in a future Thunderbird release. Please use the Android operating system font size settings instead.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 10==
* You can now empty your Spam folder by tapping {menu Empty Spam} in the Spam folder''s menu {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''''kebab'''''' menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab).
* On Android 10 or older, you now have an option to use the system theme.
*# Tap {button ≡} at the top left > tap the gear icon:{button [[Image:gear icon]]} at the bottom left.
*# Tap {button General settings} > tap {menu Display} > tap {button Use system default} under ''''''Theme''''''
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 9==
* Initial Android 15 support.
* Thunderbird attempts to use your email provider''s auto configuration database. If it fails it, it uses Mozilla''s database.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 8==
* Refer to [[New in Thunderbird for Android version 8]] please.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird for Android: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird%20android">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird-android/form">Get Support</a></div>
