</li><li> Special folders (Trash, Sent, Drafts, Archives, etc) not appearing after updating from TB11 to TB12 (github issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9771">#9771</a>) was fixed.
</li><li> The bug with outgoing email not working for certain educational and enterprise accounts is scheduled to be fixed in the next release, Thunderbird 14 for Android (github issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9160">#9160</a>).
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-12" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 12</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true"><li> If you use a password manager, Android will now use it to automatically fill in your password when you add a new account.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-11" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 11</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Mail folders are easier to navigate.
</li><li> Algorithmic darkening makes reading emails easier in dark mode.
</li><li> Thunderbird 11.1&nbsp;: Selected/read/unread message states are now easier to distinguish visually.
</li><li> You can still see font settings if you search for <strong>font</strong> in Settings. This will be removed in a future Thunderbird release. Please use the Android operating system font size settings instead.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-10" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 10</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now empty your Spam folder by tapping <span class="menu">Empty Spam</span> in the Spam folder''s menu <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <strong>kebab</strong> menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab).
</li><li> On Android 10 or older, you now have an option to use the system theme.
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the gear icon:<span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">General settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Display</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">Use system default</span> under <strong>Theme</strong>
</li></ol>
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-9" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 9</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Initial Android 15 support.
</li><li> Thunderbird attempts to use your email provider''s auto configuration database. If it fails it, it uses Mozilla''s database.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-8" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 8</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android-version-8">New in Thunderbird for Android version 8</a> please.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "326868", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 23, 2026, 8:18:34 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-23T20:18:34.082433-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add \"under Message lists\"", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 23, 2026, 8:19:53 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-23T20:19:53.200727-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:22:21+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (327347,'en-US','thunderbird-rosetta-macos','Fix Thunderbird not opening on macOS due to Rosetta','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-rosetta-macos','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-rosetta-macos/revision/327347',NULL,'2026-04-30T09:20:41.124961-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','stub only for now, do not translate please. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/186',1,'2026-04-30T09:21:05.799783-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','If Thunderbird won’t open on your Mac and you see a message about ''''''Intel-based apps'''''' or ''''''Rosetta'''''', this article will help you fix the problem.','<p>If Thunderbird won’t open on your Mac and you see a message about <strong>Intel-based apps</strong> or <strong>Rosetta</strong>, this article will help you fix the problem.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327347", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 30, 2026, 9:20:41 AM", "datetime": "2026-04-30T09:20:41.124961-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "stub only for now, do not translate please. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/186", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 30, 2026, 9:21:05 AM", "datetime": "2026-04-30T09:21:05.799783-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:22:18+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (327372,'en-US','thunderbird-rosetta-macos','Fix Thunderbird not opening on macOS due to Rosetta','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-rosetta-macos','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-rosetta-macos/revision/327372',327347,'2026-04-30T09:44:04.212689-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','added some content :-) please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/186',1,'2026-04-30T09:44:48.424369-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','If Thunderbird won’t open on your Mac and you see a message about ''''''Intel-based apps'''''' or ''''''Rosetta'''''', this article will help you fix the problem.

''''''“Support Ending for Intel-based Apps. This version of Thunderbird will not open in a future release of macOS.”''''''

This usually means your version of Thunderbird is outdated or running using Rosetta.

__TOC__

=Why this happens=
Apple is removing support for ''''''Rosetta'''''', a tool that allows apps built for Intel-based Macs to run on Apple silicon devices (such as M1, M2, and newer).
If Thunderbird is using Rosetta or is an older version:
*macOS may show a warning
*Thunderbird may stop opening entirely on newer macOS versions

=Check if Thunderbird is using Rosetta=
If your macOS version still supports Rosetta, you can turn it off:
#Quit Thunderbird.
#Open the {menu Applications} folder.
#Find {menu Thunderbird}.
#Right-click (or Control-click) it and select {button Get Info}.
#Look for {button Open using Rosetta}.
#If checked, uncheck it.
#Close the window and open Thunderbird again.
If Thunderbird opens normally, the issue is fixed.

=Update Thunderbird to the latest version=
If you don’t see the Rosetta option, or Thunderbird still doesn’t open, update to the latest version.
#Visit the [https://gethunderbird.com/ Thunderbird download page]. 
#Download the latest version of Thunderbird.
#Open the downloaded file.
#Drag Thunderbird into the {menu Applications} folder.
#Replace the existing version if prompted.
#Open Thunderbird.
{note}''''''Note:'''''' New versions of Thunderbird run natively on Apple silicon and do not require Rosetta.{/note}

=If you still see the message=
*Make sure you are using the latest version of Thunderbird
*Restart your Mac after installing updates
*Check for macOS updates
If the problem continues, you can get help from [https://support.mozilla.org/ Mozilla Support].

=Frequently asked questions=
==What is Rosetta?==
Rosetta is a compatibility feature from Apple that allows apps built for Intel-based Macs to run on newer Apple silicon devices (such as M1 and M2). To learn more, see [https://support.apple.com/102527 this Apple support article].

==Why is Rosetta being removed?==
Apple is transitioning fully to Apple Silicon. Newer versions of macOS no longer support Rosetta, so apps must run natively.

==Do I need Rosetta to use Thunderbird?==
No. Current versions of Thunderbird are built to run natively on Apple silicon and do not require Rosetta.

==What happens if I keep using an old version of Thunderbird?==
Older versions that rely on Rosetta may stop working on newer versions of macOS. Updating Thunderbird ensures it continues to work properly.

==Will updating Thunderbird affect my data?==
No. Updating Thunderbird does not remove your bookmarks, history, or saved data.

=Related articles=
*[[Install Thunderbird on Mac]]
*[[Update Thunderbird to the latest version]]','<p>If Thunderbird won’t open on your Mac and you see a message about <strong>Intel-based apps</strong> or <strong>Rosetta</strong>, this article will help you fix the problem.
</p><p><strong>“Support Ending for Intel-based Apps. This version of Thunderbird will not open in a future release of macOS.”</strong>
</p><p>This usually means your version of Thunderbird is outdated or running using Rosetta.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_why-this-happens"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Why this happens</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_check-if-thunderbird-is-using-rosetta"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Check if Thunderbird is using Rosetta</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_update-thunderbird-to-the-latest-version"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Update Thunderbird to the latest version</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_if-you-still-see-the-message"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">If you still see the message</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_frequently-asked-questions"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Frequently asked questions</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_what-is-rosetta"><span class="tocnumber">5.1</span> <span class="toctext">What is Rosetta?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_why-is-rosetta-being-removed"><span class="tocnumber">5.2</span> <span class="toctext">Why is Rosetta being removed?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_do-i-need-rosetta-to-use-thunderbird"><span class="tocnumber">5.3</span> <span class="toctext">Do I need Rosetta to use Thunderbird?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_what-happens-if-i-keep-using-an-old-version-of-thunderbird"><span class="tocnumber">5.4</span> <span class="toctext">What happens if I keep using an old version of Thunderbird?</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_will-updating-thunderbird-affect-my-data"><span class="tocnumber">5.5</span> <span class="toctext">Will updating Thunderbird affect my data?</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_related-articles"><span class="tocnumber">6</span> <span class="toctext">Related articles</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_why-this-happens">Why this happens</h1>
<p>Apple is removing support for <strong>Rosetta</strong>, a tool that allows apps built for Intel-based Macs to run on Apple silicon devices (such as M1, M2, and newer).
If Thunderbird is using Rosetta or is an older version:
</p>
<ul><li>macOS may show a warning
</li><li>Thunderbird may stop opening entirely on newer macOS versions
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_check-if-thunderbird-is-using-rosetta">Check if Thunderbird is using Rosetta</h1>
<p>If your macOS version still supports Rosetta, you can turn it off:
</p>
<ol><li>Quit Thunderbird.
</li><li>Open the <span class="menu">Applications</span> folder.
</li><li>Find <span class="menu">Thunderbird</span>.
</li><li>Right-click (or Control-click) it and select <span class="button">Get Info</span>.
</li><li>Look for <span class="button">Open using Rosetta</span>.
</li><li>If checked, uncheck it.
</li><li>Close the window and open Thunderbird again.
</li></ol>
<p>If Thunderbird opens normally, the issue is fixed.
</p>
<h1 id="w_update-thunderbird-to-the-latest-version">Update Thunderbird to the latest version</h1>
<p>If you don’t see the Rosetta option, or Thunderbird still doesn’t open, update to the latest version.
</p>
<ol><li>Visit the <a href="https://gethunderbird.com/">Thunderbird download page</a>. 
</li><li>Download the latest version of Thunderbird.
</li><li>Open the downloaded file.
</li><li>Drag Thunderbird into the <span class="menu">Applications</span> folder.
</li><li>Replace the existing version if prompted.
</li><li>Open Thunderbird.
</li></ol>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> New versions of Thunderbird run natively on Apple silicon and do not require Rosetta.</div>
<h1 id="w_if-you-still-see-the-message">If you still see the message</h1>
<ul><li>Make sure you are using the latest version of Thunderbird
</li><li>Restart your Mac after installing updates
</li><li>Check for macOS updates
</li></ul>
<p>If the problem continues, you can get help from <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/">Mozilla Support</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</h1>
<h2 id="w_what-is-rosetta">What is Rosetta?</h2>
<p>Rosetta is a compatibility feature from Apple that allows apps built for Intel-based Macs to run on newer Apple silicon devices (such as M1 and M2). To learn more, see <a href="https://support.apple.com/102527">this Apple support article</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_why-is-rosetta-being-removed">Why is Rosetta being removed?</h2>
<p>Apple is transitioning fully to Apple Silicon. Newer versions of macOS no longer support Rosetta, so apps must run natively.
</p>
<h2 id="w_do-i-need-rosetta-to-use-thunderbird">Do I need Rosetta to use Thunderbird?</h2>
<p>No. Current versions of Thunderbird are built to run natively on Apple silicon and do not require Rosetta.
</p>
<h2 id="w_what-happens-if-i-keep-using-an-old-version-of-thunderbird">What happens if I keep using an old version of Thunderbird?</h2>
<p>Older versions that rely on Rosetta may stop working on newer versions of macOS. Updating Thunderbird ensures it continues to work properly.
</p>
<h2 id="w_will-updating-thunderbird-affect-my-data">Will updating Thunderbird affect my data?</h2>
<p>No. Updating Thunderbird does not remove your bookmarks, history, or saved data.
</p>
<h1 id="w_related-articles">Related articles</h1>
<ul><li><a href="/en-US/kb/installing-thunderbird-on-mac">Install Thunderbird on Mac</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/updating-thunderbird">Update Thunderbird to the latest version</a>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327372", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 30, 2026, 9:44:04 AM", "datetime": "2026-04-30T09:44:04.212689-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "added some content :-) please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/186", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 30, 2026, 9:44:48 AM", "datetime": "2026-04-30T09:44:48.424369-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:22:16+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (327402,'en-US','getting-started-thunderbird-pro','Getting Started with Thunderbird Pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro/revision/327402',327306,'2026-04-30T12:09:37.179348-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','mobie is only optimized for Thundermail. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/191',1,'2026-04-30T12:09:57.618979-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','For the possible best experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.

Prepare for Thunderbird Pro:
* If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
* If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, then install the Thunderbird Pro add-on according to [[Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop]]. 
* Set up your Thunderbird Pro account. You must enter a payment choice, for example a credit card number.  If you have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code, you must still add a payment option. If you have a problem with the code that you received, please [https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new ask for support]. Currently, only credit cards are accepted. Apple Pay, Paypal and other 3rd party services are not yet supported. 

Set up your application:
* For Thundermail on desktop - Configure Thunderbird for Desktop for Thundermail according to the article [[Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail]].
* For Thundermail on on mobile - Configure Thunderbird for Android for Thundermail according to the article: [[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android]].
* For Appointment - Configure according to [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907 our Appointment articles].
* Configure Send as per [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 our Send articles].

Go forth! Set up some office hours with Appointment. Send some files with Send. Send and receive email with Thundermail!','<p>For the possible best experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.
</p><p>Prepare for Thunderbird Pro:
</p>
<ul><li> If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
</li><li> If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, then install the Thunderbird Pro add-on according to <a href="/en-US/kb/install-thunderbird-pro-add-thunderbird-desktop">Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop</a>. 
</li><li> Set up your Thunderbird Pro account. You must enter a payment choice, for example a credit card number.  If you have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code, you must still add a payment option. If you have a problem with the code that you received, please <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">ask for support</a>. Currently, only credit cards are accepted. Apple Pay, Paypal and other 3rd party services are not yet supported. 
</li></ul>
<p>Set up your application:
</p>
<ul><li> For Thundermail on desktop - Configure Thunderbird for Desktop for Thundermail according to the article <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail">Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail</a>.
</li><li> For Thundermail on on mobile - Configure Thunderbird for Android for Thundermail according to the article: <a href="/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android">Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li><li> For Appointment - Configure according to <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907">our Appointment articles</a>.
</li><li> Configure Send as per <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235">our Send articles</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>Go forth! Set up some office hours with Appointment. Send some files with Send. Send and receive email with Thundermail!
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327402", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 30, 2026, 12:09:37 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-30T12:09:37.179348-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "mobie is only optimized for Thundermail. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/191", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 30, 2026, 12:09:57 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-30T12:09:57.618979-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:22:13+00:00');
