</li><li> <strong>Authentication method:</strong> OAuth2
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>.
</li><li> In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>. Click on <span class="button">Edit outgoing server…</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a>
</li><li> <strong>Server Port:</strong> 465 <strong>Connection</strong> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS
</li><li> <strong>Username:''<em> your full Thundermail email address For example: </em></strong><em>nemo@thundermail.com</em>
</li><li> <strong>Authentication method:</strong> OAuth2
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_thundermail-calendar" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Calendar</button></h2>
<ol class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="menu">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Calendar</span> &gt; <span class="button">On the Network</span>.
</li><li> For <strong>Username:</strong>, enter your Thundermail email address. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>.
</li><li> For <strong>Location</strong>, enter <strong><a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a></strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Find Calendars</span>.
</li><li> In the <strong>Create New Calendar</strong> dialog, select your Thundermail calendar and click <span class="button">Subscribe</span>.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_thundermail-address-book" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Address Book</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="menu">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">New Address Book</span> &gt; <span class="button">New remote Address Book</span>.
</li><li>  For <strong>Username:</strong>, enter your Thundermail email address. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>.
</li><li> For <strong>URL/Hostname</strong>, enter <strong><a href="https://mail.thundermail.com">https://mail.thundermail.com</a></strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li><li> Select your Thundermail Address Book and click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li></ol><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_send-thundermail-use-your-thundermail-calendar-and-thundermail-address-book-and-have-some-fun">Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">Send and receive email</a> with Thundermail. If you have large files, you can also use <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235"><strong>Thunderbird Send</strong></a>. which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
</li><li> If you have a <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail</a>, here''s now to use it:
<ol><li> When composing an email, click on the email address next to <strong>From</strong>.
</li><li> Click on <span class="button">Customize From Address…</span>. 
</li><li> Finally, type in an email address for the custom domain you created the Catch-All in.
</li></ol>
</li><li> Enjoy your Thundermail Calendar: <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/products/thunderbird/email-and-messaging/calendar">Create some events, invite people to invites, etc</a>.
</li><li> Use your Thundermail Address Book for <a href="/en-US/kb/addressing-email">composing email</a>, managing your contacts, etc.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird">Get started with Thunderbird</a>.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327485", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 1, 2026, 11:58:42 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-01T23:58:42.036445-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/193", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 2, 2026, 12:00:06 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-02T00:00:06.907164-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:21:48+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (327486,'en-US','getting-started-thunderbird-pro','Getting Started with Thunderbird Pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro/revision/327486',327402,'2026-05-02T00:30:33.739729-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP please do not translate. Discussion please at: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/191',1,'2026-05-02T00:32:13.624454-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','For the possible best experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.

Prepare for Thunderbird Pro:
* If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
* If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, then install the Thunderbird Pro add-on according to [[Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop]]. 
* Set up your Thunderbird Pro account. You must enter a payment choice, for example a credit card number.  If you have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code, you must still add a payment option. If you have a problem with the code that you received, please [https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new ask for support]. Currently, only credit cards are accepted. Apple Pay, Paypal and other 3rd party services are not yet supported. 

Set up your application:
* For Thundermail on desktop - Configure Thunderbird for Desktop for Thundermail according to the article [[Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail]].
* For Thundermail on on mobile - Configure Thunderbird for Android for Thundermail according to the article: [[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android]].
* For Appointment - Configure according to [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907 our Appointment articles].
* Configure Send as per [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 our Send articles].

Go forth! Set up some office hours with Appointment. Send some files with Send. Send and receive email with Thundermail using your Thundermail Address Book, Thundermail aliases and Thundermail Catch-All addresses. Use your Thundermail Calendar to setup events.','<p>For the possible best experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.
</p><p>Prepare for Thunderbird Pro:
