__TOC__

=Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop=
{note}''''''NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires the latest ESR or the latest monthly release. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird which is documented in: [[New in Thunderbird Desktop]].{/note}
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} >  {menu New Account} > {menu Email}.
# Enter your Thundermail email address and follow the prompts to set up your Thundermail email account.

Thunderbird should have automatically added your Thundermail email in [[Configuration Options for Accounts|account settings]], a CalDAV calendar called ''''''Thundermail Calendar'''''' in your Thunderbird calendar [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]] (press {for not mac}{key Alt+3}{/for}{for mac}{key Ctrl+3}{/for}), and a CardDAV address book called ''''''Thundermail Address Book'''''' in your address book [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]] (press {for not mac}{key Alt+2}{/for}{for mac}{key Ctrl+2}{/for}) to check). If any of those are missing, please try manually changing the settings manual settings sections below, and please  report the failure using [https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/ our contact form].

=Manual settings=
<!--If Thunderbird failed to automatically add your Thundermail email, calendar or address book, please check the following
* configure your Thundermail email settings to match your [https://accounts.tb.pro/mail TB Pro Thundermail page].
* add a CalDAV calendar called ''''''Thundermail Calendar'''''' in your Thunderbird calendar [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]]. Press {key Alt+3} ({key Ctrl+3} on macOS) to check.
* add a CardDAV address book called ''''''Thundermail Address Book'''''' in your address book [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]]. Press {key Alt+2} ({key Ctrl+2} on macOS) to check. -->

If Thunderbird failed to add the expected items or you need to adjust them, please try manually changing the settings the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a Thunderbird Pro Support Ticket at: [https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/ our contact form].

[[UI:details_start]]
==Receiving Email==
# Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {menu Account Settings}.
# In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example: ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''. Then, click on the chevron “&gt;” to expand the drop down menu. Finally, click on {menu Server Settings} and set the following values:

* ''''''Server Name:'''''' [http://mail.thundermail.com mail.thundermail.com] ''''''Server Port:'''''' 993
* ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address e.g. ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''
* ''''''Authentication method:'''''' OAuth2

==Sending Email==
# Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Account Settings}.
# In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''. Click on {button Edit outgoing server…} and set the following values:
 
* ''''''Server Name:'''''' mail.thundermail.com
* ''''''Server Port:'''''' 465 ''''''Connection'''''' ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address For example: ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''
* ''''''Authentication method:'''''' OAuth2
==Thundermail Calendar==
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {menu New Account} > {menu Calendar} > {button On the Network}.
# For ''''''Username:'''''', enter your Thundermail email address. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''.
# For ''''''Location'''''', enter ''''''mail.thundermail.com''''''.
# Click {button Find Calendars}.
# In the ''''''Create New Calendar'''''' dialog, select your Thundermail calendar and click {button Subscribe}.
==Thundermail Address Book==
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {menu New Account} > {menu New Address Book} > {button New remote Address Book}.
#  For ''''''Username:'''''', enter your Thundermail email address. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''.
# For ''''''URL/Hostname'''''', enter ''''''https://mail.thundermail.com''''''.
# Click {button Continue}.
# Select your Thundermail Address Book and click {button Continue}.

[[UI:details_end]]

=Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!=
* [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|Send and receive email]] with Thundermail. If you have large files, you can also use [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 ''''''Thunderbird Send'''''']. which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
* If you have a [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail], here''s now to use it:
*# When composing an email, click on the email address next to ''''''From''''''.
*# Click on {button Customize From Address…}. 
*# Finally, type in an email address for the custom domain you created the Catch-All in.
* Enjoy your Thundermail Calendar: [https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/products/thunderbird/email-and-messaging/calendar Create some events, invite people to invites, etc].
* Use your Thundermail Address Book for [[Addressing an Email|composing email]], managing your contacts, etc.
* New to Thunderbird? Then check out [[Get started with Thunderbird]].','<p></p><div class="warning">NOTE: Thundermail (formerly known as Thunderbird Pro) is currently in its Early Bird release and available  by invitation only. To learn more and join the waitlist, visit <a href="https://tb.pro/">our website</a>. We’ll be opening Thundermail to the public once the Early Bird release concludes.</div>
<p></p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-desktop"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_manual-settings"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Manual settings</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_receiving-email"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Receiving Email</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_sending-email"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Sending Email</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thundermail-calendar"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thundermail Calendar</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thundermail-address-book"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thundermail Address Book</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_send-thundermail-use-your-thundermail-calendar-and-thundermail-address-book-and-have-some-fun"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-desktop">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop</h1>
<div class="note"><strong>NOTE</strong>: Thunderbird Pro requires the latest ESR or the latest monthly release. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird which is documented in: <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop">New in Thunderbird Desktop</a>.</div>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt;  <span class="menu">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>.
</li><li> Enter your Thundermail email address and follow the prompts to set up your Thundermail email account.
</li></ol>
<p>Thunderbird should have automatically added your Thundermail email in <a href="/en-US/kb/configuration-options-accounts">account settings</a>, a CalDAV calendar called <strong>Thundermail Calendar</strong> in your Thunderbird calendar <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar">space</a> (press <span class="for" data-for="not mac" style="display: none;"><span class="key">Alt</span> + <span class="key">3</span></span><span class="for" data-for="mac"><span class="key">Ctrl</span> + <span class="key">3</span></span>), and a CardDAV address book called <strong>Thundermail Address Book</strong> in your address book <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar">space</a> (press <span class="for" data-for="not mac" style="display: none;"><span class="key">Alt</span> + <span class="key">2</span></span><span class="for" data-for="mac"><span class="key">Ctrl</span> + <span class="key">2</span></span>) to check). If any of those are missing, please try manually changing the settings manual settings sections below, and please  report the failure using <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/">our contact form</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_manual-settings">Manual settings</h1>
<p>

</p><p>If Thunderbird failed to add the expected items or you need to adjust them, please try manually changing the settings the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a Thunderbird Pro Support Ticket at: <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/">our contact form</a>.
</p><p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_receiving-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Receiving Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>.
</li><li> In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example: <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>. Then, click on the chevron “&gt;” to expand the drop down menu. Finally, click on <span class="menu">Server Settings</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a> <strong>Server Port:</strong> 993
</li><li> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address e.g. <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>
</li><li> <strong>Authentication method:</strong> OAuth2
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>.
</li><li> In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>. Click on <span class="button">Edit outgoing server…</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a>
</li><li> <strong>Server Port:</strong> 465 <strong>Connection</strong> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS
</li><li> <strong>Username:''<em> your full Thundermail email address For example: </em></strong><em>nemo@thundermail.com</em>
</li><li> <strong>Authentication method:</strong> OAuth2
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_thundermail-calendar" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Calendar</button></h2>
<ol class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="menu">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Calendar</span> &gt; <span class="button">On the Network</span>.
</li><li> For <strong>Username:</strong>, enter your Thundermail email address. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>.
</li><li> For <strong>Location</strong>, enter <strong><a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a></strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Find Calendars</span>.
</li><li> In the <strong>Create New Calendar</strong> dialog, select your Thundermail calendar and click <span class="button">Subscribe</span>.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_thundermail-address-book" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Address Book</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="menu">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">New Address Book</span> &gt; <span class="button">New remote Address Book</span>.
</li><li>  For <strong>Username:</strong>, enter your Thundermail email address. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>.
</li><li> For <strong>URL/Hostname</strong>, enter <strong><a href="https://mail.thundermail.com">https://mail.thundermail.com</a></strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li><li> Select your Thundermail Address Book and click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li></ol><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_send-thundermail-use-your-thundermail-calendar-and-thundermail-address-book-and-have-some-fun">Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">Send and receive email</a> with Thundermail. If you have large files, you can also use <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235"><strong>Thunderbird Send</strong></a>. which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
</li><li> If you have a <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail</a>, here''s now to use it:
<ol><li> When composing an email, click on the email address next to <strong>From</strong>.
</li><li> Click on <span class="button">Customize From Address…</span>. 
</li><li> Finally, type in an email address for the custom domain you created the Catch-All in.
</li></ol>
</li><li> Enjoy your Thundermail Calendar: <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/products/thunderbird/email-and-messaging/calendar">Create some events, invite people to invites, etc</a>.
</li><li> Use your Thundermail Address Book for <a href="/en-US/kb/addressing-email">composing email</a>, managing your contacts, etc.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird">Get started with Thunderbird</a>.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327514", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 2, 2026, 9:05:38 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-02T09:05:38.408657-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/193", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:21:41+00:00');
