</li><li> In the <strong>Create New Calendar</strong> dialog, select your Thundermail calendar and click <span class="button">Subscribe</span>.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_thundermail-address-book" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Address Book</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="for" data-for="not tb152" style="display: none;"><span class="menu">New Account</span></span><span class="for" data-for="tb152"><span class="menu">Add Account</span></span> &gt; <span class="for" data-for="not tb152" style="display: none;"><span class="menu">New Address Book</span></span><span class="for" data-for="tb152"><span class="menu">Address Book</span></span> &gt; <span class="for" data-for="not tb152" style="display: none;"><span class="button">New remote Address Book</span></span><span class="for" data-for="tb152"><span class="menu">Add remote Address Book</span></span>.
</li><li>  For <strong>Username:</strong>, enter your Thundermail email address. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>.
</li><li> For <strong>URL/Hostname</strong>, enter <strong><a href="https://mail.thundermail.com">https://mail.thundermail.com</a></strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li><li> Select your Thundermail Address Book and click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li></ol><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_send-thundermail-use-your-thundermail-calendar-and-thundermail-address-book-and-have-some-fun">Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">Send and receive email</a> with Thundermail. If you have large files, you can also use <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235"><strong>Thunderbird Send</strong></a>. which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
</li><li> If you have a <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail</a>, here''s now to use it:
<ol><li> When composing or replying to an email, click on the email address next to <strong>From</strong>.
</li><li> Click on <span class="button">Customize From Address…</span>. 
</li><li> Finally, type in an email address for the custom domain you created the Catch-All in.
</li></ol>
</li><li> Enjoy your Thundermail Calendar: <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/products/thunderbird/email-and-messaging/calendar">Create some events, invite people to invites, etc</a>.
</li><li> Use your Thundermail Address Book for <a href="/en-US/kb/addressing-email">composing email</a>, managing your contacts, etc.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird">Get started with Thunderbird</a>.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327570", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 3, 2026, 10:29:56 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T22:29:56.241441-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/193", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 3, 2026, 10:32:35 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T22:32:35.882510-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:21:31+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (327572,'en-US','thundermail-and-thunderbird-android','Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android/revision/327572',327305,'2026-05-03T23:22:00.216899-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/192',1,'2026-05-03T23:24:17.683798-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[Template:TBproEarlyBirdInviteOnly]]
Here’s how to get started with Mozilla’s Thundermail service. 

=Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird for Android=
{note} ''''''NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires Thunderbird for Android version 18 or newer (also K-9). We recommend using the latest monthly release version documented in [[New in Thunderbird for Android]].{/note}
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > {menu Add account}.
# Enter your Thundermail email address. For example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
# Click {button Next}.
# The next screen will prompt you to ''''''Please specify the special folders for your account'''''', and offer some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click {button Next}. 
# On the next screen, configure your user name under ''''''Your name'''''' and optionally your signature and {button Next}.
# The next screen has sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click {button Next} .

=Manual settings=
Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your [https://accounts.tb.pro/self-serve/connection-info TB Pro accounts page]. If it doesn’t, please  manually change the receiving email and sending email settings according to the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new.
[[UI:details_start]]

==Receiving Email==
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}
# Under ''''''Accounts'''''', tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
# Tap {menu Fetching mail} > {menu Incoming Server} and set the following values:
*''''''Server:'''''' <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS ''''''Port:'''''' 993
*''''''Authentication:'''''' OAuth 2.0
*''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.

==Sending Email==
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}
# Under ''''''Accounts'''''', tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
# Tap {menu Sending mail} > {menu Outgoing server} and set the following values:
* ''''''Server Name:'''''' <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> ''''''Connection'''''' ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS ''''''Port:'''''' 465
* ''''''Authentication:'''''' OAuth 2.0
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.

[[UI:details_end]]

=Configure Catch-All aliases for use with Thunderbird=
==Setup a Thunderbird identity for each each alias you want to reply from==
If you have a [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail], you will have to setup an ''''''identity'''''' in Thunderbird for every alias in that domain that you need to reply from. 

For example, if your Catch-All is for <code>glamroc.com</code> and you would like to reply as  <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code> in addition to the default alias for <code>glamroc.com</code>, you will have to setup identities for both <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code>. 

Here''s how:
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}.
# Tap on your account, e.g. <code>roc@glamcroc.com</code> > {menu Sending mail}.
# Tap {menu Manage identities} > {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''kebab'''' menu because the three vertical dots evoke a kebab > {menu New identity}.
# Enter the desired alias in the ''''''Email address'''''' field e.g. <code>alice@glamroc.com</code>. All other fields are optional, but we recommend you enter a memorable shorter name in the ''''''Your name'''''' field.
# Save the identity by tapping {button SAVE}. When replying, you can now change the ''''''From'''''' field to this identity by tapping on it.
==Send email with the identities for your Catch-All alias==
# When composing or replying an email, tap on the email address in the  ''''''From'''''' field.
# Tap on the relevant identity.
# Write and send the email as usual.
=Send and receive email and have some fun!=
* Send and receive email with Thundermail.
* New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out [[Getting started with Thunderbird for Android]].
<!--
* If you have large files, you can send them with FIXME because Send on Mobile needs some polish: add link to Thunderbird Send which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
-->','<p></p><div class="warning">NOTE: Thundermail (formerly known as Thunderbird Pro) is currently in its Early Bird release and available  by invitation only. To learn more and join the waitlist, visit <a href="https://tb.pro/">our website</a>. We’ll be opening Thundermail to the public once the Early Bird release concludes.</div>
Here’s how to get started with Mozilla’s Thundermail service. 
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-for-android">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird for Android</h1>
<div class="note"> <strong>NOTE</strong>: Thunderbird Pro requires Thunderbird for Android version 18 or newer (also K-9). We recommend using the latest monthly release version documented in <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android">New in Thunderbird for Android</a>.</div>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add account</span>.
</li><li> Enter your Thundermail email address. For example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen will prompt you to <strong>Please specify the special folders for your account</strong>, and offer some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span>. 
</li><li> On the next screen, configure your user name under <strong>Your name</strong> and optionally your signature and <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen has sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span> .
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_manual-settings">Manual settings</h1>
<p>Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/self-serve/connection-info">TB Pro accounts page</a>. If it doesn’t, please  manually change the receiving email and sending email settings according to the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new</a>.
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_receiving-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Receiving Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Incoming Server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li><strong>Server:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 993
</li><li><strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li><strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Sending mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Outgoing server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Connection</strong> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 465
</li><li> <strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_configure-catch-all-aliases-for-use-with-thunderbird">Configure Catch-All aliases for use with Thunderbird</h1>
<h2 id="w_setup-a-thunderbird-identity-for-each-each-alias-you-want-to-reply-from">Setup a Thunderbird identity for each each alias you want to reply from</h2>
<p>If you have a <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail</a>, you will have to setup an <strong>identity</strong> in Thunderbird for every alias in that domain that you need to reply from. 
</p><p>For example, if your Catch-All is for <code>glamroc.com</code> and you would like to reply as  <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code> in addition to the default alias for <code>glamroc.com</code>, you will have to setup identities for both <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code>. 
</p><p>Here''s how:
</p>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>.
</li><li> Tap on your account, e.g. <code>roc@glamcroc.com</code> &gt; <span class="menu">Sending mail</span>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Manage identities</span> &gt; <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <em>kebab</em> menu because the three vertical dots evoke a kebab &gt; <span class="menu">New identity</span>.
</li><li> Enter the desired alias in the <strong>Email address</strong> field e.g. <code>alice@glamroc.com</code>. All other fields are optional, but we recommend you enter a memorable shorter name in the <strong>Your name</strong> field.
</li><li> Save the identity by tapping <span class="button">SAVE</span>. When replying, you can now change the <strong>From</strong> field to this identity by tapping on it.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_send-email-with-the-identities-for-your-catch-all-alias">Send email with the identities for your Catch-All alias</h2>
<ol><li> When composing or replying an email, tap on the email address in the  <strong>From</strong> field.
</li><li> Tap on the relevant identity.
</li><li> Write and send the email as usual.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_send-and-receive-email-and-have-some-fun">Send and receive email and have some fun!</h1>
<ul><li> Send and receive email with Thundermail.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-android">Getting started with Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327572", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 3, 2026, 11:22:00 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T23:22:00.216899-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/192", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 3, 2026, 11:24:17 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T23:24:17.683798-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:21:28+00:00');
