</li><li> Enter your Thundermail email address. For example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen will prompt you to <strong>Please specify the special folders for your account</strong>, and offer some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span>. 
</li><li> On the next screen, configure your user name under <strong>Your name</strong> and optionally your signature and <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen has sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span> .
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_manual-settings">Manual settings</h1>
<p>Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/self-serve/connection-info">TB Pro accounts page</a>. If it doesn’t, please  manually change the receiving email and sending email settings according to the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new</a>.
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_receiving-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Receiving Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Incoming Server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li><strong>Server:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 993
</li><li><strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li><strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Sending mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Outgoing server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Connection</strong> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 465
</li><li> <strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_configure-catch-all-aliases-for-use-with-thunderbird">Configure Catch-All aliases for use with Thunderbird</h1>
<h2 id="w_setup-a-thunderbird-identity-for-each-each-alias-you-want-to-reply-from">Setup a Thunderbird identity for each each alias you want to reply from</h2>
<p>If you have a <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail</a>, you will have to setup an <strong>identity</strong> in Thunderbird for every alias in that domain that you need to reply from. 
</p><p>For example, if your Catch-All is for <code>glamroc.com</code> and you would like to reply as  <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code> in addition to the default alias for <code>glamroc.com</code>, you will have to setup identities for both <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code>. 
</p><p>Here''s how:
</p>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>.
</li><li> Tap on your account, e.g. <code>roc@glamcroc.com</code> &gt; <span class="menu">Sending mail</span>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Manage identities</span> &gt; <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <em>kebab</em> menu because the three vertical dots evoke a kebab &gt; <span class="menu">New identity</span>.
</li><li> Enter the desired alias in the <strong>Email address</strong> field e.g. <code>alice@glamroc.com</code>. All other fields are optional, but we recommend you enter a memorable shorter name in the <strong>Your name</strong> field.
</li><li> Save the identity by tapping <span class="button">SAVE</span>. When replying, you can now change the <strong>From</strong> field to this identity by tapping on it.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_send-email-with-the-identities-for-your-catch-all-alias">Send email with the identities for your Catch-All alias</h2>
<ol><li> When composing or replying an email, tap on the email address in the  <strong>From</strong> field.
</li><li> Tap on the relevant identity.
</li><li> Write and send the email as usual.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_have-some-fun-now-that-email-setup-is-done">Have some fun now that email setup is done!</h1>
<p>Congratulations, you have done successfully setup Thundermail with Thunderbird for Android! Next:
</p>
<ul><li> Send and receive email with Thundermail.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-android">Getting started with Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327573", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 3, 2026, 11:33:22 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T23:33:22.023457-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/192", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 3, 2026, 11:34:48 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T23:34:48.935997-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:21:26+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (327574,'en-US','getting-started-thunderbird-pro','Getting Started with Thunderbird Pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro/revision/327574',327487,'2026-05-03T23:50:56.452706-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/191',1,'2026-05-03T23:51:32.701007-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','=Thunderbird Pro brief introduction=
Thunderbird is a subscription based bundle of services that consists of:
* Thundermail: an email service.
* Appintment: a collaborative scheduling service.
* Send: a secure way to send large files.

Check out our website: [https://tb.pro/tb.pro] for all the details.
{note}Please note: For the possible best experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.{/note}
=Prepare for Thunderbird Pro=
* If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
* If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, then install the Thunderbird Pro add-on according to [[Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop]]. 
* Set up your Thunderbird Pro account. You must enter a payment choice, for example a credit card number.  If you have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code, you must still add a payment option. If you have a problem with the code that you received, please [https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new ask for support]. Currently, only credit cards are accepted. Apple Pay, Paypal and other 3rd party services are not yet supported. 
=Set up your Thunderbird Pro apps: Thundermail, Send and Appointment=
* For Thundermail on desktop - Configure Thunderbird for Desktop for Thundermail according to the article [[Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail]].
* For Thundermail on on mobile - Configure Thunderbird for Android for Thundermail according to the article: [[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android]].
* For Appointment - Configure according to [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907 our Appointment articles].
* Configure Send as per [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 our Send articles].
=Let''s go!=
Go forth! Set up some office hours with Appointment. Send some files with Send. Send and receive email with Thundermail using your Thundermail Address Book, [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/46804820453907-Setting-Up-Email-Aliases Thundermail aliases] and [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias Thundermail Catch-All addresses]. Use your Thundermail Calendar to setup events.','<h1 id="w_thunderbird-pro-brief-introduction">Thunderbird Pro brief introduction</h1>
<p>Thunderbird is a subscription based bundle of services that consists of:
</p>
<ul><li> Thundermail: an email service.
</li><li> Appintment: a collaborative scheduling service.
</li><li> Send: a secure way to send large files.
</li></ul>
<p>Check out our website: <a href="https://tb.pro/tb.pro">https://tb.pro/tb.pro</a> for all the details.
</p>
<div class="note">Please note: For the possible best experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a Desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.</div>
<h1 id="w_prepare-for-thunderbird-pro">Prepare for Thunderbird Pro</h1>
<ul><li> If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
</li><li> If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, then install the Thunderbird Pro add-on according to <a href="/en-US/kb/install-thunderbird-pro-add-thunderbird-desktop">Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop</a>. 
</li><li> Set up your Thunderbird Pro account. You must enter a payment choice, for example a credit card number.  If you have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code, you must still add a payment option. If you have a problem with the code that you received, please <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">ask for support</a>. Currently, only credit cards are accepted. Apple Pay, Paypal and other 3rd party services are not yet supported. 
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_set-up-your-thunderbird-pro-apps-thundermail-send-and-appointment">Set up your Thunderbird Pro apps: Thundermail, Send and Appointment</h1>
<ul><li> For Thundermail on desktop - Configure Thunderbird for Desktop for Thundermail according to the article <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail">Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail</a>.
</li><li> For Thundermail on on mobile - Configure Thunderbird for Android for Thundermail according to the article: <a href="/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android">Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li><li> For Appointment - Configure according to <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907">our Appointment articles</a>.
</li><li> Configure Send as per <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235">our Send articles</a>.
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_lets-go">Let''s go!</h1>
<p>Go forth! Set up some office hours with Appointment. Send some files with Send. Send and receive email with Thundermail using your Thundermail Address Book, <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/46804820453907-Setting-Up-Email-Aliases">Thundermail aliases</a> and <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Thundermail Catch-All addresses</a>. Use your Thundermail Calendar to setup events.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327574", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 3, 2026, 11:50:56 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T23:50:56.452706-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/191", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 3, 2026, 11:51:32 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T23:51:32.701007-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:21:24+00:00');
