</li><li> In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>. Click on <span class="button">Edit outgoing server…</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a>
</li><li> <strong>Server Port:</strong> 465 <strong>Connection Security:</strong> SSL/TLS
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address For example: <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>
</li><li> <strong>Authentication method:</strong> OAuth2
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_thundermail-calendar" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Calendar</button></h2>
<ol class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="for" data-for="not tb152" style="display: none;"><span class="menu">New Account</span></span><span class="for" data-for="tb152"><span class="menu">Add Account</span></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Calendar</span> &gt; <span class="button">On the Network</span>.
