Here’s how to get started with Mozilla’s Thundermail service. 
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-for-android">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird for Android</h1>
<div class="note"> <strong>NOTE</strong>: Thunderbird Pro requires Thunderbird for Android version 18 or newer (also K-9). We recommend using the latest monthly release version documented in <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android">New in Thunderbird for Android</a>.</div>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add account</span>.
</li><li> Enter your Thundermail email address. For example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen will prompt you to <strong>Please specify the special folders for your account</strong>, and offer some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span>. 
</li><li> On the next screen, configure your user name under <strong>Your name</strong> and optionally your signature and click <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen has sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span> .
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_manual-settings">Manual settings</h1>
<p>Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/mail">TB Pro accounts page</a>. If it doesn’t, please  manually change the receiving email and sending email settings according to the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new</a>.
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_receiving-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Receiving Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Incoming Server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li><strong>Server:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 993
</li><li><strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li><strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Sending mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Outgoing server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Connection</strong> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 465
</li><li> <strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_configure-catch-all-aliases-for-use-with-thunderbird">Configure Catch-All aliases for use with Thunderbird</h1>
<h2 id="w_setup-a-thunderbird-identity-for-each-each-alias-you-want-to-reply-from">Setup a Thunderbird identity for each each alias you want to reply from</h2>
<p>If you have a <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail for a custom domain</a>, you will have to setup an <strong>identity</strong> in Thunderbird for every alias in that domain that you need to reply from. 
</p><p>For example, if your Catch-All is for <code>glamroc.com</code> and you would like to reply as  <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code> in addition to the default alias for <code>glamroc.com</code>, you will have to setup identities for both <code>alice@glamroc.com</code> and <code>slade@glamroc.com</code>. 
</p><p>Here''s how:
</p>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>.
</li><li> Tap on your account, e.g. <code>roc@glamcroc.com</code> &gt; <span class="menu">Sending mail</span>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Manage identities</span> &gt; <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <em>kebab</em> menu because the three vertical dots evoke a kebab &gt; <span class="menu">New identity</span>.
</li><li> Enter the desired alias in the <strong>Email address</strong> field e.g. <code>alice@glamroc.com</code>. All other fields are optional, but we recommend you enter a memorable shorter name in the <strong>Your name</strong> field.
</li><li> Save the identity by tapping <span class="button">SAVE</span>. When replying, you can now change the <strong>From</strong> field to this identity by tapping on it.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_send-email-with-the-identities-for-your-catch-all-alias">Send email with the identities for your Catch-All alias</h2>
<ol><li> When composing or replying an email, tap on the email address in the  <strong>From</strong> field.
</li><li> Tap on the relevant identity.
</li><li> Write and send the email as usual.
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_have-some-fun-now-that-email-setup-is-done">Have some fun now that email setup is done!</h1>
<p>Congratulations, you have done successfully setup Thundermail with Thunderbird for Android! Next:
</p>
<ul><li> Send and receive email with Thundermail.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-android">Getting started with Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327588", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 4, 2026, 6:48:31 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-04T06:48:31.272771-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add \"click\" in step 5", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 4, 2026, 6:48:40 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-04T06:48:40.324058-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:21:11+00:00');
