<p>No. Current versions of Thunderbird are built to run natively on Apple silicon and do not require Rosetta.
</p>
<h2 id="w_do-i-need-to-change-anything-right-now">Do I need to change anything right now?</h2>
<p>No. Thunderbird will continue to work for now when run with Rosetta, but performance and stability will be degraded.
</p><p>However, updating is recommended to ensure Thunderbird has the latest security updates. Running without Rosetta is best for Thunderbird performance and stability. 
</p>
<h2 id="w_what-happens-if-i-keep-using-an-old-version-of-thunderbird">What happens if I keep using an old version of Thunderbird?</h2>
<p>Older versions that rely on Rosetta may stop working on newer versions of macOS. Updating is recommended to ensure Thunderbird has the latest security updates. Running without Rosetta is best for Thunderbird performance and stability.
</p>
<h2 id="w_will-updating-thunderbird-affect-my-data">Will updating Thunderbird affect my data?</h2>
<p>No. Updating Thunderbird does not remove your bookmarks, history or saved data.
</p>
<h1 id="w_related-articles">Related articles</h1>
<ul><li><a href="/en-US/kb/installing-thunderbird-on-mac">Install Thunderbird on Mac</a>
</li><li><a href="/en-US/kb/updating-thunderbird">Update Thunderbird to the latest version</a>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327750", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 6, 2026, 9:15:40 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-06T09:15:40.658673-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "update to sync with the latest version of the corresponding Firefox article", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 6, 2026, 9:16:13 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-06T09:16:13.653799-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Jun 26, 2026, 11:14:38 AM", "datetime": "2026-06-26T11:14:38.693812-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "wsmwk", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:20:36+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (329422,'en-US','getting-started-thunderbird-pro','Getting Started with Thunderbird Pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-pro/revision/329422',327607,'2026-05-25T09:58:08.661243-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','fix broken link while preserving MH''s changes',1,'2026-05-25T09:59:16.485068-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','=Thunderbird Pro brief introduction=
Thunderbird Pro is a subscription-based bundle of services that consists of:
* Thundermail: An email service.
* Appointment: A collaborative scheduling service.
* Send: A secure way to send large files.

Check out our website for all the details: https://tb.pro/ 
{note}Please note: For the best possible experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send, and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.{/note}
=Prepare for Thunderbird Pro=
* If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
* If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, then install the Thunderbird Pro add-on according to [[Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop]]. 
* Set up your Thunderbird Pro account. You must enter a payment choice (for example, a credit card number). If you have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code, you must still add a payment option. If you have a problem with the code that you received, please [https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new ask for support]. Currently, only credit cards are accepted. Apple Pay, PayPal, and other 3rd party services are not yet supported. 
=Set up your Thunderbird Pro apps: Thundermail, Send, and Appointment=
* For Thundermail Desktop - Configure the Thunderbird program for Thundermail according to this article: [[Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail]].
* For Thundermail on mobile - Configure the Thunderbird Android app for Thundermail according to the article: [[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android]].
* For Appointment - Configure according to [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907 our Appointment articles].
* Configure Send as per [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 our Send articles].
=Let''s go!=
Go forth! Set up some office hours with Appointment. Transmit some files with Send. Deliver and receive email with Thundermail using your Thundermail Address Book, [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/46804820453907-Setting-Up-Email-Aliases Thundermail aliases] and [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias Thundermail catch-all addresses]. Use your Thundermail Calendar to setup events.','<h1 id="w_thunderbird-pro-brief-introduction">Thunderbird Pro brief introduction</h1>
<p>Thunderbird Pro is a subscription-based bundle of services that consists of:
</p>
<ul><li> Thundermail: An email service.
</li><li> Appointment: A collaborative scheduling service.
</li><li> Send: A secure way to send large files.
</li></ul>
<p>Check out our website for all the details: <a href="https://tb.pro/">https://tb.pro/</a> 
</p>
<div class="note">Please note: For the best possible experience, we recommend that you start with Thunderbird Desktop or a desktop browser like Firefox, Chrome, or Safari. Appointment, Send, and the Thunderbird Pro dashboard are optimized for desktop. The team is improving the mobile experience for Thunderbird Pro overall for mobile. For now, we have focused our mobile effort on Thundermail exclusively.</div>
<h1 id="w_prepare-for-thunderbird-pro">Prepare for Thunderbird Pro</h1>
<ul><li> If you are not a Thunderbird Desktop user, please register at the link in the email we sent you.
</li><li> If you have Thunderbird Desktop installed, then install the Thunderbird Pro add-on according to <a href="/en-US/kb/install-thunderbird-pro-add-thunderbird-desktop">Install the Thunderbird Pro Add-on in Thunderbird Desktop</a>. 
</li><li> Set up your Thunderbird Pro account. You must enter a payment choice (for example, a credit card number). If you have a Thunderbird Pro coupon code, you must still add a payment option. If you have a problem with the code that you received, please <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">ask for support</a>. Currently, only credit cards are accepted. Apple Pay, PayPal, and other 3rd party services are not yet supported. 
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_set-up-your-thunderbird-pro-apps-thundermail-send-and-appointment">Set up your Thunderbird Pro apps: Thundermail, Send, and Appointment</h1>
<ul><li> For Thundermail Desktop - Configure the Thunderbird program for Thundermail according to this article: <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail">Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail</a>.
</li><li> For Thundermail on mobile - Configure the Thunderbird Android app for Thundermail according to the article: <a href="/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android">Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li><li> For Appointment - Configure according to <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43161318933907">our Appointment articles</a>.
</li><li> Configure Send as per <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235">our Send articles</a>.
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_lets-go">Let''s go!</h1>
<p>Go forth! Set up some office hours with Appointment. Transmit some files with Send. Deliver and receive email with Thundermail using your Thundermail Address Book, <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/46804820453907-Setting-Up-Email-Aliases">Thundermail aliases</a> and <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">Thundermail catch-all addresses</a>. Use your Thundermail Calendar to setup events.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "329422", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "May 25, 2026, 9:58:08 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-25T09:58:08.661243-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix broken link while preserving MH''s changes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 25, 2026, 9:59:16 AM", "datetime": "2026-05-25T09:59:16.485068-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:20:33+00:00');
INSERT INTO revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at) VALUES (329955,'en-US','thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail','Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail/revision/329955',327671,'2026-06-01T22:59:59.832870-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP do not approve. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/199',1,'2026-06-01T23:02:38.537312-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[Template:TBproEarlyBirdInviteOnly]]

__TOC__

=Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop=
{note}''''''NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires the latest ESR or monthly release. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird, which is documented in: [[New in Thunderbird Desktop]].{/note}
# Click the Thunderbird menu {menu ☰} >  {menu Add Account} ({menu New Account} for older versions of Thunderbird) > {menu Email}.
# Enter your Thundermail email address and follow the prompts to set up your Thundermail email account. And for versions older than 150, please click the {button Connect} button next to ''''''Thundermail Address Book'''''' and the {button Connect} button next to ''''''Thundermail Calendar'''''' to ensure your Thundermail address book and calendar are added to Thunderbird.

Thunderbird should have automatically added your Thundermail email in [[Configuration Options for Accounts|account settings]], a CalDAV calendar called ''''''Thundermail Calendar'''''' in your Thunderbird calendar [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]] (press {for not mac}{key Alt+3}{/for}{for mac}{key Ctrl+3}{/for}), and a CardDAV address book called ''''''Thundermail Address Book'''''' in your address book [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]] (press {for not mac}{key Alt+2}{/for}{for mac}{key Ctrl+2}{/for}) to check). If any of those are missing, please try changing the settings to those in the manual settings sections below, and please [https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/ create a Thunderbird Pro support ticket] if you have any issues.
=Manual Settings=
<!--If Thunderbird failed to automatically add your Thundermail email, calendar, or address book, please check the following:
* configure your Thundermail email settings to match your [https://accounts.tb.pro/mail TB Pro Thundermail page].
* add a CalDAV calendar called ''''''Thundermail Calendar'''''' in your Thunderbird calendar [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]]. Press {key Alt+3} ({key Ctrl+3} on macOS) to check.
* add a CardDAV address book called ''''''Thundermail Address Book'''''' in your Address Book [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]]. Press {key Alt+2} ({key Ctrl+2} on macOS) to check. -->

If Thunderbird failed to add the expected items or you need to adjust them, please try manually changing the settings by following the instructions in the sections below. If manual setup fails, please [https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/ create a Thunderbird Pro support ticket].

[[UI:details_start]]

==Receiving Email==
# Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {menu Account Settings}.
# In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example: ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''. Then, click on the chevron “&gt;” to expand the drop down menu. Finally, click on {menu Server Settings} and set the following values:

* ''''''Server Name:'''''' [http://mail.thundermail.com mail.thundermail.com] ''''''Server Port:'''''' 993
* ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address e.g. ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''
* ''''''Authentication method: ''''''OAuth2''''''
==Sending Email==
# Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Account Settings}.
# In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''. Click on {button Edit outgoing server…} and set the following values:
 
* ''''''Server Name:'''''' mail.thundermail.com
* ''''''Server Port:'''''' 465 ''''''Connection Security:'''''' SSL/TLS
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address For example: ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''
* ''''''Authentication method:'''''' OAuth2
==Thundermail Calendar==
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Add Account} ({menu New Account} for older versions of Thunderbird) > {menu Calendar} > {button On the Network}.
# For ''''''Username:'''''', enter your Thundermail email address. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''.
# For ''''''Location'''''', enter ''''''mail.thundermail.com''''''.
# Click {button Find Calendars}.
# In the ''''''Create New Calendar'''''' dialog, select your Thundermail calendar and click {button Subscribe}.
==Thundermail Address Book==
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {menu Add Account} ({menu New Account} for older versions of Thunderbird) > {menu Address Book} ({menu New Address Book} for older versions of Thunderbird) > {menu Add remote Address Book} ({button New remote Address Book} for older versions of Thunderbird).
#  For ''''''Username:'''''', enter your Thundermail email address. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''.
# For ''''''URL/Hostname'''''', enter ''''''https://mail.thundermail.com''''''.
# Click {button Continue}.
# Select your Thundermail Address Book and click {button Continue}.

[[UI:details_end]]

=Custom Domain catch-all and custom aliases=
How to setup Thunderbird Desktop for [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51253809827347-Custom-Domains-and-DNS-Configuration custom domains] in Thundermail:
==Send and receive email with Thundermail custom domain aliases using Thunderbird identities==
For every custom domain [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/46804820453907-Setting-Up-Email-Aliases alias] you create in Thundermail, you will have to create a new [[Using Identities|identity]] in Thunderbird in order to send email with that alias. Here''s how using our example custom domain <code>glamroc.com</code>, our example thundermail address of <code>roc@thundermail.com</code>: and custom domain alias of <code>roc@glamroc.com</code>:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Account Settings} > Click on the thundermail.com account in the left sidebar which in our example is: <code>roc@thundermail.com > {button Manage Identities…"} > {button Add…} 
# Add your custom domain alias e.g. <code>roc@glamroc.com
# If you want this to be the default identity when composing new email, click on the new identity, and then click on {button Set Default} and {button Close}
Now the custom domain alias, <code>roc@glamroc.com</code> is the default identity when writing new email and you can send and receive email on both <code>roc@thundermail.com</code> and <code>roc@glamroc.com</code> by selecting the appropriate identity.
==Send and reply to email using a Thundermail catch-all alias==
* If you have a [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias catch-all alias configured in Thundermail for a custom domain], here''s how to use it:
*# When composing or replying to an email, click on the email address next to ''''''From''''''.
*# Click on {button Customize From Address…}. 
*# Finally, type in an email address for the custom domain you created the catch-all in.

=Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!=
* [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|Send and receive email]] with Thundermail. If you have large files, you can also use [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 ''''''Thunderbird Send'''''']. which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
* Enjoy your Thundermail Calendar: [https://support.mozilla.org/products/thunderbird/email-and-messaging/calendar Create some events, invite people to invites, etc].
* Use your Thundermail Address Book for [[Addressing an Email|composing email]], managing your contacts, etc.
* New to Thunderbird? Check out [[Get started with Thunderbird]].','<p></p><div class="warning">NOTE: Thundermail (formerly known as Thunderbird Pro) is currently in its Early Bird release and available  by invitation only. To learn more and join the waitlist, visit <a href="https://tb.pro/">our website</a>. We’ll be opening Thundermail to the public once the Early Bird release concludes.</div>
<p></p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-desktop"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_manual-settings"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Settings</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_receiving-email"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Receiving Email</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_sending-email"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Sending Email</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thundermail-calendar"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thundermail Calendar</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thundermail-address-book"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thundermail Address Book</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_custom-domain-catch-all-and-custom-aliases"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Custom Domain catch-all and custom aliases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_send-and-receive-email-with-thundermail-custom-domain-aliases-using-thunderbird-identities"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Send and receive email with Thundermail custom domain aliases using Thunderbird identities</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_send-and-reply-to-email-using-a-thundermail-catch-all-alias"><span class="tocnumber">3.2</span> <span class="toctext">Send and reply to email using a Thundermail catch-all alias</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_send-thundermail-use-your-thundermail-calendar-and-thundermail-address-book-and-have-some-fun"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-desktop">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop</h1>
<div class="note"><strong>NOTE</strong>: Thunderbird Pro requires the latest ESR or monthly release. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird, which is documented in: <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop">New in Thunderbird Desktop</a>.</div>
<ol><li> Click the Thunderbird menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt;  <span class="menu">Add Account</span> (<span class="menu">New Account</span> for older versions of Thunderbird) &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>.
</li><li> Enter your Thundermail email address and follow the prompts to set up your Thundermail email account. And for versions older than 150, please click the <span class="button">Connect</span> button next to <strong>Thundermail Address Book</strong> and the <span class="button">Connect</span> button next to <strong>Thundermail Calendar</strong> to ensure your Thundermail address book and calendar are added to Thunderbird.
</li></ol>
<p>Thunderbird should have automatically added your Thundermail email in <a href="/en-US/kb/configuration-options-accounts">account settings</a>, a CalDAV calendar called <strong>Thundermail Calendar</strong> in your Thunderbird calendar <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar">space</a> (press <span class="for" data-for="not mac" style="display: none;"><span class="key">Alt</span> + <span class="key">3</span></span><span class="for" data-for="mac"><span class="key">Ctrl</span> + <span class="key">3</span></span>), and a CardDAV address book called <strong>Thundermail Address Book</strong> in your address book <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar">space</a> (press <span class="for" data-for="not mac" style="display: none;"><span class="key">Alt</span> + <span class="key">2</span></span><span class="for" data-for="mac"><span class="key">Ctrl</span> + <span class="key">2</span></span>) to check). If any of those are missing, please try changing the settings to those in the manual settings sections below, and please <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/">create a Thunderbird Pro support ticket</a> if you have any issues.
</p>
<h1 id="w_manual-settings">Manual Settings</h1>
<p>

</p><p>If Thunderbird failed to add the expected items or you need to adjust them, please try manually changing the settings by following the instructions in the sections below. If manual setup fails, please <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/">create a Thunderbird Pro support ticket</a>.
</p><p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_receiving-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Receiving Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>.
</li><li> In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example: <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>. Then, click on the chevron “&gt;” to expand the drop down menu. Finally, click on <span class="menu">Server Settings</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a> <strong>Server Port:</strong> 993
</li><li> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address e.g. <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>
</li><li> <strong>Authentication method: </strong>OAuth2<strong>
</strong>
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>.
</li><li> In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>. Click on <span class="button">Edit outgoing server…</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a>
</li><li> <strong>Server Port:</strong> 465 <strong>Connection Security:</strong> SSL/TLS
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address For example: <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>
</li><li> <strong>Authentication method:</strong> OAuth2
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_thundermail-calendar" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Calendar</button></h2>
<ol class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add Account</span> (<span class="menu">New Account</span> for older versions of Thunderbird) &gt; <span class="menu">Calendar</span> &gt; <span class="button">On the Network</span>.
</li><li> For <strong>Username:</strong>, enter your Thundermail email address. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>.
</li><li> For <strong>Location</strong>, enter <strong><a href="http://mail.thundermail.com">mail.thundermail.com</a></strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Find Calendars</span>.
</li><li> In the <strong>Create New Calendar</strong> dialog, select your Thundermail calendar and click <span class="button">Subscribe</span>.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_thundermail-address-book" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail Address Book</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span>  &gt; <span class="menu">Add Account</span> (<span class="menu">New Account</span> for older versions of Thunderbird) &gt; <span class="menu">Address Book</span> (<span class="menu">New Address Book</span> for older versions of Thunderbird) &gt; <span class="menu">Add remote Address Book</span> (<span class="button">New remote Address Book</span> for older versions of Thunderbird).
</li><li>  For <strong>Username:</strong>, enter your Thundermail email address. For example <strong>nemo@thundermail.com</strong>.
</li><li> For <strong>URL/Hostname</strong>, enter <strong><a href="https://mail.thundermail.com">https://mail.thundermail.com</a></strong>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li><li> Select your Thundermail Address Book and click <span class="button">Continue</span>.
</li></ol><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_custom-domain-catch-all-and-custom-aliases">Custom Domain catch-all and custom aliases</h1>
<p>How to setup Thunderbird Desktop for <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51253809827347-Custom-Domains-and-DNS-Configuration">custom domains</a> in Thundermail:
</p>
<h2 id="w_send-and-receive-email-with-thundermail-custom-domain-aliases-using-thunderbird-identities">Send and receive email with Thundermail custom domain aliases using Thunderbird identities</h2>
<p>For every custom domain <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/46804820453907-Setting-Up-Email-Aliases">alias</a> you create in Thundermail, you will have to create a new <a href="/en-US/kb/using-identities">identity</a> in Thunderbird in order to send email with that alias. Here''s how using our example custom domain <code>glamroc.com</code>, our example thundermail address of <code>roc@thundermail.com</code>: and custom domain alias of <code>roc@glamroc.com</code>:
</p>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span> &gt; Click on the <a href="http://thundermail.com">thundermail.com</a> account in the left sidebar which in our example is: <code>roc@thundermail.com &gt; <span class="button">Manage Identities…"</span> &gt; <span class="button">Add…</span> 
</code></li><li><code> Add your custom domain alias e.g. &lt;code&gt;roc@glamroc.com
</code></li><li><code> If you want this to be the default identity when composing new email, click on the new identity, and then click on <span class="button">Set Default</span> and <span class="button">Close</span>
</code></li></ol><code>
</code><p><code>Now the custom domain alias, &lt;code&gt;roc@glamroc.com</code> is the default identity when writing new email and you can send and receive email on both <code>roc@thundermail.com</code> and <code>roc@glamroc.com</code> by selecting the appropriate identity.
</p>
<h2 id="w_send-and-reply-to-email-using-a-thundermail-catch-all-alias">Send and reply to email using a Thundermail catch-all alias</h2>
<ul><li> If you have a <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias">catch-all alias configured in Thundermail for a custom domain</a>, here''s how to use it:
<ol><li> When composing or replying to an email, click on the email address next to <strong>From</strong>.
</li><li> Click on <span class="button">Customize From Address…</span>. 
</li><li> Finally, type in an email address for the custom domain you created the catch-all in.
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_send-thundermail-use-your-thundermail-calendar-and-thundermail-address-book-and-have-some-fun">Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">Send and receive email</a> with Thundermail. If you have large files, you can also use <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235"><strong>Thunderbird Send</strong></a>. which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
</li><li> Enjoy your Thundermail Calendar: <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/products/thunderbird/email-and-messaging/calendar">Create some events, invite people to invites, etc</a>.
</li><li> Use your Thundermail Address Book for <a href="/en-US/kb/addressing-email">composing email</a>, managing your contacts, etc.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird? Check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird">Get started with Thunderbird</a>.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "329955", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Jun 1, 2026, 10:59:59 PM", "datetime": "2026-06-01T22:59:59.832870-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "WIP do not approve. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/199", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jun 1, 2026, 11:02:38 PM", "datetime": "2026-06-01T23:02:38.537312-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:20:31+00:00');
