><a href="#w_dns-over-https"><span class="tocnumber">9.1</span> <span class="toctext">DNS over HTTPS</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_account-hub-supports-manual-configuration-for-ews-imap-and-pop3-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">9.2</span> <span class="toctext">Account Hub supports manual configuration for EWS, IMAP and POP3 accounts</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-144"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 144</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_exchange-enhancements-and-bug-fixes"><span class="tocnumber">10.1</span> <span class="toctext">Exchange enhancements and bug fixes</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-143"><span class="tocnumber">11</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 143</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_exchange-support-enhancements-and-bug-fixes"><span class="tocnumber">11.1</span> <span class="toctext">Exchange Support enhancements and bug fixes</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-142"><span class="tocnumber">12</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 142</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_switch-to-the-old-account-setup-flow-to-fix-issues-with-hotmail-and-outlook-com-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">12.1</span> <span class="toctext">Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues with Hotmail and outlook.com accounts</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order"><span class="tocnumber">12.2</span> <span class="toctext">Reset manual folder sorting order</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf"><span class="tocnumber">12.3</span> <span class="toctext">Add a visual signature to a PDF</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release"><span class="tocnumber">12.4</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_more-stable-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">12.5</span> <span class="toctext">More stable Exchange support</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-141"><span class="tocnumber">13</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 141</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">13.1</span> <span class="toctext">Archive action added to new email notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_better-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">13.2</span> <span class="toctext">Better Exchange support</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry"><span class="tocnumber">13.3</span> <span class="toctext">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2"><span class="tocnumber">13.4</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse"><span class="tocnumber">14</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_dark-message-mode"><span class="tocnumber">14.1</span> <span class="toctext">Dark Message Mode</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings"><span class="tocnumber">14.2</span> <span class="toctext">New Appearance Panel in Settings</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_native-os-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">14.3</span> <span class="toctext">Native OS Notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_redesigned-account-hub"><span class="tocnumber">14.4</span> <span class="toctext">Redesigned Account hub</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manual-folder-sorting"><span class="tocnumber">14.5</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Folder Sorting</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users"><span class="tocnumber">14.6</span> <span class="toctext">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_export-for-mobile"><span class="tocnumber">14.7</span> <span class="toctext">Export for Mobile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">14.8</span> <span class="toctext">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">15</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">15.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">15.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">15.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">15.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-153-esr-153-meadow">Thunderbird 153 / ESR 153 "Meadow"</h1>
<ul><li> All the improvements since 140.
</li><li> Unified folders display your custom account color indicator with an account name tooltip.
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span> &gt; Click your email account e.g. <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">button</span> underneath <strong>Color:</strong> and select a color for that account e.g. pink.
<dl><dt> <img alt="tb153-change-account-color" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-07-26-20-10-20-d58a9d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li><li> You will now see an indicator with that color (in our example: pink) for that account in the message list in a unified folder. There will also be a tooltip with the account name (in our example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>).
<dl><dt> <img alt="tb-153-account-color-indicator-tooltip" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-07-26-20-21-18-cb6afb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
</li><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/tb-oauth">OAuth</a> login for email accounts (for example: gmail, Thundermail, etc) opens in the system default web browser. Thunderbird 152, and older versions opened the OAuth login in a Thunderbird tab.
</li></ul>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-152">Thunderbird 152</h1>
<h2 id="w_improved-thundermail-configuration" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Improved Thundermail configuration</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> One-click account setup for <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail">Thundermail</a> accounts.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-151">Thunderbird 151</h1>
<h2 id="w_thundermail-configuration" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Thundermail configuration</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail">Thundermail</a> configuration is now built-in to Thunderbrirfd.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_ews-oauth-improvements" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">EWS OAuth improvements</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now override OAuth provider details for EWS accounts.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-150">Thunderbird 150</h1>
<h2 id="w_account-hub-is-now-the-default" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Account hub is now the default</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><li> Account hub is opened on the first run of Thunderbird. It is now the default across mail, calendar and address book.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_alphabetical-sorting-in-recent-destinations" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Alphabetical sorting in Recent Destinations</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true"><li> <strong>Recent Destinations</strong> in General Settings now supports alphabetical sorting. See: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; Scroll down to <strong>Sort order:</strong> under <strong>Folder Management Options</strong> and choose <span class="menu">Alphabetical</span> or <span class="menu">Most recent</span>.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_custom-accent-color" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Custom Accent color</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li><li> Next to <strong>Define the color used for primary buttons and highlighted elements:</strong>, select one of the following buttons: <span class="button">Follow operating system</span>, <span class="button">Thunderbird blue</span>, <span class="button">Purple</span>, <span class="button">Orange</span>, <span class="button">Pink</span>, <span class="button">Ink</span>, or, <span class="button">Teal</span>. 
</li></ol><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-149">Thunderbird 149</h1>
<h2 id="w_exchange-improvements" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Exchange Improvements</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true"><li> Starred Exchange messages now persist across devices.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_account-hub-on-for-address-books" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Account Hub on for Address Books</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true"><li> Address books are now created in Account Hub.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_dark-mode-link-color-fixed" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Dark Mode link color fixed</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Dark mode link colors are once more readable.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-148">Thunderbird 148</h1>
<h2 id="w_ntlm-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">NTLM support</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><li> <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NTLM">NTLM authentication</a> is now supported.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_yahoo-aol-att-oauth2-authentication-update" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">Yahoo, AOL, ATT OAuth2 authentication update</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true"><li> Thunderbird switched to a more secure authorization protocol called <strong>PKCE</strong> for Yahoo, AT&amp;T and AOL accounts. This switch adds support for Yahoo/AOL calendars and adddress books. Full details: <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-yahoo">OAuth2 Authentication for Yahoo, AOL and ATT</a>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_dark-mode-link-color-issue" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Dark Mode link color issue</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Known issue: Dark mode link colors might be hard to read. Workaround: switch to a different theme. A fix has been developed for a future release; you can follow along in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2018015">bug 2018015</a>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-147">Thunderbird 147</h1>
<h2 id="w_reset-folder-order" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">Reset Folder Order</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true"><li> <span class="menu">Reset Folder Order</span> has been fixed (see the 142 section). It now restores the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_localization-of-folder-names" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Localization of folder names</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> All outstanding issues with localization of folder names have been fixed. If you notice any other issues, please <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird">file a Thunderbird desktop support request</a>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-146">Thunderbird 146</h1>
<h2 id="w_drag-and-drop-on-macos" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Drag and Drop on macOS</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true"><li> Drag and Drop for attachments on macOS is working again.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_openpgp-keyserver" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">OpenPGP Keyserver</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now add your own OpenPGP Keyserver:
<ul><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt;<span class="menu">Privacy &amp; Security</span> &gt; Under <strong>OpenPGP Keyservers</strong> <span class="menu">Add...</span>. Screenshot:
</li></ul>
</li></ul><p><img alt="tb146-add-open-pgp-keyserver" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-12-12-11-07-38-4c0f65.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-145">Thunderbird 145</h1>
<h2 id="w_dns-over-https" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-expanded="false">DNS over HTTPS</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-hidden="true"><li> Thunderbird now supports DNS over HTTPS.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_account-hub-supports-manual-configuration-for-ews-imap-and-pop3-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-expanded="false">Account Hub supports manual configuration for EWS, IMAP and POP3 accounts</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> In the <strong>Account Hub</strong>, once you enter a valid email address, you can now manually configure your email settings by clicking <span class="menu">MANUAL CONFIGURATION</span>. 
<dl><dt><img alt="tb145-account-hub-manual-configuration" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-11-12-23-06-35-21b46c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> <strong>MANUAL CONFIGURATION</strong> in the <strong>Account Hub</strong> supports manual configuration of <span class="menu">EWS</span>, <span class="menu">IMAP</span> and <span class="menu">POP3</span> accounts.
<dl><dt><img alt="tb145-ews-imap-pop-account-hub-manual-configuration" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-11-12-23-55-15-82277a.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Manual configuration of EWS accounts is now supported as per the screenshots in the above two bullet points. For more details, please see the <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange#w_manual-ews-configuration">Manual EWS configuration section of our Thunderbird and Exchange article</a>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-144">Thunderbird 144</h1>
