#* For Graph: https://graph.microsoft.com/
# Click {button Find settings}. For EWS, ''''''Exchange Web Services'''''' will automatically be selected. For Graph, ''''''Microsoft Graph'''''' will be selected.
# Your Microsoft 365 email address (e.g. <code>nemo@o365.thunderbird.net</code>) you used in step 1 should be automatically entered into the ''''''Username'''''' field (if not, then correct it).
# Follow the prompts and fill in the settings from your Exchange or Graph administrator. Full details at [[Custom OAuth for advanced users]] (scroll down to ''''''Per-account OAuth2 Microsoft Exchange customization'''''').

=Send and receive emails with your Exchange or Graph Account=
Once you have configured your Exchange or Graph Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|send and receive emails]] just like an IMAP or POP account.

=Limitations=
Not yet supported:
* Address book
* Calendar
* OAuth authentication with on-premise instances 
* Shared mailboxes 
<!--
"Phase 5" items are on the near term road map, expected to by available/resolved by 1Q2026. The full list of phase 5 is [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/showdependencytree.cgi?id=1995377&hide_resolved=1 this bug list].
-->
=Feedback and Bug Reports=
To report a problem when using version 157 or newer, please [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&component=Networking:%20Exchange&short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&blocked=1847846&bug_type=defect file a bug report].

To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].

You may use Topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta beta group] or the [https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise enterprise group].

=Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers=
Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page].','<div class="warning">Please read <a href="/en-US/kb/microsoft-ews-graph-migration">Microsoft EWS to Graph Migration October 2026</a> for details on the upcoming migration to Graph from Exchange via EWS.</div>
<div class="warning">
<p>For the best Microsoft Exchange and Microsoft Graph experience on desktop, we recommend Thunderbird 157 or newer.
</p><p>Thunderbird on desktop implements Exchange via EWS (Exchange Web Services) and Microsoft Graph. Support for Exchange and Graph is <strong>currently limited to email</strong>.
</p><p>Calendar and address book using Exchange and Graph on desktop will follow at a later date. Also in the future is Exchange and Graph support on Android, so please do not file bug reports for these items at this time.
</p>
For more technical detail, as well as things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.</div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_setup"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Setup</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_configure-your-exchange-or-graph-account"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Configure your Exchange or Graph account</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_manual-exchange-and-graph-configuration"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Exchange and Graph configuration</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-or-graph-account"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Send and receive emails with your Exchange or Graph Account</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_limitations"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Limitations</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_feedback-and-bug-reports"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Feedback and Bug Reports</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers"><span class="tocnumber">5</span> <span class="toctext">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_setup">Setup</h1>
<p>When creating a new Exchange or Graph account, once an Exchange or Graph account is detected, Thunderbird will give you options for both Exchange and Graph.
</p>
<h2 id="w_configure-your-exchange-or-graph-account">Configure your Exchange or Graph account</h2>
<p>Again, for the best experience, we recommend Thunderbird 157 or newer.
</p>
<ol><li> Click the Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span>. The <em>Account Hub</em> dialog will appear.
</li><li> Enter your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange or Graph email account.
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Continue</span> button. The password entry dialog will appear in your system web browser.<br><br><div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> In the first dialog box, you do not enter your account password. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div> Screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dd><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="450">
</dd></dl>
</li><li> Enter your password and click <span class="button">Sign in</span>. The account type selection dialog will appear.
<dl><dd><img alt="tb157-beta-exchange-graph-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-09-28-21-05-35-ae6b32.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="450">
</dd></dl>
</li><li> Select the <img alt="radio_button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-11-19-10-27-42-00d9fc.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="20"> <span class="button">Exchange</span> or the <img alt="radio_button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-11-19-10-27-42-00d9fc.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" width="20"> <span class="button">Microsoft Graph API</span> radio button and click <span class="button">Continue</span> to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange or Graph account.
</li></ol>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> The <span class="button">Exchange</span> and <span class="button">Microsoft Graph API</span> radio buttons only appear if the email you entered is an Exchange or Graph account.</div>
<h3 id="w_manual-exchange-and-graph-configuration">Manual Exchange and Graph configuration</h3>
<p>There are a diversity of Exchange and Graph servers which could cause auto configuration of your Exchange or Graph email account to fail. Here''s a potential workaround for that situation:
</p>
<ol><li> Add a new email account: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span> and enter a Microsoft 365 email address (e.g. <code>nemo@o365.thunderbird.net</code>) and then click <strong>MANUAL CONFIGURATION</strong> on the bottom left of the Account hub.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Microsoft Exchange or Microsoft 365</span> and then click <span class="button">Set up account</span>.
</li><li> In the <strong>Exchange settings</strong> dialog, type one of the following URLs into the <strong>Enter the service URL</strong> field:
<ul><li> For EWS: <a href="https://outlook.office365.com/EWS/Exchange.asmx">https://outlook.office365.com/EWS/Exchange.asmx</a>
</li><li> For Graph: <a href="https://graph.microsoft.com/">https://graph.microsoft.com/</a>
</li></ul>
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Find settings</span>. For EWS, <strong>Exchange Web Services</strong> will automatically be selected. For Graph, <strong>Microsoft Graph</strong> will be selected.
</li><li> Your Microsoft 365 email address (e.g. <code>nemo@o365.thunderbird.net</code>) you used in step 1 should be automatically entered into the <strong>Username</strong> field (if not, then correct it).
</li><li> Follow the prompts and fill in the settings from your Exchange or Graph administrator. Full details at <a href="/en-US/kb/custom-oauth-advanced-users">Custom OAuth for advanced users</a> (scroll down to <strong>Per-account OAuth2 Microsoft Exchange customization</strong>).
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-or-graph-account">Send and receive emails with your Exchange or Graph Account</h1>
<p>Once you have configured your Exchange or Graph Account in Thunderbird, you can use it to <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">send and receive emails</a> just like an IMAP or POP account.
</p>
<h1 id="w_limitations">Limitations</h1>
<p>Not yet supported:
</p>
<ul><li> Address book
</li><li> Calendar
</li><li> OAuth authentication with on-premise instances 
</li><li> Shared mailboxes 
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>
<h1 id="w_feedback-and-bug-reports">Feedback and Bug Reports</h1>
<p>To report a problem when using version 157 or newer, please <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=MailNews%20Core&amp;component=Networking:%20Exchange&amp;short_desc=%5BEWS%5D%20xxxxxxxxx&amp;blocked=1847846&amp;bug_type=defect">file a bug report</a>.
</p><p>To see open bug reports and more technical detail about bug reporting, tracking bug activity, plus things to test and look for, see the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p><p>You may use Topicbox to discuss or ask questions about Exchange, either the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/beta">beta group</a> or the <a href="https://thunderbird.topicbox.com/groups/enterprise">enterprise group</a>.
</p>
<h1 id="w_microsoft-hosted-vs-self-hosted-exchange-servers">Microsoft hosted vs. self hosted exchange servers</h1>
<p>Administrators and others interested in the details of EWS instances (Microsoft hosted, Microsoft hosted as tenant-specific, and self hosted) will want to refer to the <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a>.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "356680", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Sep 28, 2026, 9:39:51 PM", "datetime": "2026-09-28T21:39:51.892768-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "wip do not approve, or translate, discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/210", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Sep 28, 2026, 9:40:18 PM", "datetime": "2026-09-28T21:40:18.104655-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:16:48+00:00');
