<ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/automatic-account-configuration">Automatic Account Configuration</a> 
</li><li> <a href="http://mail.google.com/support/bin/answer.py?answer=180189">First steps with IMAP on Gmail</a>  
</li><li> <a href="http://mail.google.com/support/bin/topic.py?topic=12806">Gmail''s IMAP tips</a>
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_gmails-particularities">Gmail''s particularities</h1>
<h2 id="w_archiving-messages">Archiving messages</h2>
<p>In order to be consistent with Gmail''s behavior, Thunderbird archives your message in the "All Mail" folder, and not in an "Archive" folder as it does for other accounts (as described in the <a href="/en-US/kb/archived-messages">Archived Messages</a> article).
</p><p><img alt="Gmail Archive settings" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-03-17-04-13-09-41649e.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</p><p>Note that the <span class="button">Archive options...</span> button is disabled for Gmail accounts, as it is not necessary to define the archive granularity with Gmail.
</p>
<h2 id="w_subscribing-to-folders-and-synchronizing-messages">Subscribing to folders and synchronizing messages</h2>
<h3 id="w_understanding-gmail-labels-and-thunderbird-folders">Understanding Gmail labels and Thunderbird folders</h3>
<p>Gmail uses a special implementation of IMAP. In this implementation, Gmail labels become Thunderbird folders. When you apply a label to a message in Gmail, Thunderbird creates a folder with the same name as the label and stores the message in that folder. Similarly, if you move a message to a folder in Thunderbird, Gmail will create a label with the folder name and assign it to the message.
</p><p>In the example shown below, the folders at the same level as the "<em>[Gmail]</em>" folder ("g+", "Personal", "Receipts", "Travel" and "Work") correspond to Gmail labels.<br> 
</p><p><img alt="default gmail folders" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-03-22-16-07-48-8304a9.jpg" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> <br>
</p><p>There is also a set of special sub-folders for the "<em>[Gmail]</em>" folder:
</p>
<ul><li> All Mail: contains all of the messages in your Gmail account, including sent and archived messages. Any messages that you see in the inbox will also appear in the <em>[Gmail]/All Mail</em> folder.
</li><li> Drafts: contains draft messages.
</li><li> Sent Mail: contains sent messages.
</li><li> Spam: contains messages that were marked as spam (either by Gmail or Thunderbird).
</li><li> Starred: contains messages that were starred (either by Gmail or Thunderbird).
</li><li> Trash: contains deleted messages.
</li><li> Important: contains messages that Gmail has flagged as "important". (See <a href="http://support.google.com/mail/bin/answer.py?answer=186531&amp;topic=1669050&amp;ctx=topic">Priority Inbox overview</a> for more details about this Gmail feature.)
</li></ul>
<h3 id="w_subscribing-to-or-unsubscribing-from-folders-labels">Subscribing to or unsubscribing from folders (labels)</h3>
<p>You can configure which Gmail folders you want to display in Thunderbird. By default all Gmail folders are displayed, as described above. To configure folder display, right-click on the account name and select <span class="menu">Subscribe</span>. <br>
</p><p><img alt="subscribe gmail folders" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2012-03-22-16-20-21-1f5531.jpg" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</p><p>Uncheck any folders that you don''t want to display in Thunderbird. Messages will still be downloaded and available through the "All Mail" folder. They will also be included in search results. However, the Gmail label (Thunderbird folder) will not be displayed. 
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h3 id="w_synchronizing-folders-labels">Synchronizing folders (labels)</h3>
<p>If you want to see all your Gmail labels and messages in Thunderbird but prefer to avoid all the messages being downloaded to your system, you may want to tweak the synchronization settings. This allows you to define which folder should be synchronized. If you don''t synchronize a folder, the message header will still be displayed in Thunderbird, but the message content will only be downloaded when you click on the message header.
</p><p>To change how messages are downloaded, set synchronization options for the account and for individual folders. (<span class="for" data-for="win,mac"><span class="menu">Tools &gt; Account Settings...</span></span><span class="for" data-for="linux" style="display: none;"><span class="menu">Edit &gt; Account Settings...</span></span>) See <a href="/en-US/kb/imap-synchronization#w_synchronization">IMAP Synchronization</a> for more information.
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h1 id="w_useful-add-ons">Useful Add-ons</h1>
<ul><li> If you want to sync your contacts between Thunderbird and Gmail, you should try either the <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/google-contacts/">Google Contacts</a> or <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/gcontactsync/">gContactSync</a> add-ons.
</li><li> If you want to sync your calendar between Lightning and Google Calendar, you should read <a href="/en-US/kb/using-lightning-google-calendar">Using Thunderbird with Google Calendar</a>.
</li><li> <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/flat-folder-tree/">Flat Folder Tree</a>  is useful to show all the sub-folders of the [Gmail] IMAP''s folder at the same level than your other folders.
</li><li> <a href="https://addons.thunderbird.net/thunderbird/addon/gmailbuttons/">Gmail Buttons</a> makes it easier to move messages to the Trash and Spam folders. Beta version also shows all Gmail labels for each message.
</li></ul>
<p><br>
</p>
<h1 id="w_see-also">See also</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/78892?hl=en">Gmail''s support article</a>
</li><li> <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=402793">The ticket which tracks issues using Gmail with Thunderbird (Bug 402793)</a>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "241337", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 10, 2022, 9:54:29 PM", "datetime": "2022-04-10T21:54:29-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "thomas8", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/firefox877/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Fix some nits and polish the oAuth warning", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 10, 2022, 9:55:51 PM", "datetime": "2022-04-10T21:55:51-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "firefox877", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Apr 10, 2022, 9:55:51 PM", "datetime": "2022-04-10T21:55:51-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "firefox877", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:17:00+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (241666,'en-US','automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20','Automatic Conversion of Google mail accounts to OAuth 2.0 Authentication','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20/revision/241666',241274,'2022-04-14T04:10:22-07:00','YFdyh000','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/yfdyh000/','oAuth to OAuth',1,'2022-04-29T08:29:18-07:00','wsmwk',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','Thunderbird 91.8.0, released 5th April 2022, converts Gmail accounts to OAuth 2.0 to help users comply with [https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/6010255 Google''s requirement of OAuth 2.0 for Gmail logins].

Thunderbird changing the method of authentication to OAuth 2.0 will cause problems if you have cookies disabled in Thunderbird, because cookies must be enabled for OAuth 2.0 authentication flow to work properly. Without cookies to store data between page updates, the authentication flow cannot successfully complete the web pages served by Google.

To avoid or correct the problem, do one of the following:
* Ensure that ''''''Accept cookies from sites'''''' is enabled at {button ≡} > {menu Preferences} > type ''''''cookies'''''' into the search field. You can disable cookies after the OAuth process is completed, and receiving and sending mail will work with cookies disabled. But when the OAuth token for Gmail access expires at some date in the future, the OAuth process will be needed again, which will require cookies to be enabled.
* Create an exception with cookies disabled at {button ≡} > {menu Preferences} > {menu Privacy & Security} > {menu Web Content} > {menu Accept cookies from sites} (with {menu Accept} unchecked), click {menu Exceptions} and enter an address of ''''''https://accounts.google.com''''''. Pick {menu Allow}, then {menu Save Changes}.','<p>Thunderbird 91.8.0, released 5th April 2022, converts Gmail accounts to OAuth&nbsp;2.0 to help users comply with <a href="https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/6010255">Google''s requirement of OAuth&nbsp;2.0 for Gmail logins</a>.
</p><p>Thunderbird changing the method of authentication to OAuth&nbsp;2.0 will cause problems if you have cookies disabled in Thunderbird, because cookies must be enabled for OAuth&nbsp;2.0 authentication flow to work properly. Without cookies to store data between page updates, the authentication flow cannot successfully complete the web pages served by Google.
</p><p>To avoid or correct the problem, do one of the following:
</p>
<ul><li> Ensure that <strong>Accept cookies from sites</strong> is enabled at <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Preferences</span> &gt; type <strong>cookies</strong> into the search field. You can disable cookies after the OAuth process is completed, and receiving and sending mail will work with cookies disabled. But when the OAuth token for Gmail access expires at some date in the future, the OAuth process will be needed again, which will require cookies to be enabled.
</li><li> Create an exception with cookies disabled at <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Preferences</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Privacy &amp; Security</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Web Content</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Accept cookies from sites</span> (with <span class="menu">Accept</span> unchecked), click <span class="menu">Exceptions</span> and enter an address of <strong><a href="https://accounts.google.com">https://accounts.google.com</a></strong>. Pick <span class="menu">Allow</span>, then <span class="menu">Save Changes</span>.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "241666", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 14, 2022, 4:10:22 AM", "datetime": "2022-04-14T04:10:22-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "YFdyh000", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/yfdyh000/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "oAuth to OAuth", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 29, 2022, 8:29:18 AM", "datetime": "2022-04-29T08:29:18-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "wsmwk", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:04:35+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (243039,'en-US','automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20','Automatic Conversion of Google mail accounts to OAuth 2.0 Authentication','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20/revision/243039',241666,'2022-04-29T08:35:59-07:00','Wayne Mery','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/wsmwk/','greater clarity?',1,'2022-04-29T18:33:01-07:00','firefox877',1,0,1,'2022-04-29T18:33:01-07:00','firefox877','approved','Thunderbird 91.8.0, released 5th April 2022, converts Gmail accounts to OAuth 2.0 to help users comply with [https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/6010255 Google''s requirement of OAuth 2.0 for Gmail logins]. These changes are ''''''required'''''' by Google.

If you have cookies disabled in Thunderbird then the OAuth process will fail, because cookies must be enabled for OAuth 2.0 authentication flow to work properly. Without cookies to store data between page updates, the authentication flow cannot successfully complete the web pages served by Google.

To avoid or correct the problem, do one of the following:
* Ensure that ''''''Accept cookies from sites'''''' is enabled at {button ≡} > {menu Preferences} > type ''''''cookies'''''' into the search field. You can disable cookies after the OAuth process is completed, and receiving and sending mail will work with cookies disabled. But when the OAuth token for Gmail access expires at some date in the future, the OAuth process will be needed again, which will require cookies to be enabled.
* Create an exception with cookies disabled at {button ≡} > {menu Preferences} > {menu Privacy & Security} > {menu Web Content} > {menu Accept cookies from sites} (with {menu Accept} unchecked), click {menu Exceptions} and enter an address of ''''''https://accounts.google.com''''''. Pick {menu Allow}, then {menu Save Changes}.

If you still have problems, you will want to use "Get Help" to ask a question in Thunderbird support.','<p>Thunderbird 91.8.0, released 5th April 2022, converts Gmail accounts to OAuth&nbsp;2.0 to help users comply with <a href="https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/6010255">Google''s requirement of OAuth&nbsp;2.0 for Gmail logins</a>. These changes are <strong>required</strong> by Google.
</p><p>If you have cookies disabled in Thunderbird then the OAuth process will fail, because cookies must be enabled for OAuth&nbsp;2.0 authentication flow to work properly. Without cookies to store data between page updates, the authentication flow cannot successfully complete the web pages served by Google.
</p><p>To avoid or correct the problem, do one of the following:
</p>
<ul><li> Ensure that <strong>Accept cookies from sites</strong> is enabled at <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Preferences</span> &gt; type <strong>cookies</strong> into the search field. You can disable cookies after the OAuth process is completed, and receiving and sending mail will work with cookies disabled. But when the OAuth token for Gmail access expires at some date in the future, the OAuth process will be needed again, which will require cookies to be enabled.
</li><li> Create an exception with cookies disabled at <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Preferences</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Privacy &amp; Security</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Web Content</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Accept cookies from sites</span> (with <span class="menu">Accept</span> unchecked), click <span class="menu">Exceptions</span> and enter an address of <strong><a href="https://accounts.google.com">https://accounts.google.com</a></strong>. Pick <span class="menu">Allow</span>, then <span class="menu">Save Changes</span>.
</li></ul>
<p>If you still have problems, you will want to use "Get Help" to ask a question in Thunderbird support.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "243039", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 29, 2022, 8:35:59 AM", "datetime": "2022-04-29T08:35:59-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Wayne Mery", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/wsmwk/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "greater clarity?", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 29, 2022, 6:33:01 PM", "datetime": "2022-04-29T18:33:01-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "firefox877", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Apr 29, 2022, 6:33:01 PM", "datetime": "2022-04-29T18:33:01-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "firefox877", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:04:32+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (243160,'en-US','automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20','Automatic Conversion of Google mail accounts to OAuth 2.0 Authentication','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/automatic-conversion-google-mail-accounts-oauth20/revision/243160',243039,'2022-04-30T19:06:21-07:00','Michele Rodaro','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/michro/','{menu Exceptions}/{menu Allow}/{menu Save Changes} -> {button …}',1,'2022-05-04T05:39:27-07:00','wsmwk',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','Thunderbird 91.8.0, released 5th April 2022, converts Gmail accounts to OAuth 2.0 to help users comply with [https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/6010255 Google''s requirement of OAuth 2.0 for Gmail logins]. These changes are ''''''required'''''' by Google.

If you have cookies disabled in Thunderbird then the OAuth process will fail, because cookies must be enabled for OAuth 2.0 authentication flow to work properly. Without cookies to store data between page updates, the authentication flow cannot successfully complete the web pages served by Google.

To avoid or correct the problem, do one of the following:
* Ensure that ''''''Accept cookies from sites'''''' is enabled at {button ≡} > {menu Preferences} > type ''''''cookies'''''' into the search field. You can disable cookies after the OAuth process is completed, and receiving and sending mail will work with cookies disabled. But when the OAuth token for Gmail access expires at some date in the future, the OAuth process will be needed again, which will require cookies to be enabled.
* Create an exception with cookies disabled at {button ≡} > {menu Preferences} > {menu Privacy & Security} > {menu Web Content} > {menu Accept cookies from sites} (with {menu Accept} unchecked), click {button Exceptions} and enter an address of ''''''https://accounts.google.com''''''. Pick {button Allow}, then {button Save Changes}.

If you still have problems, you will want to use "Get Help" to ask a question in Thunderbird support.','<p>Thunderbird 91.8.0, released 5th April 2022, converts Gmail accounts to OAuth&nbsp;2.0 to help users comply with <a href="https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/6010255">Google''s requirement of OAuth&nbsp;2.0 for Gmail logins</a>. These changes are <strong>required</strong> by Google.
</p><p>If you have cookies disabled in Thunderbird then the OAuth process will fail, because cookies must be enabled for OAuth&nbsp;2.0 authentication flow to work properly. Without cookies to store data between page updates, the authentication flow cannot successfully complete the web pages served by Google.
</p><p>To avoid or correct the problem, do one of the following:
</p>
<ul><li> Ensure that <strong>Accept cookies from sites</strong> is enabled at <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Preferences</span> &gt; type <strong>cookies</strong> into the search field. You can disable cookies after the OAuth process is completed, and receiving and sending mail will work with cookies disabled. But when the OAuth token for Gmail access expires at some date in the future, the OAuth process will be needed again, which will require cookies to be enabled.
</li><li> Create an exception with cookies disabled at <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Preferences</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Privacy &amp; Security</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Web Content</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Accept cookies from sites</span> (with <span class="menu">Accept</span> unchecked), click <span class="button">Exceptions</span> and enter an address of <strong><a href="https://accounts.google.com">https://accounts.google.com</a></strong>. Pick <span class="button">Allow</span>, then <span class="button">Save Changes</span>.
</li></ul>
<p>If you still have problems, you will want to use "Get Help" to ask a question in Thunderbird support.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "243160", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 30, 2022, 7:06:21 PM", "datetime": "2022-04-30T19:06:21-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Michele Rodaro", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/michro/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "{menu Exceptions}/{menu Allow}/{menu Save Changes} -> {button …}", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 4, 2022, 5:39:27 AM", "datetime": "2022-05-04T05:39:27-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "wsmwk", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:04:30+00:00','M');
