If you have cookies disabled in Thunderbird then the OAuth process will fail, because cookies must be accepted for OAuth 2.0 authentication flow to work properly. Without cookies to store data between page updates, the authentication flow cannot successfully complete the web pages served by Google.

To avoid or correct an OAauth failure, ''''''assuming you have non-default setings to reject cookies'''''', do one of the following and then go through the OAuth login process again:
