</li></ol>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</button></h3><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with no accounts, you will see the older, <strong>Set Up Your Existing Email Address</strong> flow:
</p><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span> 
</li><li> Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.. <div class="note">Note: you do not need to enter your password in the <strong>Password</strong> field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div> Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button (not the one labelled <span class="button">Exchange/Office365</span>) in the <strong>Choose your email account type</strong> dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange implementation.<div class="note">Note: The <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div>
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-23-12-9340ff.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "303317", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 25, 2025, 9:43:48 PM", "datetime": "2025-08-25T21:43:48.429850-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "clarified that MS provides the OAuth panel ; needs review by Wayne, do not localize please. For discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/85 please", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 25, 2025, 9:47:05 PM", "datetime": "2025-08-25T21:47:05.921898-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:26:42+00:00','MT');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (303318,'en-US','thunderbird-and-exchange','Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange/revision/303318',303317,'2025-08-25T21:51:46.019763-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','add step 2: send and receive emails and link to relevant article ; needs review by Wayne, do not localize please. For discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/85 please',1,'2025-08-25T21:53:59.455684-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','{warning}Warning: The current built-in code for Exchange in Thunderbird is limited to email. Other features (calendar, address book) are planned to follow, but are not available yet. We recommend using Thunderbird 142 or newer for for a more polished, stable experience, Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full details.{/warning}
__TOC__
==1. Configure your Exchange account==
===Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird ''''''Account Hub'''''' flow:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email} 
# Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account. {note}Note: you do not need to enter your password in the ''''''Password'''''' field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note} Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#;[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11]] 
# Click the {button Exchange} button (not the one labelled {button Exchange  REQUIRES ADD-ON}) in the ''''''Choose your email account type'''''' dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.{note}Note: The {button Exchange} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
#;[[Image:tb142-beta-exchange-support-button]] 
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
[[UI:details_start]]
===Thunderbird profile with no accounts===
If you have a [[Profiles - Where Thunderbird stores your messages and other user data|Thunderbird profile]] with no accounts, you will see the older, ''''''Set Up Your Existing Email Address'''''' flow:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button New Account} > {menu Email} 
# Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication two factor authentication code] for your Exchange email account.. {note}Note: you do not need to enter your password in the ''''''Password'''''' field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.{/note} Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
#;[[Image:tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11]] 
# Click the {button Exchange Web Services} button (not the one labelled {button Exchange/Office365}) in the ''''''Choose your email account type'''''' dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange implementation.{note}Note: The {button Exchange Web Services} button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.{/note}
#;[[Image:tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button]] 
# Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
[[UI:details_end]]
==2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account==
Once you have configured your Exchange Account, you can use it to [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|send and receive emails]] just like an IMAP or POP account.','<div class="warning">Warning: The current built-in code for Exchange in Thunderbird is limited to email. Other features (calendar, address book) are planned to follow, but are not available yet. We recommend using Thunderbird 142 or newer for for a more polished, stable experience, Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full details.</div>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_1-configure-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">1. Configure your Exchange account</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_2-send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</span></a></li></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_1-configure-your-exchange-account">1. Configure your Exchange account</h2>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profiles-with-1-or-more-accounts">Thunderbird profiles with 1 or more accounts</h3>
<p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with one or more accounts, you will see the new Thunderbird <strong>Account Hub</strong> flow:
</p>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span> 
</li><li> Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account. <div class="note">Note: you do not need to enter your password in the <strong>Password</strong> field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div> Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Exchange</span> button (not the one labelled <span class="button">Exchange  REQUIRES ADD-ON</span>) in the <strong>Choose your email account type</strong> dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange code.<div class="note">Note: The <span class="button">Exchange</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div>
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-beta-exchange-support-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-03-20-2802fd.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h3 id="w_thunderbird-profile-with-no-accounts" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird profile with no accounts</button></h3><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>If you have a <a href="/en-US/kb/profiles-where-thunderbird-stores-user-data">Thunderbird profile</a> with no accounts, you will see the older, <strong>Set Up Your Existing Email Address</strong> flow:
</p><ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">New Account</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Email</span> 
</li><li> Follow the flow by entering your name, email address, and if required, your <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-factor_authentication">two factor authentication code</a> for your Exchange email account.. <div class="note">Note: you do not need to enter your password in the <strong>Password</strong> field of the first dialogue. You will enter your password in a separate, branded panel provided by Microsoft (not Mozilla) as part of their OAuth implementation.</div> Here is a screenshot of that panel provided by Microsoft:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb-141-oauth-microsoft-enter-password-win11" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-25-21-26-20-034f89.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button (not the one labelled <span class="button">Exchange/Office365</span>) in the <strong>Choose your email account type</strong> dialogue to use Thunderbird''s built-in Exchange implementation.<div class="note">Note: The <span class="button">Exchange Web Services</span> button only appears if the email you entered is an Exchange account.</div>
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-beta-old-pre-account-hub-flow-exchange-webservices-button" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-21-23-12-9340ff.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li><li> Follow the prompts to finish adding your Exchange account.
</li></ol><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_2-send-and-receive-emails-with-your-exchange-account">2. Send and receive emails with your Exchange Account</h2>
<p>Once you have configured your Exchange Account, you can use it to <a href="/en-US/kb/sending-and-receiving-messages-thunderbird">send and receive emails</a> just like an IMAP or POP account.
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "303318", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 25, 2025, 9:51:46 PM", "datetime": "2025-08-25T21:51:46.019763-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add step 2: send and receive emails and link to relevant article ; needs review by Wayne, do not localize please. For discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/85 please", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 25, 2025, 9:53:59 PM", "datetime": "2025-08-25T21:53:59.455684-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:26:39+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (303319,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/303319',302707,'2025-08-25T21:56:25.620453-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','link to Thunderbird and Exchange WIP, do not localize or approve please :-) For discussion please comment in: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/97',1,'2025-08-25T21:57:12.715538-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,1,'2025-08-25T21:57:12.715538-07:00','rtanglao','approved','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 142=
==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key control} click on macOS)  on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click on the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order]] 
==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]]
==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.
==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}.  Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.
==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).

This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].
== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=

==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]

==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].

==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.

==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub''''''.

==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.

==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
<p></p><p>This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release">Thunderbird Release for Desktop</a>. For full details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-142"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 142</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Reset manual folder sorting order</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Add a visual signature to a PDF</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release"><span class="tocnumber">1.3</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_more-stable-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">1.4</span> <span class="toctext">More stable Exchange support</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-141"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 141</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Archive action added to new email notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_better-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Better Exchange support</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_dark-message-mode"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Dark Message Mode</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings"><span class="tocnumber">3.2</span> <span class="toctext">New Appearance Panel in Settings</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_native-os-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">3.3</span> <span class="toctext">Native OS Notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_redesigned-account-hub"><span class="tocnumber">3.4</span> <span class="toctext">Redesigned Account hub</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manual-folder-sorting"><span class="tocnumber">3.5</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Folder Sorting</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users"><span class="tocnumber">3.6</span> <span class="toctext">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_export-for-mobile"><span class="tocnumber">3.7</span> <span class="toctext">Export for Mobile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">3.8</span> <span class="toctext">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">4.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">4.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">4.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">4.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-142">Thunderbird 142</h1>
<h2 id="w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order">Reset manual folder sorting order</h2>
<ol><li> Right click (<span class="key">control</span> click on macOS)  on the account row, e.g. <strong><a href="mailto:nemo@thunderbird.net">nemo@thunderbird.net</a></strong> in the <strong>Folder Pane</strong> (more details: <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-main-window-supernova">Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)</a> and then:
</li><li> Click on the menu item <span class="menu">Reset Folder Order</span> to clear any previously defined manual sorting. <strong>NOTE</strong>: This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-reset-folder-order" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-00-23-24-8d62b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf">Add a visual signature to a PDF</h2>
<p>Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: <a href="/en-US/kb/view-pdf-files-firefox-or-choose-another-viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf">View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer</a>
</p>
<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</h2>
<p>See the 141 section for more details.
</p>
<h2 id="w_more-stable-exchange-support">More stable Exchange support</h2>
<p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange">Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)</a> and our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-141">Thunderbird 141</h1>
<h2 id="w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Archive action added to new email notifications</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><li> You can now <span class="button">Archive</span> email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to <span class="button">Mark as Read</span>, <span class="button">Delete</span>, <span class="button">Mark as Starred</span> and <span class="button">Mark as Spam</span>.  Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird">New email notifications in Thunderbird</a> for further information.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_better-exchange-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Better Exchange support</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><p>Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
</p><p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><p>If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.
</p><p>More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in <a href="/en-US/kb/introduction-to-e2e-encryption">Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird</a> and <a href="/en-US/kb/openpgp-thunderbird-howto-and-faq">OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ</a>.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true">This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511">bug 1979511</a>.
</p></section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Dark Message Mode</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true"><p>Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl></div>


<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><p>Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-139" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 139</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-138" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 138</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-137" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 137</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-136" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 136</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "303319", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 25, 2025, 9:56:25 PM", "datetime": "2025-08-25T21:56:25.620453-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "link to Thunderbird and Exchange WIP, do not localize or approve please :-) For discussion please comment in: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/97", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 25, 2025, 9:57:12 PM", "datetime": "2025-08-25T21:57:12.715538-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Aug 25, 2025, 9:57:12 PM", "datetime": "2025-08-25T21:57:12.715538-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:26:37+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (303575,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/303575',303319,'2025-08-27T05:48:13.157253-07:00','Mark Heijl','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/markh2/','minor edits',1,'2025-08-27T08:45:37.613062-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 142=
==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key Control}+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order]]

==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]].

==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.

==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}. Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.

==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).

This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].

== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=

==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]

==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].

==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.

==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub''''''.

==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.

==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
<p></p><p>This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release">Thunderbird Release for Desktop</a>. For full details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-142"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 142</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Reset manual folder sorting order</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Add a visual signature to a PDF</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release"><span class="tocnumber">1.3</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_more-stable-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">1.4</span> <span class="toctext">More stable Exchange support</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-141"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 141</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Archive action added to new email notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_better-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Better Exchange support</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_dark-message-mode"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Dark Message Mode</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings"><span class="tocnumber">3.2</span> <span class="toctext">New Appearance Panel in Settings</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_native-os-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">3.3</span> <span class="toctext">Native OS Notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_redesigned-account-hub"><span class="tocnumber">3.4</span> <span class="toctext">Redesigned Account hub</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manual-folder-sorting"><span class="tocnumber">3.5</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Folder Sorting</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users"><span class="tocnumber">3.6</span> <span class="toctext">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_export-for-mobile"><span class="tocnumber">3.7</span> <span class="toctext">Export for Mobile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">3.8</span> <span class="toctext">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">4.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">4.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">4.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">4.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-142">Thunderbird 142</h1>
<h2 id="w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order">Reset manual folder sorting order</h2>
<ol><li> Right click (<span class="key">Control</span>+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. <strong><a href="mailto:nemo@thunderbird.net">nemo@thunderbird.net</a></strong> in the <strong>Folder Pane</strong> (more details: <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-main-window-supernova">Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)</a> and then:
</li><li> Click the menu item <span class="menu">Reset Folder Order</span> to clear any previously defined manual sorting. <strong>NOTE</strong>: This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-reset-folder-order" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-00-23-24-8d62b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf">Add a visual signature to a PDF</h2>
<p>Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: <a href="/en-US/kb/view-pdf-files-firefox-or-choose-another-viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf">View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</h2>
<p>See the 141 section for more details.
</p>
<h2 id="w_more-stable-exchange-support">More stable Exchange support</h2>
<p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange">Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)</a> and our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p><p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-141">Thunderbird 141</h1>
<h2 id="w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Archive action added to new email notifications</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><li> You can now <span class="button">Archive</span> email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to <span class="button">Mark as Read</span>, <span class="button">Delete</span>, <span class="button">Mark as Starred</span> and <span class="button">Mark as Spam</span>. Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird">New email notifications in Thunderbird</a> for further information.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_better-exchange-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Better Exchange support</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><p>Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
</p><p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><p>If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.
</p><p>More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in <a href="/en-US/kb/introduction-to-e2e-encryption">Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird</a> and <a href="/en-US/kb/openpgp-thunderbird-howto-and-faq">OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ</a>.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true">This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511">bug 1979511</a>.
</p></section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Dark Message Mode</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true"><p>Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl></div>


<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><p>Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-139" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 139</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-138" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 138</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-137" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 137</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-136" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 136</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "303575", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 27, 2025, 5:48:13 AM", "datetime": "2025-08-27T05:48:13.157253-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Mark Heijl", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/markh2/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "minor edits", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Aug 27, 2025, 8:45:37 AM", "datetime": "2025-08-27T08:45:37.613062-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:12:44+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (303620,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/303620',303575,'2025-08-27T10:57:54.143916-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','hotmail account issue with account hub in 142 for discussion please: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/102',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 142=
==Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues when adding Hotmail accounts==
If you cannot add a ''''''''Hotmail'''''' or outlook.com account here''s how to switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix the problem:
* Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings} > Untick ''''''Create accounts in the new Account Hub'''''':
*;[[Image:tb142-disable-account-hub]] 
==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key Control}+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order]]

==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]].

==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.

==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}. Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.

==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).

This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].

== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=

==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]

==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].

==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.

==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub''''''.

==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.

==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
<p></p><p>This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release">Thunderbird Release for Desktop</a>. For full details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-142"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 142</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_switch-to-the-old-account-setup-flow-to-fix-issues-when-adding-hotmail-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues when adding Hotmail accounts</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Reset manual folder sorting order</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf"><span class="tocnumber">1.3</span> <span class="toctext">Add a visual signature to a PDF</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release"><span class="tocnumber">1.4</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_more-stable-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">1.5</span> <span class="toctext">More stable Exchange support</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-141"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 141</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Archive action added to new email notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_better-exchange-support"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Better Exchange support</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_dark-message-mode"><span class="tocnumber">3.1</span> <span class="toctext">Dark Message Mode</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings"><span class="tocnumber">3.2</span> <span class="toctext">New Appearance Panel in Settings</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_native-os-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">3.3</span> <span class="toctext">Native OS Notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_redesigned-account-hub"><span class="tocnumber">3.4</span> <span class="toctext">Redesigned Account hub</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manual-folder-sorting"><span class="tocnumber">3.5</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Folder Sorting</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users"><span class="tocnumber">3.6</span> <span class="toctext">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_export-for-mobile"><span class="tocnumber">3.7</span> <span class="toctext">Export for Mobile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">3.8</span> <span class="toctext">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">4.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">4.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">4.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">4.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-142">Thunderbird 142</h1>
<h2 id="w_switch-to-the-old-account-setup-flow-to-fix-issues-when-adding-hotmail-accounts">Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues when adding Hotmail accounts</h2>
<p>If you cannot add a ''<strong>Hotmail</strong> or <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> account here''s how to switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix the problem:
</p>
<ul><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; Untick <strong>Create accounts in the new Account Hub</strong>:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-disable-account-hub" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-27-10-54-39-2636ed.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""> 
</dt></dl>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_reset-manual-folder-sorting-order">Reset manual folder sorting order</h2>
<ol><li> Right click (<span class="key">Control</span>+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. <strong><a href="mailto:nemo@thunderbird.net">nemo@thunderbird.net</a></strong> in the <strong>Folder Pane</strong> (more details: <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-main-window-supernova">Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)</a> and then:
</li><li> Click the menu item <span class="menu">Reset Folder Order</span> to clear any previously defined manual sorting. <strong>NOTE</strong>: This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
<dl><dt><img alt="tb142-reset-folder-order" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-08-19-00-23-24-8d62b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_add-a-visual-signature-to-a-pdf">Add a visual signature to a PDF</h2>
<p>Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: <a href="/en-US/kb/view-pdf-files-firefox-or-choose-another-viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf">View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</h2>
<p>See the 141 section for more details.
</p>
<h2 id="w_more-stable-exchange-support">More stable Exchange support</h2>
<p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-exchange">Thunderbird and Microsoft protocols (Exchange and Graph)</a> and our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p><p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-141">Thunderbird 141</h1>
<h2 id="w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Archive action added to new email notifications</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><li> You can now <span class="button">Archive</span> email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to <span class="button">Mark as Read</span>, <span class="button">Delete</span>, <span class="button">Mark as Starred</span> and <span class="button">Mark as Spam</span>. Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird">New email notifications in Thunderbird</a> for further information.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_better-exchange-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Better Exchange support</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><p>Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
</p><p>This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><p>If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.
</p><p>More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in <a href="/en-US/kb/introduction-to-e2e-encryption">Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird</a> and <a href="/en-US/kb/openpgp-thunderbird-howto-and-faq">OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ</a>.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true">This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511">bug 1979511</a>.
</p></section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Dark Message Mode</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true"><p>Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl></div>


<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><p>Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
</p><p>We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-139" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 139</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-138" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 138</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-137" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 137</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-136" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 136</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "303620", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Aug 27, 2025, 10:57:54 AM", "datetime": "2025-08-27T10:57:54.143916-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "hotmail account issue with account hub in 142 for discussion please: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/102", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:26:35+00:00','');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (303621,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/303621',303620,'2025-08-27T10:59:32.332429-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','updated title WIP, do not localize or approve please :-) For discussion please comment in: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/102',1,'2025-08-27T11:00:05.241011-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__

=Thunderbird 142=
==Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues when adding Hotmail and outlook.com accounts==
If you cannot add a ''''''''Hotmail'''''' or outlook.com account here''s how to switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix the problem:
* Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings} > Untick ''''''Create accounts in the new Account Hub'''''':
*;[[Image:tb142-disable-account-hub]] 
==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key Control}+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder.
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order]]

==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]].

==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.

==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}. Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.

==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).

This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].

== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=

==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]

==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].

==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.

==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub''''''.

==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.

==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
