<h1 id="w_how-to-import-from-k-9-or-other-thunderbird-for-android-apps">How To Import from K-9 or other Thunderbird for Android apps</h1>
<div class="warning">Importing from K-9 Mail requires K-9 Mail 8.0 or later.</div>
<p>Open Thunderbird for Android on your phone or tablet and follow the steps below.
</p>
<h2 id="w_first-run_2">First run</h2>
<p>After you install Thunderbird for Android and run it for the first time, here''s how to import settings from <strong>K-9</strong> or Thunderbird from Android:
</p>
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">Get started</span> on the initial screen.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Import your account settings now</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">Import from app</span>.
</li><li> Tap the email app you wish to import your email account settings from (either <strong>K-9 Mail</strong> or another release of Thunderbird for Android, for example Beta).
</li><li> Ensure the email accounts you want to import are all ticked. Tap <span class="button">Import</span>.
</li><li> If your account uses <a href="https://wikipedia.org/wiki/OAuth">OAuth</a> instead of password authentication or you have chosen not to import your passwords, you will be prompted for your passwords. Follow the prompts to complete your import.
</li></ol>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_subsequent-runs_2" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Subsequent runs</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><p>Once you have set up an email account, the next time you import email settings, the process will be slightly different:
</p><ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the <em>gear</em> icon: <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Import settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">Import from app</span>.
</li><li> Tap the email app you wish to import your email account settings from (either <strong>K-9 Mail</strong> or another release of Thunderbird for Android, for example Beta).
</li><li> Ensure the email accounts you want to import are all ticked. Tap <span class="button">Import</span>.
</li><li> If your account uses <a href="https://wikipedia.org/wiki/OAuth">OAuth</a> instead of password authentication or you have chosen not to import your passwords, you will be prompted for your passwords. Follow the prompts to complete your import.
</li></ol><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p><p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_how-to-import-email-account-settings-using-a-settings-file-from-thunderbird-or-k-9">How To Import email account settings using a settings file from Thunderbird or K-9</h1>
<div class="warning"> It is not possible to import a settings file from apps other than Thunderbird for Android or <em>K-9</em>.</div>
<h2 id="w_1-export-thunderbird-or-k-9-settings-to-a-file" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">1. Export Thunderbird or K-9 settings to a file</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><p>Open the app, K-9 or Thunderbird for Android, whose settings you wish to export.
</p><ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the <em>gear</em> icon: <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Export settings</span>.
</li><li> Tick the Email accounts you wish to export to Thunderbird for Android.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Export</span>.
</li><li> Change the directory and the filename as you see fit and tap <span class="button">Save</span>. Take note of the filename and directory, for example a directory in <em>Google Drive</em>, the <strong>Downloads</strong> directory, etc. You will need the filename and directory in order to import the settings in <em>Step 2</em>.
</li></ol></div>


<h2 id="w_2-import-the-exported-settings-file-into-thunderbird-for-android" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">2. Import the exported settings file into Thunderbird for Android</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><p>Open Thunderbird for Android on your phone or tablet and follow the steps below.
</p><h3 id="w_first-run_3">First run</h3><p>Here''s how to import settings from the file you created in <em>Step 1</em>:
</p><ol><li> Tap <span class="button">Get started</span> on the initial screen.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Import your account settings now</span> &gt; <span class="button">Select file</span>. Select the file you saved from <em>Step 1.</em>
</li><li> Ensure the email accounts you want to import are all ticked. Tap <span class="button">Import</span>.
</li><li> You will be prompted for your passwords. Follow the prompts to complete your import.
</li></ol><h3 id="w_subsequent-runs_3">Subsequent runs</h3><p>Once you have set up an email account, the next time you import email settings, the process will be slightly different:
</p><ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the <em>gear</em> icon: <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">Import settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">Select file</span>. Select the file you saved from the <em>Step 1.</em>
</li><li> Ensure the email accounts you want to import are all ticked. Tap <span class="button">Import</span>.
</li><li> You will be prompted for your passwords. Follow the prompts to complete your import.
</li></ol><p></p></div>







</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_not-seeing-all-your-email-accounts">Not seeing all your email accounts?</h1>
<p>You will not be able to import some email accounts because they are configured in a way that is not supported by Thunderbird for Android, or because of device limitations. If you have failure that does not match to one of the items below, create a qrexport log file using <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/MailNews:Logging">logging instructions</a>, and file a bug report.
</p>
<h2 id="w_not-supported">Not supported</h2>
<ul><li> Some Android devices with front facing cameras
</li><li>Email accounts with the following configurations are NOT supported (see <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919786">Bug 1919786</a> for full details):
</li><li> <a href="https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Generic_Security_Services_Application_Program_Interface">GSSAPI</a>.
</li><li> <a href="https://wikipedia.org/wiki/NTLM">NTLM</a>.
</li><li> <em>TlsCertificate</em>.
</li><li> <em>TryStartTls</em>. See <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1868517">Bug 1868517</a>.
</li><li> Non-ASCII email addresses are not supported.
</li><li> Non SMTP outgoing servers are not supported.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_multiple-outgoing-servers-are-not-exported">Multiple outgoing servers are not exported</h2>
<ul><li> Only the SMTP server for the default identity is exported for those email accounts with multiple outgoing servers.
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "313255", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Nov 10, 2025, 8:20:20 PM", "datetime": "2025-11-10T20:20:20.839453-08:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Wayne Mery", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/wsmwk/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add instructions for creating qrexport log file", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Jun 3, 2026, 9:37:44 PM", "datetime": "2026-06-03T21:37:44.356383-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:18:33+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (313621,'en-US','new-thunderbird-desktop','New in Thunderbird Desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-desktop/revision/313621',308822,'2025-11-12T22:49:32.192905-08:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP do not approve, discussion in github please at: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/108#issuecomment-3525817994',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','[[T:TBMore]]

This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in [[Thunderbird Release|Thunderbird Release for Desktop]]. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__
=Thunderbird 145=
* Thunderbird now supports DNS over HTTPS.
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 144=
==Exchange enhancements and bug fixes==
* Another bug fix release.
* Various Exchange Support fixes. This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions. We are planning a promotional splash in one of the next few releases. Getting closer!
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 143=
==Exchange Support enhancements and bug fixes==
* Bug fixes.
* Various Exchange Support fixes. This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email. Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 142=
==Switch to the old Account Setup flow to fix issues with Hotmail and outlook.com accounts==
If you see: ''''''Exchange auth error'''''' or ''''''Authentication failed. Please check the username and password'''''' when adding a ''''''Hotmail'''''' or ''''''outlook.com'''''' account, here''s how to switch to the old ''''''Account Setup'''''' flow to fix the problem:
* Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings} > {menu General} and untick ''''''Create accounts in the new Account Hub'''''':
*;[[Image:tb142-disable-account-hub|width=350]]
* Please try adding the email account again. If you still have issues, please [https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form file a support request on SUMO].
This will be fixed in a future Thunderbird release.
==Reset manual folder sorting order==
# Right click ({key Control}+click on macOS) on the account row, e.g. ''''''nemo@thunderbird.net'''''' in the ''''''Folder Pane'''''' (more details: [[Getting Started with the Thunderbird main window (Supernova and newer)]] and then:
# Click the menu item {menu Reset Folder Order} to clear any previously defined manual sorting. ''''''NOTE'''''': This feature doesn’t restore the original location of a folder that was moved inside another parent folder which will be fixed in a future release. You can follow along in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979880 bug 1979880].
#;[[Image:tb142-reset-folder-order|width=350]]
==Add a visual signature to a PDF==
Just like Firefox, you can now insert your signature into a PDF by by typing, drawing or adding an image. Please refer to the Firefox article for full details: [[View and edit PDF files using Firefox’s built-in viewer#w_add-a-signature-to-a-pdf]].
==Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release==
See the 141 section for more details.
==More stable Exchange support==
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to [[Thunderbird and Exchange]] and our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 141=
==Archive action added to new email notifications ==
* You can now {button Archive} email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to {button Mark as Read}, {button Delete}, {button Mark as Starred} and {button Mark as Spam}. Please see [[New email notifications in Thunderbird]] for further information.

==Better Exchange support==
Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).

This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

== 31 day warning for PGP Key expiry ==
If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.

More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in [[Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird]] and [[OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ]].

== Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release ==
This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in [https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511 bug 1979511].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
=Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse=
==Dark Message Mode==
Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
;[[Image:tb140-dark-mode-toggle]]

==New Appearance Panel in Settings==
The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to [[Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings]].

==Native OS Notifications==
Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.

==Redesigned Account hub==
The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu General} > search for ''''''Account hub'''''' (not enabled in ESR, we recommend the latest monthly release for the best experience).

==Manual Folder Sorting==
Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.

==Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users==
Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.

We recommend you try this in a test [[Use multiple profiles in Thunderbird|Thunderbird profile]] in [[Thunderbird Beta]] (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our [https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page] for full instructions.

==Export for Mobile==
Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to [[Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android]].

==Horizontal Scroll for Table View==
Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
[[UI:details_end]]
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 139==
* You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 138==
* Dark mode and high contrast mode improvements.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 137==
* Fixed Two-factor authentication via text or email for Office 365 using Oauth2.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 136==
* New Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {button Settings} > {menu Appearance}.
[[UI:details_end]]','<p></p><div class="warning">More for Thunderbird: <strong>o</strong> Vote on &amp; suggest improvements at <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">Connect</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://www.thunderbird.net/participate/">Participate/Contribute</a> <strong>o</strong> <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird/form">Get Support</a></div>
