<h1 id="w_thunderbird-141">Thunderbird 141</h1>
<h2 id="w_archive-action-added-to-new-email-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Archive action added to new email notifications</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true"><li> You can now <span class="button">Archive</span> email from your operating system''s new email native notifications (in addition to <span class="button">Mark as Read</span>, <span class="button">Delete</span>, <span class="button">Mark as Starred</span> and <span class="button">Mark as Spam</span>. Please see <a href="/en-US/kb/new-email-notifications-thunderbird">New email notifications in Thunderbird</a> for further information.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_better-exchange-support" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Better Exchange support</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true">Now, anyone can try the Exchange support in Thunderbird. For most, we recommend waiting for a future release which will be more stable and have additional features like on premise OAuth authentication(password authentication for on premise is supported in this release).
This release''s implementation is still limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p>
<h2 id="w_31-day-warning-for-pgp-key-expiry" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">31 day warning for PGP Key expiry</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><p>If your PGP key expires in the next 31 days, you will receive a warning when you are composing an email. For extra security, you can choose to let it expire or you can extend your key''s certificate.
</p><p>More info on PGP encrypted email can be found in <a href="/en-US/kb/introduction-to-e2e-encryption">Introduction to End-to-end encryption in Thunderbird</a> and <a href="/en-US/kb/openpgp-thunderbird-howto-and-faq">OpenPGP in Thunderbird - HOWTO and FAQ</a>.
</p></div>

<h2 id="w_folders-erroneously-renamed-to-junk-will-be-renamed-back-to-spam-and-bulk-in-a-post-142-release_2" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-expanded="false">Folders erroneously renamed to ''Junk'' will be renamed back to ''Spam'' and ''Bulk'' in a post 142 release</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-10" aria-hidden="true">This is primarily a problem in the English language locales. It was discovered a few days after the release of 141. You can follow the progress of the fix in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979511">bug 1979511</a>.
</p></section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-140-esr-140-eclipse">Thunderbird 140 / ESR 140 Eclipse</h1>
<h2 id="w_dark-message-mode" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-expanded="false">Dark Message Mode</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-11" aria-hidden="true"><p>Thunderbird now automatically displays your messages in dark mode when enabled in your operating system settings. If there are display issues with a message in dark mode, you can disable dark mode for that message by sliding the toggle to the right to disable dark message mode.
</p><dl><dt><img alt="tb140-dark-mode-toggle" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2025-06-29-22-50-16-bf91b7.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl></div>


<h2 id="w_new-appearance-panel-in-settings" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-expanded="false">New Appearance Panel in Settings</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-12" aria-hidden="true">The new Appearance panel, Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>, allows you to toggle your message list layout between Card and Table view, adjust your Cards view, and set your default folder sorting order and threading options. For more details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/appearance-panel-layout-message-list-card-view-tab">Appearance Panel - Layout, Message List, Card View, Table View, Sorting and Threading settings</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_native-os-notifications" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-expanded="false">Native OS Notifications</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-13" aria-hidden="true">Thunderbird now uses your operating system''s built-in notifications, whether you’re on Windows, Linux or Mac. You can now quickly delete, archive, or use customizable actions directly from your notifications.
</p>
<h2 id="w_redesigned-account-hub" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-expanded="false">Redesigned Account hub</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-14" aria-hidden="true">The newly redesigned Account hub makes it easier to add an account. Connect all of your emails, address books and calendars in a few easy steps. The Account hub is currently not enabled for your first account (you will see it when you add a second account). It is also not enabled by default for your address book. You can change the defaults in your Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="button">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; search for <strong>Account hub</strong> (not enabled in ESR, we recommend the latest monthly release for the best experience).
</p>
<h2 id="w_manual-folder-sorting" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-expanded="false">Manual Folder Sorting</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-15" aria-hidden="true">Drag and drop your folders to get the order you want.
</p>
<h2 id="w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-expanded="false">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-16" aria-hidden="true">Preliminary Microsoft Exchange support is available for you to try. Our current, initial implementation of Exchange is limited to email – account setup, folder management and writing, receiving and reading email.
We recommend you try this in a test <a href="/en-US/kb/using-multiple-profiles">Thunderbird profile</a> in <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-beta">Thunderbird Beta</a> (please ensure you back up your profile before starting). Please refer to our <a href="https://wiki.mozilla.org/Thunderbird:Exchange">Thunderbird:Exchange wiki page</a> for full instructions.
</p>
<h2 id="w_export-for-mobile" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-expanded="false">Export for Mobile</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-17" aria-hidden="true">Generate a QR code to quickly transfer your account settings and credentials to your Thunderbird for Android app. Please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-android-import">Import settings and data into Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-18" aria-expanded="false">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</button></h2>
<p class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-18" aria-hidden="true">Table view now supports horizontal scrolling. This allows you to view wide messages – for example, data in a table with many columns.
</p></section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-139" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-19" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 139</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-19" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now manually sort folders by dragging and dropping them in the folder pane.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
