 Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">10</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">10.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">10.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">10.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">10.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-148">Thunderbird 148</h1>
<ul><li> <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NTLM">NTLM authentication</a> is now supported.
</li><li> Thunderbird switched to a more secure authorization protocol called <strong>PKCE</strong> for Yahoo, AT&amp;T and AOL accounts. This switch adds support for Yahoo/AOL calendars and adddress books. Full details: <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-yahoo">OAuth2 Authentication for Yahoo, AOL and ATT</a>
</li><li> Known issue: Dark mode link colors might be hard to read. Workaround: switch to a different theme. A fix has been developed for a future release; you can follow along in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2018015">bug 2018015</a>.
</li></ul>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-147">Thunderbird 147</h1>
