This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in Thunderbird for Android. For full details, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-release-notes-whats-new-and-known-issu">Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues</a>.
<p></p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_thunderbird-18"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 18</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-17"><span class="tocnumber">2.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 17</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-16"><span class="tocnumber">2.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 16</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-15"><span class="tocnumber">2.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 15</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-14"><span class="tocnumber">2.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 14</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-13"><span class="tocnumber">2.5</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 13</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-12"><span class="tocnumber">2.6</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 12</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-11"><span class="tocnumber">2.7</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 11</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-10"><span class="tocnumber">2.8</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 10</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-9"><span class="tocnumber">2.9</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 9</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-8"><span class="tocnumber">2.10</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 8</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-18">Thunderbird 18</h2>
<ul><li> PNG custom avatars are now supported (as well as JPEGs and stylized letter monograms as per the Thunderbird 17 section).
</li><li> There is a new setting to display times in ISO 8601 format <em>(YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm)</em> in the message list.
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> &gt; tap the gear icon:<span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">General settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Display</span> &gt; under <strong>Messsage lists</strong>, tap <span class="menu">Date/Time Format</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">ISO</span>.
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
<h1 id="w_older-releases">Older Releases</h1>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-17" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 17</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><li> Custom avatars for email accounts are now available. JPEGs only for now. PNGs will be supported in a future release. Upload yours as follows: 
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the gear icon:<span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap your email account that you want to customize e.g. <em><a href="mailto:nemo@thunderbird.net">nemo@thunderbird.net</a></em> &gt; tap <span class="menu">General settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Image</span> to upload your custom JPEG. You can also use a stylized letter monogram by tapping <span class="menu">Monogram</span> or pick one of the built-in icons by tapping <span class="menu">Icon</span>.
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-16" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 16</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><li> The SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> have been fixed in <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312">#10312</a>.
</li><li> The following issue was fixed in TB 16.1 which was released one week after Thunderbird 16.0. <del>Known Issue: Deleted/read messages in your unified inbox may not update until you manually refresh. We hope to have a fix soon. you can can follow along on issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10243">#10243</a></del>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-15" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 15</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-2" aria-hidden="true"><li> There are further SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> and the team is testing a fix. You can follow along on issue <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312">#10312</a>. It looks like this will fixed in the next release, TB 16.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-14" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 14</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-3" aria-hidden="true"><li> SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a> have been fixed.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-13" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 13</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-4" aria-hidden="true"><li> The notification in status bar re-appearing multiple times a day issue (github issue <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/8049">#8049</a>) has been fixed.
</li><li> Special folders (Trash, Sent, Drafts, Archives, etc) not appearing after updating from TB11 to TB12 (github issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9771">#9771</a>) was fixed.
</li><li> The bug with outgoing email not working for certain educational and enterprise accounts is scheduled to be fixed in the next release, Thunderbird 14 for Android (github issue: <a href="https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9160">#9160</a>).
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-12" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 12</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true"><li> If you use a password manager, Android will now use it to automatically fill in your password when you add a new account.
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-11" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 11</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Mail folders are easier to navigate.
</li><li> Algorithmic darkening makes reading emails easier in dark mode.
</li><li> Thunderbird 11.1&nbsp;: Selected/read/unread message states are now easier to distinguish visually.
</li><li> You can still see font settings if you search for <strong>font</strong> in Settings. This will be removed in a future Thunderbird release. Please use the Android operating system font size settings instead.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-10" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 10</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-7" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> You can now empty your Spam folder by tapping <span class="menu">Empty Spam</span> in the Spam folder''s menu <span class="menu">⋮</span> (also known as the <strong>kebab</strong> menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab).
</li><li> On Android 10 or older, you now have an option to use the system theme.
<ol><li> Tap <span class="button">≡</span> at the top left &gt; tap the gear icon:<span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> at the bottom left.
</li><li> Tap <span class="button">General settings</span> &gt; tap <span class="menu">Display</span> &gt; tap <span class="button">Use system default</span> under <strong>Theme</strong>
</li></ol>
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-9" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 9</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-8" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Initial Android 15 support.
</li><li> Thunderbird attempts to use your email provider''s auto configuration database. If it fails it, it uses Mozilla''s database.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_thunderbird-8" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-expanded="false">Thunderbird 8</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-9" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> Refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android-version-8">New in Thunderbird for Android version 8</a> please.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<p></p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "326868", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 23, 2026, 8:18:34 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-23T20:18:34.082433-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "add \"under Message lists\"", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Apr 23, 2026, 8:19:53 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-23T20:19:53.200727-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:22:21+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (327305,'en-US','thundermail-and-thunderbird-android','Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thundermail-and-thunderbird-android/revision/327305',319788,'2026-04-29T18:36:53.183919-07:00','Wayne Mery','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/wsmwk/','Wayne edit, now over to Roland',1,'2026-05-03T21:21:05.856384-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[Template:TBproEarlyBirdInviteOnly]]
Here’s how to get started with Mozilla’s Thundermail service. 

=Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird for Android=

{note} ''''''NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires Thunderbird for Android version 18 or newer (also K-9). We recommend using the latest monthly release version documented in [[New in Thunderbird for Android]].{/note}
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]} > {menu Add account}.
# Enter your Thundermail email address. For example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
# Click {button Next}.
# The next screen will prompt you to ''''''Please specify the special folders for your account'''''', and offer some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click {button Next}. 
# On the next screen, configure your user name under ''''''Your name'''''' and optionally your signature and {button Next}.
# The next screen has sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click {button Next} .

=Manual settings=

Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your [https://accounts.tb.pro/self-serve/connection-info TB Pro accounts page]. If it doesn’t, please  manually change the receiving email and sending email settings according to the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new.
[[UI:details_start]]

==Receiving Email==
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}
# Under ''''''Accounts'''''', tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
# Tap {menu Fetching mail} > {menu Incoming Server} and set the following values:
*''''''Server:'''''' <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS ''''''Port:'''''' 993
*''''''Authentication:'''''' OAuth 2.0
*''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.

==Sending Email==
# Thunderbird app menu {menu ≡} > Settings gear icon {button [[Image:gear icon]]}
# Under ''''''Accounts'''''', tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
# Tap {menu Sending mail} > {menu Outgoing server} and set the following values:
* ''''''Server Name:'''''' <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> ''''''Connection'''''' ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS ''''''Port:'''''' 465
* ''''''Authentication:'''''' OAuth 2.0
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.

[[UI:details_end]]

=Send and receive email and have some fun!=
* Send and receive email with Thundermail.
* New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out [[Getting started with Thunderbird for Android]].
<!--
* If you have large files, you can send them with FIXME because Send on Mobile needs some polish: add link to Thunderbird Send which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
-->','<p></p><div class="warning">NOTE: Thundermail (formerly known as Thunderbird Pro) is currently in its Early Bird release and available  by invitation only. To learn more and join the waitlist, visit <a href="https://tb.pro/">our website</a>. We’ll be opening Thundermail to the public once the Early Bird release concludes.</div>
Here’s how to get started with Mozilla’s Thundermail service. 
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_configure-thundermail-for-thunderbird-for-android">Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird for Android</h1>
<div class="note"> <strong>NOTE</strong>: Thunderbird Pro requires Thunderbird for Android version 18 or newer (also K-9). We recommend using the latest monthly release version documented in <a href="/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android">New in Thunderbird for Android</a>.</div>
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span> &gt; <span class="menu">Add account</span>.
</li><li> Enter your Thundermail email address. For example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Click <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen will prompt you to <strong>Please specify the special folders for your account</strong>, and offer some suggested settings for your Thunderbird special folders. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span>. 
</li><li> On the next screen, configure your user name under <strong>Your name</strong> and optionally your signature and <span class="button">Next</span>.
</li><li> The next screen has sync and notification options. For most people, the defaults are fine. Configure them to your needs and click <span class="button">Next</span> .
</li></ol>
<h1 id="w_manual-settings">Manual settings</h1>
<p>Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your <a href="https://accounts.tb.pro/self-serve/connection-info">TB Pro accounts page</a>. If it doesn’t, please  manually change the receiving email and sending email settings according to the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: <a href="https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new">https://support.tb.pro/hc/en-us/requests/new</a>.
</p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h2 id="w_receiving-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-expanded="false">Receiving Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-0" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Fetching mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Incoming Server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li><strong>Server:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 993
</li><li><strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li><strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul></div>


<h2 id="w_sending-email" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-expanded="false">Sending Email</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-1" aria-hidden="true"><ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">≡</span> &gt; Settings gear icon <span class="button"><img alt="gear icon" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2014-06-13-01-42-16-c1469d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=""></span>
</li><li> Under <strong>Accounts</strong>, tap on your Thundermail email account. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li><li> Tap <span class="menu">Sending mail</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Outgoing server</span> and set the following values:
</li></ol><ul><li> <strong>Server Name:</strong> <code>mail.thundermail.com</code> <strong>Connection</strong> <strong>Security:</strong> SSL/TLS <strong>Port:</strong> 465
</li><li> <strong>Authentication:</strong> OAuth 2.0
</li><li> <strong>Username:</strong> your full Thundermail email address. For example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>.
</li></ul><p></p></div>


</section>
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_send-and-receive-email-and-have-some-fun">Send and receive email and have some fun!</h1>
<ul><li> Send and receive email with Thundermail.
</li><li> New to Thunderbird for Android? Then check out <a href="/en-US/kb/getting-started-thunderbird-android">Getting started with Thunderbird for Android</a>.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "327305", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Apr 29, 2026, 6:36:53 PM", "datetime": "2026-04-29T18:36:53.183919-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Wayne Mery", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/wsmwk/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Wayne edit, now over to Roland", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "May 3, 2026, 9:21:05 PM", "datetime": "2026-05-03T21:21:05.856384-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:19:15+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (327470,'en-US','thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail','Thunderbird for Desktop and Thundermail','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-desktop-and-thundermail/revision/327470',319677,'2026-05-01T15:21:54.706057-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','WIP, please do not translate. Discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/193',1,'2026-05-01T15:23:39.418091-07:00','rtanglao',1,0,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','[[Template:TBproEarlyBirdInviteOnly]]

__TOC__

=Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop=
{note}''''''NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires latest ESR or the latest monthly release. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird which is documented in: [[New in Thunderbird Desktop]].{/note}
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} >  {menu New Account} > {menu Email}.
# Enter your Thundermail email address and follow the prompts to set up your Thundermail email account.

=Manual settings=

Thunderbird should automatically configure your Thundermail email settings to match your [https://accounts.tb.pro/mail TB Pro Thundermail page]. If it doesn’t, please try manually changing the "Receiving Email" and "Sending Email" settings as per the sections below. If manual setup fails, please create a support ticket using our form at: [https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/ accounts.tb.pro/contact].
[[UI:details_start]]
==Receiving Email==
# Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {menu Account Settings}.
# In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. (For example: [mailto:nemo@thundermail.com nemo@thundermail.com].) Then, click on the chevron “&gt;” to expand the drop down menu. Finally, click on {menu Server Settings} and set the following values:

* ''''''Server Name:'''''' [http://mail.thundermail.com mail.thundermail.com] ''''''Server Port:'''''' 993
* ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS
