=Configure Thundermail for Thunderbird Desktop=
{note}''''''NOTE'''''': Thunderbird Pro requires the latest ESR or the latest monthly release. We recommend the latest monthly release version of Thunderbird which is documented in: [[New in Thunderbird Desktop]].{/note}
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} >  {menu New Account} > {menu Email}.
# Enter your Thundermail email address and follow the prompts to set up your Thundermail email account.

Thunderbird should have automatically added your Thundermail email in [[Configuration Options for Accounts|account settings]], a CalDAV calendar called ''''''Thundermail Calendar'''''' in your Thunderbird calendar [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]] (press {for not mac}{key Alt+3}{/for}{for mac}{key Ctrl+3}{/for}), and a CardDAV address book called ''''''Thundermail Address Book'''''' in your address book [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]] (press {for not mac}{key Alt+2}{/for}{for mac}{key Ctrl+2}{/for}) to check). If any of those are missing, please try changing the settings to those in the manual settings sections below, and please [https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/ create a Thunderbird Pro support ticket] if you have any issues.


=Manual settings=
<!--If Thunderbird failed to automatically add your Thundermail email, calendar or address book, please check the following
* configure your Thundermail email settings to match your [https://accounts.tb.pro/mail TB Pro Thundermail page].
* add a CalDAV calendar called ''''''Thundermail Calendar'''''' in your Thunderbird calendar [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]]. Press {key Alt+3} ({key Ctrl+3} on macOS) to check.
* add a CardDAV address book called ''''''Thundermail Address Book'''''' in your address book [[New in Thunderbird 102#w_take-control-of-your-personal-information-new-spaces-toolbar|space]]. Press {key Alt+2} ({key Ctrl+2} on macOS) to check. -->

If Thunderbird failed to add the expected items or you need to adjust them, please try manually changing the settings by following the instructions in the sections below. If manual setup fails, please [https://accounts.tb.pro/contact/ create a Thunderbird Pro support ticket].

[[UI:details_start]]
==Receiving Email==
# Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {menu Account Settings}.
# In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example: ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''. Then, click on the chevron “&gt;” to expand the drop down menu. Finally, click on {menu Server Settings} and set the following values:

* ''''''Server Name:'''''' [http://mail.thundermail.com mail.thundermail.com] ''''''Server Port:'''''' 993
* ''''''Security:'''''' SSL/TLS
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address e.g. ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''
* ''''''Authentication method: ''''''OAuth2''''''

==Sending Email==
# Switch to your Thundermail account: Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Account Settings}.
# In the left sidebar, click on your Thundermail email account. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''. Click on {button Edit outgoing server…} and set the following values:
 
* ''''''Server Name:'''''' mail.thundermail.com
* ''''''Server Port:'''''' 465 ''''''Connection Security:'''''' SSL/TLS
* ''''''Username:'''''' your full Thundermail email address For example: ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''
* ''''''Authentication method:'''''' OAuth2
==Thundermail Calendar==
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {for not tb152}{menu New Account}{/for}{for tb152}{menu Add Account}{/for} > {menu Calendar} > {button On the Network}.
# For ''''''Username:'''''', enter your Thundermail email address. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''.
# For ''''''Location'''''', enter ''''''mail.thundermail.com''''''.
# Click {button Find Calendars}.
# In the ''''''Create New Calendar'''''' dialog, select your Thundermail calendar and click {button Subscribe}.
==Thundermail Address Book==
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰}  > {for not tb152}{menu New Account}{/for}{for tb152}{menu Add Account}{/for} > {for not tb152}{menu New Address Book}{/for}{for tb152}{menu Address Book}{/for} > {for not tb152}{button New remote Address Book}{/for}{for tb152}{menu Add remote Address Book}{/for}.
#  For ''''''Username:'''''', enter your Thundermail email address. For example ''''''nemo@thundermail<!---->.com''''''.
# For ''''''URL/Hostname'''''', enter ''''''https://mail.thundermail.com''''''.
# Click {button Continue}.
# Select your Thundermail Address Book and click {button Continue}.

[[UI:details_end]]

=Send Thundermail, use your Thundermail Calendar and Thundermail Address Book, and have some fun!=
* [[Send and receive messages in Thunderbird|Send and receive email]] with Thundermail. If you have large files, you can also use [https://support.tb.pro/hc/sections/43937747865235 ''''''Thunderbird Send'''''']. which is included with your Thunderbird Pro subscription.
* If you have a [https://support.tb.pro/hc/articles/51338950680467-Setting-Up-a-Catch-All-Alias Catch-All Alias configured in Thundermail], here''s now to use it:
*# When composing or replying to an email, click on the email address next to ''''''From''''''.
*# Click on {button Customize From Address…}. 
*# Finally, type in an email address for the custom domain you created the Catch-All in.
* Enjoy your Thundermail Calendar: [https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/products/thunderbird/email-and-messaging/calendar Create some events, invite people to invites, etc].
* Use your Thundermail Address Book for [[Addressing an Email|composing email]], managing your contacts, etc.
