rbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-150">Thunderbird 150</h1>
<ul><li> Account hub is opened on the first run of Thunderbird. It is now the default across mail, calendar and address book.
</li><li> ''Recent Destinations'' in General Settings now supports alphabetical sorting.
</li><li> You can now choose your custom <strong>Accent Color</strong>:
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span>&gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li><li> Next to <strong>Define the color used for primary buttons and highlighted elements:</strong>, click one of the following buttons: <span class="button">Follow operating system</span>, <span class="button">Thunderbird blue</span>, <span class="button">Purple</span>, <span class="button">Orange</span>, <span class="button">Pink</span>, <span class="button">Ink</span>, <span class="button">Teal</span>. 
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
