rbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-150">Thunderbird 150</h1>
<ul><li> Account hub is opened on the first run of Thunderbird. It is now the default across mail, calendar and address book.
</li><li> <strong>Recent Destinations</strong> in General Settings now supports alphabetical sorting. See: Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">General</span> &gt; Scroll down to <strong>Sort order:</strong> under <strong>Folder Management Options</strong> and choose <span class="menu">Alphabetical</span> or <span class="menu">Most recent</span>.
</li><li> You can now choose your custom <strong>Accent Color</strong>:
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Appearance</span>.
</li><li> Next to <strong>Define the color used for primary buttons and highlighted elements:</strong>, select one of the following buttons: <span class="button">Follow operating system</span>, <span class="button">Thunderbird blue</span>, <span class="button">Purple</span>, <span class="button">Orange</span>, <span class="button">Pink</span>, <span class="button">Ink</span>, or, <span class="button">Teal</span>. 
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
