<p>Gmail does not use a standard IMAP archive folder, unlike other mail providers that use an <strong>Archive</strong> folder (as described in the <a href="/en-US/kb/archived-messages">Archived Messages</a> article). When you archive an email in Gmail, it simply removes the <strong>Inbox</strong> label while the email itself remains completely safe and searchable within your <strong>All Mail</strong> folder.
</p><p>To achieve parity with the way Gmail handles archiving messages, tick <span class="button">Keep messages in:</span> and then select <strong>Other</strong> under <strong>Message Archives</strong> like so:
