<h1 id="w_what-is-oauth">What is OAuth?</h1>
<p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OAuth">OAuth</a> is a web standard that allows you to authorize an application (such as Thunderbird) or service to sign in to a provider without divulging private information, such as the password to your provider’s account.
</p><p>For less technical people, here is a "bank" analogy for OAuth: 
</p>
<ul><li> Instead of giving Thunderbird your <strong>full access password</strong> (the one that allows you to access all of a provider’s services), you log in to your bank''s website (possibly with the bank''s ads) directly. 
