signed-account-hub"><span class="tocnumber">14.4</span> <span class="toctext">Redesigned Account hub</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manual-folder-sorting"><span class="tocnumber">14.5</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Folder Sorting</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users"><span class="tocnumber">14.6</span> <span class="toctext">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_export-for-mobile"><span class="tocnumber">14.7</span> <span class="toctext">Export for Mobile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">14.8</span> <span class="toctext">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">15</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">15.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">15.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">15.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">15.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-153-esr-153-meadow">Thunderbird 153 / ESR 153 “Meadow”</h1>
<ul><li> ESR 153 “Meadow” includes all the improvements since 140, plus these version 153 highlights…
</li><li> Unified folders display your custom account color indicator with an account name tooltip.
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span> &gt; Click your email account, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">button</span> underneath <strong>Color:</strong> and select a color for that account, for example pink.
<dl><dt> <img alt="tb153-change-account-color" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-07-26-20-10-20-d58a9d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> You will now see an indicator with that color (in our example: pink) for that account in the message list in a unified folder. There will also be a tooltip with the account name (in our example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>).
<dl><dt> <img alt="tb-153-account-color-indicator-tooltip" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-07-26-20-21-18-cb6afb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
</li><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/tb-oauth">OAuth</a> login for email accounts (for example: Gmail, Thundermail, etc.) opens in the system default web browser. Thunderbird 152 and older versions opened the OAuth login in a Thunderbird tab.
</li></ul>
