<h3 id="w_manually-configuring-imap-and-pop-accounts">Manually Configuring IMAP and POP accounts</h3>
<p>To manually configure or modify Microsoft email account settings:
</p>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>. The Account Settings dialog window will be displayed.
</li><li> Select your Microsoft email account from the list on the left.
</li><li> In the left panel, below your Microsoft email account name, click on <span class="menu">Server Settings</span>. The server settings will be displayed in the right panel.
</li></ol>
<div class="note"><strong>Note</strong>: For an explanation of IMAP and POP, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/glossary-terms-including-types-accounts">Glossary of Terms including types of Accounts</a>.</div>
<h4 id="w_imap-mail-account-settings">IMAP mail account settings</h4>
<p>Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings as of this writing.
</p>
<ul><li>Server Name: <code>outlook.office366.com</code>
</li><li>Port: 993
</li><li>User Name: your username (for example <em><a href="mailto:tbtesttb@hotmail.com">tbtesttb@hotmail.com</a></em>)
</li><li>Connection security: SSL/TLS
</li><li>Authentication method: OAuth2
</li></ul>
<h4 id="w_pop-mail-account-settings">POP mail account settings</h4>
<p>CConfigure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings:.
</p>
<ul><li>Server Name:  <code>outlook.office366.com</code>
</li><li>Port: 995
</li><li>User Name: your username (for example <em><a href="mailto:tbtesttb@hotmail.com">tbtesttb@hotmail.com</a></em>)
</li><li>Connection security: SSL/TLS
</li><li>Authentication method: OAuth2
</li><li>Configure the rest of the server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators.
</li></ul>
<h3 id="w_configuring-the-smtp-outgoing-server">Configuring the SMTP outgoing server</h3>
<p>Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings:.
</p>
<ul><li>At the bottom left, click <span class="button">Edit outgoing server…</span>. Configure them as follows:
<ul><li>Server Name: smtp-mail.outlook.com
</li><li>Port: 587
</li><li>Connection security: STARTTLS
</li><li>Authentication method:OAuth2
</li><li>User Name: your username (for example <em><a href="mailto:tbtesttb@hotmail.com">tbtesttb@hotmail.com</a></em>)
</li></ul>
</li></ul>
<div class="note"><strong>Note</strong>: If you receive a password error in Thunderbird when trying to retrieve messages using POP, you may need to sign in using webmail first and <a href="http://windows.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/outlook/send-receive-from-app">enable POP settings</a> under the Options section of your Outlook.com email account.</div>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "363928", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 13, 2026, 12:03:11 AM", "datetime": "2026-10-13T00:03:11.989945-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "wip do not approve: discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/241", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:14:42+00:00','');
