===Configuring the SMTP outgoing server===
Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings:
*At the bottom right, click {button Edit outgoing server…}. 
**Server Name: smtp-mail.outlook<!-- -->.com
**Port: ''''''587''''''
**Connection security: ''''''STARTTLS''''''
**Authentication method:''''''OAuth2''''''
**User Name: your username (for example ''''tbtesttb@hotmail.com'''')','<p>Thunderbird can be used as a client for all of Microsoft''s email services (Hotmail, Outlook.com, Windows Live Mail, Office 365, Microsoft 365, etc.) henceforth referred to as <em>Microsoft email</em>. Thunderbird will download messages from the Microsoft server and store them on your local system. Similarly, Thunderbird can be used to compose messages which are sent through Hotmail''s mail servers. You can still use Microsoft''s web-based application (for example <a href="http://outlook.com">outlook.com</a>) - Thunderbird will query the server and synchronize messages.
</p>
