</li><li>User Name: your username (for example: <em><a href="mailto:tbtesttb@hotmail.com">tbtesttb@hotmail.com</a></em>)
</li><li>Connection security: <strong>SSL/TLS</strong>
</li><li>Authentication method: <strong>OAuth2</strong>
</li></ul>
<h3 id="w_configuring-the-smtp-outgoing-server">Configuring the SMTP outgoing server</h3>
<p>Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings:
</p>
<ul><li>At the bottom right, click <span class="button">Edit outgoing server…</span>. 
<ul><li>Server Name: smtp-mail.outlook.com
</li><li>Port: <strong>587</strong>
</li><li>Connection security: <strong>STARTTLS</strong>
</li><li>Authentication method:<strong>OAuth2</strong>
</li><li>User Name: your username (for example <em><a href="mailto:tbtesttb@hotmail.com">tbtesttb@hotmail.com</a></em>)
</li></ul>
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "363931", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 13, 2026, 12:28:04 AM", "datetime": "2026-10-13T00:28:04.399998-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "fix typo, please do not translate. discussion: https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/241", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Oct 13, 2026, 12:28:20 AM", "datetime": "2026-10-13T00:28:20.045404-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization", "text": "Oct 17, 2026, 11:54:50 AM", "datetime": "2026-10-17T11:54:50.088252-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Readied for localization by", "text": "rtanglao", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:14:34+00:00','M');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (363932,'en-US','thunderbird-and-hotmail-redirect-1','Thunderbird and Hotmail','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-hotmail-redirect-1','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-hotmail-redirect-1/revision/363932',NULL,'2026-10-13T00:31:20.228062-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','REDIRECT [[Thunderbird and Microsoft email (Office365, Hotmail, outlook.com, etc)]]','<p>REDIRECT <a href="/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-hotmail">Thunderbird and Microsoft email (Office365, Hotmail, outlook.com, etc)</a>
</p>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "363932", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 13, 2026, 12:31:20 AM", "datetime": "2026-10-13T00:31:20.228062-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Roland Tanglao", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T18:14:32+00:00','');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (364910,'en-US','close-tray-starting-154','Close to tray starting in 154','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/close-tray-starting-154','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/close-tray-starting-154/revision/364910',337890,'2026-10-14T23:12:18.620791-07:00','Mark Heijl','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/markh2/','minor edits',1,'2026-10-15T04:24:19.073503-07:00','AliceWyman',1,1,0,NULL,NULL,'approved','__TOC__

If you use Thunderbird on Windows, you may be familiar with sending Thunderbird to the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taskbar#Notification_area system tray] (the notification area) so it keeps running in the background. Starting with Thunderbird 154, the way this works has changed – instead of minimizing to the tray, Thunderbird now moves to the tray when you close it. This article explains the change and shows you how to turn the feature on.
{note}''''''Note:'''''' This feature applies only to ''''''Thunderbird 154 and later'''''' on Windows 10 and 11. It is not available on macOS or Linux.{/note}

==“Close to tray” instead of “minimize to tray”==
In earlier versions, Thunderbird could be set to move to the system tray when you minimized the window. As of Thunderbird 154, that behavior has been replaced:
* The ''''''Minimize'''''' button now simply minimizes the Thunderbird window, like other applications.
* The ''''''Close'''''' (X) button can move Thunderbird to the system tray instead of quitting, so it keeps running in the background.
If you previously used the ''''''When Thunderbird is minimized, move it to the tray'''''' setting, Thunderbird 154 and newer automatically migrates you to this new “''''''close to tray''''''” behavior. This keeps Thunderbird consistent with how modern Windows applications use the system tray.

==Turn on “close to tray”==
# Click the Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings}.
# Select the {menu General} tab and scroll down to the ''''''System Integration'''''' section.
# Check the box labeled ''''''When Thunderbird is closed, move it to the tray''''''. This option is off by default. Once this is enabled, clicking the ''''''Close'''''' (X) button moves Thunderbird to the system tray instead of quitting. Thunderbird keeps running in the background so you continue to receive new messages and notifications.

==Close Thunderbird from the system tray==
When “close to tray” is turned on, you can fully quit Thunderbird directly from the tray:
# In the system tray, right-click the Thunderbird icon.
# Select ''''''Exit Thunderbird''''''.
This lets you close Thunderbird without opening the window first.

==Start Thunderbird in the tray==
You can also have Thunderbird start directly in the system tray instead of opening a window when it launches.
# Click the Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Settings}.
# Select the {menu General} tab and scroll down to the ''''''System Integration'''''' section.
# Check the box labeled ''''''Start Thunderbird in the tray''''''. This option is off by default. Once you check this option, you have to click on the Thunderbird icon in the tray to open a Thunderbird window.','<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_close-to-tray-instead-of-minimize-to-tray"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">“Close to tray” instead of “minimize to tray”</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_turn-on-close-to-tray"><span class="tocnumber">2</span> <span class="toctext">Turn on “close to tray”</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_close-thunderbird-from-the-system-tray"><span class="tocnumber">3</span> <span class="toctext">Close Thunderbird from the system tray</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_start-thunderbird-in-the-tray"><span class="tocnumber">4</span> <span class="toctext">Start Thunderbird in the tray</span></a></li></ul></div>
<p>If you use Thunderbird on Windows, you may be familiar with sending Thunderbird to the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taskbar#Notification_area">system tray</a> (the notification area) so it keeps running in the background. Starting with Thunderbird 154, the way this works has changed – instead of minimizing to the tray, Thunderbird now moves to the tray when you close it. This article explains the change and shows you how to turn the feature on.
</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> This feature applies only to <strong>Thunderbird 154 and later</strong> on Windows 10 and 11. It is not available on macOS or Linux.</div>
<h2 id="w_close-to-tray-instead-of-minimize-to-tray">“Close to tray” instead of “minimize to tray”</h2>
<p>In earlier versions, Thunderbird could be set to move to the system tray when you minimized the window. As of Thunderbird 154, that behavior has been replaced:
</p>
<ul><li> The <strong>Minimize</strong> button now simply minimizes the Thunderbird window, like other applications.
</li><li> The <strong>Close</strong> (X) button can move Thunderbird to the system tray instead of quitting, so it keeps running in the background.
</li></ul>
<p>If you previously used the <strong>When Thunderbird is minimized, move it to the tray</strong> setting, Thunderbird 154 and newer automatically migrates you to this new “<strong>close to tray</strong>” behavior. This keeps Thunderbird consistent with how modern Windows applications use the system tray.
</p>
<h2 id="w_turn-on-close-to-tray">Turn on “close to tray”</h2>
<ol><li> Click the Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span>.
</li><li> Select the <span class="menu">General</span> tab and scroll down to the <strong>System Integration</strong> section.
</li><li> Check the box labeled <strong>When Thunderbird is closed, move it to the tray</strong>. This option is off by default. Once this is enabled, clicking the <strong>Close</strong> (X) button moves Thunderbird to the system tray instead of quitting. Thunderbird keeps running in the background so you continue to receive new messages and notifications.
</li></ol>
<h2 id="w_close-thunderbird-from-the-system-tray">Close Thunderbird from the system tray</h2>
<p>When “close to tray” is turned on, you can fully quit Thunderbird directly from the tray:
</p>
<ol><li> In the system tray, right-click the Thunderbird icon.
</li><li> Select <strong>Exit Thunderbird</strong>.
</li></ol>
<p>This lets you close Thunderbird without opening the window first.
</p>
<h2 id="w_start-thunderbird-in-the-tray">Start Thunderbird in the tray</h2>
<p>You can also have Thunderbird start directly in the system tray instead of opening a window when it launches.
</p>
<ol><li> Click the Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span>.
</li><li> Select the <span class="menu">General</span> tab and scroll down to the <strong>System Integration</strong> section.
</li><li> Check the box labeled <strong>Start Thunderbird in the tray</strong>. This option is off by default. Once you check this option, you have to click on the Thunderbird icon in the tray to open a Thunderbird window.
</li></ol>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "364910", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 14, 2026, 11:12:18 PM", "datetime": "2026-10-14T23:12:18.620791-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Mark Heijl", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/markh2/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "minor edits", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "Oct 15, 2026, 4:24:19 AM", "datetime": "2026-10-15T04:24:19.073503-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed by", "text": "AliceWyman", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is approved?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Is current revision?", "text": "Yes", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:04:59+00:00','');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (366264,'en-US','thunderbird-and-hotmail','Thunderbird and Microsoft email (Office365, Hotmail, outlook.com, etc)','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-hotmail','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/thunderbird-and-hotmail/revision/366264',363931,'2026-10-23T11:38:02.313633-07:00','Teo','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/teo951/','Improved "Configuring the SMTP outgoing server" section and some corrections.',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'unreviewed','Thunderbird can be used as a client for all of Microsoft''s email services (Hotmail, Outlook<!-- -->.com, Windows Live Mail, Office 365, Microsoft 365, etc.) henceforth referred to as ''''Microsoft email''''. Thunderbird will download messages from the Microsoft server and store them on your local system. Similarly, Thunderbird can be used to compose messages which are sent through Microsoft''s mail servers. You can still use Microsoft''s web-based application (for example outlook<!-- -->.com) - Thunderbird will query the server and synchronize messages.

__TOC__

=Configuring servers=
{note}''''''Note'''''': If you receive a password error in Thunderbird when trying to send or receive messages using POP or IMAP, you may need to sign in using webmail first and [https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/outlook/pop-imap-and-smtp-settings-for-outlook-com enable POP and IMAP as appropriate] under the Settings section of your Microsoft email account.{/note}
Microsoft accounts are configured automatically in Thunderbird using Thunderbird Account Hub.

Enter your Microsoft email address (for example: <code>tbtesttb@hotmail.com</code>) and password when prompted, and Thunderbird will configure the server settings for you. Whether you are using IMAP or POP, Thunderbird will automatically configure the server settings for you. 

For more details please refer to [[Account Hub for Thunderbird Desktop]].

If Thunderbird cannot configure the server settings automatically or you wish to override the automatic configuration, you can manually configure or modify the server settings.

*As of late 2026, here is a screenshot of the IMAP server settings in the Account Hub:
*;[[Image:tb157-microsoft-email-imap-account-hub]]
*And here is a screenshot of the POP server settings in the Account Hub:
*;[[Image:tb157-microsoft-email-pop-account-hub]]

==Manually Configuring IMAP and POP accounts==
To manually configure or modify Microsoft email account settings:
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Account Settings}. The Account Settings dialog window will be displayed.
# In the left panel select your Microsoft email account.
# Below your Microsoft email account name, click on {menu Server Settings}. The server settings will be displayed in the right panel.
{note}''''''Note'''''': For an explanation of IMAP and POP, please refer to [[Glossary of Terms including types of Accounts]].{/note}

===IMAP mail account settings===
Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings as of this writing.
*Server Name: <code>outlook.office366.com</code>
*Port: ''''''993''''''
*User Name: your username (for example: ''''tbtesttb@hotmail<!-- -->.com'''')
*Connection security: ''''''SSL/TLS''''''
*Authentication method: ''''''OAuth2''''''

===POP mail account settings===
Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings:
*Server Name:  <code>outlook.office366.com</code>
*Port: ''''''995''''''
*User Name: your username (for example: ''''tbtesttb@hotmail<!-- -->.com'''')
*Connection security: ''''''SSL/TLS''''''
*Authentication method: ''''''OAuth2''''''

==Configuring the SMTP outgoing server==
Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators.
# Click Thunderbird app menu {menu ☰} > {menu Account Settings}. The Account Settings dialog window will be displayed.
# In the left panel select your Microsoft email account.
# At the bottom right corner, click {button Edit outgoing server…}. Here are some typical settings:
*Server Name: smtp-mail.outlook<!-- -->.com
*Port: ''''''587''''''
*Connection security: ''''''STARTTLS''''''
*Authentication method:''''''OAuth2''''''
*User Name: your username (for example ''''tbtesttb@hotmail<!-- -->.com'''')','<p>Thunderbird can be used as a client for all of Microsoft''s email services (Hotmail, Outlook.com, Windows Live Mail, Office 365, Microsoft 365, etc.) henceforth referred to as <em>Microsoft email</em>. Thunderbird will download messages from the Microsoft server and store them on your local system. Similarly, Thunderbird can be used to compose messages which are sent through Microsoft''s mail servers. You can still use Microsoft''s web-based application (for example outlook.com) - Thunderbird will query the server and synchronize messages.
</p>
<div id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_configuring-servers"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Configuring servers</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manually-configuring-imap-and-pop-accounts"><span class="tocnumber">1.1</span> <span class="toctext">Manually Configuring IMAP and POP accounts</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_imap-mail-account-settings"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.1</span> <span class="toctext">IMAP mail account settings</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-3"><a href="#w_pop-mail-account-settings"><span class="tocnumber">1.1.2</span> <span class="toctext">POP mail account settings</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_configuring-the-smtp-outgoing-server"><span class="tocnumber">1.2</span> <span class="toctext">Configuring the SMTP outgoing server</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_configuring-servers">Configuring servers</h1>
<div class="note"><strong>Note</strong>: If you receive a password error in Thunderbird when trying to send or receive messages using POP or IMAP, you may need to sign in using webmail first and <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/outlook/pop-imap-and-smtp-settings-for-outlook-com">enable POP and IMAP as appropriate</a> under the Settings section of your Microsoft email account.</div>
<p>Microsoft accounts are configured automatically in Thunderbird using Thunderbird Account Hub.
</p><p>Enter your Microsoft email address (for example: <code>tbtesttb@hotmail.com</code>) and password when prompted, and Thunderbird will configure the server settings for you. Whether you are using IMAP or POP, Thunderbird will automatically configure the server settings for you. 
</p><p>For more details please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/account-hub-thunderbird-desktop">Account Hub for Thunderbird Desktop</a>.
</p><p>If Thunderbird cannot configure the server settings automatically or you wish to override the automatic configuration, you can manually configure or modify the server settings.
</p>
<ul><li>As of late 2026, here is a screenshot of the IMAP server settings in the Account Hub:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb157-microsoft-email-imap-account-hub" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-10-13-00-05-51-76c18c.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li>And here is a screenshot of the POP server settings in the Account Hub:
<dl><dt><img alt="tb157-microsoft-email-pop-account-hub" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-10-13-00-08-29-23715b.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_manually-configuring-imap-and-pop-accounts">Manually Configuring IMAP and POP accounts</h2>
<p>To manually configure or modify Microsoft email account settings:
</p>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>. The Account Settings dialog window will be displayed.
</li><li> In the left panel select your Microsoft email account.
</li><li> Below your Microsoft email account name, click on <span class="menu">Server Settings</span>. The server settings will be displayed in the right panel.
</li></ol>
<div class="note"><strong>Note</strong>: For an explanation of IMAP and POP, please refer to <a href="/en-US/kb/glossary-terms-including-types-accounts">Glossary of Terms including types of Accounts</a>.</div>
<h3 id="w_imap-mail-account-settings">IMAP mail account settings</h3>
<p>Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings as of this writing.
</p>
<ul><li>Server Name: <code>outlook.office366.com</code>
</li><li>Port: <strong>993</strong>
</li><li>User Name: your username (for example: <em>tbtesttb@hotmail.com</em>)
</li><li>Connection security: <strong>SSL/TLS</strong>
</li><li>Authentication method: <strong>OAuth2</strong>
</li></ul>
<h3 id="w_pop-mail-account-settings">POP mail account settings</h3>
<p>Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators. Here are some typical settings:
</p>
<ul><li>Server Name:  <code>outlook.office366.com</code>
</li><li>Port: <strong>995</strong>
</li><li>User Name: your username (for example: <em>tbtesttb@hotmail.com</em>)
</li><li>Connection security: <strong>SSL/TLS</strong>
</li><li>Authentication method: <strong>OAuth2</strong>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_configuring-the-smtp-outgoing-server">Configuring the SMTP outgoing server</h2>
<p>Configure the  server settings according to the settings provided by your Microsoft account administrators.
</p>
<ol><li> Click Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span>. The Account Settings dialog window will be displayed.
</li><li> In the left panel select your Microsoft email account.
</li><li> At the bottom right corner, click <span class="button">Edit outgoing server…</span>. Here are some typical settings:
</li></ol>
<ul><li>Server Name: smtp-mail.outlook.com
</li><li>Port: <strong>587</strong>
</li><li>Connection security: <strong>STARTTLS</strong>
</li><li>Authentication method:<strong>OAuth2</strong>
</li><li>User Name: your username (for example <em>tbtesttb@hotmail.com</em>)
</li></ul>','[{"label": "Revision id", "text": "366264", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Created", "text": "Oct 23, 2026, 11:38:02 AM", "datetime": "2026-10-23T11:38:02.313633-07:00", "href": null}, {"label": "Creator", "text": "Teo", "datetime": null, "href": "https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/teo951/"}, {"label": "Comment", "text": "Improved \"Configuring the SMTP outgoing server\" section and some corrections.", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Reviewed", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}, {"label": "Ready for localization", "text": "No", "datetime": null, "href": null}]','2026-11-03T20:18:06+00:00','');
INSERT INTO article_revisions (revision_id, locale, article_slug, article_title, article_url, revision_url, previous_revision_id, created, creator_name, creator_url, comment, reviewed, reviewed_date, reviewed_by, is_approved, is_current, ready_for_l10n, readied_for_l10n_date, readied_for_l10n_by, status, source, content_html, info_json, scraped_at, significance) VALUES (366759,'en-US','new-thunderbird-android','New in Thunderbird for Android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/new-thunderbird-android/revision/366759',330147,'2026-10-27T00:57:47.135371-07:00','Roland Tanglao','https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/user/rtanglao/','wip do not translate. needs monica''s review https://github.com/thunderbird/knowledgebase-issues/issues/244',1,'2026-10-27T00:58:59.581881-07:00','rtanglao',1,1,1,'2026-10-27T22:27:37.465920-07:00','rtanglao','approved','[[T:TBAndroidMore]]
This article introduces the most interesting new features, improvements, and changes visible to users which are available in Thunderbird for Android. For full details, please refer to [[Thunderbird release notes - What''s new and known issues]].

__TOC__
=Thunderbird 24=
*HTML signatures now work with individual identities.
*You can now choose {menu Reply} or {menu Reply all} when both are applicable by tapping the reply arrow icon or the menu {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''''kebab'''''' menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab).
=Older Releases=
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 23==
* Multiple line signature issue fixed.
* Attachment filenames with non-ASCII characters issue fixed.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 22==
* Thundermail integration improvements.
* New indicator dot for the sort menu {button [[Image:tba24-sort-icon]]}:
**In the three horizontal bar sort menu for each folder (for example: your ''''''Inbox'''''' ):
**;[[Image:tba24-sort-menu]] 
** When you tap the icon for the sort menu {button [[Image:tba24-sort-icon]]}, it displays an indicator dot by the selected option (for example ''''''Date'''''' for sorting by date).
**;[[Image:tba24-sort-indicator-dot]] 
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 21==
* Empty trash folder action fixed in 21.1.
* Composition defaults and "Fetching mail" modernization. 
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 20==
* Thundermail email account setup improvements. Full instructions:[[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android]].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 19==
* The QR Code scanner now works with Thundermail QR codes to quickly setup your Thundermail email account. Full instructions:[[Thundermail and Thunderbird for Android]].
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 18==
* PNG custom avatars are now supported (as well as JPEGs and stylized letter monograms as per the Thunderbird 17 section).
* There is a new setting to display times in ISO 8601 format ''''(YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm)'''' in the message list.
*# Tap {button ≡} > tap the gear icon:{button [[Image:gear icon]]}.
*# Tap {button General settings} > tap {menu Display} > under ''''''Messsage lists'''''', tap {menu Date/Time Format} > tap {button ISO}.
==Thunderbird 17==
* Custom avatars for email accounts are now available. JPEGs only for now. PNGs will be supported in a future release. Upload yours as follows: 
*# Tap {button ≡} at the top left > tap the gear icon:{button [[Image:gear icon]]} at the bottom left.
*# Tap your email account that you want to customize e.g. <code>nemo@thunderbird.net</code> > tap {menu General settings} > tap {menu Image} to upload your custom JPEG. You can also use a stylized letter monogram by tapping {menu Monogram} or pick one of the built-in icons by tapping {menu Icon}.
==Thunderbird 16==
* The SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com have been fixed in [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312 #10312].
* The following issue was fixed in TB 16.1 which was released one week after Thunderbird 16.0. <del>Known Issue: Deleted/read messages in your unified inbox may not update until you manually refresh. We hope to have a fix soon. you can can follow along on issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10243 #10243]</del>
==Thunderbird 15==
* There are further SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com and the team is testing a fix. You can follow along on issue [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/10312 #10312]. It looks like this will fixed in the next release, TB 16.
==Thunderbird 14==
* SMTP issues with enterprise and educational accounts on outlook.com have been fixed.
==Thunderbird 13==
* The notification in status bar re-appearing multiple times a day issue (github issue [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/8049 #8049]) has been fixed.
* Special folders (Trash, Sent, Drafts, Archives, etc) not appearing after updating from TB11 to TB12 (github issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9771 #9771]) was fixed.
* The bug with outgoing email not working for certain educational and enterprise accounts is scheduled to be fixed in the next release, Thunderbird 14 for Android (github issue: [https://github.com/thunderbird/thunderbird-android/issues/9160 #9160]).
==Thunderbird 12==
* If you use a password manager, Android will now use it to automatically fill in your password when you add a new account.
==Thunderbird 11==
* Mail folders are easier to navigate.
* Algorithmic darkening makes reading emails easier in dark mode.
* Thunderbird 11.1 : Selected/read/unread message states are now easier to distinguish visually.
* You can still see font settings if you search for ''''''font'''''' in Settings. This will be removed in a future Thunderbird release. Please use the Android operating system font size settings instead.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 10==
* You can now empty your Spam folder by tapping {menu Empty Spam} in the Spam folder''s menu {menu ⋮} (also known as the ''''''kebab'''''' menu because the 3 vertical dots resemble a kebab).
* On Android 10 or older, you now have an option to use the system theme.
*# Tap {button ≡} at the top left > tap the gear icon:{button [[Image:gear icon]]} at the bottom left.
*# Tap {button General settings} > tap {menu Display} > tap {button Use system default} under ''''''Theme''''''
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 9==
* Initial Android 15 support.
* Thunderbird attempts to use your email provider''s auto configuration database. If it fails it, it uses Mozilla''s database.
[[UI:details_end]]
[[UI:details_start]]
==Thunderbird 8==
* Refer to [[New in Thunderbird for Android version 8]] please.
