<h1 id="w_thunderbird-159">Thunderbird 159</h1>
<ul><li> More improvements to Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span>  and Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span> strings. Most people will not notice since the changes are subtle and do not affect how you use Thunderbird. More technical and veteran Thunderbird users will notice some changesto frequently usd strings. For example, to access the Thunderbird <a href="/en-US/kb/config-editor">Config Editor</a> in 159, you click on <span class="button">Advanced settings</span> instead of <span class="button">Config Editor…</span>.
</li><li> More string changes are coming in 160.
</li><li> Changes to the Settings and Account Settings user interface itself are currently planned for a post 160 release.
</li></ul>
