ss="tocnumber">20.2</span> <span class="toctext">New Appearance Panel in Settings</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_native-os-notifications"><span class="tocnumber">20.3</span> <span class="toctext">Native OS Notifications</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_redesigned-account-hub"><span class="tocnumber">20.4</span> <span class="toctext">Redesigned Account hub</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_manual-folder-sorting"><span class="tocnumber">20.5</span> <span class="toctext">Manual Folder Sorting</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_experimental-exchange-support-for-advanced-users"><span class="tocnumber">20.6</span> <span class="toctext">Experimental Exchange Support for advanced users</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_export-for-mobile"><span class="tocnumber">20.7</span> <span class="toctext">Export for Mobile</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_horizontal-scroll-for-table-view"><span class="tocnumber">20.8</span> <span class="toctext">Horizontal Scroll for Table View</span></a></li></ul></li><li class="toclevel-1"><a href="#w_older-releases"><span class="tocnumber">21</span> <span class="toctext">Older Releases</span></a><ul><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-139"><span class="tocnumber">21.1</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 139</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-138"><span class="tocnumber">21.2</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 138</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-137"><span class="tocnumber">21.3</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 137</span></a></li><li class="toclevel-2"><a href="#w_thunderbird-136"><span class="tocnumber">21.4</span> <span class="toctext">Thunderbird 136</span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-159">Thunderbird 159</h1>
<ul><li> More improvements to Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Settings</span>  and Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span> strings. Most people will not notice since the changes are subtle and do not affect how you use Thunderbird. More technical and veteran Thunderbird users will notice some changes to strings in frequently used settings. For example, to access the Thunderbird <a href="/en-US/kb/config-editor">Config Editor</a> in 159, you click on <span class="button">Advanced settings</span> instead of <span class="button">Config Editor…</span>.
</li></ul>
<p>
</p>
<ul><li> More string changes are coming in 160.
</li><li> Changes to the Settings and Account Settings user interface itself are currently planned for a post 160 release.
</li></ul>
<p></p><section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
