<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-153-esr-153-meadow">Thunderbird 153 / ESR 153 “Meadow”</h1>
<ul><li> ESR 153 “Meadow” includes all the improvements since 140, plus these version 153 highlights…
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_account-name-custom-account-color-indicator-for-unified-folders" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-expanded="false">Account Name custom account color indicator for unified folders</button></h2>
<ul class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-5" aria-hidden="true"><li> Unified folders display your custom account color indicator with an account name tooltip.
<ol><li> Thunderbird app menu <span class="menu">☰</span> &gt; <span class="menu">Account Settings</span> &gt; Click your email account, for example <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>
</li><li> Click the <span class="button">button</span> underneath <strong>Color:</strong> and select a color for that account, for example pink.
<dl><dt> <img alt="tb153-change-account-color" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-07-26-20-10-20-d58a9d.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li><li> You will now see an indicator with that color (in our example: pink) for that account in the message list in a unified folder. There will also be a tooltip with the account name (in our example: <code>nemo@thundermail.com</code>).
<dl><dt> <img alt="tb-153-account-color-indicator-tooltip" class="wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2026-07-26-20-21-18-cb6afb.png" src="https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title="">
</dt></dl>
</li></ol>
</li></ul>
<h2 id="w_oauth-dialog-opens-in-system-web-browser" class="is-summary"><button type="button" aria-controls="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-expanded="false">OAuth dialog opens in system web browser</button></h2><div class="mzp-js-details-wrapper is-closed" id="expand-mzpcdetailshmzpcdetailsdivforh-6" aria-hidden="true"><ul><li> <a href="/en-US/kb/tb-oauth">OAuth</a> login for email accounts (for example: Gmail, Thundermail, etc.) opens in the system default web browser. Thunderbird 152 and older versions opened the OAuth login in a Thunderbird tab.
</li></ul><p></p></div>

</section>
<section class="mzp-c-details is-details">
<p></p>
<h1 id="w_thunderbird-152">Thunderbird 152</h1>
